# Vulnerability details

## Impact
In the ``NFTFloorOracle`` contract if the first asset feeder set a price that is too different of all others feeders the call to ``getPrice`` function will revert. The offending feeder can not correct such situation in this case the NFT oracle price for an given asset will be blocked.

Note: in this case the ``admin`` user needs to intervene to manually set the "correct" price to save ``getPrice`` from failing.

## Proof of Concept
1. ``getPrice`` of an asset can fail when the last update time is expired

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-11-paraspace/blob/c6820a279c64a299a783955749fdc977de8f0449/paraspace-core/contracts/misc/NFTFloorOracle.sol#L243-L246

2. If it happens that we have a first asset feeder that assigns a first price

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-11-paraspace/blob/c6820a279c64a299a783955749fdc977de8f0449/paraspace-core/contracts/misc/NFTFloorOracle.sol#L195

this first price will automatically be assigned as valid

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-11-paraspace/blob/c6820a279c64a299a783955749fdc977de8f0449/paraspace-core/contracts/misc/NFTFloorOracle.sol#L361-L364

3. all others feeders will fail if their price is too different from the first one assigned

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-11-paraspace/blob/c6820a279c64a299a783955749fdc977de8f0449/paraspace-core/contracts/misc/NFTFloorOracle.sol#L365-L372

4. and because of this there will no be any other successful price update. Even if the offending feeder tries to correct the first price it will fail for the same reason.

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
I would suggest accepting all feeders data and the in ``_combine`` function take only the filtered one to finally settle the price without the admin user to intervene.

