# Vulnerability details

## Impact

**The single guardian can add itself as a multisig address. While still having access over multisig controls leading to centralisation issues. By disabling all other multisigs via `disableMultisig`**

Scenario 1:

A guardian can gain access of the whole protocol, by adding itself as a multisig, diasble all other multisigs via `disableMultisig,`

re-enable itself `enableMultisig` and be the sole controller of multsig. (as well as being the guardian)

… proceed to soley manipulate function e.g. oracle price

Code: [https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-gogopool/blob/aec9928d8bdce8a5a4efe45f54c39d4fc7313731/contracts/contract/MultisigManager.sol#L35-L36](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-gogopool/blob/aec9928d8bdce8a5a4efe45f54c39d4fc7313731/contracts/contract/MultisigManager.sol#L35-L36)



Scenario 2:

A guardian can gain control of the whole protocol, add itself as a defender - pause all contract / diasbleMultisg and take control of contract

