# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Although zero address checks are seen low priority this following vulnerability can affect the whole protoco.

The guardian would require to be set and confirmed via `setGuardian` and `confirmGuardian`. If in the event of initiating transfer of guardian ownership a zero address ‘0x00’ is provided (during transfer) the `newAddress` is updated. 

However, the 0x00 cannot execute `confirmGuardian` leading to a frozen ownership transfer of guardian as no account can execute `confirmGuardian` given msg.sender != newGuardian, being 0x00.

Further: A malicious owner can appear to have a function that transfers guardian however can be frozen by design to appear as this could be transferred.

Note: Given addresses added to the multisig are added by guardian this would affect even setting the oraclePrice as onlyMultisig can not be called if not yet set / or no new multisig could be registered further via `registerMultisig` and `enableMultisig`.

## Proof of Concept (Foundry Solidity) 

Append test to: https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-gogopool/blob/aec9928d8bdce8a5a4efe45f54c39d4fc7313731/test/unit/Storage.t.sol

``` solidity

		function testGuardianZeroAddress() public {
		// Storage() was created by guardian in setup, so it is the guardian to start
		assertEq(store.getGuardian(), guardian);

		// Change the guardian
		vm.prank(guardian); // set zero address
		store.setGuardian(address(0x00));
		// Should not change yet, must be confirmed
		assertEq(store.getGuardian(), guardian);

		vm.startPrank(address(0x00));
		store.confirmGuardian(); //
		// however no access to 0x00. Hence protocol has essentially no guardian.
		// Blocking multisigs, and fund dependant oracle.
		assertEq(store.getGuardian(), address(0x00)); 

		vm.stopPrank();

	}


```

Test: forge test --match-test testGuardianZeroAddress -vvvvv
Test should fail given 0x00 cannot be accessed.


## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Prevent setGuardian assigning 0x00 to` newGuardian with a zero address check.

``` solidity

// Mitigation: check 
if(address == 0x00) { revert NoZeroAddress; }


```

