# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The `getGGPPriceInAVAX` function used in **Oracle.sol** returns the price provided by the `Multisig`. However, the function does not pre-validate if the price has been updated within a reasonable timeframe.

As a consequence, the `prices` can `rapidly become` `stale` if the price is not updated frequently enough, which could negatively affect user operations or protocol funds. 

## Proof of Concept
https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-gogopool/blob/main/contracts/contract/Oracle.sol#L46
```
		function getGGPPriceInAVAX() external view returns (uint256 price, uint256 timestamp) {
		price = getUint(keccak256("Oracle.GGPPriceInAVAX"));
		if (price == 0) {
			revert InvalidGGPPrice();
		}
		timestamp = getUint(keccak256("Oracle.GGPTimestamp"));
	}


```


## Recommended

It is recommended to apply one of the following oracle strategies:

- Update the logic of the `getGGPPriceInAVAX`  function to generate an error message if the asset price has not been updated within a reasonable timeframe defined in the contract.

- If the data update is more important for the protocol, an oracle with `moving averages` can be used instead, in which the accumulated price variable is measured more than once per period. See the following [reference](https://docs.uniswap.org/protocol/V2/guides/smart-contract-integration/building-an-oracle#moving-averages) for more details.

