# Vulnerability details

## Impact

`Trading.sol`, through `TradingExtension`/`TradingLibrary`, uses Chainlink to validate the user-provided `_priceData` for traded assets. The issue arises when either `_chainlinkEnabled` or `_chainlinkFeed` are not set. In this case, the [user-provided price](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-tigris/blob/b2ebb8ea1def4927a747e7a185174892506540ab/contracts/TradingExtension.sol#L181-L182) data will be taken as the verified price information (since the `verifyPrice` function will [skip the boundary checks](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-tigris/blob/b2ebb8ea1def4927a747e7a185174892506540ab/contracts/utils/TradingLibrary.sol#L112-L121)), allowing the attacker to drain all the funds from the pool by, for example, forging an extremely lucrative position being closed. 

This exploit can be made possible if either `_chainlinkEnabled` is set to `false` (possible by [owner setup](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-tigris/blob/b2ebb8ea1def4927a747e7a185174892506540ab/contracts/TradingExtension.sol#L231-L233)) or `_chainlinkFeed` is set to `address(0)` (this can happen since `PairsContract.addAsset` [does not validate](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-tigris/blob/b2ebb8ea1def4927a747e7a185174892506540ab/contracts/PairsContract.sol#L57) the `_chainlinkFeed` parameter — the same goes for [PairsContract.setAssetChainlinkFeed](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-tigris/blob/b2ebb8ea1def4927a747e7a185174892506540ab/contracts/PairsContract.sol#L36)).

## Proof of Concept

1. Alice, a developer of the Tigris protocol, adds a new asset, and mistakenly sets `chainlinkFeed` to `address(0)`
2. Bob, an attacker, opens a market position with `Trading.initiateMarketOrder` with arbitrary `_priceData` ("buy low"), taking a valid `_signature` from the oracle (so that `TradingLibrary.verifyPrice` executes successfully)
3. Bob closes his position with `Trading.initiateCloseOrder` with arbitrary  `_priceData` such that `TradingExtension._closePosition` returns a very large number for the `TradingLibrary.pnl` payout ("sell high"), thus eventually calling  `Trading._handleWithdraw` with that very high number of `_toMint`. As a result, the vault gets trained of a very high number in the desired `_outputToken` of the attacker.

Note: as this POC demonstrates, draining the vault require only a single chainlink feed for a particular asset not being properly initiated.

## Tools Used

Manual inspection

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Revert if `_chainlinkEnabled` is `false` or `_chainlinkFeed` is not set.

