# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The protocol offers a discount for auction starters when purchasing the liquidated NFT as an incentive for users to start an auction. I believe the intended discount should be 10%, but is currently implemented at 90%. 90% is too massive a discount for the auction starter.

## Proof of Concept

In our `constructor()` in `PaprController.sol`, we see the line `NFTEDAStarterIncentive(1e17)`. `1e17` is passed as a parameter to `_setCreatorDiscount()`.

[NFTEDAStarterIncentive.sol#L33-L35](https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/NFTEDA/extensions/NFTEDAStarterIncentive.sol#L33-L35)
```solidity
constructor(uint256 _auctionCreatorDiscountPercentWad){
    _setCreatorDiscount(_auctionCreatorDiscountPercentWad);
}
```

`_pricePercentAfterDiscount` is calculated this way
> `_pricePercentAfterDiscount = FixedPointMathLib.WAD - _auctionCreatorDiscountPercentWad = 1e18 - 1e17 = 1e1`.

[NFTEDAStarterIncentive.sol#L72-L77](https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/NFTEDA/extensions/NFTEDAStarterIncentive.sol#L72-L77)
```solidity
function _setCreatorDiscount(uint256 _auctionCreatorDiscountPercentWad) internal virtual {
	auctionCreatorDiscountPercentWad = _auctionCreatorDiscountPercentWad;
	_pricePercentAfterDiscount = FixedPointMathLib.WAD - _auctionCreatorDiscountPercentWad;

	emit SetAuctionCreatorDiscount(_auctionCreatorDiscountPercentWad);
}
```

`_pricePercentAfterDiscount` is used in `_auctionCurrentPrice()` to calculate the price that the auction starter has to pay. If price is 1000, we have
> `price = FixedPointMathLib.mulWadUp(price, _pricePercentAfterDiscount) = 1000 * 1e1/1e18 = 100`. 

Auction starter only pays 100 when price is 1000 i.e. a 90% discount.

[NFTEDAStarterIncentive.sol#L53-L67](https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/NFTEDA/extensions/NFTEDAStarterIncentive.sol#L53-L67)
```solidity
function _auctionCurrentPrice(uint256 id, uint256 startTime, INFTEDA.Auction memory auction)
    internal
    view
    virtual
    override
    returns (uint256)
{
    uint256 price = super._auctionCurrentPrice(id, startTime, auction);

    if (msg.sender == auctionState[id].starter) {
        price = FixedPointMathLib.mulWadUp(price, _pricePercentAfterDiscount);
    }

    return price;
}
```

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
We should be using initialising with `NFTEDAStarterIncentive(1e1)` instead of `NFTEDAStarterIncentive(1e17)`.

