# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The contract can reverts on calls of it's functions for it's high depend on one single logic

## Proof of Concept
The removeCollateral, purchaseLiquidationAuctionNFT, startLiquidationAuction, increaseDept function all heavenly relies for the asset prices on the underwritePriceForCollateral function from the ReservoirOracleUnderwriter contract only, the underwritePriceForCollateral function have a very sensitive ways to function correctly as the functions data can be valid only for 20 mins, and they can be valid only if signed by oracleSigner :

```
oracleInfo.message.timestamp > block.timestamp || oracleInfo.message.timestamp + VALID_FOR < block.timestamp

...

 if (signerAddress != oracleSigner) {
            revert IncorrectOracleSigner();
        }
```

if the oracleSigner does not provide the signatures or the nodes providing the signature get DOSed (attacked with ddos) or it's key gets compromised ..etc the all of the above function will reverts and the whole contract logics will be useless until the right signature came on, cause the contract PaprController does not rely on other oracles except for ReservoirOracleUnderwriter, and that contract relies on oracleSigner signatures, that's too sensitive as many reansactions handled that be updated for each 20 mins relies only on one user (oracleSigner) thus due to sensitivity of underwritePriceForCollateral nature it's a very critical to only rely on it. 

## Tools Used
Manual

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
In the ReservoirOracleUnderwriter contract add many roles for the signature validity (so if one gets compromised it won't stops) :

```
mapping(allowed=>bool) v_oracle;

...

 if (!v_oracle[signerAddress]) {
            revert IncorrectOracleSigner();
        }
...

function editOracle(address _v, bool situation) external onlyOwner {
    v_oracle[_v] = situation;
}

```

