# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Some tokens (like USDT) don’t correctly implement the EIP20 standard and their transfer/transferFrom function return void instead of a success
boolean on revert or failure.

As a result, there is a missing check to see whether the balance of the contract is increased once the collateral is transferred.
The contract will mark a failed or reverted transaction as a valid one due to the missing check.

## Proof of Concept
```
contract Token {
function transferFrom(address _from, address _to, uint256 _value) public returns (bool success);
}
contract MyBank{ 
mapping(address => uint) balances;
Token token;
function deposit(uint amount) public{
    token.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount); // failed to transfer the tokens
    balances[msg.sender] += amount; // the deposit of msg.sender increased even though the token.transferFrom returned a false.
}
}
```
## Tools Used
Manual Analysis

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
1. Use SafeERC20’s safeTransfer/safeTransferFrom functions
2. check the balances are updated properly after each transfer.

