# Lines of code

https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/PaprController.sol#L207-L232


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Function `buyAndReduceDebt()` removes debt from a vault and burns it by buying it on Uniswap in exchange for the controller's underlying token, but in the code when swapFee is not zero, contract tries to transfer swapFee from contract address rather than user address, if contract has underlying balance then it would lose that funds because caller should have paid that amount, and if it doesn't have then the transaction would fail and users can't use `buyAndReduceDebt()` with fee>0.

## Proof of Concept
This is `buyAndReduceDebt()` code:
```
    /// @inheritdoc IPaprController
    function buyAndReduceDebt(address account, ERC721 collateralAsset, IPaprController.SwapParams calldata params)
        external
        override
        returns (uint256)
    {
        bool hasFee = params.swapFeeBips != 0;

        (uint256 amountOut, uint256 amountIn) = UniswapHelpers.swap(
            pool,
            account,
            token0IsUnderlying,
            params.amount,
            params.minOut,
            params.sqrtPriceLimitX96,
            abi.encode(msg.sender)
        );

        if (hasFee) {
            underlying.transfer(params.swapFeeTo, amountIn * params.swapFeeBips / BIPS_ONE);
        }

        _reduceDebt({account: account, asset: collateralAsset, burnFrom: msg.sender, amount: amountOut});

        return amountOut;
    }
```
As you can see when swapFee>0 then contract transfer underlying token from its own address in the line ` underlying.transfer(params.swapFeeTo, amountIn * params.swapFeeBips / BIPS_ONE)`. this would have two impact:
1. if contract has underlying balance, then user can set swapFeeBips very high and steal all the contract underlying balance.
2. if contract don't have underlying balance, then calls to this function with swapFee>0 would fail. this can user users to get liquidated, for example a user has some smart contract which monitors his account (3rd party protocols) and whenever there is a chance of liquidation it would transfer user underlying token and pay some of the debt but because this function would revert when fee>0 so that call would fail too and user would get liquidated(scenario can happen for front-end user who wants to pay some of his debt to not get liquidating, this user transaction would fail and user can't prevent his account liquidation while he is interacting with protocol in correct way ). 

## Tools Used
VIM

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
send underlying token from msg.sender address.

