# Lines of code

https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/UniswapOracleFundingRateController.sol#L142-L147
https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/UniswapOracleFundingRateController.sol#L50


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The target price starts slowly falling after deployment and until first trade is made in the Uniswap pool. Users may take debt at a slightly lower Papr price.
## Proof of Concept
When `PaprController` is deployed, Papr token price is set to 1:1 with the underlying token in the Uniswap pool ([PaprController.sol#L85-L92](https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/PaprController.sol#L85-L92)). The pool serves as the market price discovery mechanism of Papr: changes in price of Papr in the pool will affect the interest rate of Papr. The price of Papr in the pool is used to calculate the target price ([UniswapOracleFundingRateController.sol#L45](https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/UniswapOracleFundingRateController.sol#L45)), the price at which Papr is borrowed by users of `PaprController` ([PaprController.sol#L463](https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/PaprController.sol#L463)).

When a Papr pool is deployed and initialized, the current price/tick is set to 1:1 ([UniswapHelpers.sol#L74](https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/9528f2711ff0c1522076b9f93fba13f88d5bd5e6/src/libraries/UniswapHelpers.sol#L74), [UniswapV3Pool.sol#L282-L283](https://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/main/contracts/UniswapV3Pool.sol#L282-L283)). However, pool oracle is always initialized with the zero price ([UniswapV3Pool.sol#L279](https://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/main/contracts/UniswapV3Pool.sol#L279), [Oracle.sol#L58](https://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/main/contracts/libraries/Oracle.sol#L58)). Thus, calling `updateTarget` after deployment and before first trade is made (before first observation is recorded in the pool) will reduce the target price:

```solidity
// test/uniswapOracleFundingRateController/UpdateTarget.t.sol

function testUpdateBeforeFirstRealObservation_AUDIT() public {
    // During initialization, the price is set to 0 in the pool's oracle.
    int56[] memory _tickCumulatives = new int56[](1);
    _tickCumulatives[0] = 0;
    MinimalObservablePool(fundingRateController.pool()).setTickComulatives(_tickCumulatives);

    // Ensure that `observe([0])` returns the zero price.
    uint32[] memory secondAgos = new uint32[](1);
    secondAgos[0] = 0;
    (int56[] memory tickCumulatives,) = MinimalObservablePool(fundingRateController.pool()).observe(secondAgos);
    assertEq(_tickCumulatives[0], 0);


    // Current target price is 1e6, the 1:1 price that was set during deployment.
    assertEq(fundingRateController.target(), 1e6);

    // Fast forwarding 1 day.
    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 days);

    // No swaps were made since deployment.
    (tickCumulatives,) = MinimalObservablePool(fundingRateController.pool()).observe(secondAgos);
    assertEq(_tickCumulatives[0], 0);

    // Updating the target price...
    fundingRateController.updateTarget();

    // ...the target price has reduced from 1.0 to 0.992062.
    assertEq(fundingRateController.target(), 992062);
}
```

