# Vulnerability details

Some implementations of ERC20 tokens do not revert during failure - they only return `false`. Callers of `transfer()` must check the return code to see whether the transfer was successful or not.

## Impact
The code as currently implemented does not handle these sorts of tokens properly when they're an underlying token, which would lead to fees not being paid.

## Proof of Concept
The token or a contract it relies on may be paused, causing the token to return false, and there are no checks for the return value:
