https://github.com/with-backed/papr/blob/1933da2e38ff9d47c17e2749d6088bbbd40bfa68/src/PaprController.sol#L202-L203


# Vulnerability details

Some tokens do not implement the ERC20 standard properly but are still accepted by most code that accepts ERC20 tokens.  For example Tether (USDT)'s `transfer()` and `transferFrom()` functions do not return booleans as the specification requires, and instead have no return value. When these sorts of tokens are cast to `IERC20`, their function signatures do not match and therefore the calls made revert. Another example is [BNB](https://mobile.twitter.com/UniswapProtocol/status/1072286773554876416) which caused problems in Uniswap.

## Impact
The code as currently implemented does not handle these sorts of tokens properly when they're an underlying token, which would lead to a locking of funds, since funds can be transferred in, but none can be taken back out.

## Proof of Concept
The fee can't be transferred out, blocking the increasing/reducing of debt:
