# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The sendPaprFromAuctionFees() function allows the administrator to transfer all the papr in the contract. There is no limit on the number.
```solidity
    function sendPaprFromAuctionFees(address to, uint256 amount) external override onlyOwner {
        papr.safeTransferFrom(address(this), to, amount);
    }
```
This will affect _handleExcess() due to insufficient papr in the contract. This will prevent burn(). This affects purchaseLiquidationAuctionNFT()
```solidity
    function _handleExcess(uint256 excess, uint256 neededToSaveVault, uint256 debtCached, Auction calldata auction)
        internal
        returns (uint256 remaining)
    {
        uint256 fee = excess * liquidationPenaltyBips / BIPS_ONE;
        uint256 credit = excess - fee;
        uint256 totalOwed = credit + neededToSaveVault;

        PaprToken(address(papr)).burn(address(this), fee);
```

## Proof of Concept
```solidity
    function sendPaprFromAuctionFees(address to, uint256 amount) external override onlyOwner {
        papr.safeTransferFrom(address(this), to, amount);
    }
```
## Tools Used
vscode
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Restrictions The administrator can only withdraw a certain amount of fees and cannot transfer all the Papr tokens in the contract

