# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The mint and burn functions both use the _mint and _burn functions, respectively, to update the balances of the to and account addresses. However, these functions may not include checks to ensure that the amount is within the acceptable range, potentially leading to arithmetic overflows or underflows.

## Proof of Concept
function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external onlyController {
        _mint(to, amount);
    }

    function burn(address account, uint256 amount) external onlyController {
        _burn(account, amount);
    }


## Tools Used
Remix, Ganache, others

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
To mitigate this vulnerability, it may be advisable to include checks to ensure that the amount is within the acceptable range before performing any math operations. For example, you could use the SafeMath library or manually check for overflows and underflows.

