# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Increasing the number of collateral tokens can result in unhandled gas consumption in the for loop when the arbiter is trying to calculate collaterals value during liquidating a line of credit.

## Proof of Concept

A borrower (malicious) requires Arbiter to enable token DAI as collateral. 
https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/f32cb3eeb08663f2456bf6e2fba21e964da3e8ae/contracts/modules/escrow/Escrow.sol#L100

After token DAI became enabled, the borrower can add it as collateral. So, he adds $100,000 token DAI as collateral, and borrows some fund from lenders.
https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/f32cb3eeb08663f2456bf6e2fba21e964da3e8ae/contracts/modules/escrow/Escrow.sol#L86

Everything is fine so far.

Then, the borrower requests the Arbiter to enable another valid token X. After becoming enabled, the borrower calls `addCollateral` with min amount of token X. Again the borrower requests the Arbiter to enable another token Y, and after becoming enabled, adding the minimum amount as collateral. Suppose, the borrower does this for 100 tokens, it means there are 100 token types as collateral, all has the minimum amount deposited except the first collateral DAI that has $100,000 value.

Later, due to the market condition (or deadline is passed, or any other reason), the borrower is going to be liquidated. The Arbiter calls `declareInsolvent()`. The flow of function calls will be:
`declareInsolvent()` in `LineOfCredit`=> `_canDeclareInsolvent()` in `SecuredLine` => `escrow.getCollateralValue()` => `state.getCollateralValue(oracle)` => `_getCollateralValue(self, oracle)` => `_getCollateralValue(EscrowState storage self, address oracle)`

https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/e8aa08b44f6132a5ed901f8daa231700c5afeb3a/contracts/modules/credit/LineOfCredit.sol#L143
https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/f32cb3eeb08663f2456bf6e2fba21e964da3e8ae/contracts/modules/credit/SecuredLine.sol#L112
https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/f32cb3eeb08663f2456bf6e2fba21e964da3e8ae/contracts/modules/credit/EscrowedLine.sol#L78
https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/f32cb3eeb08663f2456bf6e2fba21e964da3e8ae/contracts/modules/escrow/Escrow.sol#L136
https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/f32cb3eeb08663f2456bf6e2fba21e964da3e8ae/contracts/utils/EscrowLib.sol#L188
https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/f32cb3eeb08663f2456bf6e2fba21e964da3e8ae/contracts/utils/EscrowLib.sol#L51

In the body of `_getCollateralValue`, the for loop iterates over all the collaterals of the borrower. Since the number of collaterals are large, it will go out of gas, and the transaction will be reverted. So, declaring this line insolvent will be impossible.

