# Vulnerability details

## Impact

LineOfCredit.sol contains unbounded loop when iterating the ids array in LineOfCredit.sol

function updateOutstandingDebt can revert because the transaction running out of gas.

## Proof of Concept

User can call the function updateOUtStandingDebt()

```solidity
/// see ILineOfCredit.updateOutstandingDebt
function updateOutstandingDebt() external override returns (uint256, uint256) {
	return _updateOutstandingDebt();
}
```

Which calls

```solidity
function _updateOutstandingDebt()
	internal
	returns (uint256 principal, uint256 interest)
{
	// use full length not count because positions might not be packed in order
	uint256 len = ids.length;
	if (len == 0) return (0, 0);

	bytes32 id;
	address oracle_ = address(oracle);  // gas savings
	address interestRate_ = address(interestRate); // gas savings

	for (uint256 i; i < len; ++i) {
		id = ids[i];

		// null element in array from closing a position. skip for gas savings
		if(id == bytes32(0)) { continue; }

		(Credit memory c, uint256 _p, uint256 _i) = CreditLib.getOutstandingDebt(
		  credits[id],
		  id,
		  oracle_,
		  interestRate_
		);
		// update total outstanding debt
		principal += _p;
		interest += _i;
		// save changes to storage
		credits[id] = c;
	}
}
```

Which calls

```solidity
  // getOutstandingDebt() is called by updateOutstandingDebt()
  function getOutstandingDebt(
    ILineOfCredit.Credit memory credit,
    bytes32 id,
    address oracle,
    address interestRate
  )
    external
    returns (ILineOfCredit.Credit memory c, uint256 principal, uint256 interest)
  {
    c = accrue(credit, id, interestRate);

    int256 price = IOracle(oracle).getLatestAnswer(c.token);

    principal = calculateValue(
      price,
      c.principal,
      c.decimals
    );
    interest = calculateValue(
      price,
      c.interestAccrued,
      c.decimals
    );

    return (c, principal, interest);
  }
```

As we can see, this function _updateOutstandingDebt contains unbounded loop. because we are loop the ids array, which is all open credit lines.

```solidity
    bytes32[] public ids; // all open credit lines
```

First of all, there may be a lot of nullified ids from closed position., we still need to read the id

```solidity
// null element in array from closing a position. skip for gas savings
if(id == bytes32(0)) { continue; }
```

And for each iteraction, we read the price from chainlink oracle,

```solidity
int256 price = IOracle(oracle).getLatestAnswer(c.token);
```

There is no token price caching implementation, it is more than saving gas.

For each LineOfCredit.sol, there is one immutable borrower:

```solidity
address public immutable borrower;
```

but one borrower make deals with many lenders with different terms containg different rates with different token address.

Then the function that create Credit which makes the ids array larger maybe being called 10 times, maybe 100 times, maybe 1000 times.

As the array of ids grows larger, the function updateOutstandingDebt becomes more and more expensive to call, and the transaction can revert in running out of gas.

There are other unbounded loop in LineOfCredit.sol

```solidity
/// see ILineOfCredit.accrueInterest
function accrueInterest() external override returns(bool) {
	uint256 len = ids.length;
	bytes32 id;
	for (uint256 i; i < len; ++i) {
	  id = ids[i];
	  Credit memory credit = credits[id];
	  credits[id] = _accrue(credit, id);
	}

	return true;
}
```

Which calls:

```solidity
  /**
    * see ILineOfCredit._accrue
    * @notice called by LineOfCredit._accrue during every repayment function
    * @param interest - interset rate contract used by line that will calculate interest owed
   */
  function accrue(
    ILineOfCredit.Credit memory credit,
    bytes32 id,
    address interest
  )
    public
    returns (ILineOfCredit.Credit memory)
  { unchecked {
      // interest will almost always be less than deposit
      // low risk of overflow unless extremely high interest rate

      // get token demoninated interest accrued
      uint256 accruedToken = IInterestRateCredit(interest).accrueInterest(
          id,
          credit.principal,
          credit.deposit
      );

      // update credit line balance
      credit.interestAccrued += accruedToken;

      emit InterestAccrued(id, accruedToken);
      return credit;
  } }
}
```

While accure interest for single credit position given an id is cheap, the cost does add up when the ids length size grows.


## Tools Used

Manual Review.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider adding a upper limit for ids array to avoid unbounded loop.

For example, we can add a configuration and restrict that borrower and lender can create no more than 10 credit.

Otherwise, the function addCredit would revert

```solidity
    /// see ILineOfCredit.addCredit
    function addCredit(
        uint128 drate,
        uint128 frate,
        uint256 amount,
        address token,
        address lender
    )
	     if(ids.length > 10) { revert TooManyPosition();
```

