# Vulnerability details

### Impact

The `price` can be outdated and in case of [`return price <= 0 ? 0 : (amount * uint(price)) / (1 * 10 ** decimals);`](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/e8aa08b44f6132a5ed901f8daa231700c5afeb3a/contracts/utils/CreditLib.sol#L117) the `price` can be invalid and the function `calculateValue` return `0` instead of revert like in [`if(price <= 0 ) { revert NoTokenPrice(); }`](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/e8aa08b44f6132a5ed901f8daa231700c5afeb3a/contracts/utils/CreditLib.sol#L136)

This can broke the functions:
- [`getOutstandingDebt`](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/e8aa08b44f6132a5ed901f8daa231700c5afeb3a/contracts/utils/CreditLib.sol#L11)
- [`_getCollateralValue`](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/e8aa08b44f6132a5ed901f8daa231700c5afeb3a/contracts/utils/EscrowLib.sol#L51)

[data-feeds documentation](https://docs.chain.link/docs/data-feeds/)

### Tools Used

Review

### Recommended Mitigation Steps

- Check if the response of `latestRoundData` it's not outdated, using a time window
- Revert the transaction if the `price` it's lower or equal to `0`, move this check inside the Oracle contract
