# Lines of code

https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/audit/code4rena-2022-11-03/contracts/modules/oracle/Oracle.sol#L22-L32


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

DebtDAO uses an [Oracle](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/audit/code4rena-2022-11-03/contracts/modules/oracle/Oracle.sol):

> a simple contract that wraps Chainlink's Feed Registry to get asset prices for any tokens without needing to know the specific oracle address.

The usage of price feeds comes with some inherited risks (e.g. stale prices) and a particular disclaimer calls for additional controls on the developed app "When you build applications and protocols that depend on data feeds, include monitoring and safeguards to protect against the negative impact of extreme market events, possible malicious activity on third-party venues or contracts, potential delays, and outages". Some additional information at [Chainlink Docs](https://docs.chain.link/docs/data-feeds/#monitoring-data-feeds).

The lack of checks in [Oracle.getLatestAnswer](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/audit/code4rena-2022-11-03/contracts/modules/oracle/Oracle.sol#L22-L32) could have unintended effects on the perceived value of collaterals and debts. Direct calls in:
* [CreditLib.getOutstandingDebt](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/audit/code4rena-2022-11-03/contracts/utils/CreditLib.sol#L84)
* [CreditLib.create](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/audit/code4rena-2022-11-03/contracts/utils/CreditLib.sol#L135) - Offers protection against price being equal or under 0 (reverts).
* [EscrowLib._getCollateralValue](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/audit/code4rena-2022-11-03/contracts/utils/EscrowLib.sol#L76)
* [EscrowLib.enableCollateral](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/audit/code4rena-2022-11-03/contracts/utils/EscrowLib.sol#L126) - Offers protection against price being equal or under 0 (reverts).

Mitigating factors:
- As stated above, some controls exist against prices being equal or under 0, although the logic could arguably be misplaced.
- Tokens are whitelisted, which leads to the assumption that only credible tokens will be used.

Previous contests with similar issues: [[1]](https://code4rena.com/reports/2022-07-juicebox/#h-01-oracle-data-feed-can-be-outdated-yet-used-anyways-which-will-impact-payment-logic), [[2]](https://code4rena.com/reports/2022-08-olympus/#m-24-naz-m1-chainlinks-latestrounddata-might-return-stale-results) or [[3]](https://code4rena.com/reports/2022-04-backd#m-05-chainlinks-latestrounddata-might-return-stale-or-incorrect-results).

## Proof of Concept

In [getLatestAnswer](https://github.com/debtdao/Line-of-Credit/blob/audit/code4rena-2022-11-03/contracts/modules/oracle/Oracle.sol#L22-L32), no checks when using the returned price:
```solidity
    function getLatestAnswer(address token) external returns (int) {
        (
            /* uint80 roundID */, 
            int price,
            /* uint80 startedAt */,
            /* uint80 timeStamp */,
            /* uint80 answeredInRound */
        ) = registry.latestRoundData(token, Denominations.USD);

        return price;
    }
```

## Tools Used

VSCode

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider adding the missing checks for stale data and other issues.

For example:

```solidity
    function getLatestAnswer(address token) external returns (int) {
        (
            uint80 roundID, 
            int price,
            /* uint80 startedAt */,
            uint80 timeStamp,
            uint80 answeredInRound
        ) = registry.latestRoundData(token, Denominations.USD);

        require(price > 0, "Chainlink price <= 0"); 
        require(answeredInRound >= roundID, "Stale price");
        require(timestamp != 0, "Round not complete");

        return price;
    }
```

