# Vulnerability details

## Impact

User can borrow the asset for free from Market.sol directly, circumvant the borrowing stage.

## Proof of Concept

the function that determine collateralValueInternal, which then determines the user credit limit is

```solidity
function getCollateralValueInternal(address user) internal returns (uint) {
	IEscrow escrow = predictEscrow(user);
	uint collateralBalance = escrow.balance();
	return collateralBalance * oracle.getPrice(address(collateral), collateralFactorBps) / 1 ether;
}
```

the code does not check if predictEscrow(user) escrow is tracked by escrows[user].

Then the user can copy the implemetantion of Escrow, use the code below to create the same address before the escrow is created and tracked in escrows mapping.

```solidity
function createEscrow(address user) internal returns (IEscrow instance) {
	address implementation = escrowImplementation;
	/// @solidity memory-safe-assembly
	assembly {
		let ptr := mload(0x40)
		mstore(ptr, 0x3d602d80600a3d3981f3363d3d373d3d3d363d73000000000000000000000000)
		mstore(add(ptr, 0x14), shl(0x60, implementation))
		mstore(add(ptr, 0x28), 0x5af43d82803e903d91602b57fd5bf30000000000000000000000000000000000)
		instance := create2(0, ptr, 0x37, user)
	}
	require(instance != IEscrow(address(0)), "ERC1167: create2 failed");
	emit CreateEscrow(user, address(instance));
}
```

After this escrow is created by user, the user can call initiate to become the "market" of the escrow

```soliidty
function initialize(IERC20 _token, address) public {
	require(market == address(0), "ALREADY INITIALIZED");
	market = msg.sender;
	token = _token;
}
```

and then user the send token directly to the escrow contract to increase the balance of the escrow

```solidity
function balance() public view returns (uint) {
	return token.balanceOf(address(this));
}
```

note, user can withdraw their fund from the escrow because the user is the "market". she can call pay to withdraw the fun

```solidity
function pay(address recipient, uint amount) public {
	require(msg.sender == market, "ONLY MARKET");
	token.transfer(recipient, amount);
}
```

the building block of this exploitation is complete, the hacker can 

- deploy the escrow address himself using create2.
- initiate the escrow address to become the market (owner)
- transfer the fund to increase the credit limit
- call borrow from Market.sol to borrow fund, withdraw the fund by calling pay in the escrow.
- User borrow for free.

## Tools Used

Code check

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Easy! Please check check check if the user address is in escrows map:

```solidity
function getCollateralValueInternal(address user) internal returns (uint) {
	IEscrow escrow = predictEscrow(user);
	if(escrows[user] != escrow) return 0; // or revert or handle the 0 value in upper code block!
	uint collateralBalance = escrow.balance();
	return collateralBalance * oracle.getPrice(address(collateral), collateralFactorBps) / 1 ether;
}
```

also, check that the address(this) == escrow.market(), not other user. (check marrrket address is the escrow.market());

Thanks!❥(^_-)

