# Vulnerability details

The [Market.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-10-inverse/blob/main/src/Market.sol) contract `gov,` [BorrowController.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-10-inverse/blob/main/src/BorrowController.sol) contract `operator`, Fed.sol contract `gov` and  `chair` roles can all be changed in a single-step (no confirmation) to *any* address including `address(0)`.

The impact is high as crucial pieces of functionality would be crippled if any of these roles were changed to `address(0)` or to an address not under the team’s control.

The [Market.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-10-inverse/blob/main/src/Market.sol) contract `gov` role is linked to the `onlyGov` access modifier and the following functions would no longer be able to be executed blocking the ability to control the Market;

- `setOracle()`, `setBorrowController()`, `setGov()`, `setLender()`, `setPauseGuardian()`, `setCollateralFactorBps()`, `setReplenismentIncentiveBps()` , `setLiquidationIncentiveBps()` and `setLiquidationFeeBps()`.

The [BorrowControler.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-10-inverse/blob/main/src/BorrowController.sol) contract `operator` role is linked to the `onlyOperator` access modifier and the following functions would no longer be able to be executed blocking the ability to allow or deny borrow controller contract addresses;

- `setOperator()`, `allow()`, `deny()`

The [Fed.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-10-inverse/blob/main/src/Fed.sol) contract `gov` role is not linked to an access modifier but is checked on a number of important administrative functions. The following functions would no longer be able to be executed blocking the ability to change governance, supply ceilings or the chair;

- `changeGov()`, `changeSupplyCeiling()`, `changeChair()`

The [Fed.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-10-inverse/blob/main/src/Fed.sol) contract `chair` role is not linked to an access modifier but is checked on a number of important administrative functions. The following functions would no longer be able to be executed blocking the ability to expand/contract supply or resign;

- `resign()`, `expansion()`, `contraction()`

The use of a multisig wallet ensures that execution of these functions can only originate from a specific address but it ****************does not**************** protect against the wrong address or address(0) being specific.

### Proof of Concept

The following forge test demonstrates that all roles can be changed in a single-step to `address(0)` with no revert.

```solidity
function testGov() public {
		//As the current market gov change the gov to address(0)
    vm.prank(market.gov());
    market.setGov(address(0));
    assertEq(address(market.gov()), address(0));

		//As the current operator change the operator to address(0)
    vm.prank(borrowController.operator());
    borrowController.setOperator(address(0));

		//As the current fed gov change the gov to address(0)
    vm.prank(fed.gov());
    fed.changeGov(address(0));

		//As the current fed gov change the chair to address(0)
    vm.prank(fed.gov());
    fed.changeChair(address(0));
}
```

