### Recommended Remediation Steps

I feel that all of these important governance roles should be require two-step changes (set pending/claim) similar to the pattern used in [Oracle.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-10-inverse/blob/main/src/Oracle.sol) to protect `operator`. Furthermore  `address(0)` checks still need to be added to all of these important governance role changes.

For example the following changes can be made to Market.sol. It implements a `pendingGov`, a event for when the `gov` role is changed and a two step process to propose the new `gov` and have the new admin claim the role. Lastly it performs an `address(0)` check on all pending requests;

```solidity
		 address public gov;
+    address public pendingGov;
     address public lender;
     address public pauseGuardian;
     address public immutable escrowImplementation;
@@ -127,7 +128,17 @@ contract Market {
     @notice sets the address of governance. Only callable by governance.
     @param _gov Address of the new governance.
     */
-    function setGov(address _gov) public onlyGov { gov = _gov; }
+    function setGov(address _gov) public onlyGov { 
+        require(_gov!=address(0), "Error: cannot set gov to address zero");
+        pendingGov = _gov; 
+    }
+
+    function claimGov() public {
+        require(msg.sender == pendingGov, "ONLY PENDING GOV");
+        gov = pendingGov;
+        pendingGov = address(0);
+        emit ChangeGov(gov);
+    }

@@ -618,4 +630,5 @@ contract Market {
     event ForceReplenish(address indexed account, address indexed replenisher, uint deficit, uint replenishmentCost, uint replenisherReward);
     event Liquidate(address indexed account, address indexed liquidator, uint repaidDebt, uint liquidatorReward);
     event CreateEscrow(address indexed user, address escrow);
+    event ChangeGov(address indexed newGov);
```

