# Vulnerability details



## Impact
The Oracle contract is known to be pessimistic in way of serving the lowest prices to prevent borrowers from borrowing more than the lowest recorded value of their collateral over the past 2 days.
However, this is not possible for the tokens which are freshly added to the system and has no Oracle price feed yet. It's also the same for the tokens when the `getPrice` is not called and there is no historical data.

Hence, they're being collateralized to the first prices (`normalizedPrice`) provided by the Chainlink instead of being compared to 2 days low which the system is designed for.

I'm submitting this as a Medium since the system can not fulfill the service as it's designed.

## Proof of Concept
`getPrice` function Gets the price of a specific token in DOLA while also saving the price if it is the day's lowest;
```solidity
