# Vulnerability details

Price oracles retrieve Chainlink prices using the [deprecated](https://docs.chain.link/docs/data-feeds/price-feeds/api-reference/#latestanswer) `latestAnswer` function.

[`Oracle.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-10-inverse/blob/3e81f0f5908ea99b36e6ab72f13488bbfe622183/src/Oracle.sol#L78-L106):

```solidity
    // get price from feed
    uint price = feeds[token].feed.latestAnswer();
    require(price > 0, "Invalid feed price");
```

It's considered best practice to use the `latestRoundData` function instead. ([API docs](https://docs.chain.link/docs/price-feeds-api-reference/#latestrounddata)). `latestAnswer` returns only the value of the latest price, whereas `latestRoundData` returns additional information that can be used to validate whether a price is stale.

Impact: The price oracle may incorrectly report a DBR position as over- or undercollateralized.

Suggested:

Validate the oracle response for freshness and round completion in addition to nonzero price:

```solidity
    // get price from feed
    (uint80 roundId, int256 price, , uint256 updatedAt, uint80 answeredInRound)= feeds[token].feed.latestRoundData();
    require(price > 0, "Invalid feed price");
    require(roundID == answeredInRound, "Stale price");
    require(updatedAt > 0, "Incomplete round");
```

