# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Currently, it uses `IChainlinkFeed.latestAnswer()` to get the price and updates `dailyLows` using this price.

But the function `latestAnswer()` is deprecated and `Oracle.dailyLows` might save the incorrect prices.

As a result, wrong prices might be used in the market.

## Proof of Concept
As we can see [here](https://docs.chain.link/docs/data-feeds/price-feeds/api-reference/#latestanswer), `latestAnswer()` is deprecated and it might return a stale price.

For example, if `latestAnswer()` is called at `Oct 30, 00:30 AM`, the price of `Oct 29, 23:30 AM` might be returned.

Then this price will be compared and updated with the `dailyLows` of `Oct 30` even though the price is from `Oct 29` [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-10-inverse/blob/3e81f0f5908ea99b36e6ab72f13488bbfe622183/src/Oracle.sol#L112-L144).

```solidity
    function getPrice(address token, uint collateralFactorBps) external returns (uint) {
        if(fixedPrices[token] > 0) return fixedPrices[token];
        if(feeds[token].feed != IChainlinkFeed(address(0))) {
            // get price from feed
            uint price = feeds[token].feed.latestAnswer();
            require(price > 0, "Invalid feed price");
            // normalize price
            uint8 feedDecimals = feeds[token].feed.decimals();
            uint8 tokenDecimals = feeds[token].tokenDecimals;
            uint8 decimals = 36 - feedDecimals - tokenDecimals;
            uint normalizedPrice = price * (10 ** decimals);
            // potentially store price as today's low
            uint day = block.timestamp / 1 days;
            uint todaysLow = dailyLows[token][day];
            if(todaysLow == 0 || normalizedPrice < todaysLow) {
                dailyLows[token][day] = normalizedPrice;
                todaysLow = normalizedPrice;
                emit RecordDailyLow(token, normalizedPrice);
            }
            // get yesterday's low
            uint yesterdaysLow = dailyLows[token][day - 1];
            // calculate new borrowing power based on collateral factor
            uint newBorrowingPower = normalizedPrice * collateralFactorBps / 10000;
            uint twoDayLow = todaysLow > yesterdaysLow && yesterdaysLow > 0 ? yesterdaysLow : todaysLow;
            if(twoDayLow > 0 && newBorrowingPower > twoDayLow) {
                uint dampenedPrice = twoDayLow * 10000 / collateralFactorBps;
                return dampenedPrice < normalizedPrice ? dampenedPrice: normalizedPrice;
            }
            return normalizedPrice;

        }
        revert("Price not found");
    }
```

As a result, `dailyLows` of `Oct 30` might save the price of `Oct 29` as the lowest price.

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Recommend using [IChainlinkFeed.latestRoundData()](https://docs.chain.link/docs/data-feeds/price-feeds/api-reference/#latestrounddata-1) instead of `IChainlinkFeed.latestAnswer()` like below. `Oracle.viewPrice` should be changed according also.

```solidity
