https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-09-y2k-finance/blob/2175c044af98509261e4147edeb48e1036773771/src/VaultFactory.sol#L366-L374
https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-09-y2k-finance/blob/main/src/Controller.sol#L148


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Change of oracle without any restriction set on it opens up a potential for admin to manipulate the market by performing insurance fraud. The fact that oracle address used can be changed even after users have deposited WETH/ETH and have their assets locked in results in the protocol having an unnecessary layer of trust.

## Proof of Concept

`changeOracle()` has no restrictions placed on it, other than being able to be called by Admin.
[VaultFactory.sol#L366-374](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-09-y2k-finance/blob/2175c044af98509261e4147edeb48e1036773771/src/VaultFactory.sol#L366-L374)
```solidity
    function changeOracle(address _token, address _oracle) public onlyAdmin {
        if(_oracle == address(0))
            revert AddressZero();
        if(_token == address(0))
            revert AddressZero();

        tokenToOracle[_token] = _oracle;
        emit changedOracle(_token, _oracle);
    }
```
https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-09-y2k-finance/blob/main/src/Controller.sol#L261-L312
Oracle price is tracked in the Controller by `getLatestPrice()` in [Controller.sol#L261-L312](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-09-y2k-finance/blob/main/src/Controller.sol#L261-L312). When `triggerDepeg()` in [Controller.sol#L148](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-09-y2k-finance/blob/main/src/Controller.sol#L148) is called, it relies on the modifier `isDisaster()` to check if there exist a depeg in asset. This change will affect every deployed vaults since they are all managed by the Controller.

The oracle address being able to be changed anytime by admin can create insurance manipulation since they can buy a large sum of insurance and force a depeg.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider setting a timelock on the `changeOracle()` function that is as long as the current `endEpoch` timing  across all markets so that it only affects new markets and users who deposit their ETH/WETH are aware of the change.

