# Vulnerability details

## Impact
When a ``LDPA`` auction is created with ``createLPDASale`` function the ``sale`` attribute ``dropPerSecond`` can be set in such a way that can cause a underflow revert when we call ``getPrice``.

``getPrice`` is internally used for buying and also refunding. 

If it reverts users cannot buy/reedem until the auction is ended which defies the purpose of a auction in the first place.

## Proof of Concept
More thorough validation is missing for ``dropPerSecond``

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/LPDAFactory.sol#L29-L42

If we look at ``getPrice`` code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L123

if ``dropPerSecond * timeElapsed`` gets bigger then ``temp.startPrice`` we will get a revert.

