# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The calculation of `getPrice()` in [LPDA.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/LPDA.sol) can eventually underflow if the sale is created in a certain way and enough time passes since start of the dutch auction.
```solidity
function getPrice() public view returns (uint256) {
	Sale memory temp = sale;
	(uint256 start, uint256 end) = (temp.startTime, temp.endTime);
	if (block.timestamp < start) return type(uint256).max;
	if (temp.currentId == temp.finalId) return temp.finalPrice;

	uint256 timeElapsed = end > block.timestamp ? block.timestamp - start : end - start;
	return temp.startPrice - (temp.dropPerSecond * timeElapsed);
}
```
In case `(temp.dropPerSecond * timeElapsed)` is greater than `temp.startPrice`, the last line of the function will make the call revert.
As `getPrice` is called inside both `buy` and `refund`, both functions would revert when being called, **locking all the funds existing in the contract**.

## Proof of Concept
The following test shows this issue in action. You can copy and paste it inside [LPDA.t.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/test/LPDA.t.sol):
```solidity
function test_GetPriceRevert() public {

	LPDA.Sale memory priceRevertLpdaSale;

	// We set a price decay of 0.1 ethers every hour, so after 10 hours
	// the buy will revert
	priceRevertLpdaSale = LPDA.Sale({
		currentId: uint48(0),
		finalId: uint48(10),
		edition: address(edition),
		startPrice: uint80(uint256(1 ether)),
		finalPrice: uint80(uint256(0.1 ether)),
		dropPerSecond: uint80(uint256(0.1 ether) / 1 hours),
		startTime: uint96(block.timestamp),
		saleReceiver: payable(address(69)),
		endTime: uint96(block.timestamp + 1 days)
	});

	sale = LPDA(lpdaSales.createLPDASale(priceRevertLpdaSale));
	// authorize the lpda sale to mint tokens
	edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));

	// we force that 11 hours pass and try to buy afterwards
	vm.warp(priceRevertLpdaSale.startTime + 11 hours);
	// lets try and buy an NFT. We expect the call to revert because of the underflow
	vm.expectRevert(stdError.arithmeticError);
	sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);
}
```

