# Vulnerability details

## Impact
User cannot refund if `LPDA.getPrice` reverts. User's funds will stuck in the contract.

## Proof of Concept
There's no check if `startPrice - dropPerSecond * (endTime - startTime) >= 0` in `LPDAFactory.createLPDASale` function. The `LPDA.getPrice` will revert if `startPrice - dropPerSecond * (endTime - startTime) < 0` due to math underflow.
```solidity
    function getPrice() public view returns (uint256) {
       .......
        uint256 timeElapsed = end > block.timestamp ? block.timestamp - start : end - start;
        return temp.startPrice - (temp.dropPerSecond * timeElapsed);
    }

```
When user call `LPDA.refund` it will reverts thus user's funds will stuck in the contract forever.
```solidity
    function refund() public {
        ......
        uint80 price = uint80(getPrice()) * r.amount;
        ......
    }
```


## Tools Used
manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
check `sale.startPrice - sale.dropPerSecond * (sale.endTime - sale.startTime) >= 0` in `LPDAFactory.createLPDASale` function

```solidity
function createLPDASale(LPDA.Sale calldata sale) external returns (address clone) {
        ......
        require(sale.dropPerSecond > 0, "INVALID DROP PER SECOND");
        require(sale.startPrice - sale.dropPerSecond * (sale.endTime - sale.startTime) >= 0, "whatever");

        clone = implementation.clone();
        LPDA(clone).initialize(sale);

        emit NewLPDAContract(msg.sender, sale.edition, clone, sale);
    }
```

