# Vulnerability details

## Impact
This issue can allow attackers to gain unauthorized control over the Base contract and potentially use it to exploit vulnerabilities in the contract or in any contracts that rely on it. This can result in loss of funds or other damages.

## Proof of Concept
The Base contract includes a public **initialize** function that allows anyone to set the owner of the contract. This can allow attackers to gain unauthorized control over the contract.

Steps to reproduce:

Deploy the Base contract to the blockchain.
Call the **initialize** function with the address of the attacker as the argument.
Expected result:

The **initialize** function should not allow unauthorized users to set the owner of the contract.

Actual result:

The **initialize** function allows unauthorized users to set the owner of the contract, allowing attackers to gain unauthorized control over the contract.


## Tools Used
Manual

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
The **initialize** function should be marked as internal or private to prevent unauthorized users from calling it and changing the owner of the contract. Additionally, the contract should include a mechanism for changing the owner, and this mechanism should be restricted to the current owner or to a trusted contract that has been authorized to make changes to the contract.

The initialize function in the Base contract can be marked as private to prevent unauthorized calls, and a new function can be added to allow the owner to change the owner of the contract:

```
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.17;

import {ITokenUriDelegate} from "../interfaces/ITokenUriDelegate.sol";
import {OwnableUpgradeable} from "openzeppelin-upgradeable/access/OwnableUpgradeable.sol";

contract Base is ITokenUriDelegate, OwnableUpgradeable {
    string public baseURI;

    function setBaseURI(string memory _baseURI) external onlyOwner {
        baseURI = _baseURI;
    }

    function tokenURI(uint256) external view final returns (string memory) {
        return baseURI;
    }

    function initialize(address _owner) private initializer {
        _transferOwnership(_owner);
    }

    function changeOwner(address _newOwner) external onlyOwner {
        _transferOwnership(_newOwner);
    }
}
```

This updated contract will prevent unauthorized calls to the initialize function, and it will allow the owner of the contract to change the owner using the changeOwner function.

