# Vulnerability details

## Impact
[LPDAFactory.sol#L29-L42](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/LPDAFactory.sol#L29-L42) does not check that the price in the LPDA sale stays non-negative. If the sale isn't over and the price drops below zero, getPrice will always fail due to underflow. 

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L117-L125
This causes DOS in both buy() and refund(). 

Suppose a buyer buys tokens and forgets about them. If the price drops below zero, then the buyer's cannot get their refund. In fact, the buyer's fund is locked inside the contract and cannot be retrieved.

## Proof of Concept
Run the following test.
```
pragma solidity ^0.8.17;

import "forge-std/Test.sol";
import {EscherTest} from "./utils/EscherTest.sol";
import {LPDAFactory, LPDA} from "src/minters/LPDAFactory.sol";

contract LPDAVuln2Base is EscherTest {
    LPDAFactory public lpdaSales;
    LPDA.Sale public lpdaSale;

    function setUp() public virtual override {
        super.setUp();
        lpdaSales = new LPDAFactory();
        // set up a LPDA Sale
        lpdaSale = LPDA.Sale({
            currentId: uint48(0),
            finalId: uint48(2),
            edition: address(edition),
            startPrice: uint80(uint256(1 ether)),
            finalPrice: uint80(uint256(0.1 ether)),
            dropPerSecond: uint80(uint256(0.1 ether) / 1 days),
            startTime: uint96(block.timestamp),
            saleReceiver: payable(address(69)),
            endTime: uint96(block.timestamp + 20 days)
        });
    }
}


contract LPDAVuln2Test is LPDAVuln2Base {
    LPDA public sale;

    function test_LPDA() public {
        // make the lpda sales contract
        sale = LPDA(lpdaSales.createLPDASale(lpdaSale));
        // authorize the lpda sale to mint tokens
        edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));

        // buyer buys at the very beginning and forgets about it
        sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);
        assertEq(address(sale).balance, 1 ether);

        // time passes and price drops below 0
        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 15 days);

        // buyer can no longer get his refunds
        vm.expectRevert();
        sale.refund();

    }
}
```

## Tools Used
VSCode, Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Add a case in getPrice().
`if (temp.startPrice < (temp.dropPerSecond * timeElapsed)) return 0;`

