https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L101


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Concerning the variables within the `Sale` struct in `LPDA`, `dropPerSecond` ought to be such that:

```
dropPerSecond <= (startPrice - finalPrice) / (endTime - startTime)
```

i.e. price will drop gradually over the period of the sale, approaching `finalPrice`, without ever dropping below `finalPrice`.

However it is left as a user input in `LPDAFactory.createLPDASale()`, with the only check being that it is > 0.

If the value for `dropPerSecond` is such that the price will drop to "below zero" during the sale (`dropPerSecond > startPrice / (endTime - startTime)`), then `getPrice()` will always revert ([line 124](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L124)), which means that `buy()` will also always revert.

If no one can call `buy()` the sale will never end, and the ether from previous sales will be trapped in the `LPDA` contract forever.
(Note: `getPrice()` always reverting means it is also impossible to call `refund()`)

Such a value for `dropPerSecond` may not be immediately obvious once the sale begins, especially for sales with a long duration.

## Proof of Concept

```
function test_DropPerSecondTooHigh() public {
    // For this test I changed `lpdaSales.dropPerSecond` such that
    // the price would "drop below zero" after 10 seconds

    // setup
    sale = LPDA(lpdaSales.createLPDASale(lpdaSale));
    edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));

    // warp 10 seconds
    vm.warp(10);

    // `getPrice()` will always revert
    vm.expectRevert();
    sale.getPrice();

    // therefore `buy()` will also always revert
    vm.expectRevert();
    sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);

    // as will `refund()`
    vm.expectRevert();
    sale.refund();
}
```

## Tools Used

Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Alter the require statement in `LPDAFactory.createLPDASale()` to

```
require(dropPerSecond > 0 && dropPerSecond <= startPrice / (endTime - startTime))
```

or

```
require(dropPerSecond > 0 && dropPerSecond <= (startPrice - finalPrice) / (endTime - startTime))
```

if it is desired that price doesn't drop below `finalPrice` during the sale.

