# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The `buy ()` function of `FixedPrice`, `OpenEdition` and `LPDA` contracts does not sanitize the amount input put by the user when attempt to buy art. As a result, a user can input `0` ZERO amount in the `buy ()` function and they will be able to mint free nft as seen here 
https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/OpenEdition.sol#L57-L71, 

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L57-L74

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L58-L85

In the `FixedPrice` `buy ()` function for example, the function takes the amount and uses this to ensure the user has the right available amount (`msg.value`) as seen here
 https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L61. 

Because the input amount is passed all the checks will pass. In the for loop here https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L65-L66, the user would be minted the `currentID` nft.

## Proof of Concept
The following test case on `FixedPrice.t.sol` proves that user can buy artwork with 0 amounts
```
unction test_Buy() public {
        // make the fixed price sale
        sale = FixedPrice(fixedSales.createFixedSale(fixedSale));
        // authorize the fixed price sale to mint tokens
        edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));
        uint former = fixedSale.currentId;
        // lets buy some NFTs

        sale.buy{value: 0 ether}(0);
        uint currnt = fixedSale.currentId;
        assertEq(address(sale).balance, 0 ether);
        assertEq(former, currnt);

```

## Tools Used

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
In the `buy ()` function, consider preventing buying of artworks with 0 amounts. 
You can sanitize the input in the `buy ()` function as follows:
`require (_amount > 0);`

