# Vulnerability details

## Impact 
LPDA funds can be lost with a initial bad sale configuration

## Proof of Concept
There are possible underflows on this line [LPDA#124](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L124) :
```solidity
return temp.startPrice - (temp.dropPerSecond * timeElapsed);
```
and this other one  [LPDA#143](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L143) :
```solidity
return sale.startPrice - (sale.dropPerSecond * (sale.endTime - sale.startTime));
```
Then there are no ways to withdraw funds from the contract

A POC re-using one existing test : [LPDA.t.sol#L168-L190](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/test/LPDA.t.sol#L168-L190) is included bellow.

With a delay of 11 days in Sale configuration, instead of 1 day, this foundry test shows a systematic underflow on 4 functions : 
- getPrice
- buy
- refund 
- lowestPrice

```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.17;

import "forge-std/Test.sol";
import {EscherTest} from "./utils/EscherTest.sol";
import {LPDAFactory, LPDA} from "src/minters/LPDAFactory.sol";

contract LPDABase is EscherTest {
    LPDA.Sale public lpdaSale;
    LPDA public sale;

    function init(uint256 fewDays) public {
        EscherTest.setUp();
        LPDAFactory lpdaSales = new LPDAFactory();

        lpdaSale = LPDA.Sale({
            currentId: uint48(0),
            finalId: uint48(10),
            edition: address(edition),
            startPrice: uint80(uint256(1 ether)),
            finalPrice: uint80(uint256(0.1 ether)),
            dropPerSecond: uint80(uint256(0.1 ether) / 1 days),
            startTime: uint96(block.timestamp),
            saleReceiver: payable(address(69)),
            endTime: uint96(block.timestamp + fewDays)
        });

        // make the lpda sales contract
        sale = LPDA(lpdaSales.createLPDASale(lpdaSale));

        // authorize the lpda sale to mint tokens
        edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));

        sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);

        vm.warp(block.timestamp + fewDays);
    }

    function testLPDA_Reverts() public {
        init(12 days);

        // buy reverts
        vm.expectRevert(stdError.arithmeticError);
        sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);

        // getPrice reverts
        vm.expectRevert(stdError.arithmeticError);
        uint256 price = sale.getPrice();

        // refund reverts
        vm.expectRevert(stdError.arithmeticError);
        sale.refund();

        // lowestPrice reverts
        vm.expectRevert(stdError.arithmeticError);
        sale.lowestPrice();
    }

    function testLPDA_OK() public {
        init(1 days);

        // buy OK
        sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);
        assertEq(address(sale).balance, 2 ether);

        // getPrice OK
        uint256 price = sale.getPrice();
        assertTrue(price < lpdaSale.startPrice);

        // refund OK
        sale.refund();

        // lowestPrice OK
        sale.lowestPrice();
    }
}
```

## Tools Used
Foundry tests

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
To avoid these underflows, you can change the initial requirement on startPrice.

To do so, replace in [LPDAFactory.sol#L35](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/LPDAFactory.sol#L35)
```solidity
require(sale.startPrice > 0, "INVALID START PRICE »);
```
 with : 
```solidity
require(sale.startPrice > sale.dropPerSecond * ( sale.endTime - sale.startTime ) , "INVALID START PRICE »)
```

