# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The ether of a Fixed Price sale can get frozen (cant get withdrawed) effectively losing all the ether accumulated so far.

## Proof of Concept

The only way to get ether out of the contract is via the internal function `_end(Sale memory _sale)` that is at [LoC 107](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L107) of the FixedPrice.sol contract.

There are only two ways for this function to be called. One is at the `cancel()` function that can only happen before the start time.

The other one is at the `buy(uint256 amount)` function, more concretely at the [LoC 73](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L73):

```
if (newId == sale_.finalId) _end(sale);
```

This conditional is triggered when all the range of the token ids for this sale is sold. 

If for any other means a token id for that range gets minted, for example by another sale for the same Escher721 edition where its range overlap with the range of the first sale, or by the creator calling the `mint(address, uint256)` function at the same Escher721 edition with a token id that was in the range of the fixed sale, then the ether from the first sale will get stucked because it will revert when trying to mint the token id that was minted through the overlap.

I created a little test to show an example of this behavior:

```
function test_DoS() public {
        // make the fixed price sale
        sale = FixedPrice(fixedSales.createFixedSale(fixedSale));
        // authorize the fixed price sale to mint tokens
        edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));
        // lets buy some NFTs
        sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);
        assertEq(address(sale).balance, 1 ether);
        // Overlap token id # 2 is in the range of the fixed sale.
        edition.mint(address(sale), 2);

        vm.expectRevert("ERC721: token already minted");
        sale.buy{value: 3 ether}(3);
    }
```
## Tools Used

Manual and Tests

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Add a end time to the sale and allow the creator to withdraw all the ether (minus the fee) after that time have passed. Somethin similar like the `finalize()` function at the [OpenEdition contract](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/OpenEdition.sol#L89)

