# Vulnerability details

## Vulnerability details

The owner of Escher721 can deploy a `FixedPrice` sale overlapping the IDs, the end of the sale is defined when all of the IDs are minted, due to overlapping some of the IDs maybe is already be minted and the sale get stuck and can't be finished, leaving all ETH inside the contract.

## POC

This snippet of code explains how all ETH get stuck in the contract:

```solidity
contract FixedPriceExploitTest is EscherTest {
  FixedPriceFactory public fixedSales;

  FixedPrice public sale;
  FixedPrice.Sale public fixedSale;

  FixedPrice public saleOverlap;
  FixedPrice.Sale public fixedSaleOverlap;

  function setUp() public virtual override {
    super.setUp();
    fixedSales = new FixedPriceFactory();
    fixedSale = FixedPrice.Sale({
      currentId: uint48(0),
      finalId: uint48(2),
      edition: address(edition),
      price: uint96(uint256(1 ether)),
      saleReceiver: payable(address(69)),
      startTime: uint96(block.timestamp)
    });

    fixedSaleOverlap = FixedPrice.Sale({
      currentId: uint48(1),
      finalId: uint48(3),
      edition: address(edition),
      price: uint96(uint256(1 ether)),
      saleReceiver: payable(address(69)),
      startTime: uint96(block.timestamp)
    });
  }

  function test_ExploitMultipleBuy() public {
    // Creator's create two fixed price sale, overlapping the IDs
		//sale: [0,1,2]
		//saleOverlap: [1,2,3]
    sale = FixedPrice(fixedSales.createFixedSale(fixedSale));
    saleOverlap = FixedPrice(fixedSales.createFixedSale(fixedSaleOverlap));

    // Authorize the fixed price sales to mint tokens
    edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));
    edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(saleOverlap));

    // Lets buy some NFTs from both sales
    saleOverlap.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);
    sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);

    //If someone try to buy from first sale again, he can't buy anymore
    vm.expectRevert("ERC721: token already minted");
    sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);

    //Creator also can't cancel or finish the sale
    vm.prank(address(69));
    vm.expectRevert("TOO LATE");
    sale.cancel();

    //The eth will be stucked forever
    assertEq(address(sale).balance, 1 ether);
  }
}
```

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Is recommended to add an `endTime` in the `FixedPrice` sale, enabling the owner to finish the sale after some time, enabling to withdraw the ETH from the contract.

