  975000000000000000
```

basically once the _end is triggered, when the code wants to forward the sale fee to the fee receiver, the fee receiver re-enter the function buy and make the sale fee forwarded to the fee receiver again. the attacker can re-enter the sale contract multiple times until the fee is drained.

I use the FixedPrice.sol as an example, but this issue also exists in LPDA.sol

```solidity
if (newId == temp.finalId) {
	sale.finalPrice = uint80(price);
	uint256 totalSale = price * amountSold;
	uint256 fee = totalSale / 20;
	ISaleFactory(factory).feeReceiver().transfer(fee);
	temp.saleReceiver.transfer(totalSale - fee);
	_end();
}
```

and in OpenEdition.sol

```solidity
/// @notice finish an open edition and payout the artist
function finalize() public {
	Sale memory temp = sale;
	require(block.timestamp >= temp.endTime, "TOO SOON");
	ISaleFactory(factory).feeReceiver().transfer(address(this).balance / 20);
	_end(temp);
}
```

which calls:

```solidity
function _end(Sale memory _sale) internal {
	emit End(_sale);
	selfdestruct(_sale.saleReceiver);
}
```

to recap: the payable(transfer) does not have this issue because of the hardcode 2300 gas limit, if the project switch to payable(address).to and the owner of the factory is compromised, this reentrancy can happen.

## Tools Used

Manual Review, Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

We recommend project add input validation. does not allow 0 amount of item to be bought.

```solidity
function buy(uint256 _amount) external payable {
  require(amount > 0, 'invalid amount');
	Sale memory sale_ = sale;
	IEscher721 nft = IEscher721(sale_.edition);
	require(block.timestamp >= sale_.startTime, "TOO SOON");
	require(_amount * sale_.price == msg.value, "WRONG PRICE");
```

And use reentrancy guard for the function buy.

https://docs.openzeppelin.com/contracts/4.x/api/security#ReentrancyGuard

