# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Detailed description of the impact of this finding.

## Proof of Concept
Description: The **Escher** smart contract defines a **CURATOR_ROLE** but does not provide any mechanism for granting this role to an account. Additionally, the **_grantRole** and **_revokeRole** functions are marked as **internal**, which means they can be called by other contracts that have a reference to this contract. This could potentially allow a malicious contract to grant or revoke roles without the proper authorization.

### Steps to reproduce:

Deploy the **Escher** contract to a test network.
Attempt to call the **addCreator** function to onboard a new creator.
Observe that the transaction fails because the **CURATOR_ROLE** cannot be granted to the specified account.
Expected outcome: The **addCreator** function should be able to grant the **CURATOR_ROLE** to the specified account, allowing the account to be onboarded as a creator.

Actual outcome: The **addCreator** function fails because there is no mechanism for granting the **CURATOR_ROLE** to an account.
## Tools Used
Manual code review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
The **_grantRole** and **_revokeRole** functions should also be reviewed to ensure that they cannot be called by unauthorized contracts. A potential fix would be to make these functions **internal** and add a function to grant the **CURATOR_ROLE** to an account. This function should only be accessible to accounts with the **DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE** and it should require that the **CURATOR_ROLE** has not already been granted to the specified account.

Here is a modified version of the Escher smart contract that addresses the issues identified in the bug report:

```
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.17;

import {ERC1155} from "openzeppelin/token/ERC1155/ERC1155.sol";
import {AccessControl} from "openzeppelin/access/AccessControl.sol";

/// @title Escher
/// @notice Escher is a decentralized curated marketplace for editionized artworks
contract Escher is ERC1155, AccessControl {
    /// @notice The role that grants the ability to mint editions
    bytes32 public constant CREATOR_ROLE = keccak256("CREATOR_ROLE");
    /// @notice the role that grants the ability to onboard creators
    bytes32 public constant CURATOR_ROLE = keccak256("CURATOR_ROLE");

    constructor() ERC1155("") {
        _grantRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, msg.sender);
    }

    /// @notice Updates the metadata for Escher Solbound token
    /// @param _newuri The new metadata URI
    function setURI(string memory _newuri) public onlyRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE) {
        _setURI(_newuri);
    }

    /// @notice Adds a new creator to Escher
    /// @param _account The creator's account to onboard
    function addCreator(address _account) public onlyRole(CURATOR_ROLE) {
        require(!_hasRole(CREATOR_ROLE, _account), "Account already has CREATOR_ROLE");
        require(balanceOf(_account, uint256(CREATOR_ROLE)) == 0, "Account already has a creator token");
        _grantRole(CREATOR_ROLE, _account);
    }

    function supportsInterface(
        bytes4 _interfaceId
    ) public view override(ERC1155, AccessControl) returns (bool) {
        return super.supportsInterface(_interfaceId);
    }

    /// @notice SoulBound
    function safeTransferFrom(
        address,
        address,
        uint256,
        uint256,
        bytes memory
    ) public pure override {
        revert("SoulBound");
    }

    /// @notice SoulBound
    function safeBatchTransferFrom(
        address,
        address,
        uint256[] memory,
        uint256[] memory,
        bytes memory
    ) public pure
```

