# Vulnerability details

## Impact
in LPDA#refund()
If the user is a contract and receive()  have too much code, it may not be possible to retrieve his funds

## Proof of Concept

refund() is used to get back the funds of the user overpaid, transfer() is used when transfer eth back, this method has a gas limit of 2300
purchase is not limited to the purchaser must be EOA
if the purchaser is a contract, and the contract#receive() there are other codes can lead to transfer() more than 2300 gas, resulting this user can never get back the funds.

```solidity
    function refund() public {
        Receipt memory r = receipts[msg.sender];
        uint80 price = uint80(getPrice()) * r.amount;
        uint80 owed = r.balance - price;
        require(owed > 0, "NOTHING TO REFUND");
        receipts[msg.sender].balance = price;
        payable(msg.sender).transfer(owed); //**@audit transfer may be revert if Gas consumption exceeds 2300.****//
    }
```

## Tools Used

## Recommended Mitigation Steps


1.add Users can specify the receiver 
or 
2.use call{value}() to transfer eth;

```solidity
