# Vulnerability details


## Impact
In the case of FixedPrice and LPDA, the sale is stuck, buyers cannot `buy()` any more, and the revenue ETHs in the contract is completely frozen.
For OpenEdition, the sale is stuck, buyers cannot `buy()` any more.

## Proof of Concept
For all minters (FixedPrice, LPDA, OpenEdition), the `buy()` function will mint new NFTs with tokenId incremently from currentId one by one.

* [FixedPrice.sol#buy()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/FixedPrice.sol#L65-L67):
```
for (uint48 x = sale_.currentId + 1; x <= newId; x++) {
    nft.mint(msg.sender, x);
}
```
* [LPDA.sol#buy()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L73-L75):
```solidity
for (uint256 x = temp.currentId + 1; x <= newId; x++) {
    nft.mint(msg.sender, x);
}
```

* [OpenEdition.sol#buy()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/OpenEdition.sol#L66-L68):
```solidity
for (uint24 x = temp.currentId + 1; x <= newId; x++) {
    nft.mint(msg.sender, x);
}
```

If the MINTER of the selling NFT [`mint()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/Escher721.sol#L51) an intermediate tokenId `K` (for activity purpose, or a misoperation), all `buy()`s will revert when the `currentId` reaches `K`.

This lead to:
* All types of minters be stuck, because the `buy()` always revert
* Fund in FixedPrice and LPDA frozen, because fund can only be released after all NFTs (from currentId to finalId) are sold / minted, while the sale is stuck at `K` (`currentId < K <= finalId`)

## Tools Used
VS Code

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
One of two options is recommended to avoid this problem:
1. Add an external `burn()` function to [Escher721](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e/src/Escher721.sol).
2. Allow the owner of minters to adjust the `currentId` and `finalId`, like this:
```solidity
