# Vulnerability details

## Impact
When a whale wants to buy nfts  and they    then put a lot of funds into the buy function, they won't get the nfts, and their funds will be lost 

ex:
Alice buys uint48.max+1 
Alice will pay all that amount of eth 
when  `uint48 newId = uint48(_amount) + sale_.currentId;` it will overflow to 0 and Alice wont get any nfts 
## Proof of Concept
```
    function test_overflow() public payable {
        // make the fixed price sale
        FixedPrice.Sale memory s;
        FixedPrice other;
        s = FixedPrice.Sale({
            currentId: uint48(0),
            finalId: uint48(1),
            edition: address(edition),
            price: uint96(uint256(1)),
            saleReceiver: payable(address(6)),
            startTime: uint96(block.timestamp)
        });
        other = FixedPrice(fixedSales.createFixedSale(s));
        // authorize the fixed price sale to mint tokens
        edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(other));
        vm.prank(address(6));
        uint256 b = uint256(type(uint48).max) + 1;
        vm.deal(address(6), b);
        other.buy{value: b}(b);
        assertEq(edition.balanceOf(address(6)), 0);
    }
```
This issue is harder to do with eth and uint48  but if the contract is very made for other tokens/whale, this can become a higher vulnerability 
I think it justifies medium because it's theoretically  possible to lose  funds
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
```
 uint48 amount = uint48(_amount);
```

