# Vulnerability details

## Impact
if someone buy `1,208,925.819614629174706175` ethers or more `(1208925819614629174706175 + 1)` to `LPDA` contract, the million of ethers will be locked forever.

## Proof of Concept

Keep in mind that the version of solidity used, despite being greater than `0.8`, does not prevent integer overflows during casting, it only does so in mathematical operations.

It is necessary to safely convert between the different numeric types.

In the following proof of concept you can see how it is impossible to obtain the ether sent due to an overflow produced in the sum of the user's balance `receipts[msg.sender].balance += uint80(msg.value);`

```js
contract POCLockTest is EscherTest {
    LPDA public sale;
    LPDAFactory public lpdaSales;
    LPDA.Sale public lpdaSale;

    function setUp() public virtual override {
        super.setUp();
        lpdaSales = new LPDAFactory();
        // set up a LPDA Sale
        lpdaSale = LPDA.Sale({
            currentId: uint48(1),
            finalId: uint48(3),
            edition: address(edition),
            startPrice: 2,
            finalPrice: 1,
            dropPerSecond: 1,
            startTime: uint96(block.timestamp),
            saleReceiver: payable(address(69)),
            endTime: uint96(block.timestamp + 1 days)
        });
    }

    function test_LockPOC() public {
        sale = LPDA(lpdaSales.createLPDASale(lpdaSale));
        edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));

        uint start = address(this).balance;
        uint max = uint256(type(uint80).max) + 1;

        assertEq(sale.amountSold(), 0);
        assertEq(address(sale).balance, 0);
        sale.buy{value: max}(0);

        assertEq(address(sale).balance, max);
        assertEq(sale.amountSold(), 0);
        assertEq(address(this).balance, start - max);

        vm.expectRevert("NOTHING TO REFUND");
        sale.refund();
    }
}
```

## Affected source code

- [LPDA.sol:71](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L71)

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
- Use a [safeCast](https://docs.openzeppelin.com/contracts/3.x/api/utils#SafeCast) from Open Zeppelin.

