# Vulnerability details

## Impact

In `LPDA` sales, buyers that buy NFT will lose all their refund. (Permanent loss of funds).

The buyers impacted are buyers that their account is a smart contracts that consume more than 2300 gas when receiving funds.

Example of impacted buyers:
1. Buyers that purchase the NFT through mutlisig wallets such as Gnosis safe
2. Buyers that are smart contracts such as proxy contracts or contracts that perform actions when receiving funds.
3. Other protocols that are using Escher as part of their operations that use proxy contracts or contracts that perform actions when receiving funds.

## Proof of Concept

`payable.transfer` function limits the gas used to 2300 units. This function is deprecated, it was previously used also for reentrancy protections. 

2300 gas units is very small and performing operations when receiving the funds will make the transaction fail because of "out of gas" error. 

`LPDA` uses `payable.transfer` to refund users when the price has been lowered to make sure all buys end up paying the same amount.

`refund()` function in `LPDA`:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L105
```
    function refund() public {
        Receipt memory r = receipts[msg.sender];
        uint80 price = uint80(getPrice()) * r.amount;
        uint80 owed = r.balance - price;
        require(owed > 0, "NOTHING TO REFUND");
        receipts[msg.sender].balance = price;
        payable(msg.sender).transfer(owed);
    }
```

As refund happens in separate transaction from `buy`, buyers impacted will overpay for the NFT and lose their refund.

### Foundry POC 

The POC will demonstrate a buyer account using multisig Gnosis safe buying NFT in a LPDA sale and failing to receive the refund after the auction ends.

Add the following test to `LPDA.t.sol`:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/test/LPDA.t.sol#L190
```
    function test_LPDA_multisig() public {
        // make the lpda sales contract
        sale = LPDA(lpdaSales.createLPDASale(lpdaSale));
        // authorize the lpda sale to mint tokens
        edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));

        // buyer is a multisig gnosis safe wallet, give it 1 eth
        address gnosis_safe = 0x5f5B8942aE6325227d5d82e5759E837271Fa2a67;
        vm.deal(gnosis_safe, 1 ether);

        //lets buy an NFT
        vm.prank(gnosis_safe);
        sale.buy{value: 1 ether}(1);
        assertEq(address(sale).balance, 1 ether);

        // forward 1 day into the future
        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 days);
        assertApproxEqRel(sale.getPrice(), 0.9 ether, lpdaSale.dropPerSecond);

        // buy the rest
        // this will auto end the sale
        sale.buy{value: uint256((0.9 ether + lpdaSale.dropPerSecond) * 9)}(9);

        // forward 2 day into the future
        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 2 days);

        // Try and get refund. Expect revert because out of gas
        vm.startPrank(gnosis_safe);
        vm.expectRevert();
        sale.refund();
        vm.stopPrank();
    }
```

