https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/main/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L99-L106


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

In `LPDA`, users are allowed to call `refund()` after buying to effectively change their price paid to the updated lower price. Every new block gives them an opportunity to receive more ether as a refund.

Once all items sell out, the sale ends and the contract is destroyed within the same transaction, meaning users can no longer get their refund. An unsuspecting user will have their ether refund sacrificed to the artist.

## Proof of Concept

```
function test_SoldOutNoRefund() public {
    address alice = address(1);
    vm.deal(alice, 10 ether);

    // setup
    sale = LPDA(lpdaSales.createLPDASale(lpdaSale));
    // authorize the lpda sale to mint tokens
    edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));

    vm.startPrank(alice);

    // price = 1 ETH
    sale.buy{value: 9 ether}(9);

    vm.warp(lpdaSale.endTime + 1);

    // price = 0.9 ETH
    uint256 price = sale.getPrice();
    sale.buy{value: price}(1);

    // sold out, cannot refund first purchase of 9 ETH
    vm.expectRevert();
    sale.refund();

    // alice overpaid
    uint256 aliceAveragePrice = (10 ether - alice.balance) / 10;
    assert(aliceAveragePrice > price);
}
```

## Tools Used

Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Add a grace period to the sale contract. Make it such that `_end()` is not called when the last item is sold out, but rather the owner of the contract (the artist) is able to call an external function to call `_end()` after there has been at least `GRACE_PERIOD` seconds since the NFTs sold out. This allows users some time to collect their full refund once the sale is over.

```
contract LPDA {
    // new state variables
    uint80 private soldOutTimestamp;
    uint80 public constant GRACE_PERIOD = 1 hours;

    //...

    function buy(...) external payable {

        //...

        if (newId == temp.finalId) {
            sale.finalPrice = uint80(price);
            uint256 totalSale = price * amountSold;
            uint256 fee = totalSale / 20;
            ISaleFactory(factory).feeReceiver().transfer(fee);
            temp.saleReceiver.transfer(totalSale - fee);
            //_end(); // old line
            soldOutTimestamp = block.timestamp; // new line
        }
    }

    // new function
    function end() external onlyOwner {
        require(block.timestamp > soldOutTimestamp + GRACE_PERIOD, "TOO EARLY");
        _end();
    }

    //...
}
```

# Lines of code

