# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Due to the unpredictability of `block.timestamp`, it is impossible for a user to send the exact correct amount of ether to buy NFTs.

If they send too little, the transaction will revert. If they send too much, they will have overpaid.

This may lead to a frustrating user experience, as well as a potential for lost/wasted ether.

## Proof of Concept

```
function test_Overpay() public {
    sale = LPDA(lpdaSales.createLPDASale(lpdaSale));
    // authorize the lpda sale to mint tokens
    edition.grantRole(edition.MINTER_ROLE(), address(sale));
    //lets buy an NFT
    address alice = address(1);
    vm.deal(alice, 10 ether);
    vm.prank(alice);
    sale.buy{value: 5 ether}(1);
    assertEq(address(sale).balance, 5 ether);
    assertEq(alice.balance, 5 ether);
    assertEq(edition.balanceOf(alice), 1);
}
```

## Tools Used

Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Implement an ether refund of `msg.value - price` for each call to `buy()`.

```
function buy(...) external payable {
    //...
    payable(msg.sender).transfer(msg.value - price);
    //...
}
```

