# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Currently, the `Escher` contract stores the artists that are eligable to create `Escher721` contracts using `Escher721Factory`.

`Escher721Factory.createContract()` reverts if called by a user without the `CREATOR_ROLE` in the `Escher` contract.

However, users are able to launch their `Escher721` contract directly, without using the factory, bypassing the authorization check.


## Proof of Concept

```
function test_NonCreatorDeploy() public {
        address alice = address(1);
        assert(!escher.hasRole(keccak256("CREATOR_ROLE"), alice));

        vm.startPrank(alice);

        Escher721 newContract = new Escher721();
        address _creator = alice;
        address _uri = address(2);
        string memory _name = "NAME";
        string memory _symbol = "SYMBOL";
        newContract.initialize(_creator, _uri, _name, _symbol);

        bytes32 DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE = 0x00;
        assert(newContract.hasRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, alice));
        assert(newContract.hasRole(keccak256("URI_SETTER_ROLE"), alice));
        assert(newContract.hasRole(keccak256("MINTER_ROLE"), alice));
    }
```

## Tools Used

Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Add a require statement in `Escher721.initialize()` to ensure that `msg.sender` is `Escher721Factory`.

