# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The `LPDA` contract has a `refund ()` function where buyers will be able to get a refund on the current price difference. However, the implementation of the `refund ()` function would often underflow when calculating the `owed` amount as seen here `uint80 owed = r.balance - price;`

The project can consider to refactor the code of this function and implement it as follows:
```
  function refund() public {
        Receipt memory r = receipts[msg.sender];
        uint80 price = uint80(getPrice()) * r.amount;
        if (r.balance > price){
            uint80 owed = r.balance - price;
            receipts[msg.sender].balance = price;
            payable(msg.sender).transfer(owed);

        }

    }
```

