# Vulnerability details

## Impact

If an LPDA or FixedPrice auction don't sell out then funds will never be released to factory or feeReceiver

## Proof of Concept

[LPDA.sol#L81-L88](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L81-L88)

        if (newId == temp.finalId) {
            sale.finalPrice = uint80(price);
            uint256 totalSale = price * amountSold;
            uint256 fee = totalSale / 20;
            ISaleFactory(factory).feeReceiver().transfer(fee);
            temp.saleReceiver.transfer(totalSale - fee);
            _end();
        }

The only way to release funds to feeReceiver and factory is for an auction to sell out and end, triggered by `newId == temp.finalId`.

[LPDA.sol#L92-L96](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-escher/blob/5d8be6aa0e8634fdb2f328b99076b0d05fefab73/src/minters/LPDA.sol#L92-L96)

    function cancel() external onlyOwner {
        require(block.timestamp < sale.startTime, "TOO LATE");
        sale.finalId = sale.currentId;
        _end();
    }

The only other way to terminate an auction is to call _cancel but this can only be called before the auction starts. If an auction never sells out then funds can never be released from the contract.

## Tools Used

Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Add a finalize function to LPDA and FixedPrice to allow the auction to be closed after endTime has passed. Below I've shown an example for LPDA:

    function finalize() public onlyOwner {
        //only allow auction to close once it's reached final price
        require(block.timestamp >= sale.endTime, "TOO SOON");
        sale.finalPrice = uint80(getPrice());
        uint256 totalSale = price * amountSold;
        sale.currentId = sale.finalId;
        uint256 fee = totalSale / 20;
        ISaleFactory(factory).feeReceiver().transfer(fee);
        temp.saleReceiver.transfer(totalSale - fee);
        _end();
    }

