# Vulnerability details

## Description
A Position keeps track of its debt by guessing using the current interest rate:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L322-L333
```solidity
File: utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol

322:    function _calculateDebt(
323:        address _bathToken,
324:        uint256 _startBlock,
325:        uint256 _borrowedAmount
326:    ) internal view returns (uint256 _debt) {
327:        uint256 _blockDelta = block.number - _startBlock;
328:
329:        uint256 _interest = (
330:            (_borrowedAmount).mul(borrowRate(_bathToken).mul(_blockDelta))
331:        ).div(10 ** 18);
332:        _debt = _borrowedAmount.add(_interest);
333:    }
```

The issue is that the borrow rate can be changed. Specifically if it is lowered it will cause the calculation to underestimate the debt and the position will not be able to close.

## Impact
Lowering the interest rate will cause position open against that pool to revert when calling `closePosition`. The user must manually repay the loan and then transfer the bathTokens (cTokens) out of the position (via `withdraw`) and redeem themselves. This will leave the position in the Position contract open. Also possibly causing the trader to lose out on the trade opportunity that caused them to want to close the position.

