# Vulnerability details

## Impact
It's possible for offers to be made without being sorted. This is done when creating an offer using `make`. When one of these unsorted offers is bought with the `amount`  being the same as `pay_amt`, the following happens.

In `_buys`, we either unsort the offer if sorted, otherwise we hide it:

```
// _buys - RubiconMarket.sol:L1185-1192
if (amount == offers[id].pay_amt) {
	if (isOfferSorted(id)) {
		//offers[id] must be removed from sorted list because all of it is bought
		_unsort(id);
	} else {
		_hide(id);
	}
}
```

After the low-level buy logic, we cancel the offer since the remaining `pay_amt` has become dust:

```
// _buys - RubiconMarket.sol:L1197-1203
if (
	isActive(id) &&
	offers[id].pay_amt < _dust[address(offers[id].pay_gem)]
) {
	dustId = id; //enable current msg.sender to call cancel(id)
	cancel(id);
}
```

In `cancel`, we try again to hide the offer since it's not sorted, reverting if the result is not `true`:

```
// cancel - RubiconMarket.sol:L876-880
if (isOfferSorted(id)) {
	require(_unsort(id));
} else {
	require(_hide(id), "can't hide");
}
```

In `_hide`, when we inevitably can't find the offer since it was already hidden, we return false, causing the `require` statement in `cancel` to trigger a revert:

```
function _hide(
	uint256 id //id of maker offer to remove from unsorted list
) internal returns (bool) {
	uint256 uid = _head; //id of an offer in unsorted offers list
	uint256 pre = uid; //id of previous offer in unsorted offers list

	require(!isOfferSorted(id), "offer sorted"); //make sure offer id is not in sorted offers list

	if (_head == id) {
		//check if offer is first offer in unsorted offers list
		_head = _near[id]; //set head to new first unsorted offer
		_near[id] = 0; //delete order from unsorted order list
		return true;
	}
	while (uid > 0 && uid != id) {
		//find offer in unsorted order list
		pre = uid;
		uid = _near[uid];
	}
	if (uid != id) {
		//did not find offer id in unsorted offers list
		return false;
	}
	_near[pre] = _near[id]; //set previous unsorted offer to point to offer after offer id
	_near[id] = 0; //delete order from unsorted order list
	return true;
}
```

