## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Use a whitelist mechanism for the external contract and add that access control check.

```
mapping(address => bool) public allowed;

function ApproveContract(address _addr) OnlyAdmin{
allowed[_addr] = true;
}

function revokeContract(address _addr) OnlyAdmin{
allowed[_addr] = false;
}

 function rubicall(
        CallParams memory params
    ) external payable returns (bytes memory) {
require(allowed[msg.sender],"Not allowed");
        if (msg.value == 0) {
            return _rubicall(params);
        } else {
            return _rubicallPayable(params);
        }
    }
```

any external project that wants to use this feature must discuss it with the team directly and the team can decide to give permission since external calls are too dangerous without the proper access control.

# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L485


# Vulnerability details

## Description
Lets look at how a trade happens when closing a position.

First a price is calculated. Here the fee is added so we get out the correct amount to repay our loan:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L475-L486
```solidity
File: utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol

475:    function _marketSell(
476:        address _asset,
477:        address _quote,
478:        uint256 _minFill
479:    ) internal {
480:        uint256 _feeBPS = rubiconMarket.getFeeBPS();
481:        uint256 _fee = _minFill.mul(_feeBPS).div(10000);
482:        uint256 _payAmount = rubiconMarket.getPayAmount(
483:            ERC20(_asset),
484:            ERC20(_quote),
486:            _minFill.add(_fee)
486:        );
```
The issue here is that `makerFee` is not included. Hence when actually repaying the loan it will fail due to the `_amountToRepay` isn't enough.

## Impact
When there is a `makerFee` closing a position will revert. The user must manually repay the loan and then transfer the bathTokens (cTokens) out of the position (via `withdraw`) and redeem themselves. This will leave the position in the Position contract open. Also possibly causing the trader to lose out on the trade opportunity that caused them to want to close the position.

