# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L459
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L481
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L490


# Vulnerability details

## Description
In `RubiconMarket` a fee subdivision of `100_000` us used:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/RubiconMarket.sol#L338:
```solidity
File: RubiconMarket.sol

338:        uint256 fee = mul(spend, feeBPS) / 100_000;
```

But in `Position` a subdivision of `10_000` is used:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L459
```
File: utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol

459:        uint256 _fee = _maxFill.mul(rubiconMarket.getFeeBPS()).div(10000);
```
Same in `_marketSell`.


This is then subtracted from the amount:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L460-L464
```solidity
File: utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol

460:        uint256 _buyAmount = rubiconMarket.getBuyAmount(
461:            ERC20(_asset),
462:            ERC20(_quote),
463:            _maxFill.sub(_fee)
464:        );
```

Hence a 10% fee, (`10_000`) in `RubiconMarket` will send amount `0` to be bought and fail in `SimpeMarket::buy`.
A fee >10% will cause the `_maxFill.sub(_fee)` to revert.

Lastly a fee <10% will work but cause the position to be bought for less.

## Impact
A fee of `>=10% (10_000/10000)` will cause Position to revert. A fee below will cause a bad fee calculation in Position

