# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L220
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L385-L388


# Vulnerability details

## Description
If a position is liquidated the state of how much is borrowed, `pos.bathTokenAmount`, is no longer accurate. Since the liquidator paid of a part of the loan:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-rubicon/blob/main/contracts/utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol#L385-L388
```solidity
File: utilities/poolsUtility/Position.sol

385:        require(
386:            CErc20Interface(_bathTokenAsset).redeem(_bathTokenAmount) == 0,
387:            "_redeem: REDEEM FAILED"
388:        );
```

This will cause calls to `closePosition` to fail.

## Impact
An liquidated position cannot be closed. The user must manually repay the loan and then transfer the bathTokens (cTokens) out of the position (via `withdraw`) and redeem themselves. This will leave the position in the Position contract open. Also possibly causing the trader to lose out on the trade opportunity that caused them to want to close the position.

## Proof of Concept
PoC test in `Position.t.sol`:
