# Vulnerability details

## Impact

_performFallbackCall can revert sliently when there is insufficient ETH remaining to pay for the Layerzero fee

## Proof of Concept

In RootBridgeAgent.sol when the has fall back toggle flag is on, the smart contract aim to perform a fallback call to notify the dest chain the failure to deliver the message

for example, the relevent code is [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/f5ba4de628836b2a29f9b5fff59499690008c463/src/RootBridgeAgent.sol#L788)

```solidity
//Update tx state if execution failed
if (!success) {
	//Read the fallback flag.
	if (_hasFallbackToggled) {
		// Update tx state as retrieve only
		executionState[_srcChainId][_depositNonce] = STATUS_RETRIEVE;
		// Perform the fallback call
		_performFallbackCall(payable(_refundee), _depositNonce, _srcChainId);
	} else {
		// No fallback is requested revert allowing for retry.
		revert ExecutionFailure();
	}
}
```

and [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/f5ba4de628836b2a29f9b5fff59499690008c463/src/RootBridgeAgent.sol#L712) when retrieve the deposit 

```solidity
	//Check if deposit is in retrieve mode
	if (executionState[_srcChainId][nonce] == STATUS_DONE) {
		revert AlreadyExecutedTransaction();
	} else {
		//Set settlement to retrieve mode, if not already set.
		if (executionState[_srcChainId][nonce] == STATUS_READY) {
			executionState[_srcChainId][nonce] = STATUS_RETRIEVE;
		}
		//Trigger fallback/Retry failed fallback
		_performFallbackCall(
			payable(address(uint160(bytes20(_payload[PARAMS_START:PARAMS_START_SIGNED])))), nonce, _srcChainId
		);
	}
```

the logicof the [_performFallbackCall](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/f5ba4de628836b2a29f9b5fff59499690008c463/src/RootBridgeAgent.sol#L938) is here

```solidity
function _performFallbackCall(address payable _refundee, uint32 _depositNonce, uint16 _dstChainId) internal {
	//Sends message to LayerZero messaging layer
	ILayerZeroEndpoint(lzEndpointAddress).send{value: address(this).balance}(
		_dstChainId,
		getBranchBridgeAgentPath[_dstChainId],
		abi.encodePacked(bytes1(0x04), _depositNonce),
		payable(_refundee),
		address(0),
		""
	);
}
```

the code forward all ETH (address(this).balance) and aim to use the ETH to pay for the layerzero fee

However, in the case when there is insufficient ETH left to pay for the execution fee, the transaction send revert

but the problem is that such fallback is wrapped by the [excessivelySafeCall](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/f5ba4de628836b2a29f9b5fff59499690008c463/src/RootBridgeAgent.sol#L424)

to not blocking other passing messaging via layerzero endpoint, the excessivelySafeCall will sliently revert but does not block transaction confirm

basically this means if there are revert (insufficient ETH remaining to pay for the Layerzero fee) inside the excessivelySafeCall, fall back is never executed and even user toggle the fall back flag, asset can still be lost

which line of code will revert if there are insufficient ETH foward to pay for the layerzero fee?

after the message is [sent via the endpoint](https://github.com/LayerZero-Labs/LayerZero/blob/48c21c3921931798184367fc02d3a8132b041942/contracts/Endpoint.sol#L95), the layerzero endpoint foward the message to UltraLightNodeV2

and the code quote the execution fee and relayer fee and if the fee is insufficient, transaction revert [in this line of code](https://github.com/LayerZero-Labs/LayerZero/blob/48c21c3921931798184367fc02d3a8132b041942/contracts/UltraLightNodeV2.sol#L150)

```solidity
// compute all the fees
uint relayerFee = _handleRelayer(dstChainId, uaConfig, ua, payload.length, _adapterParams);
uint oracleFee = _handleOracle(dstChainId, uaConfig, ua);
uint nativeProtocolFee = _handleProtocolFee(relayerFee, oracleFee, ua, _zroPaymentAddress);

// total native fee, does not include ZRO protocol fee
uint totalNativeFee = relayerFee.add(oracleFee).add(nativeProtocolFee);

// assert the user has attached enough native token for this address
require(totalNativeFee <= msg.value, "LayerZero: not enough native for fees");
```

can add this test into the BranchBridgeAgentTest.t.sol to prove that the transaction revert when there is insufficient ETH remaining to pay for the Layerzero fee

