# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Deposits from `ArbitrumBranchBridgeAgent` towards `RootBridgeAgent` that rely on fallback will be left stuck on the `BranchBridgeAgent`

## Proof of Concept
`ArbitrumBranchBridgeAgent` is a special type of `BranchBridgeAgent` to be deployed on the same chain as the `RootBridgeAgent`. Because of that the `_requiresEndpoint(...)` modifier has a different implementation that allows only direct calls from the `RootBridgeAgent`. 
```solidity
    /// @notice Verifies the caller is the Root Bridge Agent.
    /// @dev Internal function used in modifier to reduce contract bytesize.
    function _requiresEndpoint(address _endpoint, bytes calldata) internal view override {
        if (msg.sender != address(this)) revert LayerZeroUnauthorizedEndpoint();
        if (_endpoint != rootBridgeAgentAddress) revert LayerZeroUnauthorizedEndpoint();
    }
```
If a message failed on the  `RootBridgeAgent` - `_performFallbackCall(...)` is called to set the Deposit on the `BranchBridgeAgent` as Failed. However, `_performFallbackCall(...)` doesn't implement a direct call when the `BranchBridgeAgent` is on the same chain as the `RootBridgeAgent` (i.e Arbitrum chain). The problem is that the message is sent through the LayerZero endpoint & when LayerZero attempts to call `lzReceive(...)` on `ArbitrumBranchBridgeAgent` the `msg.sender` (i.e LayerZero) is passed to 
`lzReceiveNonBlocking(address _endpoint, ...)` & checked in the `_requiresEndpoint(...)` modifier which only expects calls directly from the `RootBridgeAgent` and the modifier will revert.

This will leave the deposit as `STATUS_SUCCESS` on the `BranchBridgeAgent` and as `STATUS_RETRIEVE` on the `RootBridgeAgent`. Therefore, we cannot retry the deposit (since it isn't `STATUS_READY` on the `RootBridgeAgent`), we cannot retrieve the deposit since we run in the same  `_performFallbackCall(...)` that will revert and we cannot redeem the deposit since the deposit status isn't  `STATUS_FAILED`. This leaves the deposit stuck on the `ArbitrumBranchBridgeAgent`.
```solidity
function _performFallbackCall(address payable _refundee, uint32 _depositNonce, uint16 _dstChainId) internal {
        //Sends message to LayerZero messaging layer
        ILayerZeroEndpoint(lzEndpointAddress).send{value: address(this).balance}(
            _dstChainId,
            getBranchBridgeAgentPath[_dstChainId],
            abi.encodePacked(bytes1(0x04), _depositNonce),
            payable(_refundee),
            address(0),
            ""
        );
    }
```

### Coded POC
1. Place the following test in `RootTest` contract inside `RootTest.t.sol`
2. Run the test with `forge test --match-test testRevertingModifier -vv`
3. Run the test again with `forge test --match-test testRevertingModifier -vvvv`

Output with `-vv` verbosity prints the state of the deposit on the Branch & Root Agents - we can see that on the BranchBridgeAgent status is 0 (STATUS_SUCCESS) & on the RootBridgeAgent status is 2 (STATUS_RETRIEVE)

Output with `-vvvv` verbosity prints the whole trace where we can see the `"LayerZeroUnauthorizedEndpoint()"` revert message from the modifier
```solidity
function testRevertingModifier() public {
        // Add tokens
        testAddLocalTokenArbitrum();

        // Mock user
        address user = address(0x7777);

        // Mint some underlying tokens
        arbitrumMockToken.mint(user, 100 ether);

        hevm.deal(user, 1 ether);

        // Track the deposit nonce
        uint32 depositNonce = arbitrumMulticallBridgeAgent.depositNonce();

        DepositInput memory depositInput = DepositInput({
            hToken: address(newArbitrumAssetGlobalAddress),
            token: address(arbitrumMockToken),
            amount: 100 ether,
            deposit: 100 ether
        });

        GasParams memory gasParams = GasParams({
            gasLimit: 0.5 ether,
            remoteBranchExecutionGas: 0.5 ether
        });

        // invalid op code to trigger fallback
        bytes memory packedData = abi.encodePacked(bytes1(0x07), "");

        // Start user prank
        hevm.startPrank(user);

        arbitrumMockToken.approve(address(arbitrumPort), 100 ether);
        arbitrumMulticallBridgeAgent.callOutSignedAndBridge{value: 1 ether}(
            payable(user), packedData, depositInput, gasParams, true
        );

        // Examine the Deposit state on Branch & execution state on Root
        Deposit memory depInfoBranch = arbitrumMulticallBridgeAgent.getDepositEntry(depositNonce);

        console2.log("Deposit status", depInfoBranch.status);

        console2.log("Execution status", multicallBridgeAgent.executionState(rootChainId, depositNonce));

    }
```
