# Vulnerability details

## Impact
User deposits can be stolen by anyone. A malicious user can withdraw all the tokens deposited in the Maia protocol. A malicious user can call ```callOut()``` function in the ```BranchBridgeAgent.sol``` contract with maliciously crafted ```_params``` specifically the ```OutputParams``` where the malicious user can specify a desired ```amountOut``` and ```depositOut``` to drain all the funds in the contract for the specified ```outputToken```. The ```OutputParams``` are encoded with other data such as the destination chain id and supplied as ```_params``` argument in the ```callOut()``` function. In the below POC is demonstrated how ```Alice``` has ```10e18``` starting balance which she deposits in to the Maia protocol, ```Bob``` starts with ```1e18``` tokens and after executing the attack he ends up with ```11e18``` tokens.

## Proof of Concept
Add the following test to ```RootTest.t.sol```

```

