## Impact
The code in question allows the approval of multiple tokens for spending by a refundee address and subsequently transfers these tokens to the refundee address using a bridge agent. However, there is a security concern related to the refundee address potentially being a malicious smart contract that can execute arbitrary code when it receives ETH in the callOutAndBridgeMultiple function.
Malicious smart contract can contain selfdestruct() in its receive function when executor   

