# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Access control plays an important role in segregation of privileges in smart contracts and other applications. 

If this is misconfigured or not properly validated on sensitive functions, it may lead to loss of funds, tokens and in some cases compromise of the smart contract.

The contract MulticallRootRouter is importing an access control library @openzeppelin/contracts/access/Ownable.sol but the function executeResponse is missing the modifier onlyOwner.

The contract MulticallRootRouter is importing an access control library @openzeppelin/contracts/access/Ownable.sol but the function execute is missing the modifier onlyOwner.

The contract MulticallRootRouter is importing an access control library @openzeppelin/contracts/access/Ownable.sol but the function executeDepositSingle is missing the modifier onlyOwner.

The contract MulticallRootRouter is importing an access control library @openzeppelin/contracts/access/Ownable.sol but the function executeDepositMultiple is missing the modifier onlyOwner.

