# Vulnerability details

## Summary

The _params input for RootBridgeAgent's retrySettlement is calldata of arbitrary length. Users may incur losses if they submit a send request with excessively large _params, disrupting communication between networks with varying gas limits.

Arbitrum boasts a substantial gas block limit, surpassing Optimism's 20M block gas limit. If a user calls retrySettlement on the root chain with the Optimism chain as the destination, the message will fail to send. However, the settlement status is updated locally, resulting in a permanent loss of user funds

## Proof of Concept

```solidity
        // @audit generate _params large than Optimism's 20M block gas limit
        bytes memory _params =_generateLargeData();

        //Retry Settlement
        multicallBridgeAgent.retrySettlement{value: 1 ether}(
            settlementNonce, address(this), _params , GasParams(0.5 ether, 0.5 ether), true
        );

        settlement = multicallBridgeAgent.getSettlementEntry(settlementNonce);

        require(settlement.status == STATUS_SUCCESS, "Settlement status should be success.");

        // @audit settlement will not executed in branch
        require(opMulticallBridgeAgent.executionState(settlementNonce) != 1, "But Settelement will not Executed in branch");
```
## Tools Used
Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Add length check for calldata
```
    function retrySettlement(
        uint32 _settlementNonce,
        address _recipient,
        bytes calldata _params,
        GasParams calldata _gParams,
        bool _hasFallbackToggled
    ) external payable override lock {
        require(_params.length<100, "too large");
