# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The protocol's root routers, both coreRootRouter and MultiCallRootRouter do not implement the functions meant to handle processing the payload data of callOutAndBridge from a branch chain but simply revert. This results in a denial of service on the root chain. Optimistically, users can retrieve their deposits from the branch chain, but the bridging service is still denied.

