Token-Transfer

# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootPort.sol#L284-L288


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
- Bridging tokens from Branches to Root is broken, which will cause that users to not be able to use their hTokens on the different branches to bridge them to the Root environment.

## Proof of Concept
Before getting into the problem, first, let's understand how the deposit/bridging mechanism works, the flow execution looks like this: `BaseBranchRouter::callOutAndBridgeMultiple() => transfer hTokens and underlying tokens from the user to the Router contract and grants allowance to the BranchPort => BranchBridgeAgent::callOutAndBridgeMultiple() => burns hTokens and locks underlyingTokens in BranchPort => LZ.send() => RBA::lzReceive() => RBA::lzReceiveNonBlocking() => RBAExecutor::executeWithDepositMultiple() => RBAExecutor::_bridgeInMultiple() => RBA::bridgeInMultiple() => RBA::bridgeIn() => RootPort::bridgeToRoot() => globalTokens are minted to the Recipient in the RootPort`. ***(RBA stands for RootBridgeAgent & RBAExecutor for RootBridgeAgentExecutor)***
- The users interact with a BranchRouter that is deployed on the Branch/Chain from where they want to bridge their tokens & hTokens (sourceBranch), the entry point is the [`BaseBranchRouter::callOutAndBridgeMultiple()` function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/BaseBranchRouter.sol#L104-L116), this functions transfers the amount of hTokens and amount of deposit underlyingTokens from the user into the Router contract and grants allowance to the BranchPort, then the execution will go through different Branch contracts, where it will burn the hTokens being bridged and it will transfer the underylingTokens from the depositor and will left them lock in the BranchPort contract, also, the payload that is sent as the crosschain message is encoded, and finally the Branch chain sends a message through LayerZero to the Root environment with the encoded payload that contains the details of the deposit (such details are the owner, the hTokens addresses, the underlyingTokens addresses, the amounts of hTokens being bridged, the deposits of underlyingTokens being bridged). Then, LayerZero will receive, process, post, and execute the message into the Root environment (deployed in Arbitrum). In the Root environment, the [`RootBridgeAgent::lzReceive()` function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootBridgeAgent.sol#L423-L431) will receive the execution coming from the LayerZero contracts and will forward the execution to the [`RootBridgeAgentExecutor::executeWithDepositMultiple()` function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootBridgeAgentExecutor.sol#L115-L140)  to decode the payload and send it back to the [`RootBridgeAgent::bridgeInMultiple()` function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootBridgeAgent.sol#L387-L416) which will iterate over the array of tokens being bridged and will call the [`RootPort::bridgeToRoot()` function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootPort.sol#L277-L291) to mint the globalTokens to the specified recipient in the Root environment.

- **The problem with the existing process to bridge tokens from a Branch to Root is located in the final part of the execution flow**, ***in the [`RootPort::bridgeToRoot()` function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootPort.sol#L277-L291)***, specifically when the function attempts to do a safeTransfer of the hToken to the recipient.
  - The address of the hToken received in the [`RootPort::bridgeToRoot()` function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootPort.sol#L277-L291) is the address of a globalToken, in the [`RootBridgeAgent::bridgeIn()` function, the function gets the globalToken address from the LocalAddress token, and this is the address that is forwarded to the `RootPort:bridgeToRoot()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootBridgeAgent.sol#L379)
  - So, when the [`RootPort::bridgeToRoot()` function tries to transfer the globalTokens from the contract itself to the recipient](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/RootPort.sol#L284-L288), **the execution will fail because the RootPort contract hasn't received any tokens of the globalToken to cover the transfer operation.**

```solidity
function bridgeToRoot(address _recipient, address _hToken, uint256 _amount, uint256 _deposit, uint256 _srcChainId)
    external
    override
    requiresBridgeAgent
{
    //@audit-info => _hToken is a globalToken
    if (!isGlobalAddress[_hToken]) revert UnrecognizedToken();

    //@audit-info => If > 0 it means that the user burnt hToken (localToken) in the Source Branch
    if (_amount - _deposit > 0) {
        unchecked {
            //@audit-info => Will fail because the RootPort contract in the Root environment has not received any tokens of the globalToken to cover up the transfer request          
            _hToken.safeTransfer(_recipient, _amount - _deposit);
        }
    }

    //@audit-ok => Mints the deposited amount of underlyingTokens as globalTokens to the recipient in the Root environment
    if (_deposit > 0) if (!ERC20hTokenRoot(_hToken).mint(_recipient, _deposit, _srcChainId)) revert UnableToMint();
}
```

