- Now everything is ready to run the test and analyze the output:
> forge test --mc RootForkTest --match-test testCallOutAndBridgeMultiplePoC -vvvv
- As we can see, in the last part of the execution flow, the tx is reverted when the RootPort:bridgeToRoot() attempts to transfer the globalToken from the RootPort contract to the recipient, the reason is that the RootPort in the Root environment (deployed in Arbitrum) has not received any tokens of the globalToken to cover the requested amount of tokens to be transferred.
  - As a consequence of the the RootPort not being able to transfer the amount of globalTokens to the recipient, the whole process is blocked.
  - This will always happen when bridingOut/Depositing hTokens from a SourceBranch to Root

