## Recommended Mitigation Steps
- The recommendation to fix this problem is to mint in the Root environment the amount of burnt hTokens in the Source Branch + the amount of locked underlyingTokens in the Branch Port.
- When bridging to Root, the user will get the globalToken version of their underlying and local hTokens, so, makes more sense to only execute a mint operation covering up the whole amount of tokens being bridged instead of attempting to transfer from the RootPort to the user the amount of burnt localTokens and mint the amount of deposited underlyingTokens.

