# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The [multicall()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-11-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/multicall/Multicall.sol#L26) functionality allows you to club multiple calls in one. This is designed for emergency situations or to simply club multiple transactions/calls. 
- However, even if one of them reverts, the whole multicall reverts. The PoC shows a scenario where if we are trying to send ERC1155 tokens to various addresses, a single malicious address (`Attacker` contract in our case) can cause the whole multicall to revert, denying transfer to other users too.
- The multicall function has an additional risk - It uses an unbounded loop [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-11-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/multicall/Multicall.sol#L14) which carries the risk of it running out of gas during a call when `data. Length` is high.

## Proof of Concept
Create a new file `t0x1cMulticall.t.sol` inside `test/foundry/core/` & add the following code. Run it via `forge test --mt test_t0x1c_multicall -vv` to see it revert. Here, the multicall was attempting to transfer ERC1155 tokens to multiple addresses, but could not do so.

```js
