## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Instead of reverting [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-11-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/multicall/Multicall.sol#L26), we could return an array of success & failures and let the caller decide if he wants to revert or not in case of any single transaction failure. This way the caller has much more flexibility while using multicall, specially in emergency situations.
For the unbounded loop, it would be better to limit the size of `data` allowed.



