# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-party/blob/main/contracts/crowdfund/InitialETHCrowdfund.sol#L194


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Unlimited voting power for attacker and stealing of funds !
## Proof of Concept
All of the contribute functions uses `msg.value` to calculate the votingpower . For example , `contribute` function looks like this :  
```solidity 
 function contribute(
        uint256 tokenId,
        address delegate,
        bytes memory gateData
    ) public payable onlyDelegateCall returns (uint96 votingPower) {
        return
            _contribute(
                payable(msg.sender),
                delegate,
                msg.value.safeCastUint256ToUint96(), //@audit using msg.value for accounting ! 
                tokenId, 
                gateData
            );
    }
```
Using msg.value for accounting imposes a significant security risk . While delegatecalling from a payable multicall function  , given msg.value is looped throughout the calls without actually providing eth !

```solidity 
 contract Multicall {
    function multicall(bytes[] calldata data) external payable returns (bytes[] memory results) {
        results = new bytes[](data.length);
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {
            (bool success, bytes memory result) = CrowdFundAddress.delegatecall(data[i]);

            if (!success) {
              revert();
            }
            results[i] = result;
        }
    }
}
```
An exploit scenario could be this : 

The core idea behind this exploit is using msg.value inside a loop.  
Exploiter will  use a payable multicall function to delegatecall  `contribute` multiple times in a single call.  
For the first subcall  `contribute` function works perfectly without any issue. 
But in the second subcall,  msg.value will still be the same as before but no Eth is actually sent .  But  `contribute` function will execute without any issue and increase the contributors voting power as it uses msg.value for accounting purpose and doesnot check if the asset was actually provided or not. 
Afterwards, every subcall will execute  without issue and increase voting power of the contibutor like the second subcall .  

Impact: 
1. If a crowdfund is lost,  exploiter will be able to refund all of the assets before anyone refunds with his increased voting power. And other legitimate contributors will fail to refund as there's not enough asset left in the contract.  
2. If a crowdfund still wins and finalizes somehow , the exploiter gets the votingpower 
## Tools Used
manual review ! 
Inspired by The $6M [Aurora Bug ](https://medium.com/immunefi/aurora-infinite-spend-bugfix-review-6m-payout-e635d24273d)
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Implement a book keeping balance check Lock to ensure that eth is actually paid . 


