ETH-Transfer

# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-party/blob/b23c65d62a20921c709582b0b76b387f2bb9ebb5/contracts/party/PartyGovernanceNFT.sol#L457-L463
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-party/blob/b23c65d62a20921c709582b0b76b387f2bb9ebb5/contracts/party/PartyGovernanceNFT.sol#L451-L455
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-party/blob/b23c65d62a20921c709582b0b76b387f2bb9ebb5/contracts/party/PartyGovernanceNFT.sol#L454


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The data parameter in PartyGovernanceNFT's `safeTransferFrom()` function can be manipulated by a malicious ERC721 contract to exploit the disconnect between voting power transfer and token ownership transfer. This could allow an attacker to steal voting power or cause a denial of service.

## Proof of Concept 

`safeTransferFrom()` and the ordering of `_transferVotingPower()` in `transferFrom()` versus the inherited `safeTransferFrom()`.

```solidity
function safeTransferFrom(
  address owner, 
  address to,
  uint256 tokenId,
  bytes calldata data  
) public override {

  // Safe transfer calls transferFrom() first
  super.safeTransferFrom(owner, to, tokenId, data);  
}
```

The issue is that `transferFrom()` is called before the NFT's onERC721Received callback, allowing data to contain malicious code.

```solidity  
function transferFrom(address owner, address to, uint256 tokenId) public override {
  // Voting power transferred here
  _transferVotingPower(owner, to, votingPowerByTokenId[tokenId]);
  super.transferFrom(owner, to, tokenId);
}
```

- [safeTransferFrom()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-party/blob/b23c65d62a20921c709582b0b76b387f2bb9ebb5/contracts/party/PartyGovernanceNFT.sol#L457-L463): This function is the main vulnerability since it allows arbitrary data to be passed to the NFT contract's callback.

- [transferFrom()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-party/blob/b23c65d62a20921c709582b0b76b387f2bb9ebb5/contracts/party/PartyGovernanceNFT.sol#L451-L455): This function correctly transfers voting power before token ownership.

- [super.safeTransferFrom()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-party/blob/b23c65d62a20921c709582b0b76b387f2bb9ebb5/contracts/party/PartyGovernanceNFT.sol#L454): Inherited from OpenZeppelin's ERC721 implementation, calls `transferFrom()` first.

The key issue is that `safeTransferFrom()` with the `bytes calldata data` parameter allows malicious code to be executed in the NFT's `onERC721Received` callback after `_transferVotingPower()` has already been called. 

This disconnect between voting power transfer and token ownership transfer creates a window that can be exploited.

test:

```solidity
// ExploitNFT.sol
contract ExploitNFT {

  function onERC721Received(address, address, uint256, bytes calldata data) external returns(bytes4) {

    // Decode the callback function from data
    (string memory callbackFuncSig) = abi.decode(data, (string));

    // Call the exploit callback 
    if(keccak256(bytes(callbackFuncSig)) == keccak256("exploit()")) {
      exploit();
    }

    return ERC721_RECEIVED;
  }

  function exploit() internal {
    // Steal voting power or cause a revert
  }

}

// Attacker.sol
interface IPartyGovernanceNFT {

  function approve(address to, uint256 tokenId) external;

  function safeTransferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId, bytes calldata data) external;

}

contract Attacker {

  ExploitNFT public nft;

  constructor() {
    nft = new ExploitNFT(); 
  }

  function exploit(address partyGovernanceNFT, uint256 tokenId) external {

    IPartyGovernanceNFT(partyGovernanceNFT).approve(address(this), tokenId);

    bytes memory data = abi.encode("exploit()");

    IPartyGovernanceNFT(partyGovernanceNFT).safeTransferFrom(
      address(this), address(0x1), tokenId, data
    );

  }

}
```

An attacker can create a malicious NFT contract and call `safeTransferFrom` while encoding the exploit in the `data` parameter. The exploit will be called between the voting power transfer and token ownership transfer.

## Tools Used

Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation

Validate data parameter in `safeTransferFrom()` to prevent executing unapproved code.


