carefully calibrate the liquidation incentives and perform additional checks to ensure that the loan-to-value ratio accurately reflects the collateralization status of the loans. This can include setting reasonable limits on liquidation incentives or introducing additional criteria to verify the under-collateralization of loans before triggering the liquidation process.



