# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Although there is no damage to be done, the check should not be bypassed to reduce attack surface.

During liquidation, the amount that can be liquidated (`_actualTokensToLiquidate`) is controlled by minimum of `_maxTokensToLiquidate` or `_balance` calculated in `_calculateTokensToLiquidate` internal function. Liquidator can bypass the checks in 2 ways

1. Liquidate when `_usdaToSolvency * 1e18 < _badFillPrice - _ltvDiscount` aka when `_usdaToSolvency` is very small. It is possible to bypass `_maxTokensToLiquidate` due to loss during division causing `_maxTokensToLiquidate` to becomes 0.
```
    // the maximum amount of tokens to liquidate is the amount that will bring the vault to solvency
    // divided by the denominator
    uint256 _maxTokensToLiquidate = (_usdaToSolvency * 1e18) / _denominator;
    //Cannot liquidate more than is necessary to make vault over-collateralized
    if (_tokensToLiquidate > _maxTokensToLiquidate) _tokensToLiquidate = _maxTokensToLiquidate; // @audit _tokensToLiquidate now equal 0
```
Which is then used to cap the amount that they can liqudiate. But when it returns 0 the cap is bypassed.
```
    (uint256 _tokenAmount, uint256 _badFillPrice) = _liquidationMath(_id, _assetAddress, _tokensToLiquidate);
    // set _tokensToLiquidate to this calculated amount if the function does not fail
    if (_tokenAmount > 0) _tokensToLiquidate = _tokenAmount; // @audit allowing liquidator to continue with full _tokensToLiquidate
```
But no damage could be done because at the end vault solvency is checked to prevent over liquidation.
```
  // @audit safu
  if (_getVaultBorrowingPower(_vault) > _vaultLiability(_id)) revert VaultController_OverLiquidation();
```
Without this check, liquidator would be able to liquidate all of collateral.

2. Call liquidate with asset that vault doesn't have. Inside `_calculateTokensToLiquidate` cap amount to balance of vault. When try to liquidate asset that vault doesn't have, it becomes 0 and the cap is bypassed same as above.
```
    uint256 _balance = _vault.balances(_assetAddress);

    //Cannot liquidate more collateral than there is in the vault
    if (_tokensToLiquidate > _balance) _tokensToLiquidate = _balance; // _tokensToLiquidate becomes 0 since vault doesn't have any balance
```
But it is not possible to continue liquidation process since there is nothing to transfer out of vault.
```
    // finally, deliver tokens to liquidator
    _vault.controllerTransfer(_assetAddress, _msgSender(), _tokensToLiquidate - _liquidationFee); // @audit nothing to transfer here
```

## Proof of Concept
Extending `CommonE2EBase` test contract. The test showed that liquidating vault that is so close to solvency within hundreds of wei (this amount depends on bad fill price and ltv discount), liquidator can bypass `_maxTokensToLiquidate` and continue the process with input amount until it reverted due to over liquidation.
```
  function testLiquidateEdgeCase() public {
    // Bob mints vault
    uint96 bobsVaultId = _mintVault(bob);
    bobVault = IVault(vaultController.vaultIdVaultAddress(bobsVaultId));

    // Borrow the maximum amount
    deal(address(weth), bob, 100 ether);
    vm.startPrank(bob);
    weth.approve(address(bobVault), 100 ether);
    bobVault.depositERC20(address(weth), 100 ether);
    vaultController.borrowUSDA(bobsVaultId, vaultController.vaultBorrowingPower(bobsVaultId));
    vm.stopPrank();

    // Let time pass so the vault becomes liquidatable because of interest
    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1000 days);

    vaultController.calculateInterest();

    vm.startPrank(dave);
    susd.approve(address(usdaToken), 1e26);
    usdaToken.deposit(1e26);
    // Repay (or liquidate) until brim of being insolvent
    vaultController.repayUSDA(bobsVaultId, uint192(vaultController.amountToSolvency(bobsVaultId) - 120));

    // Try to liquidate up to liability
    (,,,, uint256 liquidationBonus, IOracleRelay oracle,,,,) =
      (vaultController.tokenAddressCollateralInfo(WETH_ADDRESS));
    uint256 _tokensToLiquidate = bobVault.baseLiability() * vaultController.interestFactor() * 1e18
      / (_getPriceWithDecimals(oracle.currentValue(), 18) * (1e18 - liquidationBonus));
    // Even we can bypass the cap, it failed due to solvency check at the end
    vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSignature('VaultController_OverLiquidation()'));
    vaultController.liquidateVault(bobsVaultId, WETH_ADDRESS, _tokensToLiquidate);

    vm.stopPrank();
  }
```

