# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The identified vulnerability in the smart contract arises from the potential underflow in the calculation of _lowerBounds when comparing the main value (chainlink) to the anchor value (uniswap v3). The vulnerability is contingent on the relationship between stale/WidthNumerator and stale/WidthDenominator, which determines the _buffer value used in the calculation.
 If stale/WidthNumerator is greater than stale/WidthDenominator, an underflow can occur, resulting in a very large value for _lowerBounds. 
This can lead to unintended consequences, such as reverting transactions, unexpected behavior, or even potential security risks.

## Proof of Concept

     function _getLastSecond() private view returns (uint256 _mainValue) {
    ..
    uint256 _anchorPrice = anchorRelay.peekValue();
    require(_anchorPrice > 0, 'invalid anchor value');

    uint256 _buffer;
    if (IChainlinkOracleRelay(address(mainRelay)).isStale()) {
      /// If the price is stale the range percentage is smaller
      _buffer = (staleWidthNumerator * _anchorPrice) / staleWidthDenominator;
    } else {
      _buffer = (widthNumerator * _anchorPrice) / widthDenominator;
    }
    ..
    uint256 _lowerBounds = _anchorPrice - _buffer;

    // ensure the anchor price is within bounds
    require(_mainValue < _upperBounds, 'anchor too low');
    require(_mainValue > _lowerBounds, 'anchor too high');
    }
    } 

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
check that the stale/WidthNumerator is lower than stale/WidthDenomerator


