https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-07-amphora/blob/daae020331404647c661ab534d20093c875483e1/core/solidity/contracts/periphery/oracles/ChainlinkOracleRelay.sol#L57


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
In ChainlinkOracleRelay.sol, we determine if a price is stale by calling the isStale() function. It checks if the current timestamp (block.timestamp) is greater than the timestamp of when the data was last updated plus some delay period (stalePriceDelay). If it is, that means the data has not been updated for more than the delay period, and hence is considered stale. The function then returns true, indicating the data is stale.
```solidity
    /// @notice Returns true if the price is stale
    /// @return _stale True if the price is stale
    function isStale() external view returns (bool _stale) {
        (, , , uint256 _updatedAt, ) = _AGGREGATOR.latestRoundData();
        if (block.timestamp > _updatedAt + stalePriceDelay) _stale = true;
    }
```

This validation may not be insufficient when stalePriceDelay is set to a large number. 
This could lead to stale prices according to the Chainlink documentation:
https://docs.chain.link/docs/historical-price-data/#historical-rounds

## Proof of Concept
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-07-amphora/blob/daae020331404647c661ab534d20093c875483e1/core/solidity/contracts/periphery/oracles/ChainlinkOracleRelay.sol#L57

## Tools Used
None

