## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Consider implementing slippage that will have either the first or the second phase of the auction taken care of. Here's a suggested code refactoring:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-12-ethereumcreditguild/blob/main/src/loan/AuctionHouse.sol#L166-L196

```diff
- function bid(bytes32 loanId) external {
+ function bid(bytes32 loanId, uint256 expectedAmount) external {
+    Auction memory auction = auctions[loanId];

    (uint256 collateralReceived, uint256 creditAsked) = getBidDetail(loanId);
    require(creditAsked != 0, "AuctionHouse: cannot bid 0");

+    // Determine the auction phase and apply slippage check
+    if (block.timestamp < auction.startTime + midPoint) {
+        // First phase: Validate collateral received against slippage
+        require(collateralReceived >= expectedAmount, "AuctionHouse: slippage exceeded in collateral");
+    } else {
+        // Second phase: Validate credit asked against slippage
+        require(creditAsked <= expectedAmount, "AuctionHouse: slippage exceeded in credit");
+    }

    // Remaining logic
}
