# Vulnerability details




## Impact


Protocol allows setting new auction house for lending terms to implement auction house with different midpoint & auction duration, or even different mechanisms not based on dutch auction.  Setting new auction is indeed an important governance action, as it allows the protocol to migrate to a new auction mechanism or address critical issues with the current AuctionHouse. 

Since it is a governor action, it should be callable at ease when there is need to set new address which may not be possible due to current checks implemented in the contract. The logic implemented in the contract puts an limitation on setAuctionHouse function to update Auction house address for emergency or whatever reason from protocol design perspective.



## Proof of Concept


```
    /// @notice set the address of the auction house.
    /// governor-only, to allow full governance to update the auction mechanisms.
    function setAuctionHouse(
        address _newValue
    ) external onlyCoreRole(CoreRoles.GOVERNOR) {
        // allow configuration changes only when there are no auctions in progress.
        // updating the auction house while auctions are in progress could break the loan
        // lifecycle, as it would prevent the former auctionHouse (that have active auctions)
        // from reporting the result to the lending term.
        require(
            AuctionHouse(refs.auctionHouse).nAuctionsInProgress() == 0,
            "LendingTerm: auctions in progress"
        );

        refs.auctionHouse = _newValue;
    }
```

- For setting new auction house setAuctionHouse function is implemented in LendingTerm contract which depends on the `nAuctionsInProgress` variable.
- setAuctionHouse is successfully executed on only `AuctionHouse(refs.auctionHouse).nAuctionsInProgress() == 0` condition check pass.
- There might be case where loans are getting called continuously and actions are ongoing continuously which will not allow setAutcionHouse to set new auction house address.


## Tools Used

Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

- There should be a logic to pause new auctions from being started for some time in the current AuctionHouse till ongoing auctions concluded. This would allow the protocol to temporarily halt new auctions, update the AuctionHouse, and then resume operations.
- Grant a special role or privilege that can override the normal operation in case of an emergency, allowing the AuctionHouse to be updated immediately if necessary.




