# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-badger/blob/f2f2e2cf9965a1020661d179af46cb49e993cb7e/packages/contracts/contracts/PriceFeed.sol#L98-L156


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The impact of this vulnerability is that the system may switch to using the fallback oracle with an outdated or stale price, leading to incorrect decisions and potential inaccuracies in subsequent operations.
## Proof of Concept
In the `fetchPrice` function, the code block responsible for comparing Chainlink's price change with the fallback oracle's price lacks a check for the freshness of the fallback response. This omission poses a risk of comparing the Chainlink's current price with an outdated fallback price, especially when the fallback response is frozen. Below is the relevant code snippet:
```solidity
if (_chainlinkPriceChangeAboveMax(chainlinkResponse, prevChainlinkResponse)) {
    // ... (other checks)

    // If Fallback is live but the oracles differ too much in price, conclude that Chainlink's initial price deviation was
    // an oracle failure. Switch to Fallback, and use Fallback price
    _changeStatus(Status.usingFallbackChainlinkUntrusted);
    return _storeFallbackPrice(fallbackResponse);
}
```
The vulnerability arises in the absence of a condition ensuring the freshness of the fallback response before comparing prices. If the fallback response is frozen or outdated, the system may make decisions based on inaccurate price information.
## Tools Used
Manual
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Include a freshness check for the fallback response before making the price comparison. This check should verify that the timestamp of the fallback response is recent and within an acceptable timeframe. By ensuring the freshness of the fallback oracle's response, the system can make informed comparisons and avoid using outdated prices. Below is a suggested addition to the code:
```solidity
// Additional check for freshness of the fallback response
if (_fallbackIsFrozen(fallbackResponse) || _responseTimeout(fallbackResponse.timestamp, fallbackCaller.fallbackTimeout())) {
    // If Fallback is frozen or outdated, take appropriate action (e.g., continue with Chainlink or switch to a different fallback)
    // ...
} else {
    // Proceed with the existing comparison logic
    if (_bothOraclesSimilarPrice(chainlinkResponse, fallbackResponse)) {
        return _storeChainlinkPrice(chainlinkResponse.answer);
    } else {
        _changeStatus(Status.usingFallbackChainlinkUntrusted);
        return _storeFallbackPrice(fallbackResponse);
    }
}
```


