# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The current implementation of the `AuctionDemo.sol` contract allow users to participate in the auction without confirming the approval of the token owner. This scenario may result in all bid funds being permanently locked in the contract.

The `claimAuction()` function is employed for refunding unsuccessful bids and transferring the NFT to the winner. However, if the NFT owner does not provide token approval to the auction contract or revokes the approval after the auction concludes, it can lead to all funds being trapped in the contract indefinitely.

## Proof of Concept

There are no checks in `participateToAuction()` to ensure the legitimacy of the NFT owner.

