# Vulnerability details

## Impact

User funds participating in the `AuctionDemo` can be permanently locked if the NFT holder wallet got compromised or he removed the approvals.

## Proof of Concept

#### Issue summary

The NFT holder can revoke approvals, locking all bidder funds. This is likely to happen if the NFT price soars during the auction or if a bidder's bid is insufficient for the auctioned tokenId.

Even if the NFT holder is trusted and can't turn malicious. Nonetheless, with multiple NFT holder's especially those with externally owned accounts (EOA), a compromised wallet can result in the theft of NFTs, leaving all auction participants' funds permanently locked.

> [!NOTE]  
> Though a low probability, the critical impact categorizes this as a valid Medium per C4 Severity Categorization: Assets not at direct risk, but the function of the protocol or its availability could be impacted, or leak value with a hypothetical attack path with stated assumptions, but external requirements.

#### Here is a coded PoC to demonstrate the issue:

```solidity
    function testRemoveApprovals() public {
        vm.prank(genAdminOwner);
        minterContract.mintAndAuction({
            _recipient: receiver,
            _tokenData: "",
            _saltfun_o: 0,
            _collectionID: 1,
            _auctionEndTime: block.timestamp + 1 days
        });
        console.log(
            "Is token auctioned :",
            minterContract.getAuctionStatus(10000000000)
        );

        vm.prank(receiver);
        nextGenCore.approve(address(auctionDemo), 10000000000);

        hoax(bidder1, 1e18);
        auctionDemo.participateToAuction{value: 1e18}(10000000000);

        console.log("First bid:", auctionDemo.returnHighestBid(10000000000));

        hoax(bidder2, 5e18);
        auctionDemo.participateToAuction{value: 5e18}(10000000000);

        console.log("Second bid:", auctionDemo.returnHighestBid(10000000000));

        hoax(bidder3, 10e18);
        auctionDemo.participateToAuction{value: 10e18}(10000000000);

        console.log("Third bid:", auctionDemo.returnHighestBid(10000000000));

        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 days);

        // Assume here owner wallet got compromised, and nft got stolen or he revoked the approval due to a price bump
        // Bidder's funds will be permanently locked

        vm.prank(receiver);
        nextGenCore.approve(address(0), 10000000000);

        vm.prank(bidder3);
        vm.expectRevert("ERC721: caller is not token owner or approved");
        auctionDemo.claimAuction(10000000000);
    }
```

#### Test result: 

```solidity
[PASS] testLockedFunds() (gas: 770592)
Test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 11.86ms
```

#### Test Setup:

- Clone the repository: https://github.com/0xbtk/NextGen-Setup.git
- Incorporate the tests in **`NextGenSecurityReview`**
- Execute: **`forge test --mt testLockedFunds -vvv`**

