# Vulnerability details

## Impact
" When stETH balance increases through LSD or some other reasons, the excess income is sold for EUSD, allocated to EUSD holders through rebase mechanism ". This is what protocol intent to do via ` excessIncomeDistribution() ` method in `LybraStETHDepositVault `. Extra Income is used to cover accumulated service Fee first. i.e from the extra income first service Fee will be covered.

`feeStored` is a state variable which increases every time internal method `_saveReport()` is called. A Attacker can use `mint` and `burn ` to increse feeStored. 

whenever `excessIncomeDistribution( stETHAmount)` [say first tx] tx goes into mempool , Attacker will see this tx and can use ` mint ` & `burn ` to increase `feeStored` to much higher value by giving high gas before first tx, such that `income=feeStored + _newFee()` present in `excessIncomeDistribution()` will always greater than `payAmount`.
Hence Extra money will always go as income. 


