#####  Exploit Scenario

Attacker has already collateral deposits in good number so he can mint good amount of eUSDs. As he saw the `excessIncomeDistribution` tx[say first tx] in mempool ,by paying much higher gas Fees he started minting and burning eUSD through `mint` and 'burn'. As `feeStored` is update by `feeStored + = _newFee()` also  `_newFee() ` is directly proportional to `poolTotalEUSDCirculation ` and timeInterwal{`block.timestamp-lastReportTime`}.

In this way Attcker manupulated feeStored before first tx and now in first tx `income > payAmount `. It will transform all the extra money into income.


Also only not from mempool, Attacker can always do this `mint` and `burn` all day to make `income > payAmount` during rebase mechanism via increasing feeStored in both tx{`mint`& `burn`}


