# Vulnerability details

# Inability to Claim Rewards due to Unsupported Oracle for `LBR` Token

This report addresses a vulnerability in the `EUSDMiningIncentives` contract, which prevents users from claiming their rewards. The issue arises due to the fact that Chainlink oracle does not support the `LBR` token. As a result, users are unable to withdraw their rewards using the `getReward()` function. 

*Thanks to obront, I found this issue when I was reviewing a report and found [this vulnerability](https://github.com/sherlock-audit/2023-02-blueberry-judging#issue-m-9-lp-tokens-cannot-be-valued-because-ichi-cannot-be-priced-by-oracle-causing-all-new-open-positions-to-revert).*



## Impact

In the `EUSDMiningIncentives` contract, in order to receive the rewards, `(stakedLBRLpValue(user) * 10000) / stakedOf(user) < 500` must be `true`. The calculation of `stakedLBRLpValue(user)` depends on the price of the `LBR` token. In order to get the price of the `LBR` token, the Chainlink oracle is used; however, Chainlink does not support `LBR` token. This leads to not being able to withdraw the reward using `getReward()` function, and the reward will be locked in the `EUSDMiningIncentives` contract.

## Proof of Concept

The `esLBR` reward token cannot be claimed because the `LBR` token cannot be priced by Chainlink. This issue arises in the `EUSDMiningIncentives` contract when calling the `getReward()` function:

[(EUSDMiningIncentives.sol#L192-L200)](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-lybra/blob/7b73ef2fbb542b569e182d9abf79be643ca883ee/contracts/lybra/miner/EUSDMiningIncentives.sol#L192-L200)

```solidity
function getReward() external updateReward(msg.sender) {
    require(!isOtherEarningsClaimable(msg.sender), "Insufficient DLP, unable to claim rewards");
    uint256 reward = rewards[msg.sender];
    if (reward > 0) {
        rewards[msg.sender] = 0;
        IesLBR(esLBR).mint(msg.sender, reward);
        emit ClaimReward(msg.sender, reward, block.timestamp);
    }
}
```

 In order to call this function, the `otherEarningsClaimable()` function must return `true`:

[(EUSDMiningIncentives.sol#L188-L190)](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-lybra/blob/7b73ef2fbb542b569e182d9abf79be643ca883ee/contracts/lybra/miner/EUSDMiningIncentives.sol#L188-L190)

```solidity
function isOtherEarningsClaimable(address user) public view returns (bool) {
    return (stakedLBRLpValue(user) * 10000) / stakedOf(user) < 500;
}
```

 However, this function relies on the `stakedLBRLpValue()` function, which requires the price of both the `LBR` and `ETH` tokens to be accessible by the Chainlink oracle:

[(EUSDMiningIncentives.sol#L149-L157)](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-lybra/blob/7b73ef2fbb542b569e182d9abf79be643ca883ee/contracts/lybra/miner/EUSDMiningIncentives.sol#L149-L157)

```solidity
function stakedLBRLpValue(address user) public view returns (uint256) {
    uint256 totalLp = IEUSD(ethlbrLpToken).totalSupply();
    (, int etherPrice, , , ) = etherPriceFeed.latestRoundData();
    (, int lbrPrice, , , ) = lbrPriceFeed.latestRoundData();
    uint256 etherInLp = (IEUSD(0xC02aaA39b223FE8D0A0e5C4F27eAD9083C756Cc2).balanceOf(ethlbrLpToken) * uint(etherPrice)) / 1e8;
    uint256 lbrInLp = (IEUSD(LBR).balanceOf(ethlbrLpToken) * uint(lbrPrice)) / 1e8;
    uint256 userStaked = IEUSD(ethlbrStakePool).balanceOf(user);
    return (userStaked * (lbrInLp + etherInLp)) / totalLp;
}
```

Since Chainlink does not support the `LBR` token, the function will fail, preventing users from claiming their rewards.



## Tools Used

Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

To mitigate this issue, an alternate form of oracle that can price the `LBR` token needs to be implemented. One possible solution is to use a Time-Weighted Average Price (TWAP) obtained from an Automated Market Maker (AMM) that supports the `LBR` token.


