# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-lybra/blob/5d70170f2c68dbd3f7b8c0c8fd6b0b2218784ea6/contracts/lybra/miner/EUSDMiningIncentives.sol#L152


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Users who have earned rewards will not be able to claim them due to a failure in fetching the price data from the Chainlink oracle.

## Proof of Concept


The [`stakedLBRlpValue`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-lybra/blob/5d70170f2c68dbd3f7b8c0c8fd6b0b2218784ea6/contracts/lybra/miner/EUSDMiningIncentives.sol#L152) function in the EUSDMiningIncentives contract tries to fetch the latest price data by making a call to Chainlink's lbrPriceFeed. However, as of the time of the contest there's Chainlink doesn't support [LBR](https://data.chain.link/).

```solidity
    function stakedLBRLpValue(address user) public view returns (uint256) {
        // The total supply of the ethlbrlptoken
        uint256 totalLp = IEUSD(ethlbrLpToken).totalSupply();

        (, int etherPrice, , , ) = etherPriceFeed.latestRoundData();
>        (, int lbrPrice, , , ) = lbrPriceFeed.latestRoundData();
```

However, taking a look at the contest description what type of Oracle does the project use - you can observe they confirm that it is indeed Chainlink's.
![](https://i.imgur.com/iabEou3.png)


As the lbrPriceFeed does not support LBR, this function will fail. This failure becomes apparent when users attempt to claim their rewards through the [`getReward`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-lybra/blob/5d70170f2c68dbd3f7b8c0c8fd6b0b2218784ea6/contracts/lybra/miner/EUSDMiningIncentives.sol#L192) function. 

The `getReward` function is meant to allow users to claim the rewards they have accrued.

```solidity
   function getReward() external updateReward(msg.sender) {
        require(!isOtherEarningsClaimable(msg.sender), "Insufficient DLP, unable to claim rewards");
        uint256 reward = rewards[msg.sender];
        if (reward > 0) {
            rewards[msg.sender] = 0;
            IesLBR(esLBR).mint(msg.sender, reward);
            emit ClaimReward(msg.sender, reward, block.timestamp);
        }
    }
```

However, due to the aforementioned failure in the `stakedLBRLpValue` function, this function will revert and the users won’t be able to claim their rewards. Importantly, this failure doesn't stop the reward accrual, but prevents the actual claiming of those rewards.

## Tools Used

Manual Review


## Recommended Mitigation Steps

There will need to be an alternate form of oracle that can price the LBR token. The best way to accomplish this is likely to use a TWAP of the price on an AMM.


