# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The option price become too cheap when it is near the end of an epoch.
There will be few participants to deposit WETH to VaultLP because it is not profitable relative to the risk.

## Proof of Concept
An option can be settled regardless of when it is purchased. In other words, it has no expiry.
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-dopex/blob/main/contracts/perp-vault/PerpetualAtlanticVault.sol#L333
However, a price of an option depends on how many days left until the expiry in decimal 2. One day is denoted as 100.
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-dopex/blob/main/contracts/libraries/OptionPricingSimple.sol#L66-L92

Add the code below in `tests/perp-vault/POC.sol` and run `forge test --mt test_buyOption_Cheap`.
I used `volatilityCap` and  `minOptionPricePercentage` as 1000 and 1 respectively.
The value is taken from the live contract.
https://arbiscan.io/address/0x2b99e3d67dad973c1b9747da742b7e26c8bdd67b#code
