# Vulnerability details

## Impact
`UniV3LiquidityAMO#execute()` acts as a generic proxy in the system, which is restricted to `DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE`. The logic is to do an arbitrary external call, which allows admin to steal all NFT positions in just 1 transaction because UniV3 NonfungiblePositionManager supports multicall. Or admin could just set approve for all to an malicious address through `execute()` function

