# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The rounding bug in the OracleLibrary.consult function has a significant impact on applications that rely on this function for price calculations, especially those involving asset swaps, collateral valuation, or other financial transactions. The bug causes the function to round the result down to the nearest tick, which may result in unintended and unfavorable pricing for users. The impact of this bug can be substantial for applications that depend on precise pricing and may lead to users paying more than expected.

## Proof of Concept


  function read() external view returns (uint256 _result) {
    // This call may revert with 'OLD!' if the pool doesn't have enough cardinality or initialized history
    (int24 _arithmeticMeanTick,) = OracleLibrary.consult(camelotPair, quotePeriod);
    uint256 _quoteAmount = OracleLibrary.getQuoteAtTick({
      tick: _arithmeticMeanTick,
      baseAmount: baseAmount,
      baseToken: baseToken,
      quoteToken: quoteToken
    });
    _result = _parseResult(_quoteAmount);
  }

