# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-wildcat/blob/c5df665f0bc2ca5df6f06938d66494b11e7bdada/src/WildcatSanctionsSentinel.sol#L114


# Vulnerability details

An escrow contract is created when a account address is detected to be sanctioned.

On escrow creation the offending account should be blocked from Chainalysis oracle **and** also by the borrower which is using the mapping `sanctionOverrides`. But because of a type mistake is only blocked by the Chainalysis oracle part. 

## Impact

The borrower misses the chance to block the sanctioned address.


## Proof of Concept

A blocked account is defined by the check inside the function `isSanctioned` :

```solidity
 function isSanctioned(address borrower, address account) public view override returns (bool) {
    return
      !sanctionOverrides[borrower][account] && // is blocked by the borrower ?
      IChainalysisSanctionsList(chainalysisSanctionsList).isSanctioned(account); // blocked by Chainalysis oracle 
  }
```

When a sanctioned address is detected a escrow contract is created and the borrower instead of blocking the offending account it blocks the newly created escrow contract address:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-wildcat/blob/c5df665f0bc2ca5df6f06938d66494b11e7bdada/src/WildcatSanctionsSentinel.sol#L114

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Instead of blocking the created escrow contract block the sanctioned account:

```diff
  function createEscrow(
    address borrower,
    address account,
    address asset
  ) public override returns (address escrowContract) {
    if (!IWildcatArchController(archController).isRegisteredMarket(msg.sender)) {
      revert NotRegisteredMarket();
    }


    escrowContract = getEscrowAddress(borrower, account, asset);


    if (escrowContract.codehash != bytes32(0)) return escrowContract;


    tmpEscrowParams = TmpEscrowParams(borrower, account, asset);


    new WildcatSanctionsEscrow{ salt: keccak256(abi.encode(borrower, account, asset)) }();


    emit NewSanctionsEscrow(borrower, account, asset);


-    sanctionOverrides[borrower][escrowContract] = true;
+    sanctionOverrides[borrower][account] = true;


    emit SanctionOverride(borrower, escrowContract);


    _resetTmpEscrowParams();
  }
}
```


