## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Users being able to mint low token amounts can inflate the rsETH price, specially on a pool initial state. The safest option would be to introduce a lower bound on the amount of rsETH that can be minted, in a way that ensures rsETH is not inflated. 
A party holding 1e0 rsETH is problematic, but not very reallistic for the average end user so a lower limit of 1e12 rsETH is still a very small amount that does not pose the risk of diluting one's deposits.


