# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The token(asset) balance of LRTDepositPool is increased before the minting rseth to the depositor due to which price of rseth increases which decreases the amount of rseth minted to the depositor.

## Proof of Concept
As talked with the sponsers if a user wants to mint rseth he can see how much rseth he would get by depositing certain amount of asset(tokens) which the user gets by calling the getRsETHAmountToMint view function.
```
function getRsETHAmountToMint(
        address asset,
        uint256 amount
    )
        public
        view
        override
        returns (uint256 rsethAmountToMint)
    {
        // setup oracle contract
        address lrtOracleAddress = lrtConfig.getContract(LRTConstants.LRT_ORACLE);
        ILRTOracle lrtOracle = ILRTOracle(lrtOracleAddress);

        // calculate rseth amount to mint based on asset amount and asset exchange rate
        rsethAmountToMint = (amount * lrtOracle.getAssetPrice(asset)) / lrtOracle.getRSETHPrice();
    }
```
So let's assume the following values
lrtOracle.getAssetPrice(asset) = 20eth i.e 20*10^18
Amount of tokens he deposited i.e amount = 10
lrtOracle.getRSETHPrice() = 2eth = 2*10^18
So the rsethAmountToMint i.e the depositor should receive 100 rseth

But the main logic error occurs when the depositor calls the depositAsset function
```
function depositAsset(
        address asset,
        uint256 depositAmount
    )
        external
        whenNotPaused
        nonReentrant
        onlySupportedAsset(asset)
    {
        // checks
        if (depositAmount == 0) {
            revert InvalidAmount();
        }
        if (depositAmount > getAssetCurrentLimit(asset)) {
            revert MaximumDepositLimitReached();
        }

        if (!IERC20(asset).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), depositAmount)) {
            revert TokenTransferFailed();
        }

        // interactions
        uint256 rsethAmountMinted = _mintRsETH(asset, depositAmount);

        emit AssetDeposit(asset, depositAmount, rsethAmountMinted);
    }
```
I will explain it in step wise manner 
1. When user calls the deposit function it transfers the tokens = depositedAmount into the LRTDeposit pool contract( I am guessing this is done according to checks effects and interaction pattern)
```
if (!IERC20(asset).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), depositAmount)) {
            revert TokenTransferFailed();
        }
```
2.Then it calls the _mintRseth function
``` 
uint256 rsethAmountMinted = _mintRsETH(asset, depositAmount);
```
3._mintRsETh function is as follows
```
function _mintRsETH(address _asset, uint256 _amount) private returns (uint256 rsethAmountToMint) {
        (rsethAmountToMint) = getRsETHAmountToMint(_asset, _amount);

        address rsethToken = lrtConfig.rsETH();
        // mint rseth for user
        IRSETH(rsethToken).mint(msg.sender, rsethAmountToMint);
    }
```
As can be seen from above function it also calls the getRSETHAmountToMint to get the amount of rseth to mint 
So it might seem that the depositor would receive the same amount of rseth tokens as he first view by calling the getRSEThAmountToMint view function But the main error lies in how the rsethAmountToMint is calculated in the following way 
```
// calculate rseth amount to mint based on asset amount and asset exchange rate
        rsethAmountToMint = (amount * lrtOracle.getAssetPrice(asset)) / lrtOracle.getRSETHPrice();
```
The value of lrtOracle.getRSETHPrice() should remain same until new rseth have been minted but this value changes as the depositor transfers the tokens = depositedAmount before getting the minted amount.
Which increases the lrt.getRSETHPrice() and thus the depositor receives less rseth tokens.
How this happens is as follows we will look at the getRSETHPrice() function 
```
function getRSETHPrice() external view returns (uint256 rsETHPrice) {
        address rsETHTokenAddress = lrtConfig.rsETH();
        uint256 rsEthSupply = IRSETH(rsETHTokenAddress).totalSupply();

        if (rsEthSupply == 0) {
            return 1 ether;
        }

        uint256 totalETHInPool;
        address lrtDepositPoolAddr = lrtConfig.getContract(LRTConstants.LRT_DEPOSIT_POOL);

        address[] memory supportedAssets = lrtConfig.getSupportedAssetList();
        uint256 supportedAssetCount = supportedAssets.length;

        for (uint16 asset_idx; asset_idx < supportedAssetCount;) {
            address asset = supportedAssets[asset_idx];
            uint256 assetER = getAssetPrice(asset);

            uint256 totalAssetAmt = ILRTDepositPool(lrtDepositPoolAddr).getTotalAssetDeposits(asset);
            totalETHInPool += totalAssetAmt * assetER;

            unchecked {
                ++asset_idx;
            }
        }

        return totalETHInPool / rsEthSupply;
    }
```
So the price of rseth is essentially is calculated by totalETHInPool/reEthSupply
when totalAssetAmt and totalETHInpool is calculated as follows,it calculates the totalAMount of eth present in the pool by itterating over all the supported asset and then getting the amount by calling the getTotalAssetDeposits(asset) function in lrtdeposit pool
```
 uint256 totalAssetAmt = ILRTDepositPool(lrtDepositPoolAddr).getTotalAssetDeposits(asset);
            totalETHInPool += totalAssetAmt * assetER;
```
getTotalAssetDeposits function is as follows
```
function getTotalAssetDeposits(address asset) public view override returns (uint256 totalAssetDeposit) {
        (uint256 assetLyingInDepositPool, uint256 assetLyingInNDCs, uint256 assetStakedInEigenLayer) =
            getAssetDistributionData(asset);
        return (assetLyingInDepositPool + assetLyingInNDCs + assetStakedInEigenLayer);
    }
```
this calls getAssetDistributionData function to calculate the total amount of an asset present in deposit pool,in nodeDelegator and total asset staked in eigon layer
```
function getAssetDistributionData(address asset)
        public
        view
        override
        onlySupportedAsset(asset)
        returns (uint256 assetLyingInDepositPool, uint256 assetLyingInNDCs, uint256 assetStakedInEigenLayer)
    {
        // Question: is here the right place to have this? Could it be in LRTConfig?
        assetLyingInDepositPool = IERC20(asset).balanceOf(address(this));

        uint256 ndcsCount = nodeDelegatorQueue.length;
        for (uint256 i; i < ndcsCount;) {
            assetLyingInNDCs += IERC20(asset).balanceOf(nodeDelegatorQueue[i]);
            assetStakedInEigenLayer += INodeDelegator(nodeDelegatorQueue[i]).getAssetBalance(asset);
            unchecked {
                ++i;
            }
        }
    }
```
main error lies in the following loc
```
assetLyingInDepositPool = IERC20(asset).balanceOf(address(this))
```
the above line is used to calculate the assetlying in the deposit pool,so when depositor calls the depositasset function the value of IERC20(asset).balanceOf(address(this)) increases which increases the assetlying in deposit pool which increases the value returned by getTotalAssetDeposits function which is used by the getRSETHPrice function in order to calculate total asset amount and totaleth in pool thus increasing the price of rseth.

Now as the rseth price increases the value of 
rsethAmountToMint = (amount * lrtOracle.getAssetPrice(asset)) / lrtOracle.getRSETHPrice() comes out to be less than intended.

For example as taken initially
lrtOracle.getAssetPrice(asset) = 20eth i.e 20*10^18
Amount of tokens he deposited i.e amount = 10
intended lrtOracle.getRSETHPrice() = 2eth = 2*10^18 but the real comes out to be larger than this for example 3*10^18
So now the depositor would receive = 66 tokens which are less than 100 tokens 
SO there would be discrepancy between the amount displayed to the user when he calls the getRsETHAmountToMint function to see how much tokens he would receive than the amount he actually receive after depositing the tokens = deposited amount
