The depositedAsset state variable is utilized to store the current quantity of assets deposited in the contract. When calculating the price, this value is used instead of directly employing the balanceOf function.
```
    mapping(address => uint256) depositedAsset;
```
```
   function getAssetDistributionData(address asset)
        public
        view
        override
        onlySupportedAsset(asset)
        returns (uint256 assetLyingInDepositPool, uint256 assetLyingInNDCs, uint256 assetStakedInEigenLayer)
    {   ......
        assetLyingInDepositPool = depositedAsset[asset];
        ......
    }
```
Additionally, it is updated each time assets are deposited.
```
  function depositAsset(
        address asset,
        uint256 depositAmount
    )
        external
        whenNotPaused
        nonReentrant
        onlySupportedAsset(asset)
    {
        ......
        uint256 rsethAmountMinted = _mintRsETH(asset, depositAmount);
        depositedAsset[asset]+=depositAmount;
        ......
