# Vulnerability details

### Impact
Chainlink's `latestAnswer()` is used. It's deprecated and returns 0 if no answer has been reached.
ALso, there is no check in place for stale price or round completeness. This causes incorrect pricing. See [here](https://docs.chain.link/docs/historical-price-data/#historical-rounds) for more details.
This affects the amount of `rsETH` that is minted to a user upon deposit.
### Proof of Concept
User calls the `depositAsset` function in the `LTRDepositPool` contract, upon which the required amount of `reEth` tokens to mint are calculated.
```
    function depositAsset(
      ...
        // interactions
        uint256 rsethAmountMinted = _mintRsETH(asset, depositAmount); 
  }
```
```
    function _mintRsETH(address _asset, uint256 _amount) private returns (uint256 rsethAmountToMint) {
        (rsethAmountToMint) = getRsETHAmountToMint(_asset, _amount); 
        ...
    }
```

The amount to mint is checked in the `getRsETHAmountToMint` function which makes a call to the `lrtoracle`.

```
    function getRsETHAmountToMint(
    ...
        // calculate rseth amount to mint based on asset amount and asset exchange rate
        rsethAmountToMint = (amount * lrtOracle.getAssetPrice(asset)) / lrtOracle.getRSETHPrice();
    }

```
The `ltrOracle` consults ChainLink's `getAssetPrice` which fetches the "current" price from the AggregatorInterface

```
 function getAssetPrice(address asset) public view onlySupportedAsset(asset) returns (uint256) {
        return IPriceFetcher(assetPriceOracle[asset]).getAssetPrice(asset);
    }
```
```
    function getAssetPrice(address asset) external view onlySupportedAsset(asset) returns (uint256) {
        return AggregatorInterface(assetPriceFeed[asset]).latestAnswer();
    }
```
The price is fetched using the deprecated `latestAnswer` API, which returns 0 if there's no answer. There's also no check for the freshness of the returned price, which can lead to old prices being returned. 
Depending on the case, the user might get minted more or less or 0 `rsETH` tokens for their deposit. 

### Tools Used
Manual code review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Switch to `.latestRoundData()` and implement the needed checks.
```
(uint80 roundID, int256 price, , uint256 timeStamp, uint80 answeredInRound) = priceOracle.latestRoundData();
require(answeredInRound >= roundID, "...");
require(timeStamp != 0, "...");
```



