# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The utilization of `latestAnswer()` in price feeds exposes the protocol to scenarios where the asset value calculation is incorrect, leading to the possible minting of an inaccurate amount of rsETH, the receipt token upon depositing. In the most severe case, if the price is zero, depositors could receive no compensation for their deposited assets.

## Proof of Concept
The method `ChainlinkPriceOracle.getAssetPrice()` relies on the `latestAnswer()` function of the Chainlink price oracle, which, as stated by the comments on the Chainlink contract, is deprecated and should not be used without precautions. This method is invoked by `LRTOracle.getAssetPrice()` and directly affects the calculation of assets during deposits made through the `LRTDepositPool.depositAsset()` function.

https://etherscan.io/address/0x86392dC19c0b719886221c78AB11eb8Cf5c52812#readContract#F8
> [deprecated] Use latestRoundData instead. This does not error if no answer has been reached, it will simply return 0. Either wait to point to an already answered Aggregator or use the recommended latestRoundData instead which includes better verification information. 

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
The recommendation is to upgrade the contract to leverage the `latestRoundData()` method from the Chainlink `AggregatorV3Interface`. This method provides a more comprehensive set of data, including timestamps and round IDs, allowing for additional checks to confirm the relevancy and completeness of the price data.

The specific steps include updating the interface, modifying related price-fetching methods to utilize the new interface, and implementing checks to revert transactions when stale price data is encountered.

https://github.com/smartcontractkit/chainlink/blob/master/contracts/src/v0.8/interfaces/AggregatorV3Interface.sol
```diff
    interface AggregatorInterface {
-       function latestAnswer() external view returns (uint256);

+       function latestRoundData()
+         external
+         view
+         returns (uint80 roundId, int256 answer, uint256 startedAt, uint256 updatedAt, uint80 answeredInRound);
    }

```

```diff
+   error StalePrice();
+   uint256 public constant MAX_DELAY = 1 hours; // tolerance in seconds

    /// @notice Fetches Asset/ETH exchange rate
    /// @param asset the asset for which exchange rate is required
    /// @return assetPrice exchange rate of asset
-   function getAssetPrice(address asset) external view onlySupportedAsset(asset) returns (uint256) {
+   function getAssetPrice(address asset) external view onlySupportedAsset(asset) returns (int256) {
-       return AggregatorInterface(assetPriceFeed[asset]).latestAnswer();

+       (, int256 answer, , uint256 updatedAt,) =
+           IPrice(_chainlinkFeed).latestRoundData();

+       if (updatedAt < block.timestamp - MAX_DELAY) revert StalePrice();

+       return answer;
    }
```


