# Vulnerability details

## Impact

A single mistake by an admin can significantly increase the RSETH price, causing losses for users who mint at that time.

## Proof of Concept

```solidity
function addNodeDelegatorContractToQueue(address[] calldata nodeDelegatorContracts) external onlyLRTAdmin {
        uint256 length = nodeDelegatorContracts.length;
        if (nodeDelegatorQueue.length + length > maxNodeDelegatorCount) {
            revert MaximumNodeDelegatorCountReached();
        }

        for (uint256 i; i < length;) {
            UtilLib.checkNonZeroAddress(nodeDelegatorContracts[i]);
            nodeDelegatorQueue.push(nodeDelegatorContracts[i]);
            emit NodeDelegatorAddedinQueue(nodeDelegatorContracts[i]);
            unchecked {
                ++i;
            }
        }
    }
```

addNodeDelegatorContractToQueue is a function to add NodeDelegators.

```solidity
function getAssetDistributionData(address asset)
        public
        view
        override
        onlySupportedAsset(asset)
        returns (uint256 assetLyingInDepositPool, uint256 assetLyingInNDCs, uint256 assetStakedInEigenLayer)
    {
        assetLyingInDepositPool = IERC20(asset).balanceOf(address(this));

        uint256 ndcsCount = nodeDelegatorQueue.length;
        for (uint256 i; i < ndcsCount;) {
            assetLyingInNDCs += IERC20(asset).balanceOf(nodeDelegatorQueue[i]);
            assetStakedInEigenLayer += INodeDelegator(nodeDelegatorQueue[i]).getAssetBalance(asset);
            unchecked {
                ++i;
            }
        }
    }
```

Added NodeDelegators are used in `getAssetDistributionData` to call `getAssetBalance.

This role is to fetch the quantity deposited in Eigenlayer through that particular NodeDelegator.

The retrieved values are used in `LRTOracle.getRSETHPrice` to calculate the price of RSETH.

```solidity
for (uint16 asset_idx; asset_idx < supportedAssetCount;) {
            address asset = supportedAssets[asset_idx];
            uint256 assetER = getAssetPrice(asset);

            uint256 totalAssetAmt = ILRTDepositPool(lrtDepositPoolAddr).getTotalAssetDeposits(asset);
            totalETHInPool += totalAssetAmt * assetER;

            unchecked {
                ++asset_idx;
            }
        }

        return totalETHInPool / rsEthSupply;
```

If the same NodeDelegator is added multiple times by mistake in `addNodeDelegatorContractToQueue`, the value of the deposited assets in `getRSETHPrice` will be measured much higher than actual, leading to an increase in RSETH price.

In this case, users who mint will end up minting RSETH at a higher price than its actual value.

What makes this a serious problem is that there is no logic to delete incorrectly added NodeDelegators, so you can't correct the problem.

## Tools Used

VS Code

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

A logic to check if a NodeDelegator is already registered is necessary in `addNodeDelegatorContractToQueue`.


