# Vulnerability details

## Impact

`getAssetPrice` may return a stale price, resulting in an incorrect RSETH price.

## Proof of Concept

```solidity
function getAssetPrice(address asset) external view onlySupportedAsset(asset) returns (uint256) {
        return AggregatorInterface(assetPriceFeed[asset]).latestAnswer();
    }
```

`ChainlinkPriceOracle.getAssetPrice` is using the deprecated `latestAnswer`.

Although this has been reported in a bot report, I believe it is valid to raise the issue due to the absence of a stale price check.

Since it uses `latestAnswer`, there's no way to verify if the price is stale.

Therefore, `latestRoundData` should be utilized to check the roundId.

