# Vulnerability details

## Impact
**`getAssetDistributionData()`** is designed to fetch the balances of an asset across three distinct contracts. However, it relies on the ERC20 **`balanceOf()`**, which may result in inaccuracies if funds are sent direct to the contracts unintentionally or intentionally. This could lead to an incorrect calculation of the **rsETH** price.
```Solidity
assetLyingInDepositPool = IERC20(asset).balanceOf(address(this));
```
```Solidity
 assetLyingInNDCs += IERC20(asset).balanceOf(nodeDelegatorQueue[i]);
```
## Proof of Concept
In **`LRTOracle.sol`**, **`getRSETHPrice()`** calculates the **rsETH** price using **`getAssetDistributionData()`** to obtain the TVL in the contracts for an sepcific asset.
```Solidity
uint256 totalAssetAmt = ILRTDepositPool(lrtDepositPoolAddr).getTotalAssetDeposits(asset);
totalETHInPool += totalAssetAmt * assetER;
```
Next, it computes the price of **rsETH** relative to the Total Value Locked (TVL) in the contracts (**totalETHInPool**), taking into account the total supply of **rsETH**.
```Solidity
return totalETHInPool / rsEthSupply; 
```
The issue arises when someone unintentionally or intentionally sends assets directly to the contracts, causing the **rsETH** price to be higher than reality. This occurs because the user who directly sends assets does not mint new **rsETH** and this results in a lower total supply of **rsETH** provocating a higher price. Furthermore, this issue is exacerbated by the fact that **totalETHInPool** is already incremented without a corresponding minting of new **rsETH** tokens.

## Tools Used
Manual review.
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
To calculate the **rsETH** price, employ a virtual balance (e.g., a mapping) updated when users invoke **`depositAsset()`**, instead of relying on ERC20 **`balanceOf()`**.
```diff
function depositAsset(
        address asset,
        uint256 depositAmount
    )
        external
        whenNotPaused
        nonReentrant
        onlySupportedAsset(asset)
    {
        // checks
        if (depositAmount == 0) {
            revert InvalidAmount();
        }
        if (depositAmount > getAssetCurrentLimit(asset)) {
            revert MaximumDepositLimitReached();
        }

        if (!IERC20(asset).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), depositAmount)) {
            revert TokenTransferFailed();
        }

        // interactions
+       virtualBalance[LRTDepositPoolAddress][asset] += depositAmount;
        uint256 rsethAmountMinted = _mintRsETH(asset, depositAmount);

        emit AssetDeposit(asset, depositAmount, rsethAmountMinted);
    }
```
This modification needs to be applied during the transfer of assets from **`LRTDepositPool.sol`** to **`NodeDelegator.sol`**, and similarly, when **`NodeDelegator.sol`** transfers assets to **`EigenLayer.sol`**, and vice versa.











