# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The most affected function of this is ```updateScores()``` where the function is external and anyone can call this if the length of users array passed is more, then the system will DOS leaving the contract in an undesirable state.

## Proof of Concept
The Prime.sol contract is using so many for loops which is a matter of concern for DOS because of maxGasLimit imposed by a transaction. 

To tackle this problem the protocol has initialized and set the MaxLoopLimit variable in MaxLoopsLimitHelper.sol at the time of Prime token deployment but they never make use of it leaving the protocol to potential DOS.

```js
