# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Users can steal funds in the contract to pay gas when interacting with InterchainTokenService.sol to deploy remote canonical tokens or custom token managers.

## Proof of Concept
When a user interacts with InterchainTokenService.sol through `deployRemoteCanonicalToken()` or `deployCustomTokenManager()` or `deployAndRegisterRemoteStandardizedToken()`, they need to pass `gasValue` as args to pay for gas. However, there is no check to ensure the user actually sends native tokens as `msg.value` to invoke the call in the first place.

```solidity
//InterchainTokenService.sol - deployRemoteCanonicalToken()
