# Lines of code

Claim function: https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-canto/blob/40edbe0c9558b478c84336aaad9b9626e5d99f34/canto_ambient/contracts/mixins/LiquidityMining.sol#L256-L290


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
If users claim the rewards of a pool before they have been set, they will lose these rewards.

## Proof of Concept
If rewards haven't been set for a pool, if a user claims his rewards the calculation will be like this:
 - __timeWeightedWeeklyPositionAmbLiquidity_[poolIdx][posKey][week] == X_
 - __ambRewardPerWeek_[poolIdx][week] == 0_
 - _overallTimeWeightedLiquidity == Y_
Calculation: (X * 0) / Y = 0
Moreover, this line will be executed: _ambLiquidityRewardsClaimed_[poolIdx][posKey][week] = true_

If afterwards the rewards for the pool are set, the user won't be able to claim his rewards, since the transaction will revert with "Already claimed". This will make the user lose his rewards forever.

Here I add a test with an example were a user claims rewards before they were set, and then cannot claim them. The test has comments in order to make it easier to follow the logic, even if most of it is copied from _test_canto/TestLiquidityMining.js_. I added a log in _LiquidityMining.sol_ _claimAmbientRewards()_ in order to see the _rewardsToSend_. The output will be also shown at the bottom.

	const { expect } = require("chai");
	const exp = require("constants");
	const { BigNumber } = require("ethers");
	var AbiCoder = require("@ethersproject/abi").AbiCoder;
