Invalid Validation

# Lines of code

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-bar-audit/blob/2286f80f928f41c8bc189d0657d74ba83286c668/contracts/markets/bigBang/BigBang.sol#L560-L637


# Vulnerability details

During a liquidation in BigBang, the liquidated collateral is removed and swapped to USDO YieldBox shares, with a portion of it paid to the liquidator and protocol as liquidation fees. 

However, the remaining USDO YieldBox shares are not withdrawn and are left with YieldBox as it is. That will prevent the protocol from collecting the balance using `refreshPenroseFees()`as it expects the balance to be in the asset form (e.g. USDO token) and not YieldBox shares.





## Detailed Explanation

The following code within `_liquidateUser()` will swap collateral for USDO, which remains within yieldBox.

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-bar-audit/blob/2286f80f928f41c8bc189d0657d74ba83286c668/contracts/markets/bigBang/BigBang.sol#L560-L637
```Solidity
    function _liquidateUser(
        ...
        ISwapper.SwapData memory swapData = swapper.buildSwapData(
            collateralId,
            assetId,
            0,
            collateralShare,
            true,
            true
        );
        swapper.swap(swapData, minAssetMount, address(this), "");
```

We can see from the following code that only a portion of the yieldBox shares are transfered to `penrose.FeeTo()` and the `msg.sender` (liquidator).

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-bar-audit/blob/2286f80f928f41c8bc189d0657d74ba83286c668/contracts/markets/bigBang/BigBang.sol#L639-L650
```Solidity
    function _extractLiquidationFees(
        uint256 returnedShare,
        uint256 borrowShare,
        uint256 callerReward
    ) private returns (uint256 feeShare, uint256 callerShare) {
        uint256 extraShare = returnedShare - borrowShare;
        feeShare = (extraShare * protocolFee) / FEE_PRECISION; // x% of profit goes to fee.
        callerShare = (extraShare * callerReward) / FEE_PRECISION; //  y%  of profit goes to caller.

        yieldBox.transfer(address(this), penrose.feeTo(), assetId, feeShare);
        yieldBox.transfer(address(this), msg.sender, assetId, callerShare);
    }
```

From the code below, note that Penrose will collect the fees in BigBang by depositing the asset (in token form) to the owner, which is Penrose (`msg.sender`). So leaving the balance in yieldBox shares will prevent the fee collection.

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-bar-audit/blob/2286f80f928f41c8bc189d0657d74ba83286c668/contracts/markets/bigBang/BigBang.sol#L442-L462
```Solidity
    function refreshPenroseFees(
        address
    ) external onlyOwner notPaused returns (uint256 feeShares) {
        uint256 balance = asset.balanceOf(address(this));
        totalFees += balance;
        feeShares = yieldBox.toShare(assetId, totalFees, false);

        if (totalFees > 0) {
            asset.approve(address(yieldBox), totalFees);

            yieldBox.depositAsset(
                assetId,
                address(this),
                msg.sender,
                totalFees,
                0
            );

            totalFees = 0;
        }
    }
```

## Impact
The remaining USDO YieldBox shares will be locked within YieldBox as there is no mechanism for BigBang to withdraw it. That means the protocol will lose the accumulated fees from the USDO borrowing and the liquidation penalties.


