# Vulnerability details

## Impact

aoTAP.brokerClaim() in AirdropBroker.sol and OptionBroker.sol can be frontrun in AirdropBroker.sol

## Proof of Concept

In TapiocaOptionBroker.sol and AirdropBroker.sol

there is a functoin that requires the OptionBroker.sol and AirdropBroker.sol to call  [oTAPBrokerClaim](https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tap-token-audit/blob/59749be5bc2286f0bdbf59d7ddc258ddafd49a9f/contracts/option-airdrop/AirdropBroker.sol#L297) to claim the broker role in oTAP.sol

```solidity
function brokerClaim() external {
	require(broker == address(0), "OTAP: only once");
	broker = msg.sender;
}
```

then the broker address can mint oTAP.sol option token

the problem is

before the broker address is set, anyone can call [brokerClaim()](https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tap-token-audit/blob/59749be5bc2286f0bdbf59d7ddc258ddafd49a9f/contracts/option-airdrop/aoTAP.sol#L139) and claim the broke role and mint option token

then when calling aoTAP.brokerClaim() in AirdropBroker.sol and OptionBroker.sol, the transaction will revert because the broker role is already claimed by other people

the POC proof that aoTAP.brokerClaim() would revert if the broker role is already claimed

