# Lines of code

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-yieldbox-strategies-audit/blob/master/contracts/aave/AaveStrategy.sol#L265


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
`lendingPool.withdraw()` in the AaveStrategy#`_withdraw()` would be reverted if the withdrawal amount (`toWithdraw`) from the Aave v2's LendingPool would be `0`.

Because the LendingPool#`withdraw()` of Aave v2 would revert when the withdrawal amount would be `0`.

According to the [diagram in the Overview of the README](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-07-tapioca#overview), the Yield generated via the strategy would be rebalanced in the YieldBox. So, if the AaveStrategy is selected as a strategy of the YieldBox and if the transaction would be reverted due to the reason above, the rebalance of YieldBox will also be reverted.

## Proof of Concept

Within the AaveStrategy#`_withdraw()`, the amount (`toWithdraw`) of the token (`wrappedNative`) would be withdrawn via the `lendingPool.withdraw()` of Aave v2 like this:
https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-yieldbox-strategies-audit/blob/master/contracts/aave/AaveStrategy.sol#L265
```solidity
    /// @dev burns aToken in exchange of Token and withdraws from AAVE LendingPool
    function _withdraw(
        address to,
        uint256 amount
    ) internal override nonReentrant {
        uint256 available = _currentBalance();
        require(available >= amount, "AaveStrategy: amount not valid");

        uint256 queued = wrappedNative.balanceOf(address(this));
        if (amount > queued) {
            compound("");

            uint256 toWithdraw = amount - queued;  /// @audit

            uint256 obtainedWrapped = lendingPool.withdraw(
                address(wrappedNative),
                toWithdraw, /// @audit
                address(this)
            );
            if (obtainedWrapped > toWithdraw) {
                amount += (obtainedWrapped - toWithdraw);
            }
        }

        wrappedNative.safeTransfer(to, amount);
        emit AmountWithdrawn(to, amount);
    }
```

According to the LendingPool of the Aave v2, the transaction would be reverted if the withdrawal `amount` would be `0`. Please see the following description:

As you can see, within the LendingPool#`withdraw()` of Aave v2, the ValidationLogic#`validateWithdraw()` would be called like this:
https://github.com/aave/protocol-v2/blob/master/contracts/protocol/lendingpool/LendingPool.sol#L159

Within the ValidationLogic#`validateWithdraw()`, the transaction would be reverted if the withdrawal `amount` would be `0` by the validation of `require(amount != 0, Errors.VL_INVALID_AMOUNT);` like this:
https://github.com/aave/protocol-v2/blob/master/contracts/protocol/libraries/logic/ValidationLogic.sol#L70
```solidity
  function validateWithdraw(
    address reserveAddress,
    uint256 amount,
    uint256 userBalance,
    mapping(address => DataTypes.ReserveData) storage reservesData,
    DataTypes.UserConfigurationMap storage userConfig,
    mapping(uint256 => address) storage reserves,
    uint256 reservesCount,
    address oracle
  ) external view {
    require(amount != 0, Errors.VL_INVALID_AMOUNT);  /// @audit
    ... 
```

So, the `lendingPool.withdraw()` in the AaveStrategy#`_withdraw()` would be reverted if the withdrawal amount (`toWithdraw`) from the Aave v2's LendingPool would be `0`

According to the [diagram in the Overview of the README](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-07-tapioca#overview), the Yield generated via the strategy would be rebalanced in the YieldBox. So, if the AaveStrategy is selected as a strategy of the YieldBox and if the transaction would be reverted due to the reason above, the rebalance of YieldBox will also be reverted.

