# Lines of code

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-periph-audit/blob/023751a4e987cf7c203ab25d3abba58f7344f213/contracts/oracle/modules/ModuleChainlinkMulti.sol#L49
https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-periph-audit/blob/023751a4e987cf7c203ab25d3abba58f7344f213/contracts/oracle/utils/ChainlinkUtils.sol#L51


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
ChainlinkMulti allows multiple feeds to be queried by a single contract. For each query, it verifies that the price data isn't stale. But, it only allows a single value to be defined as the max age of the data. Chainlink feeds can have different heartbeats. One can be updated every 3600 seconds while the other is only updated every 86400 seconds, see [Chainlink docs](https://docs.chain.link/data-feeds/price-feeds/addresses). If two feeds with different heartbeats are added to a ChainlinkMulti contract you're forced to use the bigger heartbeat. That means that the feed with the smaller heartbeat could provide stale data that the oracle accepts as valid.

## Proof of Concept
`stalePeriod` is a single value in ChainlinkMulti:

```sol
    constructor(
        address[] memory _circuitChainlink,
        uint8[] memory _circuitChainIsMultiplied,
        uint32 _stalePeriod,
        address[] memory guardians
    ) {
        // ...

        stalePeriod = _stalePeriod;
    }

```

`_readChainlinkFeed()` reverts if `block.timestamp - updatedAt > stalePeriod`:
```sol
    function _readChainlinkFeed(
        uint256 quoteAmount,
        AggregatorV3Interface feed,
        uint8 multiplied,
        uint256 decimals,
        uint256 castedRatio
    ) internal view returns (uint256, uint256) {
        if (castedRatio == 0) {
            (
                uint80 roundId,
                int256 ratio,
                ,
                uint256 updatedAt,
                uint80 answeredInRound
            ) = feed.latestRoundData();
            if (
                ratio <= 0 ||
                roundId > answeredInRound ||
                block.timestamp - updatedAt > stalePeriod
            ) revert InvalidChainlinkRate();
            castedRatio = uint256(ratio);
        }
```

## Tools Used
none

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Each feed should have its own value for `stalePeriod`.


