# Vulnerability details

## Impact

When `BigBang` market or `Singularity` is added to the `Penrose` using `Penrose::addBigBang`, `Penrose::addSingularity`, The `Penrose::executeMarketFn` on those markets will revert. As the result, no config can be updated and cannot be paused or unpaused.

## Proof of Concept

`Penrose` allows owners to deploy `BigBang` and `Singularity` markets and add using `Penrose::addBigBang`, `Penrose::addSingularity` functions.

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-bar-audit/blob/a4793e75a79060f8332927f97c6451362ae30201/contracts/Penrose.sol#L381-L389

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-bar-audit/blob/a4793e75a79060f8332927f97c6451362ae30201/contracts/Penrose.sol#L414-L421

However, these functions fail to update `masterContractOf`  mapping, which keeps track of the master contract of the deployed markets. The `masterContractOf` mapping is updated if the markets are deployed using `Penrose::registerBigBang` or `Penrose::registerSingularity`, since they are using `BoringFactory::deploy` function.

This `masterContractOf` was used in the `Penrose` to check whether the master contract of the deployed market is registered.

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-bar-audit/blob/a4793e75a79060f8332927f97c6451362ae30201/contracts/Penrose.sol#L438-L443

Even if the added market is using a registered master contract, the call `Penrose::executeMarketFn` will fail, due to the logic error in the `Penrose::addBigBang` and `Penrose::addSingularity`. This will render any onlyOwner function call to the market impossible.


The following is a proof of concept. It shows that a BigBang market is deployed using registered master contract and added using `addBigBang` function. However, the call `Penrose::executeMarketFn` on the added market reverts with `Penrose: MC not registered`.

To use the test, add it to the exsiting `penrose.test.ts` in the `tapioca-bar-audit` repo.

```javascript
      it('adds Bigbang but fails executeMarketFn PoCaddMarket', async () => {
            const {
                bar,
                wethBigBangMarket,
                weth,
                wethAssetId,
                usd0WethOracle,
                yieldBox,
                deployer,
                eoa1,
                mediumRiskBigBangMC,
            } = await loadFixture(register);
            const data = new ethers.utils.AbiCoder().encode(
                [
                    'address',
                    'address',
                    'uint256',
                    'address',
                    'uint256',
                    'uint256',
                    'uint256',
                    'uint256',
                    'uint256',
                ],
                [
                    bar.address,
                    weth.address,
                    wethAssetId,
                    usd0WethOracle.address,
                    ethers.utils.parseEther('1'),
                    0,
                    0,
                    0,
                    0,
                ],
            );

            const isMC = await bar.isBigBangMasterContractRegistered(mediumRiskBigBangMC.address);
            console.log(isMC);

            // deploy bigbang
            const myBigBang = await (await ethers.getContractFactory('BigBang')).deploy();
            await myBigBang.deployed();

            // add bigbang
            await bar.addBigBang(mediumRiskBigBangMC.address, myBigBang.address);
            const masterContractOfAdded = await bar.masterContractOf(myBigBang.address);
            console.log("master contract of newly added bigbang is", masterContractOfAdded);

            // cannot executeMarketFn on the added BigBang

            await expect(
                bar.executeMarketFn(
                    [myBigBang.address],
                    [ethers.utils.toUtf8Bytes('')],
                    true,
                ),
            ).to.be.revertedWith('Penrose: MC not registered');
      });
```

