# Lines of code

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-bar-audit/blob/2286f80f928f41c8bc189d0657d74ba83286c668/contracts/markets/bigBang/BigBang.sol#L698-L703


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The variable `totalCollateralShare` is not updated after a liquidation. The bad accounting can lead to the following scenarios:

- The `skim` feature will revert due to underflow.
- A user that uses the `skim` feature may loss his funds.

The same issue is also present in the Singularity markets (SGLLiquidation.sol) not only in BigBang.

## Proof of Concept

The function `_addTokens` looks as follows:

```solidity
function _addTokens(
        address from,
        uint256 _tokenId,
        uint256 share,
        uint256 total,
        bool skim
    ) internal {
        if (skim) {
            require(
                share <= yieldBox.balanceOf(address(this), _tokenId) - total,
                "BigBang: too much"
            );
        } else {
            yieldBox.transfer(from, address(this), _tokenId, share);
        }
}
```

When it is called on the context of the collateral, the `total` variable represents `totalCollateralShare`. Due to the erroneous accounting, the variable `totalCollateralShare` will be larger than it should be. Hence, the `skim` branch will revert due to underflow, or if the user makes the execution non-atomically, that means first sending the collateral and then calling, for example, `addCollateral`, his funds may get lost.

### Coded PoC

1.- Copy and paste the following test in `test/bigBang.test.ts` file under the test `describe('liquidate()')`:

