# Vulnerability details


## Impact

The ARBTriCryptoOracle and SGOracle contracts utilize chainlink's oracle functionality. However, it is important to note that there is currently no check in place to determine if the return value from chainlink indicates stale data. This can lead to inaccurate or outdated results if not handled properly.

Furthermore, it is crucial to address the fact that the chainlink latestAnswer function has already expired. To ensure up-to-date data, it is recommended to replace the usage of latestAnswer with the latestRoundData function.


```solidity
function _get() internal view returns (uint256 _maxPrice) {
    uint256 _vp = TRI_CRYPTO.get_virtual_price();

    // Get the prices from chainlink and add 10 decimals
    uint256 _btcPrice = uint256(BTC_FEED.latestAnswer()) * 1e10;
    uint256 _wbtcPrice = uint256(WBTC_FEED.latestAnswer()) * 1e10;
    uint256 _ethPrice = uint256(ETH_FEED.latestAnswer()) * 1e10;
    uint256 _usdtPrice = uint256(USDT_FEED.latestAnswer()) * 1e10;
```

and 

```solidity 
function _get() internal view returns (uint256 _maxPrice) {
    uint256 lpPrice = (SG_POOL.totalLiquidity() *
        uint256(UNDERLYING.latestAnswer())) / SG_POOL.totalSupply();

    return lpPrice;
}
```


This could lead to stale prices according to the [Chainlink documentation](https://docs.chain.link/data-feeds/historical-data).


