# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Protocol will not sense stale prices and will continue to work with old prices leading to economic impact for both protocol and investors.

## Proof of Concept
The oracle does not have a mechanism to track the stale prices and it will continue to report prices
even when there were no new updates.
```
function getPrice() public view whenNotPaused returns (uint256 price) { // @audit dos attack as range coud grow longer in some time
    uint256 length = ranges.length;
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < length; ++i) {
      Range storage range = ranges[(length - 1) - i];
      if (range.start <= block.timestamp) {
        if (range.end <= block.timestamp) {
          return derivePrice(range, range.end - 1);
        } else {
          return derivePrice(range, block.timestamp);
        }
      }
    }
  }
```

```
function derivePrice(
    Range memory currentRange,
    uint256 currentTime
  ) internal pure returns (uint256 price) {
    uint256 elapsedDays = (currentTime - currentRange.start) / DAY;
    return
      roundUpTo8(
        _rmul(
          _rpow(currentRange.dailyInterestRate, elapsedDays + 1, ONE),
          currentRange.prevRangeClosePrice
        )
      );
  }
```

## Tools Used
manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Implement a logic to track old prices. there should be threshold beyond which the admin/owner should be alerted to update the price. The current implementation assumes active participation by human to keep the prices upto date.


