This line may also be a problem due to precision errors if _shares is less than 10,000 and oracle.getPrice() returns a value 1e18 or less

```
  function getRUSDYByShares(uint256 _shares) public view returns (uint256) {
>   return (_shares * oracle.getPrice()) / (1e18 * BPS_DENOMINATOR);
  }
```

This would be a negligible issue since honestly the unrecovered amount is extremely little but will leave the issue open for the sponsor and judge to review.

