# Vulnerability details

## Impact

In `rUSDY.sol`, the number of shares (usdyAmount) is derived from the `getSharesByRUSDY()`. However, the calculations of shares depends on the price of usdy:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/main/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L388-392
```
return (_rUSDYAmount * 1e18 * BPS_DENOMINATOR) / oracle.getPrice();
```
As the price is in the denominator, the more it is, the less shares users are going to get. And, in the case of the huge usdy purchase (or sellout) that pushed the price a lot, such functions as `unwrap()`, `burn()` may transfer incorrect amount and even revert. 

## Proof of Concept

1) The first scenario: 

1. Let's say user has 100 shares and now the price of usdy is 1.05. And if he wants to `unwrap()` all of them, he puts 105 as the param:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/main/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L449-456
```
function unwrap(uint256 _rUSDYAmount) external whenNotPaused {
    require(_rUSDYAmount > 0, "rUSDY: can't unwrap zero rUSDY tokens");
    uint256 usdyAmount = getSharesByRUSDY(_rUSDYAmount);
    if (usdyAmount < BPS_DENOMINATOR) revert UnwrapTooSmall();
    _burnShares(msg.sender, usdyAmount);
    usdy.transfer(msg.sender, usdyAmount / BPS_DENOMINATOR);
    emit TokensBurnt(msg.sender, _rUSDYAmount);
```

The function then calls _burnShares and, inside of it, there is un update on the user's share balance:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/main/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L590
```
shares[_account] = accountShares - _sharesAmount;
```

However, if there is a sell order or buy order on the usdy in the same block, the user will get less shares (in the case of sellout) and therefore we'll have to pay the gas for another tx or (huge purchase) his tx will be reverted as the user may not have sufficient amount.

2) The second scenario:

In this case, admin calls `burn()` function and burns `rUSDY` from someone else's account. This has the same reasoning but now the admin tx may revert due to the unsufficient amount in the user's account if it's front-runned by the huge purchase:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/main/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L672-683
```
 function burn(
    address _account,
    uint256 _amount
  ) external onlyRole(BURNER_ROLE) {
    uint256 sharesAmount = getSharesByRUSDY(_amount);

    _burnShares(_account, sharesAmount);

    usdy.transfer(msg.sender, sharesAmount / BPS_DENOMINATOR);

    emit TokensBurnt(_account, _amount);
  }
```

## Tools Used

Manual review. 

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Change the logic of how the shares are calculated.


