# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The rUSDY contract heavily relies on the oracle price for vital functions like converting between USDY and rUSDY shares, and calculating supply and balance. Any disruptions to the getPrice function could critically compromise the entire contract's functionality.

The oracle price in the rUSDY contract facilitates the conversion between USDY amounts and rUSDY shares, and vice versa. This is evident from the functions:

- [rUSDy.getSharesByRUSDY](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L388-L392)
- [rUSDY.getRUSDYByShares](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L397-L399)

Both these functions dictate the number of shares to be [minted](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L436) or [burned](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L453) during the [wrap](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L434-L440) or [unwrap](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L449-L456) tokens.

Additionally, the oracle price is utilized in the calculations of:

- [rUSDY.totalSupply](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L216-L218)
- [rUSDY.balanceOf](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L226-L228)

Therefore, any malfunction in the getPrice function could severely disrupt the entire rUSDY contract.

<hr>

- **Impact**: High. If `getPrice` fails, the system cannot recover, and there is no way to reduce its size.
- **Likelihood**: Low. Because the `SETTER_ROLE` is trusted, and the low probability of numerous price modifications.

Considering the above, the risk is assessed as medium.

### Vulnerability Details

Solidity has a high cap for the maximum block gas limit. [source](https://ethereum.org/en/developers/docs/gas/#block-size)

> Each block targets 15 million gas. However, block sizes can adjust depending on network demand, reaching up to a limit of 30 million gas (twice the target size).

[RWADynamicOracle.setRange](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.sol#L151-L171) updates the price for the specified timestamp range, potentially causing an overflow in `ranges`.

Subsequently, the `ranges` array is used in [RWADynamicOracle.getPrice](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/47d34d6d4a5303af5f46e907ac2292e6a7745f6c/contracts/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.sol#L76) to determine the current price range, looping over every element.

```solidity
 function getPrice() public view whenNotPaused returns (uint256 price) {
    uint256 length = ranges.length;
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < length; ++i) {
      ...
    }
  }
```

Each new entry in the `ranges` array increases the `getPrice` cost by `588` gas, implying a limit of around 51,020 for `getPrice` ranges.

## Proof of Concept

Below is a simple test case that sets over `52,000` ranges and then attempts to retrieve the price. All operations to push ranges consume `3,815,995,473` gas units, thus the `block-gas-limit` is configured to `3,845,995,473`.

Insert the test case into [forge-tests/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.t.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/main/forge-tests/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.t.sol) and execute with the command: `yarn test-forge -vvv --mt test_max_ranges_limit --block-gas-limit 3845995473`.

```solidity
function test_max_ranges_limit() external {
  uint rangesToAdd = 51_020;

  setRangeFirst();

  uint256 lastRangeIndex = 0;
  uint256 lastRangeEnd = periodEnd;

  for (uint i; i < rangesToAdd; i++) {
    oracleUSDY.setRange(lastRangeEnd + 1 days, 1);

    lastRangeIndex++;
    lastRangeEnd += 1 days;
  }

  vm.expectRevert();
  oracleUSDY.getPrice();
}

```

## Tools Used

- Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Introduce a mechanism to delete entries from the `ranges` array, or reconsider the structure that maintains the range timestamps and prices.



