# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/b88271d64112234b7a7273cd7f3cea73c350e6a7/contracts/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.sol#L80-L81
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/b88271d64112234b7a7273cd7f3cea73c350e6a7/contracts/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.sol#L186
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/b88271d64112234b7a7273cd7f3cea73c350e6a7/forge-tests/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.t.sol#L219-L234


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The RWADynamicOracle will provide outdated prices and cause a loss of interest for rUSDY users in those gap days. It affects all the operations of the protocol that rely on the oracle.

## Proof of Concept

When getting the price from the RWADynamicOracle, it checks the current block timestamp against the range end of the current range. If the block timestamp is after the range end, then it will return the price at the range end minus one.

        if (range.end <= block.timestamp) {
          return derivePrice(range, range.end - 1);

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/b88271d64112234b7a7273cd7f3cea73c350e6a7/contracts/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.sol#L80-L81

Therefore, if there is a gap between the current range and the next range, the price will not correctly reflect the actual price since the interest from USDY is accumulating every day without skipping.

There are two cases that this can happen.
1. The range is not updated on time. 
=> However, this is not likely to happen since the range is updated in advance for 1 and 2 months.

2. There is a time gap between the ranges.
This can happen if the admin overrides the previous set range by calling `overrideRange`

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/b88271d64112234b7a7273cd7f3cea73c350e6a7/contracts/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.sol#L186

The function `overrideRange` only enforces that the range being overridden does not overlap with any other set ranges. However, it allows the range to be set with a gap between the previous range. This is an expected case in this test case where a mid range is shortened.

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/b88271d64112234b7a7273cd7f3cea73c350e6a7/forge-tests/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.t.sol#L219-L234

In those gap days, the rUSDY price will be stale and no interest will be accrued for users.

POC: Put into forge-tests/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.t.sol

```javascript
  function test_stale_price_overrideRange()
    public
    {
    setSeptRange();
    setOctRange();

    // Override the range index 1 to start 2 days after the Aug range periodEnd
    oracleUSDY.overrideRange(
        1,
        periodEnd + 2 days, // set to September 2, 2023 8:00:00 PM
        periodEnd + 29 days, // set to September 29, 2023 8:00:00 PM
        dailyIR,
        100 * 1e18
    );


    vm.warp(periodEnd);
    console.log('timestamp at August 31: ', block.timestamp); // August 31, 2023 8:00:00 PM
    (uint256 priceBefore, ) = oracleUSDY.getPriceData();
    console.log('price at August 31: ', priceBefore);

    vm.warp(periodEnd + 1 days);
    console.log('timestamp at September 1: ', block.timestamp); // September 1, 2023 8:00:00 PM
    (uint256 priceAfter, ) = oracleUSDY.getPriceData();
    console.log('price at September 1: ', priceAfter);

    // The September 1 is not fall in any range, therefore it will return the last price of the previous range (price at August 31, 2023 8:00:00 PM)
    // Price is stale, no interest is calculated for that day
    assertEq(priceBefore, priceAfter);
}
```

## Tools Used

Manual

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

When `overrideRange`, do not allow for a gap between ranges.


