# Vulnerability details

## Impact
There is no default return value for ```getPrice()``` functions. It means if there is no appropriate ```ranges```, the ```getPrice()``` function will return 0 (because the function has claimed that the return value is an ```uint``` and 0 is the default value of uint). This will makes customers very confused and causes the revert.  

The return value will also be divided in the ```getSharesByRUSDY``` function so it will also cause the divideBy0 issue which makes ```transfer``` failed.
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-ondo/blob/main/contracts/usdy/rUSDY.sol#L388-L391

```
  function getSharesByRUSDY(
    uint256 _rUSDYAmount
  ) public view returns (uint256) {
    return (_rUSDYAmount * 1e18 * BPS_DENOMINATOR) / oracle.getPrice();
  }
```

