# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Due to lack of enough validations, a stale price might be retrieved when the AggregatorV3Interface#`latestRoundData()` would be called via the ChainlinkOracle#`getChainlinkPrice()`.


## Proof of Concept
Within the ChainlinkOracle#`getChainlinkPrice()`, the price of a token would be retrieved from Chainlink Oracle and then the returned-value would be checked by some validations like this:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-07-moonwell/blob/main/src/core/Oracles/ChainlinkOracle.sol#L100-L103
```solidity
    /// @notice Get the price of a token from Chainlink
    /// @param feed The Chainlink feed to get the price of
    /// @return The price of the asset from Chainlink scaled by 1e18
    function getChainlinkPrice(
        AggregatorV3Interface feed
    ) internal view returns (uint256) {
        (, int256 answer, , uint256 updatedAt, ) = AggregatorV3Interface(feed)
            .latestRoundData();  /// @audit
        require(answer > 0, "Chainlink price cannot be lower than 0");  /// @audit
        require(updatedAt != 0, "Round is in incompleted state");  /// @audit

        // Chainlink USD-denominated feeds store answers at 8 decimals
        uint256 decimalDelta = uint256(18).sub(feed.decimals());
        // Ensure that we don't multiply the result by 0
        if (decimalDelta > 0) {
            return uint256(answer).mul(10 ** decimalDelta);
        } else {
            return uint256(answer);
        }
    }
```

However, Within the ChainlinkOracle#`getChainlinkPrice()`, there is not enough validations that lead to retrieving a stale price via the AggregatorV3Interface#`latestRoundData()` like this:
- There is only check whether or not the `updatedAt` would be `0`. If the `updatedAt` would be more than `0`, this validation can be passed.
- There is no validation for `timestamp`. This is problematic. Because even if the `timestamp`, which is one of the returned-value from the AggregatorV3Interface#`latestRoundData()`, would be `0`, it would not be validated and the process can be proceeded.

Due to lack of enough validations above, a stale price might be retrieved when the AggregatorV3Interface#`latestRoundData()` would be called via the ChainlinkOracle#`getChainlinkPrice()`



