# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-07-moonwell/blob/main/src/core/Oracles/ChainlinkCompositeOracle.sol#L189


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The Chainlink feed's `latestRoundData` needs a staleness check. If there is a problem with Chainlink starting a new round and finding consensus on the new value for the oracle (e.g. Chainlink nodes abandon the oracle, chain congestion, vulnerability/attacks on the chainlink system) other contracts using ChainlinkCompositeOracle will continue using outdated values.

Furthermore, there is no check on the `updatedAt` value coming from the feed, which can be 0 if the round is in an incomplete state. This check is present in the [ChainlinkOracle](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-07-moonwell/blob/main/src/core/Oracles/ChainlinkOracle.sol#L103) contract but not here.

## References
- https://solodit.xyz/issues/m-05-chainlinks-latestrounddata-might-return-stale-or-incorrect-results-code4rena-mochi-mochi-contest-git
- https://0xmacro.com/blog/how-to-consume-chainlink-price-feeds-safely/

## Tools Used
Manual review.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
We should do the following additional checks:
```
require(updatedAt != 0, "Round is in incompleted state");
require(answeredInRound >= roundId, "Stale price");
if (block.timestamp - updatedAt > TIMEOUT) {
    // stale price, either revert or use secondary oracle
    // ...
} else {
    continue;
}
```
Notice that the check on `answeredInRound` is deprecated and it will be equal to `roundId`. But some legacy feeds might still require it.


