# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The `PositionManager.getPoolAddresses` function is used to get the important address details of the `RoePool` to be used in the critical function executions of the `OptionsPositionManager` contract such as `executeBuyOptions`, `executeLiquidation`, `withdrawOptionAssets` etc ... 

But the issue is that `deprecated` markets can be used in the above function executions since the `RoePool.isDeprecated` parameter is ignored in the `getPoolAddresses` function as shown below:

    (address lpap, address _token0, address _token1, address r, ) = ROEROUTER.pools(poolId);

Hence as it is seen above the `isDeprecated` value is not retrieved via the `ROEROUTER.pools(poolId)`. Hence even if the pool is deprecated by the `owner` of the `RoeRouter` contract, the pool will still be used in the execution of the critical functions of the `OptionsPositionManager` contract.

## Proof of Concept

