# Vulnerability details

## Impact
When rebalance happens, the tokens will first be removed from the ticks and then redistribute based on the price movement. However, attacker can prevent or manipulate this re-distribution from some tick by flash loan the TokenisableRange inside lendingPool to prevent vault from withdrawing from certain ticks.

## Proof of Concept

When `rebalance` is triggered, first it will try to call `removeFromAllTicks` :

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-goodentry/blob/main/contracts/GeVault.sol#L202-L206

```solidity
  function rebalance() public {
    require(poolMatchesOracle(), "GEV: Oracle Error");
    removeFromAllTicks();
    if (isEnabled) deployAssets();
  }
```

Inside `removeFromAllTicks`, it will try to iterate trough all registered ticks and withdraw the `TokenisableRange` token balance of this vault from lending pool and then call `TokenisableRange`'s withdraw to get the underlying token0 and token1.

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-goodentry/blob/main/contracts/GeVault.sol#L313-L317

```solidity
  function removeFromAllTicks() internal {
    for (uint k = 0; k < ticks.length; k++){
      removeFromTick(k);
    }    
  }
```
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-goodentry/blob/main/contracts/GeVault.sol#L321-L333

```solidity
  function removeFromTick(uint index) internal {
    TokenisableRange tr = ticks[index];
    address aTokenAddress = lendingPool.getReserveData(address(tr)).aTokenAddress;
    uint aBal = ERC20(aTokenAddress).balanceOf(address(this));
    uint sBal = tr.balanceOf(aTokenAddress);

    // if there are less tokens available than the balance (because of outstanding debt), withdraw what's available
    if (aBal > sBal) aBal = sBal;
    if (aBal > 0){
      lendingPool.withdraw(address(tr), aBal, address(this));
      tr.withdraw(aBal, 0, 0);
    }
  }
```

Notice that the amount of withdrawn asset is not only determined by aToken balance of this vault but also the available tr token of aTokenAddress. Attacker can trigger a flash loan of all available tr from some ticks before the rebalance to prevent some ticks to be withdrawn.

After that the `deployAssets` will be performed to redistribute tokens to ticks to finish the rebalance process.

Now the vault forced to hold the bad price ticks and attacker can perform deposit/withdraw to get profit.

## Tools Used

Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider to prevent this by checking the diff of `aBal` and `sBal` inside `removeTick` operation, when the difference is too high, consider to revert the operation.





