# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-goodentry/blob/71c0c0eca8af957202ccdbf5ce2f2a514ffe2e24/contracts/PositionManager/PositionManager.sol#L63-L73


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
RoeRouter allows owner to deprecate poolId record. It means that pool record contains wrong parameters, for example different router should be used.
However this field `isDeprecated` is never checked in PositionManager.sol.
As a result OptionsPositionManager.sol will use deprecated data.

## Proof of Concept
PositionManager fetches record by poolId from RoeRouter. And it doesn't check last parameter `isDeprecated`:
```solidity
  function getPoolAddresses(uint poolId) 
    internal view 
    returns( ILendingPool lp, IPriceOracle oracle, IUniswapV2Router01 router, address token0, address token1) 
  {
@>  (address lpap, address _token0, address _token1, address r, ) = ROEROUTER.pools(poolId);
    token0 = _token0;
    token1 = _token1;
    lp = ILendingPool(ILendingPoolAddressesProvider(lpap).getLendingPool());
    oracle = IPriceOracle(ILendingPoolAddressesProvider(lpap).getPriceOracle());
    router = IUniswapV2Router01(r);
  }
```
However record can be deprecated by RoeRouter owner:
```solidity
  /// @notice Deprecate a pool
  /// @param poolId pool ID
  /// @dev isDeprecated is a statement about the pool record, and does not imply anything about the pool itself
  function deprecatePool(uint poolId) public onlyOwner {
    pools[poolId].isDeprecated = true;
    emit DeprecatePool(poolId);
  }
```

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Revert if pool record is deprecated


