# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Pool can be deprecated by the ROERouter owner. If the pool is marked as deprecated, then pool should not participate in transactions which is not the case here.



## Proof of Concept
The ROERouter owner marks the pool as deprecated. The transactions are initiated on the OptionPositionManager, the pool information is read through ROERouter before the transaction can be performed.

If the pool was marked as deprecated, then transaction should revert. It is not the case in the current implementation.

Example:
In the below function, the pool information is retrieved but the isDeprecated is ignored.  

