...

The same is the case with other functions 

function executeLiquidation()
function withdrawOptionAssets()
function buyOptions()
function liquidate()
function close()
function closeDebt()

Also, Deprecating the pool needs to have additional logic to release the funds in the pool before deprecating. 

So, it is not clear as to what is the intention of deprecating the pool. 

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
a) To prevent any activity on the pool that is deprecated, the getPoolAddresses can be revised as below.

```
 function getPoolAddresses(uint poolId) 
    internal view 
    returns( ILendingPool lp, IPriceOracle oracle, IUniswapV2Router01 router, address token0, address token1) 
  {
    (address lpap, address _token0, address _token1, address r, bool isDeprecated ) = ROEROUTER.pools(poolId);

     // @audit     
     require(!isDeprecated,"Pool is deprecated");

    token0 = _token0;
    token1 = _token1;
    lp = ILendingPool(ILendingPoolAddressesProvider(lpap).getLendingPool());
    oracle = IPriceOracle(ILendingPoolAddressesProvider(lpap).getPriceOracle());
    router = IUniswapV2Router01(r);
  }
```
The circumstances under which the pool is being deprecated needed to be defined and those should be met before the pool can be deprecated.




