# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-05-maia/blob/54a45beb1428d85999da3f721f923cbf36ee3d35/src/ulysses-omnichain/BranchBridgeAgent.sol#L1032
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-05-maia/blob/54a45beb1428d85999da3f721f923cbf36ee3d35/src/ulysses-omnichain/BranchBridgeAgent.sol#L1066


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Using `tx.gasPrice` to calculate the gas cost is not credible, because `tx.gasPrice` can be manipulated at will. By setting `tx.gasPrice` to minimum, the gas cost is minimum, which leads to the protocol being unable to pay out.  

## Proof of Concept

When a user interacts with `BranchBridgeAgent`, maia checks `requiresFallbackGas`, and when it passes, maia calls `anyCall` 
to forward cross-chain messages, which integrates multichain and relies on the middleware `AnycallExecutor`. When the message is executed on `RootBridgeAgent`, the gas cost is calculated through `tx.gasPrice`.  
The problem is that `tx.gasPrice` is controllable. Through private miner pools such as flashbot or bloXroute, `tx.gasPrice` can be set to the lowest: baseFee(EIP-1559) on Ethereum, 0 on BSC. 
```solidity
    function _performCall(bytes memory _calldata) internal virtual {
        //Sends message to AnycallProxy
        IAnycallProxy(localAnyCallAddress).anyCall(
            rootBridgeAgentAddress, _calldata, rootChainId, AnycallFlags.FLAG_ALLOW_FALLBACK, ""
        );
    }

    function _performCall(bytes memory _calldata, uint256 _toChain) internal {
        address callee = getBranchBridgeAgent[_toChain];

        if (callee == address(0)) revert UnrecognizedBridgeAgent();

        if (_toChain != localChainId) {
            //Sends message to AnycallProxy
            IAnycallProxy(localAnyCallAddress).anyCall(
                callee, _calldata, _toChain, AnycallFlags.FLAG_ALLOW_FALLBACK_DST, ""
            );
        } else {
            //Execute locally
            IBranchBridgeAgent(callee).anyExecute(_calldata);
        }
    }
```
There are two different multichain's gas fee payment methods according to the code:
- pay gas fee on the source chain(BranchBridgeAgent)
- pay gas fee on the target chain(RootBridgeAgent)

This corresponds to two types of attack:
- BranchBridgeAgent -> RootBridgeAgent. Malicious users can send 0 `tx.gasPrice` and 0 `msg.value` messages to bypass the `requiresFallbackGas` check and invoke `anyCall` on BranchBridgeAgent to perform cross-chain messages for free.
- RootBridgeAgent -> BranchBridgeAgent. Malicious users can send 0 `tx.gasPrice` and 0 `msg.value` messages to bypass the `requiresFallbackGas` and invoke `anyCall` on RootBridgeAgent. Multichain's SMPC network relay messages are executed on the target chain. If the user colludes with SMPC network executor node, or node could simply publish transactions through a private pool, taking into privacy, atomization, and other factors, when execute messages on BranchBridgeAgent, the fee can be reduced to minimum, or even zero.

