# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The function being called may revert, which will be indicated by the return value to call()/delegatecall(). If the return value is not checked, the code will continue on as if there was no error, rather than reverting with the error encountered. This is especially dangerous in a multicall, where the behavior of different calls may depend on the order of the calls being made.

