To illustrate how this vulnerability can be exploited, let's consider John a hacker attempting to execute the addAndReturnProjectivePoint function using the inputs (0, 0, 0, 0). In this scenario, the inverseMod function will be invoked with the parameter m set to 0, which may lead to a division-by-zero error.

