# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Detailed description of the impact of this finding.

An attacker could take advantage of the unbounded array parameter in both ``` proveAndClaim ``` and ```proveAndClaimWithResolver``` functions to prevent others from making successful claims. Imagine a scenario where attacker passes too many ```DNSSEC.RRSetWithSignature[]``` struct arrays into the function so that it consumes so much gas and exceeds the block gas limit of a block due to its complex computational requirements that run through the ```_claim``` function  to the ```verifyRRSet``` function in the DNS oracle contract (DNSSECImpl.sol) down to other internal function calls like ```verifyDSHash```. In a case like this, the gas cost of operations could eventually exceeds gas limit that it blocks the operations and subsequent ones from happening at all. Even in absence of an attacker, transaction will revert (according to the code logic) the moment one of the inputs fails - meaning the loop will never complete and could result into the above stated situation if the caller keeps trying again.

DNSRegistar.sol
