# Vulnerability details

## Impact

    * @param name The name to claim, in DNS wire format. 

above format is used in `DNSRegistrar.proveAndClaim()` and `DNSRegistrar.proveAndClaimWithResolver()` functions

    * @param name The name of the RRSIG record, in DNS label-sequence format.

above format is used in `DNSSECImpl.verifySignature()` function.

As per the above two comments, the `name` provided by the user for claim is given in the `DNS wire format` in `DNSRegistrar.proveAndClaim()` and `DNSRegistrar.proveAndClaimWithResolver()` functions.

And the name decoded via the `RRSet` is given in the `DNS label-sequence format` in `DNSSECImpl.verifySignature()` function. 

Due to the use of different encoding schemes used for `length bytes` in the byte representation of domain name, with `DNS wire format` and `DNS label-sequence format`, trying to cross check the `domain name` provided by the user against the `domain name` retrieved via `RRSet` could lead to unexpected failure due to bytes array mismatch of respective domain names. 

## Proof of Concept

Following function uses the `DNS wire format` for the `domain name`.

    function proveAndClaim(
        bytes memory name,
        DNSSEC.RRSetWithSignature[] memory input
    ) public override {
        (bytes32 rootNode, bytes32 labelHash, address addr) = _claim(
            name,
            input
        );
        ens.setSubnodeOwner(rootNode, labelHash, addr);
    }

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-ens/blob/main/contracts/dnsregistrar/DNSRegistrar.sol#L91

Following function uses the `DNS label-sequence format` for the `domain name`.

    function verifySignature(
        bytes memory name,
        RRUtils.SignedSet memory rrset,
        RRSetWithSignature memory data,
        bytes memory proof
    ) internal view {
        // o  The RRSIG RR's Signer's Name field MUST be the name of the zone
        //    that contains the RRset.
        if (!name.isSubdomainOf(rrset.signerName)) {
            revert InvalidSignerName(name, rrset.signerName);
        }

        RRUtils.RRIterator memory proofRR = proof.iterateRRs(0);
        // Check the proof
        if (proofRR.dnstype == DNSTYPE_DS) {
            verifyWithDS(rrset, data, proofRR);
        } else if (proofRR.dnstype == DNSTYPE_DNSKEY) {
            verifyWithKnownKey(rrset, data, proofRR);
        } else {
            revert InvalidProofType(proofRR.dnstype);
        }
    }

