# Vulnerability details

## Impact
There is a redundant length check in the `compare` function of the `BytesUtils` library. The length check is performed twice, once at the beginning of the function and again later in the code. This redundancy does not affect the behavior of the function but can cause unnecessary gas consumption and increase the size of the compiled code.

## Proof of Concept
The vulnerable code block in the `BytesUtils` library: [#L52-L100](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-ens/blob/45ea10bacb2a398e14d711fe28d1738271cd7640/contracts/dnssec-oracle/BytesUtils.sol#L52-L100)
```solidity
    function compare(
        bytes memory self,
        uint256 offset,
        uint256 len,
        bytes memory other,
        uint256 otheroffset,
        uint256 otherlen
    ) internal pure returns (int256) {
        if (offset + len > self.length) {
            revert OffsetOutOfBoundsError(offset + len, self.length);
        }
        if (otheroffset + otherlen > other.length) {
            revert OffsetOutOfBoundsError(otheroffset + otherlen, other.length);
        }


        uint256 shortest = len;
        if (otherlen < len) shortest = otherlen;


        uint256 selfptr;
        uint256 otherptr;


        assembly {
            selfptr := add(self, add(offset, 32))
            otherptr := add(other, add(otheroffset, 32))
        }
        for (uint256 idx = 0; idx < shortest; idx += 32) {
            uint256 a;
            uint256 b;
            assembly {
                a := mload(selfptr)
                b := mload(otherptr)
            }
            if (a != b) {
                // Mask out irrelevant bytes and check again
                uint256 mask;
                if (shortest - idx >= 32) {
                    mask = type(uint256).max;
                } else {
                    mask = ~(2 ** (8 * (idx + 32 - shortest)) - 1);
                }
                int256 diff = int256(a & mask) - int256(b & mask);
                if (diff != 0) return diff;
            }
            selfptr += 32;
            otherptr += 32;
        }


        return int256(len) - int256(otherlen);
    }
```
As can be seen on lines [60-61](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-ens/blob/45ea10bacb2a398e14d711fe28d1738271cd7640/contracts/dnssec-oracle/BytesUtils.sol#L60-L61), the function checks if `offset + len` is greater than the length of the byte string `self`. This check is performed again later in the code on line 87-90, where it is used to determine the number of iterations in a loop.

[#L87-L90](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-04-ens/blob/45ea10bacb2a398e14d711fe28d1738271cd7640/contracts/dnssec-oracle/BytesUtils.sol#L87-L91)
```solidity
                if (shortest - idx >= 32) {
                    mask = type(uint256).max;
                } else {
                    mask = ~(2 ** (8 * (idx + 32 - shortest)) - 1);
                }
```
Upon Comparing the gas usage of the `compare()` function before and after removing the length check.

Logs:
