The staticcall here will return "ok" even if the dnsresolver doesn’t exist at any incorrect-but-not-zero address. Therefore, resolveCallback() may fail silently.

As a result, it is possible that staticcall will not work but resolveCallback() will not notice anything went wrong. It would be better to also check for the contract’s existence prior to executing address(dnsresolver).staticcall(query);



