# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Currently the PrivatePool intends to block the use of stolen NFTs by quering the `IStolenNftOracle.validateTokensAreNotStolen` function. This validation has been added to `sell` and `change` functions.

```solidity
    function sell(
        uint256[] calldata tokenIds,
        uint256[] calldata tokenWeights,
        MerkleMultiProof calldata proof,
        IStolenNftOracle.Message[] memory stolenNftProofs // put in memory to avoid stack too deep error
    ) public returns (uint256 netOutputAmount, uint256 feeAmount, uint256 protocolFeeAmount) {
        // ~~~ Checks ~~~ //

        // calculate the sum of weights of the NFTs to sell
        uint256 weightSum = sumWeightsAndValidateProof(tokenIds, tokenWeights, proof);

        // calculate the net output amount and fee amount
        (netOutputAmount, feeAmount, protocolFeeAmount) = sellQuote(weightSum);

        //  check the nfts are not stolen
        if (useStolenNftOracle) {
            IStolenNftOracle(stolenNftOracle).validateTokensAreNotStolen(nft, tokenIds, stolenNftProofs);
        }

        // ...
    }

    function change(
        uint256[] memory inputTokenIds,
        uint256[] memory inputTokenWeights,
        MerkleMultiProof memory inputProof,
        IStolenNftOracle.Message[] memory stolenNftProofs,
        uint256[] memory outputTokenIds,
        uint256[] memory outputTokenWeights,
        MerkleMultiProof memory outputProof
    ) public payable returns (uint256 feeAmount, uint256 protocolFeeAmount) {
        // ~~~ Checks ~~~ //

        // check that the caller sent 0 ETH if base token is not ETH
        if (baseToken != address(0) && msg.value > 0) revert InvalidEthAmount();

        // check that NFTs are not stolen
        if (useStolenNftOracle) {
            IStolenNftOracle(stolenNftOracle).validateTokensAreNotStolen(nft, inputTokenIds, stolenNftProofs);
        }

        // ...
    }
```
Ir should be noted that for `change` function the validation is only performed for the incoming NFTs (i.e., only for `inputTokenIds` and not for `outputTokenIds`).

There exists scenarios/functions in which the stolen NFT validation is not performed. They are:
 - buy
 - deposit
 - change (where output NFT is stolen)
 - withdraw
 - when the NFT is sold to pool as soon as it gets stolen, i.e. before the oracle report it as stolen.

In the above mentioned cases the PrivatePool simply allows unrestricted usage of stolen NFTs. As the protocol docs also mentions that:
> each time a user sells or attempts to change one NFT for another, they must submit a signed message from the reservoir.tools oracle proving that the NFT that they are transferring has not been marked as stolen.

This lack of validation can result in users buying stolen NFTs or changing their legitimate NFTs to stolen NFTs. 

Note: it was assumed that the `useStolenNftOracle` was set as `true` by the pool owner.

## Proof of Concept
Consider these scenarios:
 - deposit
    A stolen NFT can be deposited into the PrivatePool using the `deposit` function
 - buy
    A stolen NFT present in the PrivatePool can be bought by anyone using the `buy` function
 - change
    Anyone can exchange their legitimate NFTs to the stolen NFTs present inside the PrivatePool
 - withdraw
    PrivatePool owner can withdraw stolen NFTs from the private pool
 - The oracle will not report NFTs as stolen as soon as they gets stolen. There will be delay in confirming and tagging an NFT as stolen. In this case, before the oracle gets updated anyone can sell the stolen NFT to PrivatePool. After a while even when the oracle reports it as stolen, the NFT can still be bought and changed by any user.

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Consider adding the stolen NFT validation in most functions of the pool so that the pool doesn't allow trading of stolen NFTs at all. Adding the check on `withdraw` function is on the discretion of sponsors.

