if the baesToken is not ETH, the baseTokenAmount is expected to pull from msg.sender, who is msg.sender? 

msg.sender is the EthRouter.sol contract,

but in EthRouter.sol contract, befow calling PrivatePool.sol#deposit, the code does not give allowance to PrivatePool to pool the token from the msg.sender contract.

then transaction would just revert in insuffiicent allowance, note, this issue persists for all transaction (buy / sell / change / deposit) when user trying to call from EthRouter.sol to PrivatePool.sol if the baseToken is a ERC20 token.

