# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The [preBorrowHook function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-05-venus/blob/8be784ed9752b80e6f1b8b781e2e6251748d0d7e/contracts/Comptroller.sol#L324-L380) creates an `AccountLiquiditySnapshot` to check if a borrower has enough collateral to borrow a given amount of the underlying asset. But, it does not check if there is sufficient collateral to borrow before creating the snapshot, which can cause the function to revert if there is not enough collateral. If the function reverts, the rewards distributors will not update, which can lead to an inconsistency in the state of the contract.
If a borrower attempts to borrow more than they have enough collateral for, the `preBorrowHook` function will revert and rewards distributors will not update. This can cause an inconsistency in the state of the contract, which can potentially affect other users' interactions with the contract.

## Proof of Concept
Specifically when the snapshot object is created by calling the [_getHypotheticalLiquiditySnapshot ](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-05-venus/blob/8be784ed9752b80e6f1b8b781e2e6251748d0d7e/contracts/Comptroller.sol#L359). If there is not enough collateral to borrow, the function will revert, and the rewards distributors will not update, which can lead to an inconsistency in the state of the contract.
```solidity
        AccountLiquiditySnapshot memory snapshot = _getHypotheticalLiquiditySnapshot(
```
If the `_getHypotheticalLiquiditySnapshot` function reverts due to an insufficient amount of collateral, the rewards distributors will not be updated

The function checks if a borrower can borrow a given amount of an asset from the lending market.
```solidity
    function preBorrowHook(
        address vToken,
        address borrower,
        uint256 borrowAmount
    ) external override {
        _checkActionPauseState(vToken, Action.BORROW);


        oracle.updatePrice(vToken);


        if (!markets[vToken].isListed) {
            revert MarketNotListed(address(vToken));
        }


        if (!markets[vToken].accountMembership[borrower]) {
            // only vTokens may call borrowAllowed if borrower not in market
            _checkSenderIs(vToken);


            // attempt to add borrower to the market or revert
            _addToMarket(VToken(msg.sender), borrower);
        }


        if (oracle.getUnderlyingPrice(vToken) == 0) {
            revert PriceError(address(vToken));
        }


        uint256 borrowCap = borrowCaps[vToken];
        // Skipping the cap check for uncapped coins to save some gas
        if (borrowCap != type(uint256).max) {
            uint256 totalBorrows = VToken(vToken).totalBorrows();
            uint256 nextTotalBorrows = totalBorrows + borrowAmount;
            if (nextTotalBorrows > borrowCap) {
                revert BorrowCapExceeded(vToken, borrowCap);
            }
        }


        AccountLiquiditySnapshot memory snapshot = _getHypotheticalLiquiditySnapshot(
            borrower,
            VToken(vToken),
            0,
            borrowAmount,
            _getCollateralFactor
        );


        if (snapshot.shortfall > 0) {
            revert InsufficientLiquidity();
        }


        Exp memory borrowIndex = Exp({ mantissa: VToken(vToken).borrowIndex() });


        // Keep the flywheel moving
        uint256 rewardDistributorsCount = rewardsDistributors.length;


        for (uint256 i; i < rewardDistributorsCount; ++i) {
            rewardsDistributors[i].updateRewardTokenBorrowIndex(vToken, borrowIndex);
            rewardsDistributors[i].distributeBorrowerRewardToken(vToken, borrower, borrowIndex);
        }
    }
```

## Tools Used
Manual
VsCode

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Add a check for sufficient collateral before creating the `AccountLiquiditySnapshot` in the `preBorrowHook` function. This will prevent the function from reverting and ensure that rewards distributors update correctly.


