# Vulnerability details



The function setPriceOracle allows the owner of the contract to change the price oracle. This could be exploited by a malicious user to manipulate the price of an asset.

For example, a malicious user could create a malicious price oracle contract that always returns a price that is higher than the actual price. Then, the malicious user could set the price oracle of the contract to the malicious price oracle contract. 

function preRepayHook(address vToken, address borrower) external override {
        _checkActionPauseState(vToken, Action.REPAY);

        oracle.updatePrice(vToken);

        if (!markets[vToken].isListed) {
            revert MarketNotListed(address(vToken));
        }

        // Keep the flywheel moving
        uint256 rewardDistributorsCount = rewardsDistributors.length;

        for (uint256 i; i < rewardDistributorsCount; ++i) {
            Exp memory borrowIndex = Exp({ mantissa: VToken(vToken).borrowIndex() });
            rewardsDistributors[i].updateRewardTokenBorrowIndex(vToken, borrowIndex);
            rewardsDistributors[i].distributeBorrowerRewardToken(vToken, borrower, borrowIndex);
        }
    }


Issues:

The function setPriceOracle allows the owner of the contract to change the price oracle.
The preRedeemHook function calls the oracle.updatePrice function to get the current price of the asset being redeemed.
If the price oracle is controlled by a malicious user, they could set the price to an artificially low value.
This would allow the malicious user to redeem more assets than they are entitled to.

function setPriceOracle(PriceOracle newOracle) external onlyOwner {
        require(address(newOracle) != address(0), "invalid price oracle address");

        PriceOracle oldOracle = oracle;
        oracle = newOracle;
        emit NewPriceOracle(oldOracle, newOracle);
    }


## Impact

Malicious user can manipulate price

## Tools Used
vs code

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Only allow the price oracle to be changed by a multisig wallet.
Use a decentralized price oracle that is not controlled by any single entity.



