# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-llama/blob/main/src/LlamaCore.sol#L465


# Vulnerability details

## Description

A caller can create action, approve action, or disapprove action using a policyHolder signature that has been created off-chain by calling the functions that accept signatures.
In order to prevent replay attack, or prevent user to use same signature twice to do same action, the system use `nonce` values that got increment each time.

The system also give the signer the ability to revoke any signature created for any action by incrementing the nonce value by calling `LlamaCore::incrementNonce` which will increment their nonce so any signature will be invalidated. This is clearly defined in the function NetSpec:

***Increments the caller's nonce for the given `selector`. This is useful for revoking signatures that have not been used yet.***

However, this flow simply introduce a front-run attack, user can simply front-run the call to `incrementNonce` and finalize the action they have signature for.

## Impact

User will be able to use the signer signature either for creation, approval or disapproval actions without signer intentional

## Proof of Concept

1. Let's take an example for `castApprovalBySig`:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-llama/blob/main/src/LlamaCore.sol#LL378C3-L391C4
```
function castApprovalBySig(
    address policyholder,
    uint8 role,
    ActionInfo calldata actionInfo,
    string calldata reason,
    uint8 v,
    bytes32 r,
    bytes32 s
  ) external {
    bytes32 digest = _getCastApprovalTypedDataHash(policyholder, role, actionInfo, reason);
    address signer = ecrecover(digest, v, r, s);
    if (signer == address(0) || signer != policyholder) revert InvalidSignature();
    return _castApproval(signer, role, actionInfo, reason);
  }
```

2. At L387 the function call `_getCastApprovalTypedDataHash`:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-llama/blob/main/src/LlamaCore.sol#LL746C3-L764C4
```
function _getCastApprovalTypedDataHash(
    address policyholder,
    uint8 role,
    ActionInfo calldata actionInfo,
    string calldata reason
  ) internal returns (bytes32) {
    bytes32 castApprovalHash = keccak256(
      abi.encode(
        CAST_APPROVAL_TYPEHASH,
        policyholder,
        role,
        _getActionInfoHash(actionInfo),
        keccak256(bytes(reason)),
        _useNonce(policyholder, msg.sig)
      )
    );

    return keccak256(abi.encodePacked("\x19\x01", _getDomainHash(), castApprovalHash));
  }
```

3. This function use `keccak256` to generate a new bytes32 variable using different argument, one of them is `_useNonce(policyholder, msg.sig)`
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-llama/blob/main/src/LlamaCore.sol#LL698C3-L701C4
```
function _useNonce(address policyholder, bytes4 selector) internal returns (uint256 nonce) {
    nonce = nonces[policyholder][selector];
    nonces[policyholder][selector] = LlamaUtils.uncheckedIncrement(nonce);
  }
``` 

4. This function simply return the current nonce for the policyHolder, if this nonce got incremented by the signer by calling `incrementNonce` the signature will be invalid as excepted:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-llama/blob/main/src/LlamaCore.sol#L463
```
function incrementNonce(bytes4 selector) external {
    // Safety: Can never overflow a uint256 by incrementing.
    nonces[msg.sender][selector] = LlamaUtils.uncheckedIncrement(nonces[msg.sender][selector]);
  }
```

5. However, a user can front-run the call to `incrementNonce` and call `castApprovalBySig` which will pass. 

## Tools Used

Manual
## Recommended Mitigation Steps

createActionBySig shouldn't have any issue as the policyHolder (signer) can call `cancelAction`. I could think of a function that allow policyHolder to delete their approvals/disapprovals as well, so even if a caller managed to use their signature, they can delete their approval/disapproval.


