# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The impact of this finding is a potential loss of precision in the getReportableBlockFor function. The current implementation performs a division operation followed by a multiplication operation, which can introduce rounding errors and result in a loss of precision. This can lead to incorrect reportable block numbers and affect the accuracy of the system's functionality.

## Proof of Concept
```
 function getReportableBlockFor(bytes32 _key) internal view returns (uint256) {
        uint256 updateFrequency = updateFrequencyMap[_key];
        if (updateFrequency == 0) {
            revert UpdateFrequencyNotSet();
        }
        return (block.number / updateFrequency) * updateFrequency;
    }
```

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Multiply first before dividing to keep the precision.


