# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-06-stader/blob/7566b5a35f32ebd55d3578b8bd05c038feb7d9cc/contracts/StaderOracle.sol#L172-L193


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
There is an interesting code path within `StaderOracle.sol` that allows any caller to decide whether or not the exchange rate should be updated with the `inspectionModeExchangeRate` data. If exchange rate data is submitted outside the expected bounds, `Inspection mode` is initiated. After the cooldown period has passed following its initiation (7 days), any user can either call `closeERInspectionMode()` or `disableERInspectionMode()`. Only one function is callable because `closeERInspectionMode()` requires that `erInspectionMode == true` and calls `disableERInspectionMode()`, while `disableERInspectionMode()` sets `erInspectionMode = false`. Both functions are either external or public.

`closeERInspectionMode()` will overwrite the `exchangeData` struct with `inspectionModeExchangeRate`, altering the exchange rate used across the entire Stader protocol.

`disableERInspectionMode()` will not overwrite the `exchangeData` struct. Since `erInspectionMode` is set to false, the `inspectionModeExchangeRate` is essentially deleted and can not be used.

Understanding that the 7 day cooldown period will likely not be reached under normal operations prior to the `manager` calling either function, the ability for a user to arbitrarily decide the exchange rate for the protocol feels like a power that should not be given out.

## Proof of Concept
```
    function closeERInspectionMode() external override whenNotPaused {
        if (!erInspectionMode) {
            revert ERChangeLimitNotCrossed();
        }
        disableERInspectionMode();
        _updateExchangeRate(
            inspectionModeExchangeRate.totalETHBalance,
            inspectionModeExchangeRate.totalETHXSupply,
            inspectionModeExchangeRate.reportingBlockNumber
        );
    }

    // turn off erInspectionMode if `inspectionModeExchangeRate` is incorrect so that oracle/POR can push new data
    function disableERInspectionMode() public override whenNotPaused {
        if (
            !staderConfig.onlyManagerRole(msg.sender) &&
            erInspectionModeStartBlock + MAX_ER_UPDATE_FREQUENCY > block.number
        ) {
            revert CooldownNotComplete();
        }
        erInspectionMode = false;
    }
```

As stated above:
- Only one of the above functions is callable.
- One updates the global `exchangeRate`
- One does not.

## Tools Used
Manual review.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Potentially the best mitigation would be to add manager access control to `closeERInspectionMode()`. This would ensure that only the manager has the power to overwrite the `exchangeRate` struct. All users will still be able to deactivate the ER Inspection mode while NOT overwriting `exchangeRate`.


## Assessed type

Access Control

