# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Chainlink and Tellor are used to check for price. Both uses the hardcoded TIMEOUT of 4 hours to make sure that both oracle are recent with price. However, some price feeds have heartbeats of 20 minutes and a hardcoded value of 4 hours will result in some price feeds returning stale value from Chainlink.

## Proof of Concept

Chainlink fetches latest round data and returns them in a chainlinkResponse object. 

```solidity
        try priceAggregator[_collateral].latestRoundData() returns
        (
            uint80 roundId,
            int256 answer,
            uint256 /* startedAt */,
            uint256 timestamp,
            uint80 /* answeredInRound */
        )
        {
            // If call to Chainlink succeeds, return the response and success = true
            chainlinkResponse.roundId = roundId;
            chainlinkResponse.answer = answer;
            chainlinkResponse.timestamp = timestamp;
            chainlinkResponse.success = true;
            return chainlinkResponse;
        } catch {
            // If call to Chainlink aggregator reverts, return a zero response with success = false
            return chainlinkResponse;
        }
    }
```

As we see here in `fetchPrice` function, the chainlinkResponse response contains the timestamp of the data.

