https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/Deployer.sol#L102


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
In contrast to the [Test File](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/test/Upgradeability.test.ts), in which you're deploying the proxies directly, the setup from `Deployer` will keep the Proxy Admin to a zero value.

Meaning nobody will be able to upgrade them after the deployment.

See POC below to show that the admin slot is address(0)

Contract below shows a basic setup, which uses the same dependencies as yours (OZ @ 4.7.3, Solidity 0.8.9)

As you'll see, the setup makes it so that no admin is set, meaning the contract will be a proxy which is not actually upgradeable.

## Proof of Concept

```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: BlueOak-1.0.0
pragma solidity 0.8.9;

import "@openzeppelin/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol";


contract Child {
  bool public initialized;
  function init() external {
    initialized = true;
  }
}

contract TestAdmin {
  address public logic;
  constructor () {
    logic = address(new Child());
  }

  function deploy() external returns (address) {
      // Main - Proxy
      Child proxy = Child(address(new ERC1967Proxy(address(logic), new bytes(0))));
      proxy.init();

      return address(proxy);
  } 
}
