## Impact

https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RevenueTrader.sol#L53-L64

1. Reentrancy vulnerability.
An attacker could repeatedly call the `manageToken` function by making recursive calls to this contract via the distributor contract. This could potentially cause the contract to execute unintended logic multiple times, leading to a loss of funds. For example, attacker could repeatedly call the `distributor.distribute()` method, using a malicious distributor contract, thereby taking an excessive amount of the intended target asset.

## Proof of Concept

An attacker could potentially exploit the reentrancy vulnerability by creating a malicious version of the distributor contract that calls back into the `manageToken` function. The attacker could then repeatedly call the `manageToken` function, potentially causing unintended effects.

Example of a malicious distributor contract that demonstrates the general concept of the attack.

```
contract MaliciousDistributor {
    function distribute(IERC20 erc20, address revenueTrader, uint256 amount) public {
        // Distribute the asset as intended
        erc20.transfer(msg.sender, amount);
        // Call back into the revenueTrader contract
        IRevenueTrader(revenueTrader).manageToken(erc20);
    }
}
```
An attacker could then use this malicious distributor contract to repeatedly call the `manageToken` function on a vulnerable `revenueTrader` contract.

## Tools Used

Manual audit, vs code

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

A recommended step is to use a guard condition to prevent reentrant call in the `manageToken` function, using a mutex such as the Ethereum Alarm Clock library, or using the `require(address(this).balance >= msg.value)` as a guard condition. Another approach is to use the new Solidity feature `reentrancy guard`, which is a built-in protection for reentrancy attacks by making sure the fallback function of the contract is not called during external function calls.

```
pragma solidity >=0.8.0 <0.9.0;

contract RevenueTrader {
    // ...
    function manageToken(IERC20 erc20) external notPausedOrFrozen {
        require(address(this).balance >= msg.value, "reentrancy detected");
        // rest of the function
    }
    // ...
}
```


