# Vulnerability details

## Impact

RToken may be distributed to StRSR and frozen.
RSR may be distributed to Furnace and frozen.

## Proof of Concept

Both Furnace and StRSR are added to the destinations of Distributor in [DistributorP1#init()](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/Distributor.sol#L41):
```
function init(IMain main_, RevenueShare calldata dist) external initializer {
    // omitted
    _setDistribution(FURNACE, RevenueShare(dist.rTokenDist, 0));
    _setDistribution(ST_RSR, RevenueShare(0, dist.rsrDist));
}
```
They are both added with a mapping address:
```
address public constant FURNACE = address(1);
address public constant ST_RSR = address(2);
```

At the same time, in order to prevent funds from being trapped by distributing RToken to StRSR or RSR to Furnace, their configuration is specifically checked in [DistributorP1#_setDistribution()](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/Distributor.sol#L163-L164):
```
function _setDistribution(address dest, RevenueShare memory share) internal {
    require(dest != address(0), "dest cannot be zero");
    if (dest == FURNACE) require(share.rsrDist == 0, "Furnace must get 0% of RSR");
    if (dest == ST_RSR) require(share.rTokenDist == 0, "StRSR must get 0% of RToken");
    // omitted
}
```

However, if an actual Furnace address or StRSR address is used when calling [DistributorP1#setDistribution()](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/Distributor.sol#L61), it will be added to destinations as if it is a regular address.
Then, these two special contracts will be distributed twice in [DistributorP1#distribute](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/Distributor.sol#L87)
And since `_setDistribution` didn't check the share parameter when they are added as regular address:
* RToken may be distributed to StRSR and frozen.
* RSR may be distributed to Furnace and frozen.

## Tools Used

Manual

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

We should treat the real addresses of Furnace and StRSR as their mapping addresses in [DistributorP1#setDistribution()](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/Distributor.sol#L61):
```
diff --git a/contracts/p1/Distributor.sol b/contracts/p1/Distributor.sol
index 53322973..28a05d67 100644
--- a/contracts/p1/Distributor.sol
+++ b/contracts/p1/Distributor.sol
@@ -160,6 +160,12 @@ contract DistributorP1 is ComponentP1, IDistributor {
     //   distribution' = distribution.set(dest, share)
     function _setDistribution(address dest, RevenueShare memory share) internal {
         require(dest != address(0), "dest cannot be zero");
+        if (dest == furnace) {
+            dest = FURNACE;
+        }
+        if (dest == stRSR) {
+            dest = ST_RSR;
+        }
         if (dest == FURNACE) require(share.rsrDist == 0, "Furnace must get 0% of RSR");
         if (dest == ST_RSR) require(share.rTokenDist == 0, "StRSR must get 0% of RToken");
         require(share.rsrDist <= 10000, "RSR distribution too high");
```

