VIM

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
prevent reading reentrancy attack by central reentrancy guard or by proxy interface contract that has reentrancy guard. 
or create contract state (similar to basket nonce) which changes after each interaction and check for contracts states change during the call. (start and end of the call)

# Lines of code

https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L378


# Vulnerability details

Per the shown [CToken](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/plugins/assets/CTokenFiatCollateral.sol#L44) and [AToken](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/plugins/assets/ATokenFiatCollateral.sol#L45)'s `refPerTok` can change

e.g. for CToken
```solidity
    function refPerTok() public view override returns (uint192) {
        uint256 rate = ICToken(address(erc20)).exchangeRateStored();
        int8 shiftLeft = 8 - int8(referenceERC20Decimals) - 18;
        return shiftl_toFix(rate, shiftLeft);
    }
```
https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/plugins/assets/CTokenFiatCollateral.sol#L44

and 
```solidity
    function refPerTok() public view override returns (uint192) {
        uint256 rateInRAYs = IStaticAToken(address(erc20)).rate(); // {ray ref/tok}
        return shiftl_toFix(rateInRAYs, -27);
    }
```

https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/plugins/assets/ATokenFiatCollateral.sol#L45


For these tokens, [`vest`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L378) will not update it's quote based on the current exchangeRate.

Since the system is coded to have a never decreasing refPerTok, this will cause a loss, of the delta of the `refPerTok` change to the early depositors.

### Proof of Concept

- Depositor A `issue`s at X rate (due to refPerTok which is computed at `quantity` in `quote`)
- Price is locked in and we vest over T time

- refPerTok changes by Y% (system is adaptive to it)
- New quote would cost: (100% - Y%) * X
- Later depositors all use this cheaper quote

- Initial Depositor took a worse deal and they are still vesting, they will receive R rTokens
- Later depositors are getting the surplus from them, R + Y rTokens


### Code Explanation
The reason for this discrepancy stands in the fact that:

[`issue`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L237) will use `quote`
https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L237-L240

```solidity
    (address[] memory erc20s, uint256[] memory deposits) = basketHandler.quote(
        amtBaskets,
        CEIL
    );
```

[`quote`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/BasketHandler.sol#L407-L425) which will use [`quantity`]

```solidity
    quantities[i] = quantity(basket.erc20s[i]).mul(amount, rounding).shiftl_toUint(
        int8(IERC20Metadata(address(basket.erc20s[i])).decimals()),
        rounding
    );
```

(https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/BasketHandler.sol#L296-L310) which will account for `refPerTok` at the time the vesting start.

```solidity
    function quantity(IERC20 erc20) public view returns (uint192) {
        try assetRegistry.toColl(erc20) returns (ICollateral coll) {
            if (coll.status() == CollateralStatus.DISABLED) return FIX_ZERO;

            uint192 refPerTok = coll.refPerTok(); // {ref/tok}
            if (refPerTok > 0) {
                // {tok/BU} = {ref/BU} / {ref/tok}
                return basket.refAmts[erc20].div(refPerTok, CEIL);
            } else {
                return FIX_MAX;
            }
        } catch {
            return FIX_ZERO;
        }
    }
```

While [`vest`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L378) will not check if the `quote` has changed, effectively locking in that `refPerTok` at T0.

### Mitigation
`vest` should check the new price and use that or a linear interpolation of it, it should also issues the excess value to the original issuer, instead of allowing this excess yield to be redistributed to everyone.

