# Lines of code

https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RevenueTrader.sol#L63


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
There is no revenue balance check in the RevenueTrade.manageToken(). When distribute revenue  to users it may cause transactions to fail frequently

## Proof of Concept
```
 function manageToken(IERC20 erc20) external notPausedOrFrozen {
        if (address(trades[erc20]) != address(0)) return;

        uint256 bal = erc20.balanceOf(address(this));
        if (bal == 0) return;

        if (erc20 == tokenToBuy) {
            // == Interactions then return ==
            IERC20Upgradeable(address(erc20)).safeApprove(address(distributor), 0);
            IERC20Upgradeable(address(erc20)).safeApprove(address(distributor), bal);
            distributor.distribute(erc20, address(this), bal);
            return;
        }
```
The function call RevenueTrade.manageToken() will distribute token if the parameters passed is tokenToBuy.
The function will internally call  distributor.distribute(). In the function call distribute(), the protocol calculate the tokensPerShare according to the formula  .
```
tokensPerShare = amount / totalShares

```
The amount is the balance in the revenue trader contract.

Next ,get number of shares according to every destination

Then calculate the transfer amount according to the formula 
```
            uint256 transferAmt = tokensPerShare * numberOfShares;
````
Finally, the token are transferred from the revenue contract to the destination address.

However there is no balance check in the revenue contract before calling  function distributor.distribute() , If the balance is less than the amount to be transferred out， transactions will often fail.

