# Vulnerability details

## Impact
An attacker can manipulate the issue price of RToken.
An attacker can make BackingManager to [sell assets](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/BackingManager.sol#L134-L144), [mint rToken](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/BackingManager.sol#L118), or execute other operations based on a wrong intermediate state.

## Proof of Concept
A similar issue is reported in [Solidified - Oct 16 2022.pdf](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-01-reserve/blob/main/audits/Solidified%20-%20Oct%2016%202022.pdf):
> Issue#22: RToken.sol (P1): Reentrancy attack possible if token is ever upgraded to ERC777 token
And the [commit#4597ac8c](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/pull/342/commits/4597ac8ce06c351427441363f9a94aa90e12b52f) solved the issue.

But in reality, the problem is more complex than the report describes.
At least the following two points have not been covered or fixed:
1. When the RToken is upgraded to use the ERC777 standard, the attacker may reenter the protocol through other contracts (like BackingManager) in addition to the RToken itself.
2. Adding any ERC777 token to the basket would cause a reentrancy problem too. It would be more likely to happen and be overlooked.

The main logic of a cross-contract reentrancy attack is:
Call [`RToken.issue()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L177) or [`RToken.vest()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L378) or [`RToken.redeem()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L439) to trigger an ERC777 callback(`tokensToSend()` or `tokensReceived()`) through [`issue - _mint()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L268) or [`issue - safeTransferFrom()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L271) or [`vest - _mint()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L791) or [`redeem - safeTransferFrom()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L506-L510) or [`redeem - _burn()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L498)
Then call [`BackingManager - manageTokens()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/BackingManager.sol#L83) within the ERC777 callback.
The `manageTokens()` will cause errors becase it is called in an intermediate state, when RToken's state has been updated but not yet finished transferring all assets to BackingManager.

For example, the following test code shows one of the attack scenarios:
- Call [`RToken.issue()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L177)
- The ERC777 callback - `tokensReceived()` will be triggered by [`issue - _mint()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L268)
- Within the `tokensReceived()`, call [`BackingManager - manageTokens()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/BackingManager.sol#L83). Becase it is not fully collateralized now(assets has not been transferred to BackingManager), it will make BackingManager call [`setBasketsNeeded()`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/BackingManager.sol#L204) to set a smaller [RToken.basketsNeeded](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L67).
- `RToken.issue()` return.
- From now on, because [`RToken.basketsNeeded`](https://github.com/reserve-protocol/protocol/blob/df7ecadc2bae74244ace5e8b39e94bc992903158/contracts/p1/RToken.sol#L67) is wrong, the attacker (or any user) can issue cheaper RToken (with less assets) and sell RToken to earn profit.

