# Vulnerability details

## Impact

`settlement.cairo` contract maintains a list of whitelisted validators (`chakra_validators_pubkey`) and a `required_validators_num` count, which specifies the number of validators required to sign the same message hash to protect the Settlement from malicious validator requests. However, `settlement.cairo`'s `check_chakra_signatures` does not check if the provided signatures come from the same validator, allowing a malicious validator to easily bypass the `required_validators_num` requirement.

## Proof of Concept

When `settlement.cairo`'s `receive_cross_chain_msg` or `receive_cross_chain_callback` is called, it verifies the validity of the request by checking that at least the `required_validators_num` number of valid validators have signed the request with valid `signatures`. This is done by providing the hashed message and `signatures` to the `check_chakra_signatures` operation.

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/main/cairo/handler/src/settlement.cairo#L350

