# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The EVM-based Settlement contract maintains a list of whitelisted validators and a `required_validators` count, which specifies the number of validators required to sign the same message hash to protect the Settlement from malicious validator requests. However, `SettlementSignatureVerifier.verify` does not check if the provided signatures come from the same validator, allowing a malicious validator to easily bypass the `required_validators` requirement.

## Proof of Concept

When `Settlement.receive_cross_chain_msg` or `receive_cross_chain_callback` is called, it verifies the validity of the request by checking that at least the `required_validators` number of valid validators have signed the request with valid `signatures`. This is done by providing the `message_hash` and `signatures` to the `signature_verifier.verify` operation.

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/main/solidity/settlement/contracts/ChakraSettlement.sol#L194-L197

```solidity
    function receive_cross_chain_msg(
        uint256 txid,
        string memory from_chain,
        uint256 from_address,
        uint256 from_handler,
        address to_handler,
        PayloadType payload_type,
        bytes calldata payload,
        uint8 sign_type, // validators signature type /  multisig or bls sr25519
        bytes calldata signatures // signature array
    ) external {
        {
            // verify signature
            bytes32 message_hash = keccak256(
                abi.encodePacked(
                    txid,
                    from_chain,
                    from_address,
                    from_handler,
                    to_handler,
                    keccak256(payload)
                )
            );

            require(
>>>             signature_verifier.verify(message_hash, signatures, sign_type),
                "Invalid signature"
            );

            require(
                receive_cross_txs[txid].status == CrossChainMsgStatus.Unknow,
                "Invalid transaction status"
            );
        }

        receive_cross_txs[txid] = ReceivedCrossChainTx(
            txid,
            from_chain,
            contract_chain_name,
            from_address,
            from_handler,
            address(this),
            payload,
            CrossChainMsgStatus.Pending
        );

        bool result = ISettlementHandler(to_handler).receive_cross_chain_msg(
            txid,
            from_chain,
            from_address,
            from_handler,
            payload_type,
            payload,
            sign_type,
            signatures
        );

        // ...
    }
```

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/main/solidity/settlement/contracts/ChakraSettlement.sol#L265-L272

```solidity
