# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-loopfi/blob/main/src/proxy/PositionAction.sol#L431-L492


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
`decreaseLever` is inoperable when flash loan fees are applied
## Proof-of-Concept
The bug affects the `decreaseLever` function in the **PositionAction** contract, specifically its interaction with the **Flashlender** contract's `creditFlashLoan` feature. The execution flow is as follows:

```
UserProxy
    --delegateCall--> (UserProxy) PositionAction.decreaseLever
        --call--> Flashlender.creditFlashLoan
            --call--> (Self) PositionAction.onCreditFlashLoan
            --call--> underlyingToken.transferFrom(PositionAction, pool, amount+fee)
```

The bug occurs in the `onCreditFlashLoan` function, which fails to account for the flash loan fee when approving the repayment amount. This oversight causes the `decreaseLever` function to fail when there's a non-zero flash loan fee.  

The issue manifests as follows:

1. In `decreaseLever`, the flash loan amount is set from `primarySwap.amount`:  
See: [PositionAction.sol#L364-L369](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-loopfi/blob/main/src/proxy/PositionAction.sol#L364-L369)
   ```solidity
   uint loanAmount = leverParams.primarySwap.amount;
    flashlender.creditFlashLoan(
        ICreditFlashBorrower(self),
        loanAmount,
        abi.encode(leverParams, subCollateral, residualRecipient)
    );
   ```

2. `onCreditFlashLoan` approves only this amount for repayment:  
See: [PositionAction.sol#L431-L492](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-loopfi/blob/main/src/proxy/PositionAction.sol#L431-L492)
   ```solidity
    function onCreditFlashLoan(
        address /*initiator*/,
        uint256 /*amount*/,
        uint256 /*fee*/,
        bytes calldata data
    ) external returns (bytes32) {
        if (msg.sender != address(flashlender)) revert PositionAction__onCreditFlashLoan__invalidSender();
        (
            LeverParams memory leverParams,
            uint256 subCollateral,
            address residualRecipient
        ) = abi.decode(data,(LeverParams, uint256, address));

        uint256 subDebt = leverParams.primarySwap.amount;
        ...
        ...
        underlyingToken.forceApprove(address(flashlender), subDebt);
   ```
   Where `subDebt` equals `loanAmount`.

3. However, **Flashlender** expects repayment of the loan amount plus fee:  
See: [Flashlender.sol#L117-L137](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-loopfi/blob/main/src/Flashlender.sol#L117-L137)
   ```solidity
    function creditFlashLoan(
        ICreditFlashBorrower receiver,
        uint256 amount,
        bytes calldata data
    ) external override nonReentrant returns (bool) {
        uint256 fee = wmul(amount, protocolFee);
        uint256 total = amount + fee; <-- expect amount + fee

        pool.lendCreditAccount(amount, address(receiver));

        emit CreditFlashLoan(address(receiver), amount, fee);

        if (receiver.onCreditFlashLoan(msg.sender, amount, fee, data) != CALLBACK_SUCCESS_CREDIT)
            revert Flash__creditFlashLoan_callbackFailed();

        // reverts if not enough Stablecoin have been send back
        underlyingToken.transferFrom(address(receiver), address(pool), total); <-- attempt to transfer amount + fee
        pool.repayCreditAccount(total - fee, fee, 0);

        return true;
    }
   ```

4. When **Flashlender** attempts to collect the repayment:
   ```solidity
   underlyingToken.transferFrom(address(receiver), address(pool), total);
   ```
   It fails due to insufficient approval, as the approved amount doesn't include the fee.

This bug renders the `decreaseLever` function inoperable when flash loan fees are applied, effectively blocking users from reducing their leverage positions through this mechanism.  

## Recommended Mitigations  
Account for flashloan fee when calling approve for **Flashlender**. The same mechanism actually presents in `onFlashLoan` function.  
```solidity
    function onFlashLoan(...
    ...
    ...
    // derive the amount of normal debt from the swap amount out
    uint256 addDebt = amount + fee; <-- account for flashloan fee

    // add collateral and debt
    ICDPVault(leverParams.vault).modifyCollateralAndDebt(
        leverParams.position,
        address(this),
        address(this),
        toInt256(collateral),
        toInt256(addDebt)
    );

    underlyingToken.forceApprove(address(flashlender), addDebt);
```

## Coded PoC
The following PoC utilizes the decreaseLever test from `PositionAction20.lever.t.sol` and switch to Flashlender with non-zero flash loan fee instead.  
