# Vulnerability details

The `TVL` calculation represents the total assets managed in the vault. The formula is:

```solidity
    function TVL() public view returns (uint256) {
        return TVLHelper.getTVL(vaultId, registry, address(baseToken))
		        + baseToken.balanceOf(address(this))
            - depositQueue.totalAWFDeposit;
    }
```

- The `TVLHelper` calculates the total `TVL` of all `holdingPositions`. The `getPositionTVL` formula is specific to the protocol's connector.

```solidity
    function getTVL(uint256 vaultId, PositionRegistry registry, address baseToken) public view returns (uint256) {
        uint256 totalTVL;
        uint256 totalDebt;
        HoldingPI[] memory positions = registry.getHoldingPositions(vaultId);
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < positions.length; i++) {
            if (positions[i].calculatorConnector == address(0)) {
                continue;
            }
            uint256 tvl = IConnector(positions[i].calculatorConnector).getPositionTVL(positions[i], baseToken);
            bool isPositionDebt = registry.isPositionDebt(vaultId, positions[i].positionId);
            if (isPositionDebt) {
                totalDebt += tvl;
            } else {
                totalTVL += tvl;
            }
        }
        if (totalTVL < totalDebt) {
            return 0;
        }
        return (totalTVL - totalDebt);
    }
```

- Executed deposits in the `AccountingManager` (`balanceOf(AccountingManager)` - `totalAWFDeposit`)

Let's first look how a user can deposit funds and how these funds are deposited into a specific protocol to gain yield:

1. The user calls `AccountingManager.deposit()`, which transfers the tokens from the user to the `AccountingManager`. This action creates a deposit request and adds it to the deposit queue.
2. The strategy manager calls `AccountingManager.calculateDepositShares()` to calculate the shares that should be received by the `depositRequest` owners.
3. The strategy manager calls `AccountingManager.executeDeposit()`. During this step, two actions occur:
   1. The shares calculated in the previous step are minted to the users.
   2. The liquidity from the users' deposits is transferred to the specified connector.

The transfer of the liquidity is happening through [Connector.addLiquidity()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/accountingManager/AccountingManager.sol#L293)

```solidity
    function executeDeposit(uint256 maxI, address connector, bytes memory addLPdata)
        public
        onlyManager
        whenNotPaused
        nonReentrant
    {
        ...
        if (registry.isAnActiveConnector(vaultId, connector) && processedBaseTokenAmount > 0) {
            uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);
            amounts[0] = processedBaseTokenAmount;
            address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);
            tokens[0] = address(baseToken);
            IConnector(connector).addLiquidity(tokens, amounts, addLPdata);
        }
        ...
    }
```

This makes a callback to [sendTokensToTrustedAddress](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/BaseConnector.sol#L181) in the `AccountingManager`

```solidity
    function addLiquidity(address[] memory tokens, uint256[] memory amounts, bytes memory data)
        external
        override
        nonReentrant
    {
        ...
        ITokenTransferCallBack(msg.sender).sendTokensToTrustedAddress(tokens[i], amounts[i], msg.sender, "");
        ...
    }
```

The `AccountingManager` then [transfers](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/accountingManager/AccountingManager.sol#L156) the tokens to the connector.

```solidity
function sendTokensToTrustedAddress(address token, uint256 amount, address _caller, bytes calldata _data)
    external
    returns (uint256)
{
    ...
        IERC20(token).safeTransfer(address(msg.sender), amount);
    ...
}
```

Next, the function [\_updateTokenInRegistry()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/BaseConnector.sol#L190) is called internally. This function then calls another function with the same name, passing `false` as the second parameter, which determines if the position should be removed. This is because `IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this))` is more than 0, since the tokens have already been transferred.

```solidity
function _updateTokenInRegistry(address token) internal {
    _updateTokenInRegistry(token, IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this)) == 0);
}
```

The purpose of this function is to `calculatePositionId` and `updateHoldingPositions`, which will [create](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/accountingManager/Registry.sol#L311-L321) a new holding position in this case.

```solidity
    function _updateTokenInRegistry(address token, bool remove) internal {
        (address accountingManager,) = registry.getVaultAddresses(vaultId);
        // the value function is inside the accounting manager contract (so we can use the accounting manager address as the calculator connector)
        bytes32 positionId = registry.calculatePositionId(accountingManager, 0, abi.encode(token));
        // if the token is not in the registry, we add it or remove it if the remove flag is true
        uint256 positionIndex =
            registry.getHoldingPositionIndex(vaultId, positionId, address(this), abi.encode(address(this)));
        if ((positionIndex == 0 && !remove) || (positionIndex > 0 && remove)) {
            emit UpdateTokenInRegistry(token, remove);
            registry.updateHoldingPosition(vaultId, positionId, abi.encode(address(this)), "", remove);
        }
    }
```

The newly added holding positions are included in the `TVL` calculation, which is performed by calling the specified `Connector.getPositionTVL`.

However, when all of the funds from this position are deposited into the connector’s protocol, let's consider [AaveConnector.supply](http://AaveConnector.supplyhttp://aaveconnector.supplyhttps//github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/connectors/AaveConnector.sol#L46-L54) as an example. `_updateTokenInRegistry` is called again. This time, though, `IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this))` is 0, which will remove the position from the registry’s holding positions.

```solidity
function supply(address supplyToken, uint256 amount) external onlyManager nonReentrant {
    _approveOperations(supplyToken, pool, amount);
    IPool(pool).supply(supplyToken, amount, address(this), 0);
    registry.updateHoldingPosition(
        vaultId, registry.calculatePositionId(address(this), AAVE_POSITION_ID, ""), "", "", false
    );
    _updateTokenInRegistry(supplyToken);
    emit Supply(supplyToken, amount);
}
```

