```solidity
function updateHoldingPosition(
    uint256 vaultId,
    bytes32 _positionId,
    bytes calldata _data,
    bytes calldata additionalData,
    bool removePosition
) public vaultExists(vaultId) returns (uint256) {
    Vault storage vault = vaults[vaultId];
    if (!vault.connectors[msg.sender].enabled) revert UnauthorizedAccess();
    if (!vault.trustedPositionsBP[_positionId].isEnabled) revert InvalidPosition(_positionId);
    bytes32 holdingPositionId = keccak256(abi.encode(msg.sender, _positionId, _data));
    uint256 positionIndex = vault.isPositionUsed[holdingPositionId];
    if (positionIndex == 0 && removePosition) return type(uint256).max;
    if (removePosition) {
        if (positionIndex < vault.holdingPositions.length - 1) {
            vault.holdingPositions[positionIndex] = vault.holdingPositions[vault.holdingPositions.length - 1];
            vault.isPositionUsed[keccak256(
                abi.encode(
                    vault.holdingPositions[positionIndex].calculatorConnector,
                    vault.holdingPositions[positionIndex].positionId,
                    vault.holdingPositions[positionIndex].data
                )
            )] = positionIndex;
        }
@>      vault.holdingPositions.pop();
        vault.isPositionUsed[holdingPositionId] = 0;
        emit HoldingPositionUpdated(vaultId, _positionId, _data, additionalData, removePosition, positionIndex);
        return type(uint256).max;
    }
    return
        updateHoldingPosition(vault, vaultId, _positionId, _data, additionalData, positionIndex, holdingPositionId);
}

```

## Impact

When all of the connector's available funds are deposited into specific protocol, the holding position is removed from the registry. As a result, the liquidity provided to the protocol is not included in the `TVL`, leading to a significant decrease in the `TVL`, which will break other functions that are dependent on it.

## Proof of Concept

The given example is for the AaveConnector, but the issue also occurs in all other connectors.

The scenario shown in this POC is:

- Alice deposits `10 * amount` into `AccountingManager` - the `TVL` here is 0
- Strategy manager calculates `calculateDepositShares` and executes `executeDeposit` - here the `TVL` is `10 * amount`
- Strategy manager calls [AaveConnector.supply](http://AaveConnector.supplyhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/connectors/AaveConnector.sol#L46-L54) to transfer `5 * amount` to AAVE - the `TVL` remains unchanged
- Strategy manager calls [AaveConnector.supply](http://AaveConnector.supplyhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/connectors/AaveConnector.sol#L46-L54) again to transfer the remaining `5 * amount` to AAVE

There lies the problem. When all of the connector's available funds are deposited into AAVE, the holding position is removed from the registry. As a result, it is not included in the `TVL`, leading to a significant decrease in the `TVL`.

Also, as shown in the test, the next deposits will result in wrong `TVL`. After the initial holding position removal, the `TVL` will be double the deposited money.

_Place the following test in_ [testFoundry/SupplyAllPOC.t.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/tree/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/testFoundry) and run it with the command `forge test --mt testSupplyAll`

