```

Initially, three connectors each have one USDC holding position, with indices 1, 2, and 3, respectively. After the first connector transfers its holding position to the third connector using the `transferPositionToAnotherConnector` function, the balance of the first connector becomes zero, triggering the removal of its holding position. The removal logic replaces the position with the last holding position, but the incorrect calculation causes errors in indexing.

