# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Using both `Chainlink` and `Uniswap` will make the `minAmount` calculations in swaps exposed to sandwich attacks due to the difference in asset prices.

## Proof of Concept

In cases when there is no direct price feed between token A and token D, **multiple price sources** should be added to calculate the price of token D in terms of token A:

[NoyaValueOracle.sol#L81-L93](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/NoyaValueOracle.sol#L81-L93)

```solidity
function _getValue(address asset, address baseToken, uint256 amount, address[] memory sources)
    internal
    view
    returns (uint256 value)
{
    uint256 initialValue = amount;
    address quotingToken = asset;
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < sources.length; i++) {
        initialValue = _getValue(asset, sources[i], initialValue);//NOTE if Uniswap is mixed with Chainlink we can receive big deviations
        quotingToken = sources[i];
    }
    return _getValue(quotingToken, baseToken, initialValue);
}
```

When calculating prices from both `Chainlink` and `Uniswap` in times of moderate to high volatility there will be numerous of issues that will arise in the system because `Uniswap` uses TWAP that updates his price relatively slow compared to Chainlink. 

From the following [article](https://smartcontentpublication.medium.com/twap-oracles-vs-chainlink-price-feeds-a-comparative-analysis-8155a3483cbd):

```solidity
**Price Precision**
- TWAP is a lagging indicator that becomes out of sync with the market-wide price during times of moderate to high volatility, leading to inaccurate data being consumed by smart contracts that put protocols at risk of under-collateralization.
- Chainlink Price Feeds use a Volume Weighted Average Price (VWAP) to deliver accurate, real-time financial market data regardless of market volatility.
```

Looking at `GenericSwapAndBridgeHandler::executeSwap` which will be used from the connectors to swap **any assets** we can see that the price of the `token D` is calculated automatically without giving the function caller to specify it**:**

[BaseConnector.sol#L204-L223](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/BaseConnector.sol#L204-L223)

```solidity
function swapHoldings(
    address[] memory tokensIn,
    address[] memory tokensOut,
    uint256[] memory amountsIn,
    bytes[] memory swapData,
    uint256[] memory routeIds
) external onlyManager nonReentrant {
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < tokensIn.length; i++) {
        _executeSwap(
            SwapRequest(address(this), routeIds[i], amountsIn[i], tokensIn[i], tokensOut[i], swapData[i], true, 0)//@audit last 2 arguments are related to slippage, checkForSlippage and minAmount respectivelly
        );
        _updateTokenInRegistry(tokensIn[i]);
        _updateTokenInRegistry(tokensOut[i]);
        emit SwapHoldings(tokensIn[i], tokensOut[i], amountsIn[i], swapData[i]);
    }
}

function _executeSwap(SwapRequest memory swapRequest) internal returns (uint256 amountOut) {
    amountOut = swapHandler.executeSwap(swapRequest);
}
```

[GenericSwapAndBridgeHandler.sol#L90-L120](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/SwapHandler/GenericSwapAndBridgeHandler.sol#L90-L120)

```solidity
  function executeSwap(SwapRequest memory _swapRequest)
      external
      payable
      onlyEligibleUser
      onlyExistingRoute(_swapRequest.routeId)
      nonReentrant
      returns (uint256 _amountOut)
  {
      if (_swapRequest.amount == 0) revert InvalidAmount();
      RouteData memory swapImplInfo = routes[_swapRequest.routeId];
      if (swapImplInfo.isBridge) revert RouteNotAllowedForThisAction();

      if (_swapRequest.checkForSlippage && _swapRequest.minAmount == 0) {
          // set minAmount so that slippage can be checked
          uint256 _slippageTolerance = slippageTolerance[_swapRequest.inputToken][_swapRequest.outputToken]; //ISSUE when 2 Uniswap and Chainlink are combined this will have to be set to big number, TWAP is lagging with prices
          if (_slippageTolerance == 0) {
              _slippageTolerance = genericSlippageTolerance;
          }
          INoyaValueOracle _priceOracle = INoyaValueOracle(valueOracle);
          uint256 _outputTokenValue =
              _priceOracle.getValue(_swapRequest.inputToken, _swapRequest.outputToken, _swapRequest.amount);

          _swapRequest.minAmount = (((1e6 - _slippageTolerance) * _outputTokenValue) / 1e6);
      }

      _amountOut = ISwapAndBridgeImplementation(swapImplInfo.route).performSwapAction(msg.sender, _swapRequest);

      emit ExecutionCompleted(
          _swapRequest.routeId, _swapRequest.amount, _amountOut, _swapRequest.inputToken, _swapRequest.outputToken
      );
  }
```

From here we can clearly see that the `_outputTokenValue` will be highly **unsatisfactory** number due to the price difference in between `Uniswap` and `Chainlink`. Simple example is the difference in prices between the 2 sources in one of the most stable assets: `ETH/USD` :

### Chainlink

![Screenshot1](https://i.imgur.com/6VHf5Nh.png)

### Uniswap

![Screenshot2](https://i.imgur.com/pAIGzpA.png)

> Differences will be even more in times of high volatility and when pools with low liquidity are being used.
> 

The issue that will happen is that `swapHoldings` functions will be constantly sandwiched by MEV bots extracting value because of the innacurate `minAmount` calculation and the result will be loss of funds of connectors and decreased yield for all the positions in this particular vault.

To fix it there is a function which can update the period for which the prices are calculated in the `Uniswap` oracle but it is not sufficient because `maintainer` will be forced to set it to small number in order to minimise the difference, which exposes the **routes that use only this oracle to cheap pool price manipulations**. 

## Tools Used

Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider modifying the `BaseConnector::swapHoldings` to be able to pass `minAmount` parameter, and calculate the expected returned amount off-chain.

```diff
  function swapHoldings(
        address[] memory tokensIn,
        address[] memory tokensOut,
        uint256[] memory amountsIn,
        bytes[] memory swapData,
        uint256[] memory routeIds,
+       uint256 minAmount 
    ) external onlyManager nonReentrant {
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < tokensIn.length; i++) {
            _executeSwap(
-               SwapRequest(address(this), routeIds[i], amountsIn[i], tokensIn[i], tokensOut[i], swapData[i], true, 0)
+               SwapRequest(address(this), routeIds[i], amountsIn[i], tokensIn[i], tokensOut[i], swapData[i], true, minAmount)
            );
            _updateTokenInRegistry(tokensIn[i]);
            _updateTokenInRegistry(tokensOut[i]);
            emit SwapHoldings(tokensIn[i], tokensOut[i], amountsIn[i], swapData[i]);
        }
    }
```


