# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/NoyaValueOracle.sol#L89


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Erroneous `_getValue()` implementation causing TVL DOS or invalid TVL

## Proof of Concept
In NoyaValueOracle::_getValue, a token price is calculated in multiple steps (intermediate token oracles), which is implemented in a for-loop. 

The problem is this for-loop has incorrect quotingToken implementation and will always result in a wrong price.

Suppose this case: Asset -> TokenB -> TokenC -> Base. The intended iteration:  (Asset, TokenB) -> (TokenB, TokenC) ... However, current implementation will result in: (Asset, TokenB) -> (Asset, TokenC)...

```solidity
//contracts/helpers/valueOracle/NoyaValueOracle.sol
    function _getValue(address asset, address baseToken, uint256 amount, address[] memory sources)
        internal
        view
        returns (uint256 value)
    {
        uint256 initialValue = amount;
        address quotingToken = asset;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < sources.length; i++) {
            //@audit asset should be changed to quotingToken
|>          initialValue = _getValue(asset, sources[i], initialValue);
            quotingToken = sources[i];
        }
        return _getValue(quotingToken, baseToken, initialValue);
    }
```
(https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/NoyaValueOracle.sol#L89)

Based on the above example, (1) if (Asset, TokenC) oracle doesn't exist, [NoyaValueOracle::getValue](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/NoyaValueOracle.sol#L78) will revert, DOS parent TVL flows. (2) if (Asset, TokenC) oracle exists, the resulting `initialValue` will be incorrect, because (Asset, TokenC) will be calculated with the balance(previous `initialValue`) denominated in TokenB.

## Tools Used

Manual

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Change `asset` into `quotingToken`.



