# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/NoyaValueOracle.sol#L87-L89


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Can't accept a price that requires combining values from two or more oracles.

## Proof of Concept
_getValue is a function that returns the quantity of baseToken equal to the amount of asset.

In this case, revert may occur if there are more than two sources.

In the iteration, the value corresponding to the sources is put into the baseToken to calculate the value, and then the quotingToken is changed to the source token.

The next _getValue should get the value for quotingToken, but it will revert because the asset is passed as is.

Consider the following scenario

A → D If the path [A,B,C,D] needs to be calculated to get the price, then the sources will be [B,C].

Therefore, it would be called in the following order

_getValue(A,D,amount) → _getValue(A,B,result) → _getValue(A,C,result) → _getValue(C,D,result)

However, the third call, _getValue(A,C,result), will cause a revert because the price oracle does not exist.

The correct order is

_getValue(A,D,amount) → _getValue(A,B,result) → _getValue(B,C,result) → _getValue(C,D,result)

Below is a POC that reproduces the above situation.

```solidity
    function testRevertMultiplePath() public {
        vm.startPrank(owner);
        address[] memory assets = new address[](2);
        assets[0] = address(B);
        assets[1] = address(C);

        noyaOracle.updatePriceRoute(address(A), address(D), assets);

        addTokenToChainlinkOracle(address(A), address(B), address(A_B_FEED));
        addTokenToChainlinkOracle(address(B), address(C), address(B_C_FEED));
        addTokenToChainlinkOracle(address(C), address(D), address(C_D_FEED));

        addTokenToNoyaOracle(address(A), address(chainlinkOracle));
        addTokenToNoyaOracle(address(B), address(chainlinkOracle));
        addTokenToNoyaOracle(address(C), address(chainlinkOracle));
        addTokenToNoyaOracle(address(D), address(chainlinkOracle));

        console.log("----------- Test getValue ETH -----------");

        uint256 value = noyaOracle.getValue(address(A), address(D), 1e18); // @audit revert
    }
```

## Tools Used

VS Code

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

```solidity
    function _getValue(address asset, address baseToken, uint256 amount, address[] memory sources)
        internal
        view
        returns (uint256 value)
    {
        uint256 initialValue = amount;
        address quotingToken = asset;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < sources.length; i++) {
@>          initialValue = _getValue(quotingToken, sources[i], initialValue);
            quotingToken = sources[i];
        }
        return _getValue(quotingToken, baseToken, initialValue);
    }
```


