# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/helpers/SwapHandler/GenericSwapAndBridgeHandler.sol#L102-L113


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
1. When high slippage tolerance like the default 5% is set, mempool bots will profit from the swap transaction through sandwich attack.

2. When low slippage tolerance is set like 0.5% is set, a lot of transaction will revert during market turbulence when prices are not stable causing denail of service at the period of the turbulent price swing.


## Proof of Concept
The `minAmount` output is calculated onchain. The `genericSlippageTolerance` which is initially set to 5% is used on some ocassions. 

The 5% slippage tolerance is a very high amount that allows users lose 5% of their output tokens to sandwich attack. 

On the other hand setting very low slippage tolerance can cause most swap transactions to revert during market turbulence. 

Allow slippage tolerance to be flexible by allowing the slippage tolerance to be passed as input parameter to the `executeSwap` function. This way the frontend will handle the calculation and the user can modify their slippage tolerance at the moment.


Below is the slippage tolerance calculation onchain

```
File: GenericSwapAndBridgeHandler.sol
function executeSwap(SwapRequest memory _swapRequest)
        external
        payable
        onlyEligibleUser
        onlyExistingRoute(_swapRequest.routeId)
        nonReentrant
        returns (uint256 _amountOut)
    {
        if (_swapRequest.amount == 0) revert InvalidAmount();
        RouteData memory swapImplInfo = routes[_swapRequest.routeId];
        if (swapImplInfo.isBridge) revert RouteNotAllowedForThisAction();

        if (_swapRequest.checkForSlippage && _swapRequest.minAmount == 0) {
            // set minAmount so that slippage can be checked
            uint256 _slippageTolerance = slippageTolerance[_swapRequest.inputToken][_swapRequest.outputToken];
            if (_slippageTolerance == 0) {
                _slippageTolerance = genericSlippageTolerance;
            }
            INoyaValueOracle _priceOracle = INoyaValueOracle(valueOracle);
            uint256 _outputTokenValue =
                _priceOracle.getValue(_swapRequest.inputToken, _swapRequest.outputToken, _swapRequest.amount);

            _swapRequest.minAmount = (((1e6 - _slippageTolerance) * _outputTokenValue) / 1e6);
        }

        _amountOut = ISwapAndBridgeImplementation(swapImplInfo.route).performSwapAction(msg.sender, _swapRequest);

        emit ExecutionCompleted(
            _swapRequest.routeId, _swapRequest.amount, _amountOut, _swapRequest.inputToken, _swapRequest.outputToken
        );
    }

```

## Tools Used
Manual review


## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Allow the `minAmount` to be passed as input parameter so that frontend allows users set slippage which can be changed for any user.


