# Vulnerability details

## Summary

ChainlinkOracleConnector uses incorrect checks for checking returned oracle data

## Vulnerability Details

The function [getValueFromChainlinkFeed](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/oracles/ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol#L115-L135) assumes the same heartbeat (staleness period) of `2 hours` no matter what feed is being queried or what chain the feed is deployed on.

```
>>> uint256 public chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold = 2 hours;

```

However, different feeds on the same chain (i.e. ETH / USD, BTC / USD) use different heartbeats. Not only that but the same feeds across different chains use different heartbeats.

For example see the ETH / USD oracle heartbeats on different chains:

On Ethereum, the oracle will update the price data every [~1 hour](https://data.chain.link/feeds/ethereum/mainnet/eth-usd)
On Polygon, the oracle will update the price data every [~25 seconds](https://data.chain.link/feeds/polygon/mainnet/eth-usd)
On BNB (BSC), the oracle will update the price data every [~60 seconds](https://data.chain.link/feeds/bsc/mainnet/eth-usd)
On Optimism, the oracle will update the price data every [~20 minutes](https://data.chain.link/feeds/optimism/mainnet/eth-usd)
On Arbitrum, the oracle will update the price data every [~24 hours](https://data.chain.link/feeds/arbitrum/mainnet/eth-usd)
On Avalanche, the oracle will update the price data every [~24 hours](https://data.chain.link/feeds/avalanche/mainnet/eth-usd)

```
    function getValueFromChainlinkFeed(
        AggregatorV3Interface source, uint256 amountIn, uint256 sourceTokenUnit, bool isInverse
    ) public view returns (uint256) {

        int256 price;
        uint256 updatedAt;
        (, price,, updatedAt,) = source.latestRoundData();

        uint256 uintprice = uint256(price);

        // @audit : 2 hour threshold for all chainlink feeds
>>>     if (block.timestamp - updatedAt > chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold) {
            revert NoyaChainlinkOracle_DATA_OUT_OF_DATE();
        }
    // SOME CODE
    }
```

## Impact

Stale prices, if prices are incorrect it will negatively affect `depositing`, `withdrawing` and `TVL()` calculations

## Tools Used

Manual Review
Foundry Testing

## Recommendations

Consider creating a new data struct to hold more information about a feed than just it's address.
Currently only the address is stored in the `assetsSources` mapping when `setAssetSources()` is called to add a new trusted asset. Instead the new struct can be stored and retrieved when checking returned oracle data.


