# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/connectors/UNIv3Connector.sol#L127-L150


# Vulnerability details


# **Finding Description**
`_getPositionTVL` which is a core function used in calculating the current position TVL from uniswap has all the right logic but not importing the necessary module required to carry out the function implementation.

The `(uint160 sqrtPriceX96,,,,,,) = pool.slot0();` gets the the uniswap storage slot0 and returns the sqrtPriceX96, but in order to access uniswap storage, it is required to create an interface of the functions to be called in the calling contract which was rightly implemented by the protocol in `IUniswapV3Pool.sol";`.

The problem lies in the fact that the already created interface is not being imported in the `UNIv3Connector.sol` contract and makes it impossible to get the position Tvl when calling `_getPositionTVL`. 


<details><summary>Details</summary>

The contract has no access to this function from the interface `IUniswapV3Pool.sol` which is necessary for getting the `uint160 sqrtPriceX96`

```solidity
   function slot0() external view returns (uint160, int24, uint16, uint16, uint16, uint32, bool);
```

Here is the implementation where the `slot0` is being called 👇

```solidity
   function _getPositionTVL(HoldingPI memory p, address base) public view override returns (uint256 tvl) {
        PositionBP memory positionInfo = registry.getPositionBP(vaultId, p.positionId);
        uint256 tokenId = abi.decode(p.data, (uint256));
        (address token0, address token1) = abi.decode(positionInfo.data, (address, address));
        uint256 amount0;
        uint256 amount1;
        (int24 tL, int24 tU, uint24 fee) = abi.decode(p.additionalData, (int24, int24, uint24));
        {
            IUniswapV3Pool pool = IUniswapV3Pool(factory.getPool(token0, token1, fee));
            bytes32 key = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(positionManager, tL, tU));
            (uint128 liquidity,,, uint128 tokensOwed0, uint128 tokensOwed1) = pool.positions(key);

            // @audit slot0 cannot be accessed
            (uint160 sqrtPriceX96,,,,,,) = pool.slot0();
            (amount0, amount1) = LiquidityAmounts.getAmountsForLiquidity(
                sqrtPriceX96, TickMath.getSqrtRatioAtTick(tL), TickMath.getSqrtRatioAtTick(tU), liquidity
            );
            amount0 += tokensOwed0;
            amount1 += tokensOwed1;
        }

        tvl += valueOracle.getValue(token0, base, amount0);
        tvl += valueOracle.getValue(token1, base, amount1);
    }
```

</details>


