# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/oracles/ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol#L57


# Vulnerability details


## Impact
The incorrect validation logic in the `updateChainlinkPriceAgeThreshold` function allows setting the threshold to values outside the intended range of 1 day to 10 days as per the NATSPEC. This can lead to the use of outdated or incorrect price data.

## Proof of Concept
The current implementation of the `updateChainlinkPriceAgeThreshold` function checks if the threshold is between `1 hour and 10 days`, which is incorrect according to the NatSpec comments that state it should be between 1 day and 10 days.

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/oracles/ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol#L57

```solidity
/*
 * @notice Updates the threshold for the age of the price data
 * @param _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold The new threshold
 * @dev The threshold should be between 1 day and 10 days
 */
function updateChainlinkPriceAgeThreshold(uint256 _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold) external onlyMaintainer {
    if (_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold <= 1 hours || _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold >= 10 days) {
        revert NoyaChainlinkOracle_INVALID_INPUT();
    }
    chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold = _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold;
    emit ChainlinkPriceAgeThresholdUpdated(_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold);
}
```

The condition `if (_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold <= 1 hours || _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold >= 10 days)` is incorrect. It should be `if (_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold < 1 days || _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold > 10 days)` to match the intended range of 1 day to 10 days.


## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Update the validation logic in the `updateChainlinkPriceAgeThreshold` function to correctly check if the threshold is between 1 day and 10 days. Also, ensure the NatSpec comments accurately reflect this range.

```diff
/*
 * @notice Updates the threshold for the age of the price data
 * @param _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold The new threshold
 * @dev The threshold should be between 1 day and 10 days
 */
function updateChainlinkPriceAgeThreshold(uint256 _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold) external onlyMaintainer {
-      if (_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold <= 1 hours || _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold >= 10 days) {
+    if (_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold < 1 days || _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold > 10 days) {
        revert NoyaChainlinkOracle_INVALID_INPUT();
    }
    chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold = _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold;
    emit ChainlinkPriceAgeThresholdUpdated(_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold);
}
```




