# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/oracles/ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol#L14


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Currently, the ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol contract stores a staleness period timeout variable i.e. chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold, which is currently 2 hours but can be set in the range from 1 hours to 10 days.

The issue with this is that [different price feeds have different staleness thresholds](https://docs.chain.link/data-feeds/price-feeds/addresses?network=ethereum&page=1). Some might have 1 hour while the other can range upto 1 day.

If we take the example of AAVE/USD on mainnet, it has 1 hour as the heartbeat. But since our contract uses 2 hours as the staleness timeout, the price that had remained stale since an hour is not realized. This is problematic since stale prices would be used in case the [getValue()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/oracles/ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol#L89) function is called on the oracle contract in order to update the TVL or calculate minAmount for swaps. 

- [Connectors](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/tree/main/contracts/connectors) - Uses oracle to retrieve the holding position TVL in terms of the base token. Due to this issue, the TVL reported would be stale when updating the TVL from normal chains to the base chain.
 - [GenericSwapAndBridgeHandler](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/helpers/SwapHandler/GenericSwapAndBridgeHandler.sol#L90) - Uses oracle to determine the best output token amount, which is used to calculate the minimum amount out for slippage when swapping through LiFi. If the price returned is stale, the minAmountOut is set to an incorrect value, which can cause problems during swaps.

## Proof of Concept

Let's take the example of AAVE/USD:

1. When function [getValueFromChainlinkFeed()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/oracles/ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol#L115) is called, the following occurs:
 - On Line 127, the price of AAVE is retrieved in terms of USD.
 - On Line 129, the block.timestamp - updatedAt is used to check the time since the last update to the price feed was made. This is then checked to be greater than chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold i.e. 2 hours. 
 - But if block.timestamp - updatedAt is greater than 1 hour but less than 2 hours, the feed is technically stale according to chainlink but the contract still uses the stale price.
 - This causes stale prices to be used by the connectors for tvl updates and swap handlers for minAmount calculations.
