# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/oracles/ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol#L125-L127


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Connectors depending on the Chainlink oracle to calculate their positions' TVL will not be able to do so due to the low `chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold`, resulting in the entire vault (AccountingManager) not being able to calculate its TVL resulting in DOSed deposits as they depend on `TVL()`.
## Proof of Concept
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/oracles/ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol#L115-L135
```solidity
    function getValueFromChainlinkFeed(
        AggregatorV3Interface source,
        uint256 amountIn,
        uint256 sourceTokenUnit,
        bool isInverse
    ) public view returns (uint256) {
        int256 price;
        uint256 updatedAt;
        (, price,, updatedAt,) = source.latestRoundData();
        uint256 uintprice = uint256(price);
→       if (block.timestamp - updatedAt > chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold) {
            revert NoyaChainlinkOracle_DATA_OUT_OF_DATE();
        }
        if (price <= 0) {
            revert NoyaChainlinkOracle_PRICE_ORACLE_UNAVAILABLE(address(source), address(0), address(0));
        }
        if (isInverse) {
            return (amountIn * sourceTokenUnit) / uintprice;
        }
        return (amountIn * uintprice) / (sourceTokenUnit);
    }
```

The Chainlink oracle checks the 'age' of reported value from the price feed. However [not all price feeds have the same heartbeat](https://docs.chain.link/architecture-overview/architecture-decentralized-model?parent=dataFeeds#aggregator) (time between updates):

> Aggregators receive updates from the oracle network only when the **Deviation Threshold** or **Heartbeat Threshold** triggers an update during an aggregation round. The first condition that is met triggers an update to the data.
> – Deviation Threshold: A new aggregation round starts when a node identifies that the off-chain values deviate by more than the defined deviation threshold from the onchain value. Individual nodes monitor one or more data providers for each feed.
> – Heartbeat Threshold: A new aggregation round starts after a specified amount of time from the last update.

As can be seen, `chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold` is set to `2 hours` by default, which is a rather sensible value. However, most Chainlink price feeds have a heartbeat of 24 hours and a deviation of 1-2% and imposing the 2 hour threshold on them is rather improper, as they'll be considered stale by the ChainlinkOracleConnector when in fact they are functioning correctly.

On the other side, widening `chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold` to 24 hours would make no sense for price feeds with a lower timeframe heartbeat and such a high threshold would make no sense to them, allowing the consumption of stale prices, so the `chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold` makes general sense to be around the `2 hour` mark.
## Tools Used
Manual review
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Remove the price age check altogether or store different price age thresholds per aggregators address in a mapping.



