# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/helpers/valueOracle/oracles/ChainlinkOracleConnector.sol#L56-#L62


# Vulnerability details

## Vulnerability details
Function `updateChainlinkPriceAgeThreshold()` is used to update chainlink threshold of specific price feed:

    function updateChainlinkPriceAgeThreshold(uint256 _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold) external onlyMaintainer {
        if (_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold <= 1 hours || _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold >= 10 days) {  // <---
            revert NoyaChainlinkOracle_INVALID_INPUT();
        }
        chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold = _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold;
        emit ChainlinkPriceAgeThresholdUpdated(_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold);
    }

From that checking condition, it is considered that chainlink price must in range [1 hours; 10 days], but some price feed  have heartbeat very small like [USDC/USD](https://data.chain.link/feeds/polygon/mainnet/usdc-usd) is 30 seconds, [UNI/USD](https://data.chain.link/feeds/polygon/mainnet/uni-usd) is 30 seconds, limiting `chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold` must be at least 1 hour can lead to stale price returned

## Impact
Price feed with small heart beat that return stale price is still accepted because `chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold` is too big

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Remove that checking condition:

    function updateChainlinkPriceAgeThreshold(uint256 _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold) external onlyMaintainer {
     -  if (_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold <= 1 hours || _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold >= 10 days) {
     -      revert NoyaChainlinkOracle_INVALID_INPUT();
     -  }
        chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold = _chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold;
        emit ChainlinkPriceAgeThresholdUpdated(_chainlinkPriceAgeThreshold);
    }


