# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/helpers/SwapHandler/GenericSwapAndBridgeHandler.sol#L30


# Vulnerability details

## Description
The `SwapAndBridgeHandler` contract contains a logic error in the `onlyExistingRoute` modifier, which is intended to validate the existence and enablement of a route. The current logic fails to properly disable routes that the `isEnabled` have been set to `false`, leading to potential misuse.

The `onlyExistingRoute` modifier is defined as follows:
```solidity
modifier onlyExistingRoute(uint256 _routeId) {
    if (routes[_routeId].route == address(0) && !routes[_routeId].isEnabled) revert RouteNotFound();
    _;
}
```

However, this logic incorrectly allows routes that exist (i.e., `routes[_routeId].route != address(0)`) but have been disabled (`routes[_routeId].isEnabled = false`) to pass validation. As a result, disabled routes are still considered valid and can be executed by various functions such as `executeSwap`, `executeBridge`, and `verifyRoute`.

Here is the `setEnableRoute` function which is used to enable or disable a route:
```solidity
function setEnableRoute(uint256 _routeId, bool enable) external onlyMaintainerOrEmergency {
    routes[_routeId].isEnabled = enable;
    emit RouteUpdate(_routeId, false);
}
```

## Impact
The logic error allows disabled routes to be mistakenly treated as valid, enabling their execution. Thi could lead to potential misuse by managers, resulting in unintended and potentially risky operations. Specifically, the issue can impact the correct functioning of the `executeSwap`, `executeBridge`, and `verifyRoute` functions, leading to economic risks and other vulnerabilities.

## Proof of Concept
Below is a proof-of-concept test case that demonstrates the issue. The test modifies the `testSetterFunctions` function in the `testSwapHandler.sol` file to highlight the problem.

```solidity
function testSetterFunctions() public {
    uint256 _amount = 10 * 1e6;
    _dealWhale(baseToken, address(connector), USDC_Whale, _amount);
    vm.startPrank(owner);

    swapHandler.setValueOracle(address(noyaOracle));

    swapHandler.setGeneralSlippageTolerance(1000);
    swapHandler.setSlippageTolerance(USDC, WETH, 10_000);

    bytes memory _data =
        hex"";

    address[] memory tokensIn = new address[](1);
    address[] memory tokensOut = new address[](1);
    uint256[] memory amountsIn = new uint256[](1);
    bytes[] memory swapData = new bytes[](1);
    uint256[] memory routeIds = new uint256[](1);

    tokensIn[0] = USDC;
    tokensOut[0] = WETH;
    amountsIn[0] = _amount;
    routeIds[0] = 0;
    swapData[0] = _data;

    swapHandler.setEnableRoute(0, false);
    connector.swapHoldings(tokensIn, tokensOut, amountsIn, swapData, routeIds);
}
```

After disabling the route by setting `isEnabled` to `false`, the `swapHoldings` function of the connector contract is called:
```solidity
function swapHoldings(
    address[] memory tokensIn,
    address[] memory tokensOut,
    uint256[] memory amountsIn,
    bytes[] memory swapData,
    uint256[] memory routeIds
) external onlyManager nonReentrant {
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < tokensIn.length; i++) {
        _executeSwap(
            SwapRequest(address(this), routeIds[i], amountsIn[i], tokensIn[i], tokensOut[i], swapData[i], true, 0)
        );
        _updateTokenInRegistry(tokensIn[i]);
        _updateTokenInRegistry(tokensOut[i]);
        emit SwapHoldings(tokensIn[i], tokensOut[i], amountsIn[i], swapData[i]);
    }
}

function _executeSwap(SwapRequest memory swapRequest) internal returns (uint256 amountOut) {
    amountOut = swapHandler.executeSwap(swapRequest);
}
```

Despite the route being disabled, the erroneous validation logic allows the `executeSwap` function to complete.

## Tools Used
- Manua review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Correct the `onlyExistingRoute` modifier to properly validate both the existence and enablement of the route:

```solidity
modifier onlyExistingRoute(uint256 _routeId) {
    if (routes[_routeId].route == address(0) || !routes[_routeId].isEnabled) revert RouteNotFound();
    _;
}
```


