# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/connectors/GearBoxV3.sol#L62-L85


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Due to the unique nature of GearBox, it allows you to interact with other protocols such as Uniswap, Curve, Lido, EigenLayer, Yearn, Sushiswap, etc. through its Multicall feature.

NOYA also integrates with some of the integrations that GearBox does as well, but the connectors have a lot of restrictions in regards to trusted tokens, trusted positions, swaps, etc.

Since Gearbox's credit account basically serves as a smart contract wallet and `executeCommands` doesn't employ any restrictions in terms of tokens, positions, as well as circuit-breakers related to health factor, this can be utilized for many non-allowed activities:

- Swapping tokens which aren't trusted.
- Investing/staking/depositing into different strategies which haven't been approved by the Vault Maintainer.
- Borrowing untrusted assets, considering that the LTV ration on Gearbox ranges between 0% to 90%+, this can be dangerous and lead to immediate liquidations.
- Withdrawing unapproved tokens, which were swapped on third-party integrations through Gearbox utilizing Multicall.
- Utilizing Gearbox to interact with unapproved tokens/strategies on integrations that are also connectors on NOYA, such as Curve, Lido, Uniswap, etc.


## Proof of Concept
When it comes to Gearbox, according to their documentation:

"Gearbox is a generalized leverage protocol: it allows anyone to take leverage in a DeFi-native way and then use it across various DeFi protocols. You take leverage with Gearbox and then use it on other protocols. For example, you can leverage trade on Uniswap, leverage farm on Yearn or Curve and Convex, make complex delta-neutral strategies involving options and derivatives, get Leverage-as-a-Service for your structured product doing complex positions, etc."

https://dev.gearbox.fi/intro

The prerequisite for interacting with Gearbox is opening a Credit account:

```
 function openAccount(address facade, uint256 ref) public onlyManager {
        address c = ICreditFacadeV3(facade).openCreditAccount(address(this), new MultiCall[](0), ref);
        registry.updateHoldingPosition(
            vaultId,
            registry.calculatePositionId(address(this), GEARBOX_POSITION_ID, abi.encode(facade)),
            abi.encode(c),
            "",
            false
        );
        emit OpenAccount(facade, ref);
    }
```

The credit account on Gearbox, according to its documentation serves as a smart contract:

"A Credit Account is an isolated smart contract which contains both the user funds and the borrowed funds. This is where your leverage is. After you open an account, all the operations go through this account and the assets stay on it as well. You can see a Credit Account as your automated DeFi wallet where you not only keep positions, but can also potentially program it the way you want.

Funds on Credit Accounts are used as collateral for debt, and users can operate these funds by sending financial orders to their Credit Accounts. That could be: margin trading on Uniswap or Sushiswap; leverage farming on Yearn; arbitraging pegged assets on Curve, and more!"

Taking this into consideration, once the account is opened, the `executeCommands` function on the Gearbox connector can be utilized for basically anything, and any kind of interaction:

```
 function executeCommands(
        address facade,
        address creditAccount,
        MultiCall[] calldata calls,
        address approvalToken,
        uint256 amount
    ) public onlyManager nonReentrant {
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < calls.length; i++) {
            if (calls[i].target != facade) revert IConnector_InvalidTarget(calls[i].target);
            bytes4 method = bytes4(calls[i].callData[:4]);

            if (method == ICreditFacadeV3Multicall.enableToken.selector) {
                (address token) = abi.decode(calls[i].callData[4:], (address));
                _updateTokenInRegistry(token);
            }
        }
        if (approvalToken != address(0)) {
            _approveOperations(approvalToken, ICreditFacadeV3(facade).creditManager(), amount);
        }
        ICreditFacadeV3(facade).multicall(creditAccount, calls);
        if (approvalToken != address(0)) {
            _revokeApproval(approvalToken, ICreditFacadeV3(facade).creditManager());
        }
        emit ExecuteCommands(facade, creditAccount, calls, approvalToken, amount);
    }
```

According to the Gearbox documentation, Multicalls can do anything on the Gearbox protocol:

"Multicalls are the main way Credit Accounts are managed by their owners in Gearbox. They essentially are a sequence of specifically encoded (target, calldata) that correspond to various actions, such as managing credit account's debt, adding collateral, or interacting with external protocols. The sequence is submitted to the Credit Facade, which instructs the Credit Manager and the adapters to perform required actions with the Credit Account."

https://dev.gearbox.fi/core/multicall

From this point forward we can utilize Muticall to perform any call(s) we want:
- Swap unallowed/untrusted tokens on Uniswap.
- Borrow all kinds of tokens.
- Stake into unallowed strategies, etc.

For example, here is a list of allowed tokens that can be swapped/borrowed/interacted with on Gearbox by leveraging the integrations:

https://docs.gearbox.finance/overview/credit-account/allowedlist-integrations

Some of those have a liquidation threshold of 0%, and there are no health checks utilized on a connector level to make sure that after the Multicall execution is finished that the health factor is still healthy.

Besides this there are no utilizations of any kind of checks related to the trusted tokens, positions, etc. as it is the standard with other protocols. 


## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Utilize trusted token/position checks, as well as check the health status of the account. Many of these checks can be leveraged through querying the Account Data on the Gearbox account, more info: 

https://dev.gearbox.fi/credit/account-data


