# Vulnerability details

## ISSUE

In [`Registry.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/accountingManager/Registry.sol#L32-L36), the modifier `onlyVaultMaintainer` is used in several important functions to restrict access to who can call such functions. It performs checks to ensure the caller is either the vault maintainer **OR** has the `EMERGENCY_ROLE` role. The issue is that the modifier uses a logical OR (`||`) instead of a logical AND (`&&`) which flaws the logic thus causing all calls performed by the modifier to revert.

```solidity
      modifier onlyVaultMaintainer(uint256 _vaultId) {
        if (msg.sender != vaults[_vaultId].maintainer || hasRole(EMERGENCY_ROLE, msg.sender) == false) {    //@audit-issue - || used here instead of &&. This modifier will cause a revert in the functions that uses it.
            revert UnauthorizedAccess();
        }
        _;
    }
```

The `||` operator is used to combine two conditions, where if either/one (or both) of the conditions evaluates to `true`, then the whole expression evaluates to `true`. Analyzing the conditions:

a. `msg.sender != vaults[_vaultId].maintainer`: This condition checks if the `msg.sender` (caller) is not the maintainer of the vault. If `msg.sender` is not the maintainer, this condition evaluates to `true`. If the `msg.sender` is indeed the maintainer, the condition evaluates to `false` (i.e. it fails because `msg.sender` == maintainer).

b. `hasRole(EMERGENCY_ROLE, msg.sender) == false`: This condition checks if the `msg.sender` does not have the `EMERGENCY_ROLE`. If `msg.sender` does not have this role, the condition evaluates to `true`. If `msg.sender` has this role, the condition evaluates to `false`.

**CASE 1** - Caller is maintainer:
Then condition "a" is `false` (caller is maintainer so it fails), while "b" is `true` (maintainer/caller does not have role. Only emergency address has this role). Overall: `false` || `true` = `true`.

**CASE 2** - Caller has the emergency role:
Then condition "a" is `true` (caller is not maintainer so it passes), while "b" = `false` (caller has emergency role). Overall: `true` || `false` = `true`.

Since both cases will either evaluate to `true` the modifier will always execute the code in the `if` block i.e. `revert Unauthorized();`, which will cause any function using the `onlyVaultMaintainer` modifier to revert.

![Failed Test onlyVaultMaintainer Modifier](<Screenshot 2024-05-04 025251.png>)

Similar modifier uses `&&` and does not have this issue:

```solidity
    modifier onlyVaultMaintainerWithoutTimeLock(uint256 _vaultId) {
        if (msg.sender != vaults[_vaultId].maintainerWithoutTimeLock && hasRole(EMERGENCY_ROLE, msg.sender) == false) {
            revert UnauthorizedAccess();
        }
        _;
    }

    modifier onlyVaultGoverner(uint256 _vaultId) {
        if (msg.sender != vaults[_vaultId].governer && hasRole(EMERGENCY_ROLE, msg.sender) == false) {
            revert UnauthorizedAccess();
        }
        _;
    }
```

Below is a tabular guide of the behavior of Logical Operators (`&&` and `||`) in `if` statements:

| Condition A | Condition B | A `&&` B Result | A `\|\|` B Result | Execution of `if {…}` Block for `&&`                       | Execution of `if {…}` Block for `\|\|`                     |
| ----------- | ----------- | --------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| true        | true        | true            | true              | Execute the code within the if statement block             | Execute the code within the if statement block             |
| true        | false       | false           | true              | Do not execute/ Move to subsequent code after if statement | Execute the code within the if statement block             |
| false       | true        | false           | true              | Do not execute/ Move to subsequent code after if statement | Execute the code within the if statement block             |
| false       | false       | false           | false             | Do not execute/ Move to subsequent code after if statement | Do not execute/ Move to subsequent code after if statement |

