# Vulnerability details

## Impact
CompoundConnector.sol calls the `getPrice` function in comet to query the latest prices. The `getPrice` function in comet, uses chainlink's `latestRoundData` but only checks that the returned price is not <= 0. It doesn't verify the freshness of the returned data based on the timestamp. This causes that integrators, including CompoundConnector.sol is at risk of using stale or outdated price data is used in significant financial calculations or decision-making processes. 

## Proof of Concept

The function queries `comet.getPrice` in two different places, the `getBorrowBalanceInBase` function
```solidity
    function getBorrowBalanceInBase(IComet comet) public view returns (uint256 borrowBalanceInVirtualBase) {
        ...
        uint256 basePriceInVirtualBase = comet.getPrice(basePriceFeed);
        borrowBalanceInVirtualBase = (borrowBalanceInBase * basePriceInVirtualBase) / comet.baseScale();
    }
```
and the `getCollBlanace` function.
```solidity
    function getCollBlanace(IComet comet, bool riskAdjusted) public view returns (uint256 CollValue) {
        IComet.UserBasic memory userBasic = comet.userBasic(address(this));
        uint16 assetsIn = userBasic.assetsIn;
        uint256 basePrice = comet.getPrice(comet.baseTokenPriceFeed());
        ...
                uint256 collateralPriceInVirtualBase = comet.getPrice(info.priceFeed);

                uint256 collateralValueInVirtualBase =
                    collateralBalance * collateralPriceInVirtualBase * baseScale / info.scale / basePrice;
                if (riskAdjusted) CollValue += collateralValueInVirtualBase * info.liquidateCollateralFactor / 1e18;
                else CollValue += collateralValueInVirtualBase;
            } // else user collateral is zero.
        }
    }
```
These values are used extensively in the contract to determine position tvl, updating position holding, account health factors and so on, hence, the values should be as accurate as possible.

But the `getPrice` function in Comet.sol looks like this; only reverting when price is <= 0, potentially allowing stale prices.
```solidity
    function getPrice(address priceFeed) override public view returns (uint256) {
        (, int price, , , ) = IPriceFeed(priceFeed).latestRoundData();
        if (price <= 0) revert BadPrice();
        return uint256(price);
    }
```

Same can be observed in some of the [provided](https://github.com/compound-finance/comet/tree/b303912ded46f7feb00286964e733b31c6bc30f3/contracts/pricefeeds) pricefeeds, [WBTCPriceFeed.sol](https://github.com/compound-finance/comet/blob/b303912ded46f7feb00286964e733b31c6bc30f3/contracts/pricefeeds/WBTCPriceFeed.sol#L64-L73) for instance; in which stale prices are also acceptable.

```solidity
    function latestRoundData() override external view returns (uint80, int256, uint256, uint256, uint80) {
        (, int256 WBTCToBTCPrice, , , ) = AggregatorV3Interface(WBTCToBTCPriceFeed).latestRoundData();
        (uint80 roundId_, int256 BTCToUSDPrice, uint256 startedAt_, uint256 updatedAt_, uint80 answeredInRound_) = AggregatorV3Interface(BTCToUSDPriceFeed).latestRoundData();

        // We return the round data of the BTC / USD price feed because of its shorter heartbeat (1hr vs 24hr)
        if (WBTCToBTCPrice <= 0 || BTCToUSDPrice <= 0) return (roundId_, 0, startedAt_, updatedAt_, answeredInRound_);

        int256 price = WBTCToBTCPrice * BTCToUSDPrice * priceFeedScale / combinedScale;
        return (roundId_, price, startedAt_, updatedAt_, answeredInRound_);
    }
```

## Tools Used
Manual code review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
I'd recommend not using the provided feed at all, or directly quering chainlink for the token prices, and checking for stale price. A modified comet contract may also be created, mirroring comet's own implementation, but with the addition of a stale price check.


