# Vulnerability details

## Title
SiloConnector and other lending related connectors `_getPositionTVL()` may revert in underflow and make tvl query revert and block deposit

## Line of code
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/connectors/Dolomite.sol#L106

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/connectors/SiloConnector.sol#L109

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/connectors/PrismaConnector.sol#L145

## Impact
The `_getPositionTVL()` in SiloConnector, Dolomite and PrismaConnector is used to calculate the TVL of a position. The TVL is calculated at the last line from totalCollateral subtracted totalDebt as `tvl = totalDepositAmount - totalBAmount;`. This implementation might lead to `_getPositionTVL()` revert if when the position is liquidated. 

If position is liquidated the `totalDepositAmount` will become lesser than the borrow amount leading to underflow in the `tvl = totalDepositAmount - totalBAmount;` line. The same applies with the prisma connector and dolomite. The impact of this `_getPositionTVL()` revert will block the deposit in [AccountManager::Deposit()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/accountingManager/AccountingManager.sol#L211):

```solidity
    function deposit(address receiver, uint256 amount, address referrer) public nonReentrant whenNotPaused {
        ...
        ...

@>      if (TVL() > depositLimitTotalAmount) {
            revert NoyaAccounting_TotalDepositLimitExceeded();
        }
        ...
        ...
    }
```

## Proof of Concept
We are adding all the three instances here one by one:

1. [SiloConnector::_getPositionTVL()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/connectors/SiloConnector.sol#L109C1-L128C6): Here the TVL calculation is followed as `tvl = totalDepositAmount - totalBAmount;` which will revert due to underflow if position is liquidated.
```solidity
    function _getPositionTVL(HoldingPI memory p, address base) public view override returns (uint256 tvl) {
        PositionBP memory bp = registry.getPositionBP(vaultId, p.positionId);
        (address siloToken) = abi.decode(bp.data, (address));
        ISilo silo = ISilo(siloRepository.getSilo(siloToken));
        (address[] memory assets, IBaseSilo.AssetStorage[] memory assetsS) = silo.getAssetsWithState();
        uint256 totalDepositAmount = 0;
        uint256 totalBAmount = 0;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < assets.length; i++) {
            uint256 depositAmount = IERC20(assetsS[i].collateralToken).balanceOf(address(this));
            depositAmount += IERC20(assetsS[i].collateralOnlyToken).balanceOf(address(this));
            uint256 borrowAmount = IERC20(assetsS[i].debtToken).balanceOf(address(this));
            if (depositAmount == 0 && borrowAmount == 0) {
                continue;
            }
            uint256 price = _getValue(assets[i], base, 1e18);
            totalDepositAmount += depositAmount * price / 1e18;
            totalBAmount += borrowAmount * price / 1e18;
        }
@>      tvl = totalDepositAmount - totalBAmount;
    }
```

2. [Dolomit::_getPositionTVL()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/connectors/Dolomite.sol#L106C1-L122C6): Here the TVL calculation is followed as `return totalCollateral - totalDebt;` if position is liquidated, the collateral is decrease and will be lesser than total debt, resulting underflow revert of TVL calculation.

```solidity
    function _getPositionTVL(HoldingPI memory p, address base) public view override returns (uint256 tvl) {
        uint256 accountId = abi.decode(p.data, (uint256));

        (uint256[] memory markets, address[] memory tokens,, Types.Wei[] memory amounts) =
            dolomiteMargin.getAccountBalances(Info(address(this), accountId));
        uint256 totalDebt = 0;
        uint256 totalCollateral = 0;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < markets.length; i++) {
            uint256 value = valueOracle.getValue(tokens[i], base, amounts[i].value);
            if (amounts[i].sign) {
                totalCollateral += value;
            } else {
                totalDebt += value;
            }
        }
@>      return totalCollateral - totalDebt;
    }
```

3. [PrismaConnector::_getPositionTVL()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/main/contracts/connectors/PrismaConnector.sol#L145C1-L156C6): Here the TVL calculation is followed as `_getValue(collateral, base, collateralBalance) - _getValue(debTtoken, base, debtBalance);` 

if position is liquidated, the collateral is decrease and will be lesser than total debt, resulting underflow revert of TVL calculation.

or depends on the token price change, debtBalance can be greater than collateral balance.

```solidity
    function _getPositionTVL(HoldingPI memory p, address base) public view override returns (uint256 tvl) {
        PositionBP memory positionInfo = registry.getPositionBP(vaultId, p.positionId);
        if (positionInfo.positionTypeId == PRISMA_POSITION_ID) {
            (address zap, address troveManager) = abi.decode(positionInfo.data, (address, address));
            IBorrowerOperations borrowerOperations = IStakeNTroveZap(zap).borrowerOps();
            address collateral = borrowerOperations.troveManagersData(troveManager).collateralToken;
            address debTtoken = ITroveManager(troveManager).debtToken();
            (uint256 collateralBalance, uint256 debtBalance) =
                ITroveManager(troveManager).getTroveCollAndDebt(address(this));
@>          return _getValue(collateral, base, collateralBalance) - _getValue(debTtoken, base, debtBalance);
        }
    }
```

the problem is that when deposit, the code query the tvl and the tvl queries the tvl of each connector, and if one connector get position value revert in underflow

all deposit get blocked

