# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Underflow revert will DOS TVL() flows in the accounting manager

## Proof of Concept
Multiple connectors provide supply and borrowing through an external market (e.g. aave). However, the calculation of positionTVL of collateral value and debt value is vulnerable to underflow under certain external market conditions. 

For example, in [AaveConnector::_getPositionTVL](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/connectors/AaveConnector.sol#L116), `totalDebtBase` is directly subtracted from `totalCollateralBase` value without checking for underflow risks. 

This assumes `totalDebtBase` <= `totalCollateralBase` at all times. This cannot be guaranteed during volatile collateral /debt asset price movements. And before liquidation in external market is executed,  `_getPositionTVL` will revert, DOS all flows that consume [AccountingManager::TVL](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/accountingManager/AccountingManager.sol#L627)(including [deposit()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/accountingManager/AccountingManager.sol#L211), [totalAssets()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/accountingManager/AccountingManager.sol#L591), calculateDepositShares(),  calculateWithdrawShares(), getProfit(), recordProfitForFee(), etc)

See below for vulnerable implementation instances:
(1)
```solidity
