# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Deposit and withdraw process can be DOSed by under-collateralized connector.

## Proof of Concept
`AaveConnector.sol#_getPositionTVL` function is as follows.
```solidity
    function _getPositionTVL(HoldingPI memory, address base) public view override returns (uint256 tvl) {
        (uint256 totalCollateralBase, uint256 totalDebtBase,,,,) = IPool(pool).getUserAccountData(address(this));
116     uint256 poolBaseAmount = totalCollateralBase - totalDebtBase;
        return valueOracle.getValue(poolBaseToken, base, poolBaseAmount);
    }
```
As you can see above, in some cases such as under-collateralized condition, it can be `totalCollateralBase < totalDebtBase` and `_getPositionTVL()` is reverted.   
Therefore, `calculateDepositShares() and calculateWithdrawShares()` of `AccountingManager` linked to this connector can be DOSed.   
In fact, the path of call is as follows.   
`calculateDepositShares() and calculateWithdrawShares()`=>`previewDeposit(), previewRedeem()` => `AccountingManager.sol#totalAssets()`=>`AccountingManager.sol#TVL()`=>`TVLHelper.sol#getTVL()`=>`BaseConnector.sol#getPositionTVL()`=>`AaveConnector.sol#_getPositionTVL()`   
This problem exists in several another contracts such as `CompoundConnector`.

## Tools Used

Manual Review


## Recommended Mitigation Steps
We have to fix this problem for several connectors such as `AaveConnector.sol`.
For example, `AaveConnector.sol#_getPositionTVL()` function has to be modified as follows.
```solidity
    function _getPositionTVL(HoldingPI memory, address base) public view override returns (uint256 tvl) {
        (uint256 totalCollateralBase, uint256 totalDebtBase,,,,) = IPool(pool).getUserAccountData(address(this));
+       if(totalCollateralBase < totalDebtBase) return 0;
        uint256 poolBaseAmount = totalCollateralBase - totalDebtBase;
        return valueOracle.getValue(poolBaseToken, base, poolBaseAmount);
    }
```


