# Vulnerability details

[SiloConnector::_getPositionTVL()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-noya/blob/9c79b332eff82011dcfa1e8fd51bad805159d758/contracts/connectors/SiloConnector.sol#L109-L128)

### Description
NOYA uses connectors to interact with other protocols. Also in each connector there is a function present to calculate the total value locked in the protocol.
In the `SiloConnector` the function to calculate the position is as follows
<details>

```javascript
    function _getPositionTVL(HoldingPI memory p, address base) public view override returns (uint256 tvl) {
        PositionBP memory bp = registry.getPositionBP(vaultId, p.positionId);
        (address siloToken) = abi.decode(bp.data, (address));
        ISilo silo = ISilo(siloRepository.getSilo(siloToken));
        (address[] memory assets, IBaseSilo.AssetStorage[] memory assetsS) = silo.getAssetsWithState();
        uint256 totalDepositAmount = 0;
        uint256 totalBAmount = 0;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < assets.length; i++) {
            uint256 depositAmount = IERC20(assetsS[i].collateralToken).balanceOf(address(this));
            depositAmount += IERC20(assetsS[i].collateralOnlyToken).balanceOf(address(this));
            uint256 borrowAmount = IERC20(assetsS[i].debtToken).balanceOf(address(this));
            if (depositAmount == 0 && borrowAmount == 0) {
                continue;
            }
            uint256 price = _getValue(assets[i], base, 1e18);
            totalDepositAmount += depositAmount * price / 1e18;
            totalBAmount += borrowAmount * price / 1e18;
        }
        tvl = totalDepositAmount - totalBAmount;
    }
```

</details>

It gets a list of assets that are 'active' in the silo:
```javascript
(address[] memory assets, IBaseSilo.AssetStorage[] memory assetsS) = silo.getAssetsWithState();
```
Then it iterates over them and depending on the type of the position (**borrow** or **deposit**) adds it to a variable for the corresponding position multiplied by the price of the token.
```javascript
    uint256 price = _getValue(assets[i], base, 1e18);
    totalDepositAmount += depositAmount * price / 1e18;
    totalBAmount += borrowAmount * price / 1e18;
```

At the end the TVL is calculated by subtracting the total borrow amount from the total deposited amount 
```javascript
    tvl = totalDepositAmount - totalBAmount;
```

This however is problematic since if `totalDepositAmount` < `totalBAmount` the transaction would revert due to underflow.
This will occur in scenarios where the price of the borrowed asset goes up fast and/or the price of the collateral asset crashes, which is pretty common in the volatile market of crypto.

Going up the call stack the `_getPositionTVL()` function is used to calculate the TVL and ensure the total deposit limit is not surpassed.

`SiloConnector::_getPositionTVL()` is called by `BaseConnector::getPositionTVL()`.
`BaseConnector::getPositionTVL()` in turn is called by `TVLHelper::getTVL()` to calculate the TVL for a vault's positions in the registry
```javascript
    function getTVL(uint256 vaultId, PositionRegistry registry, address baseToken) public view returns (uint256) {
        uint256 totalTVL;
        uint256 totalDebt;
        HoldingPI[] memory positions = registry.getHoldingPositions(vaultId);
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < positions.length; i++) {
            if (positions[i].calculatorConnector == address(0)) {
                continue;
            }
=>          uint256 tvl = IConnector(positions[i].calculatorConnector).getPositionTVL(positions[i], baseToken);
            bool isPositionDebt = registry.isPositionDebt(vaultId, positions[i].positionId);
            if (isPositionDebt) {
                totalDebt += tvl;
            } else {
                totalTVL += tvl;
            }
        }
        if (totalTVL < totalDebt) {
            return 0;
        }
        return (totalTVL - totalDebt);
    }
```

`TVLHelper::getTVL()` is called by `AccountingManager::TVL()`
```javascript
function TVL() public view returns (uint256) { // holding positions (from connectors) + baseToken balance - deposits in deposit queue
    return TVLHelper.getTVL(vaultId, registry, address(baseToken)) + baseToken.balanceOf(address(this))
        - depositQueue.totalAWFDeposit;
}
```
which is used in `AccountingManager::deposit()` to ensure the total deposit limit is not reached.
```javascript
    function deposit(address receiver, uint256 amount, address referrer) public nonReentrant whenNotPaused {
...

=>      if (TVL() > depositLimitTotalAmount) {
            revert NoyaAccounting_TotalDepositLimitExceeded();
        }

...
    }
```
This means that if underflow occurs the `deposit()` function would revert and users would not be able to deposit funds in the protocol.
Also, the `TVL()` to in the `totalAssets()` function which according to EIP-4626 Must not revert https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-4626#totalassets

### Root Cause
Math, Underflow

### Impact
Users would be unable to deposit tokens in the protocol

### PoC
For the PoC we are using USDC and WETH, but it could be any other pair. <br>
Add the following test to `SiloConnector.t.sol` and run with `forge test --mt test_getPositionTVLUnderflow -vvv`
```javascript
function test_getPositionTVLUnderflow() public {        
    // Get value of 1 WETH in USDC
    uint256 wethPrice = chainlinkOracle.getValue(address(WETH), address(840), 1 ether);
    console.log("weth price :", wethPrice); // 2903,25841858

    // Deal a bit more (15%) USDC than the amount of 2 ETH. Mul by 23 and div by 10 so we deposit 115% USDC per ETH - 23/2 ETH = 1.15
    uint256 _amount = wethPrice * 23 / 100 / 10; // Divide by 100 because oracle price is 8 dec and USDC is 6. 
    console.log("USDC deposited:", _amount);

    _dealWhale(baseToken, address(connector), USDC_Whale, _amount);

    vm.startPrank(address(owner));

    // siloToken, deposit token, amount, open position
    connector.deposit(USDC, USDC, _amount, true);

    // siloToken, borrow token, amount
    connector.borrow(USDC, WETH, 2e18);

    bytes32 positionId = registry.calculatePositionId(address(connector), connector.SILO_LP_ID(), abi.encode(USDC));
    HoldingPI memory holdingPI = HoldingPI(
        address(0),
        address(0),
        positionId,
        bytes(""),
        bytes(""),
        0
    );

    // Mock the next call to the oracle so it returns lower price 
    vm.mockCall(
        address(connector.valueOracle()),
        abi.encodeWithSelector(INoyaValueOracle.getValue.selector),
        abi.encode(110325841858)
    );

    // Expect revert due to underflow
    vm.expectRevert(stdError.arithmeticError);
    uint256 tvl = connector._getPositionTVL(holdingPI, USDC);

    vm.stopPrank();
}
```

### Suggested Mitigation
Add the following change in `SiloConnector::_getPositionTVL()`:

```diff
    function _getPositionTVL(HoldingPI memory p, address base) public view override returns (uint256 tvl) {
        PositionBP memory bp = registry.getPositionBP(vaultId, p.positionId);
        (address siloToken) = abi.decode(bp.data, (address));
        ISilo silo = ISilo(siloRepository.getSilo(siloToken));
        (address[] memory assets, IBaseSilo.AssetStorage[] memory assetsS) = silo.getAssetsWithState();
        uint256 totalDepositAmount = 0;
        uint256 totalBAmount = 0;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < assets.length; i++) {
            uint256 depositAmount = IERC20(assetsS[i].collateralToken).balanceOf(address(this));
            depositAmount += IERC20(assetsS[i].collateralOnlyToken).balanceOf(address(this));
            uint256 borrowAmount = IERC20(assetsS[i].debtToken).balanceOf(address(this));
            if (depositAmount == 0 && borrowAmount == 0) {
                continue;
            }
            uint256 price = _getValue(assets[i], base, 1e18);
            totalDepositAmount += depositAmount * price / 1e18;
            totalBAmount += borrowAmount * price / 1e18;
        }
+        if (totalDepositAmount < totalBAmount) return 0;
        tvl = totalDepositAmount - totalBAmount;
    }
```


