# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/4572617124bed39add9025317d2c326acfef29f1/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L327


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
`gasValue` is not checked to be  equal or lesser than msg.value sent in during cross chain messaging/execution. This causes two things 
- user A can overpay with no direct way to refund the excess payment back to user A
- User B can spend user A's left over ether on its own remote token deployment/execution requests. user A's excess eth is lost forever. 

## Proof of Concept
For example when deploying an Interchain token remotely, users are required to specify the gas amount they wish to use for gas costs payment on the remote chain. This gas cost amount is sent in the same transaction as the `deployInterchainToken()` is payable function. 

In `deployInterchainToken()`, there is no check for if the `gasValue` amount specified by the user is equal to the ether value sent in the same function by the user, this gives a chance for users to specify a bigger  `gasValue` than the ether they send in. 

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/4572617124bed39add9025317d2c326acfef29f1/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L327-L349
```solidity
    function deployInterchainToken(
        bytes32 salt,
        string calldata destinationChain,
        string memory name,
        string memory symbol,
        uint8 decimals,
        bytes memory minter,
        uint256 gasValue
    ) external payable whenNotPaused returns (bytes32 tokenId) {
        address deployer = msg.sender;

        if (deployer == interchainTokenFactory) deployer = TOKEN_FACTORY_DEPLOYER;

        tokenId = interchainTokenId(deployer, salt);

        if (bytes(destinationChain).length == 0) {
            address tokenAddress = _deployInterchainToken(tokenId, minter, name, symbol, decimals);

            _deployTokenManager(tokenId, TokenManagerType.NATIVE_INTERCHAIN_TOKEN, abi.encode(minter, tokenAddress));
        } else {
            _deployRemoteInterchainToken(tokenId, name, symbol, decimals, minter, destinationChain, gasValue);
        }
    }
```

In the internal function `_deployRemoteInterchainToken()` we can see that there is no check if `msg.value == gasValue` still

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/4572617124bed39add9025317d2c326acfef29f1/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L1028-L1046
```solidity
    function _deployRemoteInterchainToken(
        bytes32 tokenId,
        string memory name,
        string memory symbol,
        uint8 decimals,
        bytes memory minter,
        string calldata destinationChain,
        uint256 gasValue
    ) internal {
        // slither-disable-next-line unused-return
        validTokenManagerAddress(tokenId);

        // slither-disable-next-line reentrancy-events
        emit InterchainTokenDeploymentStarted(tokenId, name, symbol, decimals, minter, destinationChain);

        bytes memory payload = abi.encode(MESSAGE_TYPE_DEPLOY_INTERCHAIN_TOKEN, tokenId, name, symbol, decimals, minter);

        _callContract(destinationChain, payload, IGatewayCaller.MetadataVersion.CONTRACT_CALL, gasValue);
    }
```

Now the execution has gone into `_callContract()` and we can see there is still no check for this. `_callContract()` proceeds to delegate call `gatewayCaller.callContract()`. The call in `gatewayCaller.callContract()` sends the eth amount for gas to the protocol and then proceeds to forward an interchain message to deploy the token on the remote chain. All these while there is still no verification for if `msg.value >= gasValue`. 

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/4572617124bed39add9025317d2c326acfef29f1/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L816-L837
```solidity
    function _callContract(
        string memory destinationChain,
        bytes memory payload,
        IGatewayCaller.MetadataVersion metadataVersion,
        uint256 gasValue
    ) internal {
        //@audit no checks for if msg.value == gasValue, excess eth can be paid and lost by user, especially if tx amount for the call changes abruptly
        string memory destinationAddress;

        (destinationChain, destinationAddress, payload) = _getCallParams(destinationChain, payload);

        (bool success, bytes memory returnData) = gatewayCaller.delegatecall(
            abi.encodeWithSelector(
                IGatewayCaller.callContract.selector,
                destinationChain,
                destinationAddress,
                payload,
                metadataVersion,
                gasValue
            )
        );

        if (!success) revert GatewayCallFailed(returnData);
    }
```

`gatewayCaller.callContract()` snippet below
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/4572617124bed39add9025317d2c326acfef29f1/interchain-token-service/contracts/utils/GatewayCaller.sol#L35-L69
```solidity
    function callContract(
        string calldata destinationChain,
        string calldata destinationAddress,
        bytes calldata payload,
        MetadataVersion metadataVersion,
        uint256 gasValue
    ) external payable override {
        if (gasValue > 0) {
            if (metadataVersion == MetadataVersion.CONTRACT_CALL) {
                // slither-disable-next-line arbitrary-send-eth
                gasService.payNativeGasForContractCall{ value: gasValue }(
                    address(this),
                    destinationChain,
                    destinationAddress,
                    payload,
                    // solhint-disable-next-line avoid-tx-origin
                    tx.origin //@audit using tx.orgin as refund address is bad, especially if tx.orgin is a contract/smart wallet with a complex fallback, this will cause the tx to always run out of gas
                );
            } else if (metadataVersion == MetadataVersion.EXPRESS_CALL) {
                // slither-disable-next-line arbitrary-send-eth
                gasService.payNativeGasForExpressCall{ value: gasValue }(
                    address(this),
                    destinationChain,
                    destinationAddress,
                    payload,
                    // solhint-disable-next-line avoid-tx-origin
                    tx.origin
                );
            } else {
                revert InvalidMetadataVersion(uint32(metadataVersion));
            }
        }

        gateway.callContract(destinationChain, destinationAddress, payload);
    }
```

because  the `gasService.payNativeGasForContractCall{ value: gasValue }()` uses `gasValue` amount specified by user and not the `msg.value` amount it is possible for a user to send in 0 eth for example and specify 0.05 eth or more as `gasValue` cost for the interchain execution. And if the interchainTokenService contract currently holds that amount of eth in its balance, this 0.05 eth amount will be paid for the user and used to execute the user's cross chain call. 

`Gateway.callContract()` actually has a comment which says "`msg.value` must be at least gasValue." as seen [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/4572617124bed39add9025317d2c326acfef29f1/interchain-token-service/contracts/utils/GatewayCaller.sol#L33-L34) but this is not actually implemented in the function logic. 

So this vuln exploit can work if:

- user A specifies `gasValue` amount and sends in more eth than `gasValue`, i.e msg.value > gasValue for an interchain execution
- this causes the excess eth to remain on the interchainTokenService contract and user A isnt refunded the excess (only gasValue amount (and not msg.value) goes to the gasService which processes refunds). 
- user B sees this excess eth in the contract and uses by it by calling `deployInterchainToken()` to deploy interchain token on a remote chain with 0 eth gas value and specifying a `gasValue` sufficient for remote chain execution. This allows user B to use the eth on the `InterchainTokenService` contract to pay for its remote chain execution request, thus executing on a remote chain for free. 

