# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-10-ramses-exchange/blob/4a40eba36bc47eba8179d4f6203a4b84561a4415/contracts/CL/core/RamsesV3Pool.sol#L152-L174


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Because `feeProtocol` is set to 0 when initializing a new pool, all swapFees will remain in the pool for LP providers and one of the fees will be given to the protocol which will result in revenue loss of the protocol and thereby revenue loss for the treasury and the pools gauge.


## Proof of Concept

Every time a user makes a swap in a pool, he pays swapFees. These swaFees are split between the protocol and the LP providers. The variable `feeProtocol` in the pool determine what percentage of the swapFees are supposed to go to the protocol. This fee is set by calling `setFeeProtocol` which in turn call the `RamsesV3PoolFactory` to determine the `feeProtocol` for the pool.

The issue arises from the fact that when a pool is initialized, the feeProtocol is set to 0 instead of the value saved in the `RamsesV3PoolFactory`. This means that the percentage of the swapFees send to the protocol are 0 and all fees remain in the pool for the LP provider. Since the fees for the protocol go partially to the treasury and partially to the gauge of the pool to incentivise Ramses token holders, not setting the `feeProtocol` for a new pool will result in revenue loss of the above-mentioned parties.`

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

When initializing a pool, make sure to determine the value for `feeProtocol` saved in the `RamsesV3PoolFactory` and setting the `feeProtocol` accordingly:

```diff
    function initialize(uint160 sqrtPriceX96) external {
        PoolStorage.PoolState storage $ = PoolStorage.getStorage();

        if ($.slot0.sqrtPriceX96 != 0) revert AI();

        int24 tick = TickMath.getTickAtSqrtRatio(sqrtPriceX96);

        (uint16 cardinality, uint16 cardinalityNext) = Oracle.initialize($.observations, 0);
+       uint8 _feeProtocol = IRamsesV3Factory(factory).poolFeeProtocol(address(this));


        _advancePeriod();

        $.slot0 = Slot0({
            sqrtPriceX96: sqrtPriceX96,
            tick: tick,
            observationIndex: 0,
            observationCardinality: cardinality,
            observationCardinalityNext: cardinalityNext,
-           feeProtocol: 0,
+           feeProtocol: _feeProtocol,
            unlocked: true
        });

        emit Initialize(sqrtPriceX96, tick);
    }
```

Also make the `setFeeProtocol` function public so it is callable in the constructor.



