# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Several tokens are registered in the `AssetRegistry`, and some of them may be part of the current `basket`. 
When the `basket` is under-collateralized, the `recollateralization` process takes place in the `BackingManager`. 
Even if certain tokens are not part of the current `basket` but are registered in the `AssetRegistry`, they can still be used in `trades`.

If the `refPerTok` value of a token becomes `0`, it indicates that the token has been disabled and should be unregistered. 
However, before it is unregistered, this token should not interfere with the normal workflow of the protocol. 
Despite this, it currently obstructs the `recollateralization` and `custom redemption` processes.
## Proof of Concept
During `recollateralization`, we calculate the quantity of each token in the `basket`(`line 290`). 
```
function tradingContext(BasketRange memory basketsHeld)
    public
    view
    returns (TradingContext memory ctx, Registry memory reg)
{
    reg = assetRegistry.getRegistry();

    for (uint256 i = 0; i < reg.erc20s.length; ++i) {
290:        ctx.quantities[i] = basketHandler.quantityUnsafe(reg.erc20s[i], reg.assets[i]);
    }

    ctx.bals = new uint192[](reg.erc20s.length);
}
```
If a token is not part of the current `basket`, its quantity is set to `0`. 
However, if a token's `refPerTok` is `0`, the quantity function returns `FIX_MAX`(`line 397`).
```
function _quantity(
    IERC20 erc20,
    ICollateral coll,
    RoundingMode rounding
) internal view returns (uint192) {
    uint192 refPerTok = coll.refPerTok();
397:    if (refPerTok == 0) return FIX_MAX;

    return basket.refAmts[erc20].div(refPerTok, rounding);
}
```

When determining the next `trade pair`, the following calculation is performed for each token (`line 297`). 
```
function nextTradePair(
    TradingContext memory ctx,
    Registry memory reg,
    BasketRange memory range
) private view returns (TradeInfo memory trade) {
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < reg.erc20s.length; ++i) {
        if (address(reg.erc20s[i]) == address(ctx.rToken)) continue;
        else if (reg.erc20s[i] == ctx.rsr) {
            rsrIndex = i;
            continue;
