# Vulnerability details


A well-known exploit involves using `multicall()` to recursively call itself.
In this Size project, such self-multicall can reset `state.data.isMulticall` to false, leading to further vulnerabilities.

## Impact

Currently, `isMulticall` is only used for harmless validation of the total supply of deposit tokens.
However, since the Size contract is a proxy upgradeable contract, future upgrades may introduce important logic that relies on `isMulticall`, potentially introducing hidden security issues if this vulnerability is not addressed.
Therefore, self-multicall should be disabled before `isMulticall` is used in any critical logic in future upgrades.

## Proof of Concept

The `Size.multicall()` function lacks reentrancy protection:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-size/blob/8850e25fb088898e9cf86f9be1c401ad155bea86/src/Size.sol#L141-L150

`multicall()` is a public function and can be called through `address(this).delegatecall.`

Exploiter can craft multicall data like this:

```solidity
    function testMulticallBypass() public {
        getFund(alice);
        vm.startPrank(alice);
        USDC.approve(address(size), type(uint256).max);
        bytes[] memory _data = new bytes[](3);
        //first multicall into itself doing nothing
        _data[0] = abi.encodeWithSelector(Size.multicall.selector, new bytes[](0));
        //second just deposit normally
        _data[1] = abi.encodeWithSelector(
            Size.deposit.selector, DepositParams({token: address(WETH), amount: 1e18, to: alice})
        );//deposit will use isMulticall as normal
        //withdraw
        _data[2] = abi.encodeWithSelector(
            Size.withdraw.selector, WithdrawParams({token: address(WETH), amount: 0.5e18, to: alice})
        );

        size.multicall{value: 1e18}(_data);
        printBalance(alice);
    }
```
Multicall first action is self-multicall with empty data.
From the second action onward, `state.data.isMulticall` will be reset to false.
The only instance where `isMulticall` is used is here:
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-size/blob/8850e25fb088898e9cf86f9be1c401ad155bea86/src/libraries/actions/Deposit.sol#L80-L82

It merely checks if the deposit does not exceed the supply limit.
When multicall is checked, it disables the check and just verifies the supply limit again, which currently has no potential exploit.

## Tools Used

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Add reentrancy protection to multicall function.
Add a warning in the documentation about security use of `isMulticall`.



