# Vulnerability details

## Impact

During the [Launch Liquidity Phase](https://docs.vultisig.com/vultisig-token/launch#launch-liquidity) a whitelist is applied for 24 hours to prevent sale operations and restrict buy operations. 

The problem is that this also affects claiming operations as well, and the Treasury can't claim liquidity while the whitelist is active, restricting its operations. 

The Treasury should be able to claim their liquidity right away after the launch, since [it doesn't have any cliff](https://docs.vultisig.com/vultisig-token/launch#lp-ownership) in their vesting, but it can't.

This would also affect any other party that has no cliff (in case the project decides to update the initial distribution).

## Proof of Concept

When the whitelist is active, some checks are applied when transferring tokens. This is intended just to restrict buy operations, and thus are only applied when `from == _pool && to != owner()`:

```solidity
    function checkWhitelist(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external onlyVultisig {
@>      if (from == _pool && to != owner()) {
```

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-vultisig/blob/main/hardhat-vultisig/contracts/Whitelist.sol#L205

There exists a check regarding the "contributed ETH" via `_contributed[to]`:

```solidity
    // Calculate rough ETH amount for VULT amount
    uint256 estimatedETHAmount = IOracle(_oracle).peek(amount);
    if (_contributed[to] + estimatedETHAmount > _maxAddressCap) {
        revert MaxAddressCapOverflow();
    }

    _contributed[to] += estimatedETHAmount;
```

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-vultisig/blob/main/hardhat-vultisig/contracts/Whitelist.sol#L220-L226

The problem is that this also restricts [`claim()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-vultisig/blob/main/src/ILOPool.sol#L184) operations, even if `owner()` is the Treasury, and the ILO Pool is whitelisted.

The `claim()` operation involves transferring the tokens `from` the Uniswap `_pool` to the ILO Pool when liquidity [is burnt](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-vultisig/blob/main/src/ILOPool.sol#L205), so the whitelist will be applied as `from == _pool && to != owner()`.

This means that the checks will still be applied when the Treasury tries to `claim()` their liquidity as long as the whitelist is active, restricting its operations.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

```diff
    function checkWhitelist(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external onlyVultisig {
-        if (from == _pool && to != owner()) {
+        if (from == _pool && to != owner() && to != _iloPool) {
```


