# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-vultisig/blob/cb72b1e9053c02a58d874ff376359a83dc3f0742/hardhat-vultisig/contracts/Whitelist.sol#L205


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
In the early stages of sales, only whitelisted addresses can purchase limited quantities of VULT tokens from VULT/ETH pool.
However, the user's flashloan operation may be mistakenly included in the _contributed mapping,This may prevent them from making normal purchases.

## Proof of Concept
CheckWhitelist is called during transfer. If from is VULT/ETH pool, it will add to address whether it is a whitelist account, and then check if the transaction exceeds the limit. If it exceeds the limit, the transaction will be reverted.

github:[https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-vultisig/blob/cb72b1e9053c02a58d874ff376359a83dc3f0742/hardhat-vultisig/contracts/Whitelist.sol#L204C1-L228C6](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-vultisig/blob/cb72b1e9053c02a58d874ff376359a83dc3f0742/hardhat-vultisig/contracts/Whitelist.sol#L204C1-L228C6)
```solidity
    function checkWhitelist(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external onlyVultisig {
        if (from == _pool && to != owner()) {
            // We only add limitations for buy actions via uniswap v3 pool
            // Still need to ignore WL check if it's owner related actions
            if (_locked) {
                revert Locked();
            }

            if (_isBlacklisted[to]) {
                revert Blacklisted();
            }

            if (_allowedWhitelistIndex == 0 || _whitelistIndex[to] > _allowedWhitelistIndex) {
                revert NotWhitelisted();
            }

            // // Calculate rough ETH amount for VULT amount
            uint256 estimatedETHAmount = IOracle(_oracle).peek(amount);
            if (_contributed[to] + estimatedETHAmount > _maxAddressCap) {
                revert MaxAddressCapOverflow();
            }

            _contributed[to] += estimatedETHAmount;
        }
    }
```
However, when users use flashloan to borrow VULT tokens, it also triggers an increase in _contributed, which can result in a loss of the original purchase limit for whitelisted users
POC:
1. The whitelist user made a flash loan and lent out VULT worth 1 ether, which was later repaid
2.  _contributed[user] will add 1 ether
3. Now, he can only purchase VULT token worth 2 ether


## Tools Used
Manual audit
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Consider using other methods to track purchases


