# Vulnerability details

## Summary

Due to reentrancy, a user may corrupt internal data and disable functionality.

## Vulnerability Details

[`_buyCurvesToken`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/516aedb7b9a8d341d0d2666c23780d2bd8a9a600/contracts/Curves.sol#L263-L280) calls [`_transferFees`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/516aedb7b9a8d341d0d2666c23780d2bd8a9a600/contracts/Curves.sol#L218-L261), which makes external calls, then checks `curvesTokenBalance` in the subsequent line. 
It's possible for an external call to mutate `curvesTokenBalance`, such that [the check](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/516aedb7b9a8d341d0d2666c23780d2bd8a9a600/contracts/Curves.sol#L277C80-L277C80) fails, even when it is expected to succeed.
The reason for this is that as part of the external call, the contract may be re-entered again. 
If the callback triggers another purchase, we end up in a state where the token balance, for a given token holder is nonzero, but the token is not recorded in [`ownedCurvesTokenSubjects[holder]`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/516aedb7b9a8d341d0d2666c23780d2bd8a9a600/contracts/Curves.sol#L101).


## Impact

When a token holder `holder` possesses a nonzero amount of `token`, and `token` is absent from `ownedCurvesTokenSubjects[holder]`, this causes [`transferAllCurvesTokens`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/516aedb7b9a8d341d0d2666c23780d2bd8a9a600/contracts/Curves.sol#L302-L311) to behave incorrectly.
If `token`, is the only token held by `holder`, then `transferAllCurvesTokens` does nothing, otherwise, it transfers all tokens except `token` (and any other tokens absent from `ownedCurvesTokenSubjects[holder]`,  for which balance is positive).

## Proof of Concept

We need to deploy a contract, which implements a custom `receive()` method, triggering a purchase:
```sol
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

import "./Curves.sol";

// If anything is sent to his contract address, it will attemmpt to buy N of its own tokens, 
// on the condition that the current supply == 1
contract MyContract {
    string public name = "My Contract";

    Curves private curves;

    constructor(Curves _curves) { 
        curves = _curves;
    }

    function buy() external payable {
        curves.buyCurvesToken(payable(this), 1);  
    }

    receive() external payable {
        if (curves.curvesTokenSupply(address(this)) == 1) {
            uint256 N = 20; // arbitrary #
            uint256 price = curves.getPrice(1, N);
            curves.buyCurvesToken{value: price}(address(this), N); 
        }
    }
}
```

The PoC is as follows: 
1. Deploy `MyContract` to `addr` (= `token`)
1. Call `buy()`
    1. This invokes `Curves.buyCurvesToken(token)`
    1. part of `_buyCurvesToken` [is executed](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/516aedb7b9a8d341d0d2666c23780d2bd8a9a600/contracts/Curves.sol#L272-L273), setting token balance to 1 and supply to 1
    1. `_transferFees` is called, such that `curvesTokenSubject` is `token`
    1. a callback to `addr` [happens](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/516aedb7b9a8d341d0d2666c23780d2bd8a9a600/contracts/Curves.sol#L236)
    1. This triggers `receive()` on `MyContract`
        1. if-condition in `receive()` holds
        1. This re-enters `Curves.buyCurvesToken(token)`
        1. part of `_buyCurvesToken` is executed, setting token balance to `1 + N`, and supply to `1 + N`
        1. `_transferFees` is called, such that `curvesTokenSubject` is `token`
        1. a callback to `addr` happens
        1. This triggers `receive()` on `MyContract`
            1. if-condition no longer holds, since supply is greater than 1
        1. scope returns to the inner `_buyCurvesToken`, since balance is now `1 + N` and `amount` is `N`, [the if-condition](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/516aedb7b9a8d341d0d2666c23780d2bd8a9a600/contracts/Curves.sol#L277) does not hold
    1. scope returns to the outer `_buyCurvesToken`, since balance is now `1 + N` and `amount` is `1`, the if-condition does not hold
1. Attempt `transferAllCurvesTokens`
1. Nothing happens, because `token` never got added to `ownedCurvesTokenSubjects[addr]`

Below is a test file, which can be added to `./test/` as `poc.ts`:
