# Vulnerability details


## Impact

PoolOwners have too much power, which impose a centralization risk. They can 1) Set `pricefeed` for pricing tokens, and 2) Set `allowedTraders[]` to disable Market contract from trading.

## Bug Description

In the Discord channel, is it announced that for the scope of this audit: `Anyone can freely add pairs to the PredyPool`. However, the PoolOwners simply have too much power and can cause loss of funds to users who use their pool for trading.

Two of the most major centralization risk is:

1. PoolOwners can freely toggle `allowedTraders[]` and simply remove PerpMarketV1/GammaMarket from allowed traders. This means if users have already opened a position using PerpMarketV1, after the PoolOwner disables PerpMarketV1, they will never be able to close their positions again, and their tokens would be forever stuck in PredyPool.

2. PoolOwners can freely set oracle `priceFeed`. The `priceFeed` is used for calculating a vault value, and is used to check whether a vault is safe. If the PoolOwner changes it to a malicious price feed, they can perform liquidation on any safe vault.

PredyPool.sol
```solidity
