# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The `LibOracle::getOraclePrice()` does not detect or handle the Chainlink aggregators' `minAnswer` and `maxAnswer`. For instance, in case of a significant price drop, the asset price reported by the Chainlink price feed will continue to be at the pre-determined `minAnswer` instead of the actual price (below the `minAnswer`). For more, refer to the case of [Venus Protocol and Blizz Finance in the crash of LUNA](https://rekt.news/venus-blizz-rekt/).

In other words, in the flash crash event, Chainlink's price feeds can report incorrect `basePrice` and/or `price` variables. These incorrectly reported price variables lead to miscalculating the `basePriceInEth` (base price in ETH) or `priceInEth` (non-base price in ETH).

Whereas the calculation of the `basePriceInEth` has a price deviation detection mechanism to partially mitigate the issue, the calculation of the `priceInEth` does not validate or handle the issue.

Subsequently, the `getOraclePrice()` will return the miscalculated `basePriceInEth` and/or `priceInEth` (especially this one) to the protocol's core functions to consume, harming the protocol's and users' funds.

*Please refer to the `Proof of Concept` section for more details.*

## Proof of Concept

This PoC section can be categorized into three sub-sections.
1. **Introduction**
2. **Vulnerability Details**
3. **Lack of Detecting Chainlink Aggregators' `minAnswer` and `maxAnswer`**

### 1. Introduction

The `getOraclePrice()` calculates the base price in ETH (`ETH/USD` asset oracle) or non-base price in ETH (`non-ETH/USD` asset oracle) for the protocol's core functions to consume. The function can be divided into four code paths.
1. To calculate the [base price in ETH (ETH/USD asset oracle) in a `try` case](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L28-L32)
2. To calculate the [base price in ETH (ETH/USD asset oracle) in a `catch` case](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L48-L49)
3. To calculate the [non-base price in ETH (non-ETH/USD asset oracle) in a `try` case](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L33-L46)
4. To calculate the [non-base price in ETH (non-ETH/USD asset oracle) in a `catch` case](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L50-L65)

In the first code path, the base price in ETH (`basePriceInEth`) is calculated from the [`basePrice`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L30) fed by Chainlink's `ETH/USD` price feed. The function validates and handles the flash crash event using the [price deviation detection mechanism](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L85-L111). In the second code path, the function will [derive the `basePriceInEth` from Uniswap's TWAP](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L49) instead (in case Chainlink's price feed reverts a query). Both code paths can partially mitigate the flash crash event. Thus, I will leave out discussing these two code paths for brevity's sake.

This report will discuss the [third](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L33-L46) and [fourth](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L50-L65) code paths of the `getOraclePrice()`, which calculate the non-base price in ETH (`non-ETH/USD` asset oracle). I discovered neither code path validates or handles the flash crash event. As a result, the `getOraclePrice()` will return a miscalculated non-base price (i.e., the `priceInEth` variable).

### 2. Vulnerability Details

The [third](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L33-L46) code path of the `getOraclePrice()` calculates the `priceInEth` using [`uint256(price).div(uint256(basePrice))`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L43)(see `@1.1` below) . Where the [`price`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L37) (see `@1.2`) is fed by Chainlink's `non-ETH/USD` price feed (e.g., `XAU/USD`), and the [`basePrice`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L27) (see `@1.3`) is from Chainlink's `ETH/USD` price feed.

Meanwhile, the [fourth](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L50-L65) code path of the `getOraclePrice()` calculates the `priceInEth` using [`uint256(price * C.BASE_ORACLE_DECIMALS).mul(twapInv)`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L63) (see `@2.1`). Where the [`price`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L54)  (see `@2.2`) is reported by Chainlink's `non-ETH/USD` price feed, and the [`twapInv`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L62) (see `@2.3`) is returned from Uniswap's TWAP (`WETH/USDC` pool).

```solidity
