# Vulnerability details

## Summary
The base oracle price isn't checked for staleness when it's used with another oracle but it is checked when it is used alone.

## Description
The base oracle has a staleness value of 2 hours. This is checked in the `baseOracleCircuitBreaker()` function when it is the used oracle. 

The check if it's the current oracle is done below and `baseOracleCircuitBreaker()` is called.
**[LibOracle.sol#L28-L32](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L28-L32)**
```solidity
❌           if (oracle == baseOracle) {
                // @dev multiply base oracle by 10**10 to give it 18 decimals of precision
                // @audit-low C.BASE_ORACLE_DECIMALS may change
                uint256 basePriceInEth = basePrice > 0 ? uint256(basePrice * C.BASE_ORACLE_DECIMALS).inv() : 0;
❌              basePriceInEth = baseOracleCircuitBreaker(protocolPrice, baseRoundID, basePrice, baseTimeStamp, basePriceInEth);
```

`baseOracleCircuitBreaker()` applies the check here.
**[LibOracle.sol#L76-L77](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOracle.sol#L76-L77)**
```solidity
