# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/LibOrders.sol#L882-L952


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The `cancelShort` function provided is designed to cancel a short order and handle the associated short record based on the current state of the order and the short record.

If a user wants to quickly cancel an order that is fully filled before calling `cancelShort`, the function should be able to handle this scenario. The current implementation seems to handle the cancellation of a fully filled short order correctly, as it updates the short record status to `FullyFilled` and adjusts the vault and asset values accordingly.
## Proof of Concept
Let's analyze the code to ensure it works as intended:

1. The function checks if the order is already `Cancelled` or `Matched`. If it is, it reverts with `Errors.NotActiveOrder()`.
2. It calculates the amount of ETH to be returned to the shorter.
3. It checks the status of the associated short record. If the short record is `Closed`, it deletes the short record. If it's not `Closed`, it updates the short record to `FullyFilled`.
4. It updates the vault and asset values based on the short order and short record details.
5. Finally, it cancels the short order using the `cancelOrder` function.


However, we should not cancel a fullyfilled order. The code those not handle such cases as it only handles when it is Closed or Partilly filled. one potential improvement could be to add a check to handle the case where the short order is already fully filled before calling `cancelShort`. This would prevent unnecessary updates to the short record and vault and asset values when a short order is already filled.

## Tool

Manual code analysis

## Suggested Mitigation
Here's a revised version of the `cancelShort` function with this improvement:

```solidity
function cancelShort(address asset, uint16 id) internal {
    AppStorage storage s = appStorage();
    STypes.Order storage shortOrder = s.shorts[asset][id];

    O orderType = shortOrder.orderType;
    if (orderType == O.Cancelled || orderType == O.Matched) revert Errors.NotActiveOrder();

    uint88 eth = shortOrder.ercAmount.mulU88(shortOrder.price).mulU88(LibOrders.convertCR(shortOrder.shortOrderCR));

    STypes.Asset storage Asset = s.asset[asset];
    uint256 vault = Asset.vault;

    uint8 shortRecordId = shortOrder.shortRecordId;
    address shorter = shortOrder.addr;
    STypes.ShortRecord storage shortRecord = s.shortRecords[asset][shorter][shortRecordId];

    if (shortRecord.status == SR.FullyFilled) {
        revert("Order is already fully filled");
    }

    if (shortRecord.status == SR.Closed) {
        // @dev creating shortOrder automatically creates a closed shortRecord which also sets a shortRecordId
        // @dev cancelling an unmatched order needs to also handle/recycle the shortRecordId
        LibShortRecord.deleteShortRecord(asset, shorter, shortRecordId);
    } else {
        uint88 minShortErc = uint88(LibAsset.minShortErc(asset));
        if (shortRecord.ercDebt < minShortErc) {
            // @dev prevents leaving behind a partially filled SR is under minShortErc
            // @dev if the corresponding short is cancelled, then the partially filled SR's debt will == minShortErc
            uint88 debtDiff = minShortErc - shortRecord.ercDebt;
            {
                STypes.Vault storage Vault = s.vault[vault];

                uint88 collateralDiff = shortOrder.price.mulU88(debtDiff).mulU88(LibOrders.convertCR(shortOrder.shortOrderCR));

                LibShortRecord.fillShortRecord(
                    asset,
                    shorter,
                    shortRecordId,
                    SR.FullyFilled,
                    collateralDiff,
                    debtDiff,
                    Asset.ercDebtRate,
                    Vault.dethYieldRate
                );

                Vault.dethCollateral += collateralDiff;
                Asset.dethCollateral += collateralDiff;
                Asset.ercDebt += debtDiff;

                // @dev update the eth refund amount
                eth -= collateralDiff;
            }
            // @dev virtually mint the increased debt
            s.assetUser[asset][shorter].ercEscrowed += debtDiff;
        } else {
            shortRecord.status = SR.FullyFilled;
        }
    }

    s.vaultUser[vault][shorter].ethEscrowed += eth;

    // Approximating the startingShortId, rather than expecting exact match
    if (id == Asset.startingShortId) {
        uint256 savedPrice = LibOracle.getPrice(asset);
        uint256 prevPrice = s.shorts[asset][shortOrder.prevId].price;
        if (prevPrice >= savedPrice) {
            Asset.startingShortId = shortOrder.prevId;
        } else {
            Asset.startingShortId = shortOrder.nextId;
        }
    }

    cancelOrder(s.shorts, asset, id);
}
```

In this revised version, I added a check to revert the transaction with a clear error message if the short order is already fully filled (`shortRecord.status == SR.FullyFilled`).







