https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/libraries/UniswapOracleLibrary.sol#L43


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

When handling price calculations in Uniswap, the overflow behaviour is desired, hence the <0.8.0 soldity versions of uniswap calculations library. This is neeeded to handle any forms of overflow and also prevents unexpected reversions.

The UniswapOracleLibrary contract acting as a fork of the Oracle library integrates with v3Pool to estimate twap prices, chief function of which is the `getQuoteAtTick` function.

A side by side comparison of the codebase's `getQuoteAtTick` function and uniswap's shows that the `mulDiv` calculations are handled by different libraries. Uniswap uses the `FullMath` library whereas the codebase uses `PRBMathHelper`, an extension of the prb math's `Common` library.

Uniswap's fullmath handles overflow behaviour due to its solidity version being `>=0.4.0 <0.8.0` or using unchecked blocks in updated versions,  whereas prb's common offers protection from overflow and reverts. 

The effect of this is that calls made to the `estimateTWAP` function carry the risk of reverting unexpectedly which can lead to weird behaviour especially during bid creations, LST withdrawals or during the use of circuit breakers when getting oracle price and so on. 

## Proof of Concept

Uniswap's `getQouteAtTick` function, note the `mulDiv` functions are called in the FullMath library which uses ether solidity less than 0.8.0 or uses unchecked blocks.

```
    function getQuoteAtTick(
        int24 tick,
        uint128 baseAmount,
        address baseToken,
        address quoteToken
    ) internal pure returns (uint256 quoteAmount) {
        uint160 sqrtRatioX96 = TickMath.getSqrtRatioAtTick(tick);

        // Calculate quoteAmount with better precision if it doesn't overflow when multiplied by itself
        if (sqrtRatioX96 <= type(uint128).max) {
            uint256 ratioX192 = uint256(sqrtRatioX96) * sqrtRatioX96;
            quoteAmount = baseToken < quoteToken
                ? FullMath.mulDiv(ratioX192, baseAmount, 1 << 192)
                : FullMath.mulDiv(1 << 192, baseAmount, ratioX192);
        } else {
            uint256 ratioX128 = FullMath.mulDiv(sqrtRatioX96, sqrtRatioX96, 1 << 64);
            quoteAmount = baseToken < quoteToken
                ? FullMath.mulDiv(ratioX128, baseAmount, 1 << 128)
                : FullMath.mulDiv(1 << 128, baseAmount, ratioX128);
        }
    }

```
The codebase's `getQouteAtTick` function. It's more or less the same except the use of `U256` for the `mulDiv` function.
```
    function getQuoteAtTick(int24 tick, uint128 baseAmount, address baseToken, address quoteToken)
        internal
        pure
        returns (uint256 quoteAmount)
    {
        uint160 sqrtRatioX96 = TickMath.getSqrtRatioAtTick(tick);

        // Calculate quoteAmount with better precision if it doesn't overflow when multiplied by itself
        if (sqrtRatioX96 <= type(uint128).max) {
            uint256 ratioX192 = uint256(sqrtRatioX96) * sqrtRatioX96;
            quoteAmount =
                baseToken < quoteToken ? U256.mulDiv(ratioX192, baseAmount, 1 << 192) : U256.mulDiv(1 << 192, baseAmount, ratioX192);
        } else {
            uint256 ratioX128 = U256.mulDiv(sqrtRatioX96, sqrtRatioX96, 1 << 64);
            quoteAmount =
                baseToken < quoteToken ? U256.mulDiv(ratioX128, baseAmount, 1 << 128) : U256.mulDiv(1 << 128, baseAmount, ratioX128);
        }
    }
```

`U256` is from the [`PRBMathHelper`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/main/contracts/libraries/PRBMathHelper.sol) library which finished up the calls to PRB math's [Common](https://github.com/PaulRBerg/prb-math/blob/5b6279a0cf7c1b1b6a5cc96082811f7ef620cf60/src/Common.sol#L2) contract compiled with solidity `>=0.8.19;` and [reverts](https://github.com/PaulRBerg/prb-math/blob/5b6279a0cf7c1b1b6a5cc96082811f7ef620cf60/src/Common.sol#L14) when `mulDiv` for uint256 overflows. 

## Tools Used
Manual code review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Recommend switching to Uniswap's FullMath library instead, just like TickMath is also in use.


