# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Potential array length mismatch between the orderHintArray and the shortHintArray in function createBid(), createForcedBid(), and  createLimitShort()
## Vulnerability details:
There is a potential array length mismatch in the aforementioned functions. the array length mismatch is between the orderHintArray and the shortHintArray when creating limit shorts in function createLimitShort() and when creating bids in function createBid() and createForcedBid().

[ShortOrdersFacet.sol#L39-L40](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/facets/ShortOrdersFacet.sol#L39-L40)
```
    function createLimitShort(
        address asset,
        uint80 price,
        uint88 ercAmount,
@>      MTypes.OrderHint[] memory orderHintArray,
@>      uint16[] memory shortHintArray,
        uint16 shortOrderCR
    ) external isNotFrozen(asset) onlyValidAsset(asset) nonReentrant {}
```
[BidOrdersFacet.sol#L45-L46 ](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/facets/BidOrdersFacet.sol#L45-L46)
```
    function createBid(
        address asset,
        uint80 price,
        uint88 ercAmount,
        bool isMarketOrder,
@>      MTypes.OrderHint[] calldata orderHintArray,
@>      uint16[] calldata shortHintArray
    ) external isNotFrozen(asset) onlyValidAsset(asset) nonReentrant returns (uint88 ethFilled, uint88 ercAmountLeft) {
        LibOrders.updateOracleAndStartingShortViaTimeBidOnly(asset, shortHintArray);

        return _createBid(msg.sender, asset, price, ercAmount, isMarketOrder, orderHintArray, shortHintArray);
    }
```
[BidOrdersFacet.sol#L65 ](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-dittoeth/blob/91faf46078bb6fe8ce9f55bcb717e5d2d302d22e/contracts/facets/BidOrdersFacet.sol#L65)
```
@>    function createForcedBid(address sender, address asset, uint80 price, uint88 ercAmount, uint16[] calldata shortHintArray)
        external
        onlyDiamond
        returns (uint88 ethFilled, uint88 ercAmountLeft)
    {
        // @dev leave empty, don't need hint for market buys
        MTypes.OrderHint[] memory orderHintArray;

        // @dev update oracle in callers
        return _createBid(sender, asset, price, ercAmount, C.MARKET_ORDER, orderHintArray, shortHintArray);
    }
```

The functions do not check if the length of the arrays provided are equal when creating a limit order or a bids order. This can lead to a potential array length mismatch between the orderHintArray and the shortHintArray in these functions The vulnerability is similar to [maia #643](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-05-maia-findings/issues/643) where the array length was not properly checked.

