# Vulnerability details

## Vulnerability Description
[_getRequiredCollateralAtTickSinglePosition](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L1238-L1268) function calculates the required collateral for a single position based on the position size, tick, and pool utilization. The calculations involve multiplying the position size by the collateral ratio, which is determined based on the pool utilization and the long/short status of the position.

The code uses the [Math.unsafeDivRoundingUp](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L1486-L1496) to perform division operations, which rounds up the result to avoid underestimating the required collateral.

> There is a potential issue with the calculation of the `maxNumRangesFromStrike` variable in the `exerciseCost`. The division operation `uint256(Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)) / range)` may result in unexpected behavior if range is zero, leading to a division by zero error.

## Impact
The [exerciseCost](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L650-L735) function may be vulnerable to a division by zero error when calculating the [maxNumRangesFromStrike](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L659-L727) variable if the range value is zero.

Code: [CollateralTracker.sol::exerciseCost](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L659-L679)
```solidity
    // ...

    unchecked {
        for (uint256 leg = 0; leg < positionId.countLegs(); ++leg) {
            // ...

            {
                int24 range = int24(
                    int256(
                        Math.unsafeDivRoundingUp(
                            uint24(positionId.width(leg) * positionId.tickSpacing()),
                            2
                        )
                    )
                );
                maxNumRangesFromStrike = Math.max(
                    maxNumRangesFromStrike,
                    uint256(Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)) / range)
                );
            }

            // ...
        }

        // ...
    }
}
```
Calculation of [maxNumRangesFromStrike](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L675-L678) inside the loop that iterates over the legs of the position is vulnerable.

[#L675-L678](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L675-L678)
```solidity
maxNumRangesFromStrike = Math.max(
    maxNumRangesFromStrike,
    uint256(Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)) / range)
);
```
If the `range` variable is zero, the division operation `Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)) / range` will result in a division by zero error.

This can occur if `positionId.width(leg)` or `positionId.tickSpacing()` is zero, leading to the range being calculated as zero.

## Proof of Concept
> If the `range` variable is zero, the division operation `Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)) / range` will throw a division by zero error. This will cause the function to revert and fail to calculate the exercise cost. The function will not return the expected exercise fees.

The division by zero can prevent users from exercising their option positions when certain conditions are met (i.e., when `positionId.width(leg)` or `positionId.tickSpacing()` is zero).

**Root Cause:**
`exerciseCost` function calculates the cost of exercising an option position based on the distance between the position's strike and the current price.
Inside the loop that iterates over the legs of the position, the function calculates the `maxNumRangesFromStrike` variable.

The calculation of `maxNumRangesFromStrike` involves dividing the absolute difference between the current tick and the strike price by a `range` value. [#L667-L677](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L667-L679)
   ```solidity
   int24 range = int24(
       int256(
           Math.unsafeDivRoundingUp(
               uint24(positionId.width(leg) * positionId.tickSpacing()),
               2
           )
       )
   );
   maxNumRangesFromStrike = Math.max(
       maxNumRangesFromStrike,
       uint256(Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)) / range)
   );
   ```
The `range` value is calculated by dividing the product of `positionId.width(leg)` and `positionId.tickSpacing()` by 2.
If either `positionId.width(leg)` or `positionId.tickSpacing()` is zero, the `range` value will be zero.
When `range` is zero, the division operation `Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)) / range` will result in a division by zero error.

1. If a user attempts to exercise a position with a leg where `positionId.width(leg)` or `positionId.tickSpacing()` is zero, the `exerciseCost` function will revert due to the division by zero error.
2. This will prevent the user from exercising their position, leading to a denial of service.
3. The user will not be able to retrieve the expected exercise fees for their position.

**(PoC):**
Assume a user has a position with the following parameters:
   - `positionId`: A valid position ID with at least one leg.
   - `positionBalance`: A non-zero balance for the position.
   - `longAmounts`: Non-zero amounts for the long positions.

The user attempts to exercise their position by calling the `exerciseCost` function with the following inputs:
   - `currentTick`: The current price tick.
   - `oracleTick`: The price oracle tick.
   - `positionId`: The user's position ID.
   - `positionBalance`: The balance of the user's position.
   - `longAmounts`: The amounts of the user's long positions.

Inside the `exerciseCost` function, the code iterates over the legs of the position.

For a specific leg, if `positionId.width(leg)` or `positionId.tickSpacing()` is zero, the `range` value will be calculated as zero. [#L667-L670](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L667-L674)
   ```solidity
   int24 range = int24(
       int256(
           Math.unsafeDivRoundingUp(
               uint24(positionId.width(leg) * positionId.tickSpacing()),
               2
           )
       )
   );
   ```
When calculating `maxNumRangesFromStrike`, the division operation `Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)) / range` will be performed.

Since `range` is zero, the division operation will throw a division by zero error. [#L675-L677](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L675-L679)
   ```solidity
   maxNumRangesFromStrike = Math.max(
       maxNumRangesFromStrike,
       uint256(Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)) / range)
   );
   ```

The `exerciseCost` function will revert, preventing the user from exercising their position and retrieving the exercise fees. The user will experience a denial of service, as they will not be able to complete the exercise process for their position.

The protocol's normal functioning will be disrupted, and the user will not receive the expected outcome.

## Tools Used
VsCode

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
It is necessary to handle the case when `range` is zero by adding a check before performing the division operation and providing an alternative calculation or default value when `range` is zero. Additionally, input validation can be implemented to ensure that `positionId.width(leg)` and `positionId.tickSpacing()` are non-zero values when creating positions.
```solidity
uint256 distance = uint256(Math.abs(currentTick - positionId.strike(leg)));
if (range != 0) {
    maxNumRangesFromStrike = Math.max(
        maxNumRangesFromStrike,
        distance / range
    );
} else {
    // Handle the case when range is zero
    // For example, set maxNumRangesFromStrike to a maximum value
    maxNumRangesFromStrike = type(uint256).max;
}
```


