# Vulnerability details


## Proof of Concept

Take a look at https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/libraries/PanopticMath.sol#L241-L268

```solidity
    function twapFilter(IUniswapV3Pool univ3pool, uint32 twapWindow) external view returns (int24) {
        uint32[] memory secondsAgos = new uint32[](20);

        int256[] memory twapMeasurement = new int256[](19);

        unchecked {
            // construct the time stots
            for (uint256 i = 0; i < 20; ++i) {
                secondsAgos[i] = uint32(((i + 1) * twapWindow) / 20);
            }

            // observe the tickCumulative at the 20 pre-defined time slots
            (int56[] memory tickCumulatives, ) = univ3pool.observe(secondsAgos);

            // compute the average tick per 30s window
            //@audit
            for (uint256 i = 0; i < 19; ++i) {
                twapMeasurement[i] = int24(
                    (tickCumulatives[i] - tickCumulatives[i + 1]) / int56(uint56(twapWindow / 20))
                );
            }

            // sort the tick measurements
            int256[] memory sortedTicks = Math.sort(twapMeasurement);

            // Get the median value
            return int24(sortedTicks[10]);
        }
    }
```

This function is used to compute the twap of a Uniswap V3 pool using data from its oracle, issue here is that it just takes the median price and this would lead to a heavy break in pricing in the case where an abrupt increment or decrement in pricing is registered, note that this is not uncommon in the current crypto world.

The current method of getting price in Panoptic, is to query an array of 20 prices, sort them with the help of `Math.sol` and then chose the median price as the `twap` price.

Let's just hint a somewhat applicable example, in native implementation of twaps, say our prices in the array is [100, 101, 99, 93, 97, 104, 135, 119, 109, 127, 102, 109, 143, 136, 126, 133, 148, 152, 154, 132, 128] , using the python script below.

```python
def calculate_average(numbers):
  # Step 1: Sum up all the numbers
  total = sum(numbers)
  # Step 2: Divide the sum by the total number of elements
  average = total / len(numbers)
  return average


# The array for which you want to calculate the average
numbers =  [100, 101, 99, 93, 97, 104, 135, 119, 109, 127, 102, 109, 143, 136, 126, 133, 148, 152, 154, 132, 128]

# Calculate and print the average
average = calculate_average(numbers)
print(f"The average of the array is: {average}")


# Sort the array and print the sorted list
sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)
print(f"The sorted array is: {sorted_numbers}")

```

Result:

```markdown
The average of the array is: 121.28571428571429
The sorted array is: [93, 97, 99, 100, 101, 102, 104, 109, 109, 119, 126, 127, 128, 132, 133, 135, 136, 143, 148, 152, 154]
```

We can see that our generic/correct twap price should be `121.286`.

However the price returned from ` PanopticMath.twapFilter()` would be `126` which is `~ 4%` higher than the real twap price.

Note that this report **is not** trying to indicate that the twap price is stale since even in the example above both prices (generic/implemented twap) would be considered stale compared to the current price, also the bug idea _(stale twap compared to current price)_ [has already been stated to be OOS in the readMe](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/README.md#L32)

```markdown
- Attacks that stem from the TWAP being extremely stale compared to the market price within its period (currently 10 minutes)
```

However, this report is indicating that the TWAP implementation currently is not a TWAP as only one specific `twapMeasurement[i] ` ends up getting used instead of getting the average across different `twapMeasurements`, which contrary to protocol's thoughts this actually breaks core logics.

## Impact

- Protocol's core pricing logic is broken, the `TWAP_WINDOW` has been hardcoded as `10 minutes` and is supposed to be the duration over which the twap is being calculated for, but code implementation indicates otherwise as twap is not being calculated for and instead a median is just being queried.

- The TWAP values computed by this function is almost always going be inaccurate compared to the real twap price as shown in the example.

- The [value of the liquidation bonus](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/PanopticPool.sol#L1097-L1107) calculated would be off since the wrong `twapTick` would be used.

- Extended broken functionality on other functions, considering this function is queried indirectly when liquidating, the discrepancy between the expected and actual behaviour of the TWAP calculation could then cause [this check in `liquidate()` to revert](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/PanopticPool.sol#L1035-L1036) where as it shouldn't or it could even cause users to be unfairly liquidated, additionally this could cause the [amount of fee paid for force exercising](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/PanopticPool.sol#L1231-L1238) a single position to be off or even cause protocol to assume a wrong [amount to be redistributed](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-panoptic/blob/833312ebd600665b577fbd9c03ffa0daf250ed24/contracts/PanopticPool.sol#L1242-L1248).

> NB: The disparity between the real generic TWAP price and Panoptic's is highly dependent on how volatile the asset was in price window, i.e the higher the volatility the higher the disparity.

> Also, `twapFilter` gets calls routed to it via the path `PanopticPool.liquidate() -> getUniV3TWAP() ->  PanopticMath.twapFilter()`, so all cases above are valid.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider implementing twaps accurately as is done in popular protocols and
RareSkills have a great article on how a TWAP operation should work, can be seen [here](https://www.rareskills.io/post/twap-uniswap-v2).




