The code above shows how Solvency is validated in the PanopticPool, the implementation above from the pointers with the comment description shows that the absolute difference between fastOracleTick & slowOracleTick was first checked if it is above MAX_SLOW_FAST_DELTA, this would have warrant direct reversion but based on the comment description there is a fall back to the more conservative tick i.e the slow tick . At the concluding statement, it can be noted that the user must be solvent at both the fast and slow oracle ticks. The problem is that the protocol validating only the slow oracle tick does not give an absolute guaranty that the fast oracle tick is also solvent due to event of of high price volatility as as the slow oracle ticks covers more ground. 
