Due to such implementation error, functions like `RestakeManager.depositETH` and `WithdrawQueue.withdraw` that call the `RestakeManager.calculateTVLs` function can malfunction as well. For example, when the `totalTVL` returned by the `RestakeManager.calculateTVLs` function is lower than what it should be because of such implementation error, `amountToRedeem` that equals `renzoOracle.calculateRedeemAmount(_amount, ezETH.totalSupply(), totalTVL)` can be lower than what it should be when calling the `WithdrawQueue.withdraw` function below; in this case, the user is forced to redeem a collateral token amount that is less than what the user is entitled to for giving up the same amount of ezETH and therefore lose the collateral token amount difference that the user deserves.

