```

`RestakeManager::deposit()` and `WithdrawQueue::withdraw()` are vulnerable due to the fact that they fetch the price of the passed asset from an oracle. The caller might fall victim to sudden market fluctuations or malicious actors who deliberately frontrun them with another transaction to make them mint/redeem less than the amount they expected at the time of sending their transaction.

Another possibility for slippage is the fact that `totalTVL` and `ezETH.totalSupply()` can frequently change.

## Tools Used

Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Introduce additional parameter to the affected functions where the caller can specify a guaranteed minimum amount they want to get minted/redeemed.



