# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-renzo/blob/519e518f2d8dec9acf6482b84a181e403070d22d/contracts/Bridge/L2/xRenzoDeposit.sol#L330-L359


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The price on L2 bridges is updated from the L1 bridge via CCIP or Context bridges. The admin calls the `sendPrice` function in the `xRenzoBridge.sol` contract, and the updated price is sent to the L2 bridge via connext or via CCIP. This value is then used in the `_updatePrice` function in the `xRenzoDeposit.sol` contract to update the price.

```solidity
    // Check for 0
    if (_price == 0) revert InvalidZeroInput();

    // Check for price divergence - more than 10%
    if (
        (_price > lastPrice && (_price - lastPrice) > (lastPrice / 10)) ||
        (_price < lastPrice && (lastPrice - _price) > (lastPrice / 10))
    ) revert InvalidOraclePrice();

    // Do not allow older price timestamps
    if (_timestamp <= lastPriceTimestamp) revert InvalidTimestamp(_timestamp);

    // Do not allow future timestamps
    if (_timestamp > block.timestamp) revert InvalidTimestamp(_timestamp);

    // Update values and emit event
    lastPrice = _price;
    lastPriceTimestamp = _timestamp;
```

The function does a few sanity checks, and then updates the price. The issue is that there is no check for staleness of the price. During periods of high usage, bridge messages can get delayed, and thus the price being sent can already be stale. This can lead to the bridge updating the price to older values, allowing arbitragers to take advantage of the price difference with respect to the base chain price.

## Proof of Concept

If the bridge gets bogged down by multiple transactions, the price updates can be very slow. In this situation, the bridge can be updated with values which are already outdated, and thus lead to misleading prices and over/under mints of ezETH.

## Tools Used

Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider adding a staleness check in the price update. If the passed timestamp is too old, reject the value or pause the bridge until a fresher price appears.



