# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Every time the liquidator liquidates another user's `NOTE` at or above 100%, the leftover collateral not rolled over can be claimed or withdrawn by the initial user who caused the bad debt thereby resulting in a gain for such user and a loss for the liquidator.

## Proof of Concept
```solidity
function liquidate(
    uint id,
    uint to
  ) 
    external 
      isValidDNft(id)
      isValidDNft(to)
    {
      uint cr = collatRatio(id);
      if (cr >= MIN_COLLATERIZATION_RATIO) revert CrTooHigh();
@>      dyad.burn(id, msg.sender, dyad.mintedDyad(address(this), id)); // @note burns all DYAD minted in the NOTE to be liquidated from the caller

      uint cappedCr               = cr < 1e18 ? 1e18 : cr; // @note used to calc how much collateral is rolled over
      uint liquidationEquityShare = (cappedCr - 1e18).mulWadDown(LIQUIDATION_REWARD); // @note used to calc how much collateral is rolled over
      uint liquidationAssetShare  = (liquidationEquityShare + 1e18).divWadDown(cappedCr); // @note used to calc how much collateral is rolled over

      uint numberOfVaults = vaults[id].length();
      for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
          Vault vault      = Vault(vaults[id].at(i));
          uint  collateral = vault.id2asset(id).mulWadUp(liquidationAssetShare);
          vault.move(id, to, collateral); // @note changes the calculated collateral's ownership from the NOTE being liquidated to the other NOTE being used to funnel the assets
      }
      emit Liquidate(id, msg.sender, to);
  }

```

```solidity
function move(
    uint from,
    uint to,
    uint amount
  )
    external
      onlyVaultManager
  {
    id2asset[from] -= amount; // @note take from
    id2asset[to]   += amount; // @note give to
    emit Move(from, to, amount);
  }
```

- Suppose Bob mints a `NOTE`, deposits USD1500 worth of `wETH` collateral, then proceeds to mint USD1000 worth of `DYAD`. At the same time, George minted a `NOTE`, supplied USD3500 `wETH` collateral, and minted USD1000 `DYAD` stablecoins all while the price of each `wETH` was USD1000 a piece.

- The price of `wETH` then drops to USD750 a piece leaving Bob's `NOTE` positions to be undercollateralized and up for liquidation.

- George decides to take on the liquidation. The collateral ratio for Bob's positions is currently 112.5%. Regardless of this CR, the protocol proceeds to burn all USD1000 `DYAD` stablecoins that Bob minted on his `NOTE` from George while moving `1.366666666666666667 wETH` from the internal accounting of Bob's `NOTE` to George's `NOTE`.

- Since `0.13 wETH` still remains of Bob's initial `1.5 wETH` collateral supplied, Bob can come back and redeem those even though George took on the full `DYAD` token liquidation/burn.

