# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/src/core/Vault.sol#L79-L103


# Vulnerability details

If the answer from `oracle.latestRoundData()` is 0, liquidations will be possible on any vault that has an open position, preventing users from redeeming their DYAD tokens.

## Vulnerability Details
The protocol implements Chainlink price feeds in `Vault::assetPrice` using the `latestRoundData` function. In some extreme cases, oracles may go offline or token prices may fall to zero. In these instances, `Vault::getUsdValue` will return 0. The `liquidate` function uses `VaultManager::collatRatio` to determine if a position can be liquidated, and `getTotalUsdValue` would return 0. 

## Proof of Concept

Add the following code to the [`VaultManagerHelper.t.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/test/VaultManagerHelper.t.sol) file:

```javascript
contract VaultManagerTestHelper is BaseTest {
    ...
    function setOraclePrice(uint price) public {
        console.log("daiOracle setOraclePrice to %s", price);
        console.log("wethOracle setOraclePrice to %s", price);
        daiOracle.setPrice(price);
        wethOracle.setPrice(price);
    }
}
```

Add the following code to the [`VaultManager.t.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/test/VaultManager.t.sol) file:

```javascript
    function testAudit_Liquidate_ZeroPriceFromOracle() public {
        uint id = mintDNft();
        uint WETH_AMOUNT = 1e18;

        deposit(weth, id, address(wethVault), WETH_AMOUNT);
        vaultManager.mintDyad(id, 1e16, address(this));

        uint idMinimumAmount = mintDNft();
        deposit(weth, idMinimumAmount, address(wethVault), WETH_AMOUNT);

        // Mint the minimum amount (1)
        vaultManager.mintDyad(idMinimumAmount, 1, address(this));

        uint idReceiver = mintDNft();

        // Set the price from the oracle to 0 to simulate the scenario where the oracle fails to retrieve the asset price.
        setOraclePrice(0);
        vaultManager.getTotalUsdValue(id);
        uint crAfterOracleSetToZero = vaultManager.collatRatio(id);

        // The collatRatio is now set to 0
        assertEq(crAfterOracleSetToZero, 0);
        vaultManager.liquidate(id, idReceiver);

        // The user who minted the minimum amount of DYAD can be liquidated
        vaultManager.liquidate(idMinimumAmount, idReceiver);

        // User can no longer redeem dyad
        vm.expectRevert();
        vaultManager.redeemDyad(id, address(wethVault), 1e16, address(this));
    }
```

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Ensure that the data feed consistently returns a value greater than zero to prevent unfair liquidations.

```js diff
interface IVault {
    event Withdraw(uint indexed from, address indexed to, uint amount);
    event Deposit(uint indexed id, uint amount);
    event Move(uint indexed from, uint indexed to, uint amount);

+   error OracleNotActive();
    error StaleData();
    error IncompleteRound();
    error NotVaultManager();

    // A vault must implement these functions
    function deposit(uint id, uint amount) external;
    function move(uint from, uint to, uint amount) external;
    function withdraw(uint id, address to, uint amount) external;
    function getUsdValue(uint id) external view returns (uint);
}
```

```js diff
contract Vault is IVault {
    ...
    function assetPrice() public view returns (uint) {
        (, int256 answer, , uint256 updatedAt, ) = oracle.latestRoundData();
+	if (answer == 0) revert OracleNotActive();
	if (block.timestamp > updatedAt + STALE_DATA_TIMEOUT) revert StaleData();
	return answer.toUint256();
    }
}
```






## Assessed type

Oracle

