# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/Vault.kerosine.unbounded.sol#L50-L68


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
While calculating kerosene value from `vault.kerosene.unbounded::asetPrice`, the function call will always revert since it will always self call itself and will run out of gas.
## Proof of Concept
In order to deposit kerosene vaults using `VaultManagerV2::addKerosene`, where a check is being made:
```javascript
function addKerosene(
      uint    id,
      address vault
  ) 
    external
      isDNftOwner(id)
  {
    if (vaultsKerosene[id].length() >= MAX_VAULTS_KEROSENE) revert TooManyVaults();
@>    if (!keroseneManager.isLicensed(vault))                 revert VaultNotLicensed();
    if (!vaultsKerosene[id].add(vault))                     revert VaultAlreadyAdded();
    emit Added(id, vault);
  }

```

In order to be licensed vault in kerosene manager, it should just be added in the kerosene manager.
Which means that unbounded & bounded kerosene vault will be added afterwards by the owner in the Kerosine Manager.

Because of which one major issue arises.

In the deploy script the wethVault & wstEthVault is being being added, where the lead dev, @Shafu in his video said that for calculating TVL, these are being added, and TVL only consists of exogenous collateral.

But as been said above, in order to add kerosene vault, it should be added in the Kerosine manager.

Which means while calculating kerosene value in `Vault.kerosene.unbounded::assetPrice()` function : 

```javascript
function assetPrice() 
    public 
    view 
    override
    returns (uint) {
      uint tvl;
@>      address[] memory vaults = kerosineManager.getVaults();
      uint numberOfVaults = vaults.length;
      for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
        Vault vault = Vault(vaults[i]);
        tvl += vault.asset().balanceOf(address(vault)) 
@>                * vault.assetPrice() * 1e18 // @SuS assetPrice for unbounded will re-entre the function.
                / (10**vault.asset().decimals()) 
                / (10**vault.oracle().decimals());
      }
      uint numerator   = tvl - dyad.totalSupply();
      uint denominator = kerosineDenominator.denominator();
      return numerator * 1e8 / denominator;
  }
```
When `keroseneManager.getVaults()` will also return unbounded and bounded kerosene vaults

And then while iterating through vaults, when vault will be unbounded kerosene vault, `vault.assetPrice` will self call assetPrice function of unbounded kerosene vault.

And it will go on self calling itself, where at the end will run out of gas and revert.

Hence kerosene price will never be able to calculated.

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
As being stated before in an issue, for calculating kerosene price, the exogenous vaults should be stored in a different variable/mapping, and not in KeroseneManager.

i.e TVL calculation vaults i.e exogenous vault & Kerosene vaults should be stored separately.


