# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The purpose of [getNonKeroseneValue()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L250-L267) is to calculate amount of USD inside each NonKerosene vaults (wstEth and wEth).

```solidity
function getNonKeroseneValue(
uint id
) 
public 
view
returns (uint) {
  uint totalUsdValue;
  uint numberOfVaults = vaults[id].length(); 
  for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
    Vault vault = Vault(vaults[id].at(i));
    uint usdValue;
    if (vaultLicenser.isLicensed(address(vault))) {
      usdValue = vault.getUsdValue(id);        
    }
    totalUsdValue += usdValue;
  }
  return totalUsdValue;
}
```

Function does particular check `vaultLicenser.isLicensed(address(vault))` to be sure vault is nonKerosene. However, inside deploy script `Deploy.V2.s.sol` we're adding given vaults:

```solidity
vaultLicenser.add(address(ethVault));
vaultLicenser.add(address(wstEth));
vaultLicenser.add(address(unboundedKerosineVault));
// vaultLicenser.add(address(boundedKerosineVault));
```

Because of that user can use [VaultManagerV2::add](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L67-L78) to add all vaults leading to increase his $USD amount of so called nonKerosene vaults.

[getNonKeroseneValue()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L250-L267) is used in couple of functions:
1. [getTotalUsdValue](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L241-L248)
2. Inside [withdraw](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L134-L153)
```solidity
if (getNonKeroseneValue(id) - value < dyadMinted) revert NotEnoughExoCollat();
```
3. Inside [mintDyad](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L156-L169)
```solidity
if (getNonKeroseneValue(id) < newDyadMinted)     revert NotEnoughExoCollat();
```

Also [getTotalUsdValue](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L241-L248) is used inside [collatRatio](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L230-L239), which calculates collateralization ratio used inside [liquidate](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L205-L228)
```solidity
function collatRatio(
uint id
)
public 
view
returns (uint) {
  uint _dyad = dyad.mintedDyad(address(this), id);
  if (_dyad == 0) return type(uint).max;
  return getTotalUsdValue(id).divWadDown(_dyad);
}
```

In summary, User can exploit [liquidate](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L205-L228) by increasing his collateralization ratio and can exploit [mintDyad](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L156-L169) by bypassing check for minting.

