# Vulnerability details

## Impact
[withdraw](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L134-L153) function inside `VaultManagerV2.sol` is used to withdraw vault asset. It work correctly in `wstEth` and `wEth`. However, when we want towithdraw asset from [Vault.kerosine.unbounded](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/src/core/Vault.kerosine.unbounded.sol), function reverts without any error. What causes that revert is missed `oracle` variable, which exist inside `wstEth` and `wEth` vaults.

## Proof Of Concept
Inside [this gist](https://gist.github.com/jacsonikowy/12ed78a70edd7625ade353edc33ff112) there are two functions:

1. Withdraw from unbounded kerosine vault
2. Withdraw from wstEth

The first one will revert, because of that missing `oracle` variable, but second one will pass without problem.

