# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Users can manipulate kerosene's price by burning or minting tokens on the VaultManagerV1.

## Proof of Concept
When upgrading to V2, the team intends to leave V1 as it is, and deploy different vaults that will be used in V2. The users will have a choice whether they want to stay on V1 or migrate to V2.

Inside of `UnboundedKerosineVault::assetPrice()` we are deterministically calculating the price of Kerosene.
```javascript
function assetPrice() public view override returns (uint) {
        uint tvl;
        address[] memory vaults = kerosineManager.getVaults();
        uint numberOfVaults = vaults.length;
        for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
            Vault vault = Vault(vaults[i]);

            tvl +=
                (vault.asset().balanceOf(address(vault)) * //@audit - balanceOf() can be manipulatable
                    vault.assetPrice() *
                    1e18) /
                (10 ** vault.asset().decimals()) /
                (10 ** vault.oracle().decimals());
        }
        @review - Determintistically calculate the price
@>      uint numerator = tvl - dyad.totalSupply();
        uint denominator = kerosineDenominator.denominator();
        return (numerator * 1e8) / denominator;
    }
```

However, due to the V2 system having a completely different tvl than V1, but share the same dyad total supply. A Malicious actor can take advantage of this. Since the V1 manager is not protected from flash loan attacks, an attacker can take a flash loan and mint just enough dyad, so that the price of kerosene drops drastically, without causing underflow revert.
Which then can open doors for liquidating healthy positions.

[Coded PoC of manipulating kerosene just by depositing](https://gist.github.com/kostadin-m/af4350c5f91686568d586808ee5ba66c)

Run a forked test at a specific block number to have accurate results:
```bash
forge test --fork-url <MAINNET_FORK_URL> --fork-block-number 19720983   --match-test testUserCanManipulateKeroseneThroughV1Manager -vv 

```

## Tools Used
Foundry, Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
It is really hard to recommend something due to the nature of the upgrade.
1. If we add the old vaults to `KeroseneManager::vaults` the tvl will still be manipulatable by flashloan attacks through the old manager.
2. If we completely abandon the old manager, all of the dyad minted from V1 will be lost.


