# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Users are unable to mint dyad stable coin when they add kerosine vault to their notes in addition to other non kerosine vaults. When users do not add kerosine vault to their notes, they are able to mint dyad stable-coins without any issues. This issue can be traced to the  `getKeroseneValue` function.

```solidity
function getKeroseneValue(
    uint id
  ) 
    public 
    view
    returns (uint) {
      uint totalUsdValue;
      uint numberOfVaults = vaultsKerosene[id].length(); 
      for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
        Vault vault = Vault(vaultsKerosene[id].at(i));
        uint usdValue;
        if (keroseneManager.isLicensed(address(vault))) {
@>          usdValue = vault.getUsdValue(id);        
        }
        totalUsdValue += usdValue;
      }
      return totalUsdValue;
  }
```

``` solidity
 function getUsdValue(
    uint id
  )
    public
    view 
    returns (uint) {
 @>     return id2asset[id] * assetPrice() / 1e8;
  }
```

```solidity
function assetPrice() 
    public 
    view 
    override
    returns (uint) {
      uint tvl;
      address[] memory vaults = kerosineManager.getVaults();
      uint numberOfVaults = vaults.length;
      for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
        Vault vault = Vault(vaults[i]);
        tvl += vault.asset().balanceOf(address(vault)) 
@>                * vault.assetPrice() * 1e18
                / (10**vault.asset().decimals()) 
@>                / (10**vault.oracle().decimals());
      }
      uint numerator   = tvl - dyad.totalSupply();
      uint denominator = kerosineDenominator.denominator();
      return numerator * 1e8 / denominator;
  }


```
When the user tries to mint dyad tokens, the `mintDyad` function calls the `getKeroseneValue` at a point in order to calculate the totalUsdValue for all kerosene vault. The problem is that after the keroseneManager checks that the vault is licensed, the function vault.getUsdValue(id) was called in order to get the usdValue of the vault which then calls the assetPrice() function. This function makes another call to the vault oracle but kerosene vaults do not have an oracle function.

Only non kerosine vaults have an oracle function because it is needed to get the current price of the underlying assets. The transaction will revert when any kerosine vault tries to call the oracle function which does not exists in kerosine vaults contract.


## Proof of Concept
1. User buys DNFT.
2. User adds Kerosine vault to the Vault Manager.
3. User approves Vault Manager to spend kerosene tokens on its behalf
4. User deposits 10 kerosine tokens to the kerosine vault
5. User adds Eth vault to the Vault Manager
6. User approves Vault Manager to spend weth tokens on its behalf
7. User deposits 1 weth token to the eth vault.
8. User tries to mint DYAD
9. User is unable to mint DYAD stablecoin

