# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Kerosene price may be calculated incorrectly or transations dosed while misbehavior of ChainlinkOracle for any vault in `vaults`. 

## Proof of Concept
assetPrice in UnboundedKeroseneVault contract is calculated to below. 
```solidity
function assetPrice() 
    public 
    view 
    override
    returns (uint) {
      uint tvl;
      address[] memory vaults = kerosineManager.getVaults();
      uint numberOfVaults = vaults.length;
      for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
        Vault vault = Vault(vaults[i]);
        tvl += vault.asset().balanceOf(address(vault)) 
                * vault.assetPrice() * 1e18
                / (10**vault.asset().decimals()) 
                / (10**vault.oracle().decimals());
      }
      uint numerator   = tvl - dyad.totalSupply();
      uint denominator = kerosineDenominator.denominator(); // @audit donation attack
      return numerator * 1e8 / denominator;
  }
```
vault.assetPrice can be 0 because vault contract can return zero value if Chainlink Oracle misbehaves (vault contract only reverts if price is less than 0 but not zero.).
So if an oracle returns zero price for an asset, then TVL can be underestimated.
It affects collatRatio, and therefore mint, withdraw resulting in inaccurate accounting. 
Furthermore, if underestimated tvl is less than total minted dyad, then all transactions that is related to tvl are reverted. 

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Use fallback mechanism for misbehaving of Chainlink oracle.


## Assessed type

DoS

# Lines of code

