# Vulnerability details

## Impact
As per the readme of the contest, the ``Deploy.V2.s.sol`` contract is in scope, and in this file the steps to migrate to the new ``VaultManagerV2.sol`` are defined. However the protocol team has neglected the fact that there is already a circulating supply of DYAD tokens. As of writing the report the [total supply](https://etherscan.io/address/0x305b58c5f6b5b6606fb13edd11fbdd5e532d5a26#readContract) is: **632_967_400_000_000_000_000_000** ≈ **632_967e18**. And when the Unbounded Kerosine Vault is [deployed](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/script/deploy/Deploy.V2.s.sol#L71-L76) the address of the already existing DYAD token is set. 
```solidity
    UnboundedKerosineVault unboundedKerosineVault = new UnboundedKerosineVault(
      vaultManager,
      Kerosine(MAINNET_KEROSENE), 
      Dyad(MAINNET_DYAD),
      kerosineManager
    );
```
In ``Vault.kerosine.unbounded.sol`` the asset price is calculated in the following way:
```solidity
  function assetPrice() public view override returns (uint) {
      uint tvl;
      address[] memory vaults = kerosineManager.getVaults();
      uint numberOfVaults = vaults.length;
      for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
        Vault vault = Vault(vaults[i]);
        tvl += vault.asset().balanceOf(address(vault)) 
                * vault.assetPrice() * 1e18
                / (10**vault.asset().decimals()) 
                / (10**vault.oracle().decimals());
      }
      uint numerator = tvl - dyad.totalSupply();
      uint denominator = kerosineDenominator.denominator();
      return numerator * 1e8 / denominator;
  }
```
As we can see the DYAD token total supply is subtracted from the tvl, and later on some addition calculations are performed. However in the deployment script new [wethVault](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/script/deploy/Deploy.V2.s.sol#L49-L53) and [wstETHVault](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/script/deploy/Deploy.V2.s.sol#L56-L60) are created with 0 funds, and added to the [kerosineManager](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/script/deploy/Deploy.V2.s.sol#L64-L65). When a function calls the [assetPrice()]() function it will revert as the TVL will initially be 0, and the DYAD token supply is approximately **632_967e18**. Functions like ``withdraw()``, ``liquidate()``, ``redeemDyad()``, ``mintDyad()`` will always revert if the Note owner, has added the unbounded kerosine vault to his list of ``vaults``, no matter if he has deposited funds in it or not. It will require at least \$632_967 worth of collateral to be deposited to the vaults, before any new DYAD can be minted. 


