https://github.com/pavankv241/2024-04-dyad-ICP/blob/main/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L153


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The withdraw() function can be halted by DNFT owner. 

## Summary

The withdraw() function used to withdraw the collateral by the user who deposited in the DNft. In below code snippet we can observe that `value` is calculated by the various factors(ex. assetPrice and decimals) and  last check says if `dyadMinted` is greater than the `getNonKeroseneValue(id) - value` it will revert the withdraw process.

```solidity
uint dyadMinted = dyad.mintedDyad(address(this), id);

    Vault _vault = Vault(vault);

    uint value = amount * _vault.assetPrice() * 1e18 / 10**_vault.oracle().decimals()/ 10**_vault.asset().decimals();

    if (getNonKeroseneValue(id) - value < dyadMinted) revert NotEnoughExoCollat();

```

In below [code snippet](https://github.com/pavankv241/2024-04-dyad-ICP/blob/main/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L169C1-L175C73) we can see that `dyad` can be minted by the DNft owner by intentionally or non-intentionally. If the DNft owner have intension to halt the withdraw function he can front-run the `withdraw()` transaction by his `mintDyad()` function it will increase the minted value of dyad then it will directly subsequent withdraw() transaction.

```solidity
  function mintDyad(
    uint    id,
    uint    amount,
    address to
  )
    external 
      isDNftOwner(id)
  {
    uint newDyadMinted = dyad.mintedDyad(address(this), id) + amount;

    if (getNonKeroseneValue(id) < newDyadMinted)     revert NotEnoughExoCollat();

    dyad.mint(id, to, amount);

    if (collatRatio(id) < MIN_COLLATERIZATION_RATIO) revert CrTooLow(); 

    emit MintDyad(id, amount, to);
  }
```

Then below [check](https://github.com/pavankv241/2024-04-dyad-ICP/blob/main/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L153) will revert the withdraw() transaction:-

```solidity
if (getNonKeroseneValue(id) - value < dyadMinted) revert NotEnoughExoCollat();
```

## Proof of Concept

1. User calls withdraw() transaction then DNft owner can see the transaction in mem pool and calls the `mintDyad()` function to increase the minted dyad value.

2. The [check](https://github.com/pavankv241/2024-04-dyad-ICP/blob/main/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L153) in the withdraw() function will revert due minted Dyad value is greater than the `getNonKeroseneValue(id) - value`

## Tools Used
Manual Code Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Instead of getting direct value of Minted Dyad value from the state while withdraw() ,implement delay mechanism between mint and withdraw or rebasing mechanism.





