# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The protocol allows the owner of a loan to front-run liquidation events to their advantage. This includes liquidating their own loan or others' smaller positions to prevent their own liquidation, or front-running to burn their issued Dyad. The absence of interest payments on loans within the protocol reduces the urgency for debtors to maintain a healthy `CR`, allowing them to behave opportunistically without any financial repercussions. 
When the CR drops below 150%, debtors can strategically use MEV tactics to front-run and eliminate their debt, putting the protocol stability at risk. While also disincentivizing liquidators from engaging which could put the protocol liquidity at risk.

## Proof of Concept
The protocol's design does not penalize debtors from allowing their collateralization ratios to fall below safe thresholds if they decide to front-run a liquidation event. A debtor can take three actions to avoid a liqidation:
1. Front-runs to liquidate their own loan when CR drops
2. Liquidates another user's smaller position to reduce their own debt
3. Burns their own Dyad strategically before a liquidation event can occur

Any token withdrawal/burn has no interest payments :
`_vault.withdraw(id, to, amount);`

Consider the follwing test :

```js
    function test_FrontRunLiquidation() public {
        uint256 id = mintDNft();
        uint256 id2 = mintDNft();

        // Follow script deployement. Weth Vault is licensed in both VaultManager and KerosineManager
        // vaultManagerV2.add(id, address(unboundedKerosineVault));
        vaultManagerV2.add(id, address(wethVaultV2));

        // User deposits weth
        depositV2(weth, id, address(wethVaultV2), 1e22); //weth 1000 Usd

        //Then mint dyad
        vaultManagerV2.mintDyad(id, 1e24, RECEIVER);
        // Assume price decreases
        wethOracle.setPrice(100e8);

        vm.prank(RECEIVER);
        vaultManagerV2.burnDyad(id,3.5e23);

        vm.expectRevert(IVaultManager.CrTooHigh.selector);
        vm.prank(RECEIVER);
        vaultManagerV2.liquidate(id, id2);
    }
```

Because of the lack of interest payments on the debt, users are not worried about their CR falling below `MIN_COLLATERIZATION_RATIO`. And if it does, front-run the liquidation event without any consequence. Doing this means less opportunities for other liquidators which are now relunctant to intervene the next time a position needs to be liquidated. 

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider implementing interest rates on borrowed amounts. This would incentivize users to maintain their positions and manage their CR more actively. Users will also avoid front-running their own positions since even if they repay or liquidate their debt, they will also have to pay interest. 





