# Vulnerability details

## Impact
There is no check to ensure that the vault being deposited into has already been added by the user. Consequently, a user could deposit into a vault that has not been added yet. This could be problematic, especially if the user has reached the `MAX_VAULTS` limit and needs to deposit assets to avoid liquidation.

## Proof of Concept
In `VaultManagerV2::deposit`, there is no check to ensure that the vault being deposited into is one that the user has already added.

```solidity
  function deposit(
    uint    id,
    address vault,
    uint    amount
  ) 
    external 
      isValidDNft(id)
  {
    idToBlockOfLastDeposit[id] = block.number;
@=>    Vault _vault = Vault(vault);
    _vault.asset().safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(vault), amount);
    _vault.deposit(id, amount);
  }
```

If a user has reached the `MAX_VAULTS` limitation and is at risk of being liquidated, he must deposit additional assets to increase his `NonKeroseneValue`.

However, if he deposits into a vault he has not added before, the return value of `getNonKeroseneValue` will not change since the vault is not in `vaults[id]`, leaving himeself still at risk of being liquidated.

```solidity
  function getNonKeroseneValue(
    uint id
  ) 
    public 
    view
    returns (uint) {
      uint totalUsdValue;
      uint numberOfVaults = vaults[id].length(); 
      for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
@=>        Vault vault = Vault(vaults[id].at(i));
        uint usdValue;
        if (vaultLicenser.isLicensed(address(vault))) {
          usdValue = vault.getUsdValue(id);        
        }
        totalUsdValue += usdValue;
      }
      return totalUsdValue;
  }
```

He cannot withdraw the funds directly since he is currently below or near the MIN_COLLATERIZATION_RATIO.

```solidity
  function withdraw(
    uint    id,
    address vault,
    uint    amount,
    address to
  ) 
    public
      isDNftOwner(id)
  {
    if (idToBlockOfLastDeposit[id] == block.number) revert DepositedInSameBlock();
    uint dyadMinted = dyad.mintedDyad(address(this), id);
    Vault _vault = Vault(vault);
    uint value = amount * _vault.assetPrice() 
                  * 1e18 
                  / 10**_vault.oracle().decimals() 
                  / 10**_vault.asset().decimals(); 
    if (getNonKeroseneValue(id) - value < dyadMinted) revert NotEnoughExoCollat();
    _vault.withdraw(id, to, amount);
@=>    if (collatRatio(id) < MIN_COLLATERIZATION_RATIO)  revert CrTooLow(); 
  }

```

He cannot remove an existing vault for the same reason. If he has no additional funds to deposit correctly, his current funds will be locked.


## Tools Used
Manual

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
It is recommended to add checks to ensure the `vault` to deposit into has already been added by the user.


