# Vulnerability details


If an nft owner buy DYAD from a DEX because he spotted an arbitrage opportunity ( for example DEX price dropped for a slight period to 0,97 USD for 1 DYAD, but just on dex) it will not be able to redeem that DYAD back into an asset to the price of 1 USD trough the vaults if his nft have not minted any tokens so far or minted less tokens then the amount he wants to redeem.
That is happening because the DYAD contract is tracking how many tokens have an Vault Manager minted for a certain NftID and when burning is happening the amount of tokens you want to burn will be subtracted from the minted amount and because that NftId have not minted any tokens and only bough them an underflow revert will happen

## Impact
Redeem function is failing when trying to convert DYAD bought from DEX or received as debt/collateral will be seen as 0 for that NftId and it will stop the user from performing arbitrage operations and helping bringing the pegging back.

## Proof of Concept

