# Vulnerability details

## Description
Integration to Chainlink oracle is done through `EACAggregatorProxy` contracts which call implementation of [stETH](https://etherscan.io/address/0xdA31bc2B08F22AE24aeD5F6EB1E71E96867BA196#readContract) and [ETH](https://etherscan.io/address/0xE62B71cf983019BFf55bC83B48601ce8419650CC#readContract) aggregator implementation.

Current stETH agregator implementation enforce a min answer of 1 USD, if for any reason the price of stETH goes below this price then, given no check related to thist constraint is done, anyone would be able to use this asset to mint undercollateralize DYAD thorugh `VaultManagerV2.mintDyad` by simply creating and Note NFT, depositing DYAD and then selling it in a DEX.

## Impact
Undercollateralize DYAD minting in a scenario similar to [Venus and Blizz finance exploit during Terra crash](https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-protocols-declare-losses-as-attackers-exploit-luna-price-feed-discrepancy) for 1 minute and 30 seconds given implemented time staleness check


