# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The withdrawal function in the contract currently performs the collateral ratio check after executing the withdrawal, which poses a risk of under-collateralization. This means that if a user withdraws assets and the resulting collateral ratio falls below the minimum required ratio, the function should revert to prevent the vault from becoming under-collateralized. However, the current implementation checks the collateral ratio after the withdrawal is executed, potentially leaving the vault under-collateralized.


## Proof of Concept

```javascript
function withdraw(
        uint id,
        address vault,
        uint amount,
        address to
    ) public isDNftOwner(id) {
        if (idToBlockOfLastDeposit[id] == block.number)
            revert DepositedInSameBlock();
        uint dyadMinted = dyad.mintedDyad(address(this), id);
        Vault _vault = Vault(vault);
        uint value = (amount * _vault.assetPrice() * 1e18) / //@audit----info chainlink
            10 ** _vault.oracle().decimals() /
            10 ** _vault.asset().decimals();
        if (getNonKeroseneValue(id) - value < dyadMinted)
            revert NotEnoughExoCollat();
        _vault.withdraw(id, to, amount);
        if (collatRatio(id) < MIN_COLLATERIZATION_RATIO) revert CrTooLow();
    }
```


## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
The collateral ratio check should be performed before executing the withdrawal to ensure that the vault remains adequately collateralized after the withdrawal operation. This will prevent potential financial risks to the protocol and its users.

```javascript
function withdraw(
    uint id,
    address vault,
    uint amount,
    address to
) public isDNftOwner(id) {


    // Check if the deposit was made in the same block
    if (idToBlockOfLastDeposit[id] == block.number) {
        revert DepositedInSameBlock();
    }

    uint dyadMinted = dyad.mintedDyad(address(this), id);
    Vault _vault = Vault(vault);
    uint value = (amount * _vault.assetPrice() * 1e18) / //@audit----info chainlink
        10 ** _vault.oracle().decimals() /
        10 ** _vault.asset().decimals();

    // Calculate the collateral ratio after withdrawal
    uint finalCollatRatio = collatRatio(id) * dyad.totalSupply() - value;

    // Check if the collateral ratio is sufficient after withdrawal
    if (finalCollatRatio < MIN_COLLATERIZATION_RATIO) {
        revert CrTooLow();
    }

    // Check if there is enough collateral to cover the minted Dyad tokens
    if (getNonKeroseneValue(id) - value < dyadMinted) {
        revert NotEnoughExoCollat();
    }

    // Withdraw the assets
    _vault.withdraw(id, to, amount);
}
```



