MEV

# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/4a987e536576139793a1c04690336d06c93fca90/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L205-L228


# Vulnerability details

## Summary
In some extreme cases, `oracles` can be taken offline or token prices can fall to zero. In these cases, liquidations will be frozen (all calls will revert) for any `undercollateralized positions`, even though they may be some of the most important times to allow liquidations to retain the solvency of the protocol.

## Proof of Concept
`Chainlink` has taken oracles offline in extreme cases. For example, during the `UST collapse`, Chainlink paused the `UST/ETH` price oracle, to ensure that it wasn't providing inaccurate data to protocols.

In such a situation, all liquidations for users holding `undercollateralized positions` would revert.

### Scenario
A `liquidator` calls the [liquidate()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/4a987e536576139793a1c04690336d06c93fca90/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L205-L228) function to liquidate a user whose `collateral value in USD has dropped below 150% of its DYAD minted balance`.

```solidity
  function liquidate(
    uint id,
    uint to
  ) 
    external 
      isValidDNft(id)
      isValidDNft(to)
    {
      uint cr = collatRatio(id);
      if (cr >= MIN_COLLATERIZATION_RATIO) revert CrTooHigh();
      dyad.burn(id, msg.sender, dyad.mintedDyad(address(this), id));


      uint cappedCr               = cr < 1e18 ? 1e18 : cr;
      uint liquidationEquityShare = (cappedCr - 1e18).mulWadDown(LIQUIDATION_REWARD);
      uint liquidationAssetShare  = (liquidationEquityShare + 1e18).divWadDown(cappedCr);


      uint numberOfVaults = vaults[id].length();
      for (uint i = 0; i < numberOfVaults; i++) {
          Vault vault      = Vault(vaults[id].at(i));
          uint  collateral = vault.id2asset(id).mulWadUp(liquidationAssetShare);
          vault.move(id, to, collateral);
      }
      emit Liquidate(id, msg.sender, to);
  }
```
This function calls [collatRatio()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/4a987e536576139793a1c04690336d06c93fca90/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L230-L239) which is intended to return the `collateral ratio` associated with users collateral to minted `DYAD`.
The [getTotalUsdValue()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/4a987e536576139793a1c04690336d06c93fca90/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L241-L248) is called here internally which returns the summation of two values.
The two functions [getNonKeroseneValue()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/4a987e536576139793a1c04690336d06c93fca90/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L262C22-L262C44) and [getKeroseneValue()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/4a987e536576139793a1c04690336d06c93fca90/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L281) calls the [vault.getUsdValue()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/4a987e536576139793a1c04690336d06c93fca90/src/core/Vault.sol#L85) which invokes the `chainlink oracle` to fetch the assets prices.

The call to [Chainlink's oracle.latestRoundData()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/4a987e536576139793a1c04690336d06c93fca90/src/core/Vault.sol#L100C11-L100C35) would fail on this check:

```solidity
if (block.timestamp > updatedAt + STALE_DATA_TIMEOUT) revert StaleData();
```

If the oracle price lookup reverts, liquidations will be frozen, and the user will be immune to liquidations. 

## Impact
Liquidations may not be possible at a time when the protocol needs them most. As a result, the value of user's asset may fall below `150% of its DYAD minted balance`, turning off any liquidation incentive and pushing the protocol into insolvency.

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Ensure there is a safeguard in place to protect against this possibility.


