# Lines of code

https://github.com/limitbreakinc/PermitC/blob/c431dc5e80690c1d8c3727f5992d519df3d38254/src/PermitC.sol#L1110
https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-periph/blob/2ddbcb1cde03b548e13421b2dba66435d2ac8eb5/contracts/tapiocaOmnichainEngine/extension/TapiocaOmnichainExtExec.sol#L170-L179


# Vulnerability details

### Impact
As detailed in [Trusts Article](https://www.trust-security.xyz/post/permission-denied) the fundamental aspect of the grief is just the front-run of permit + call

This is because permit can be made to revert

The mitigations in place by using Pearlmit don't address this aspect

As calls are uncaught, front-running to consume the nonce is still possible, which will cause xChain calls to revert.


### Pearlmit Reverts on used nonce

As you can see, the code from `PermitC` will still revert on re-using a nonce:

https://github.com/limitbreakinc/PermitC/blob/c431dc5e80690c1d8c3727f5992d519df3d38254/src/PermitC.sol#L1110

```solidity
    function _checkAndInvalidateNonce(address account, uint256 nonce) internal {
        unchecked {
            if (uint256(_unorderedNonces[account][uint248(nonce >> 8)] ^= (ONE << uint8(nonce))) & 
                (ONE << uint8(nonce)) == ZERO) {
                revert PermitC__NonceAlreadyUsedOrRevoked();
            }
        }
    }
```

And `msg.sender` is not checked (since `permit` works by signature):

https://github.com/limitbreakinc/PermitC/blob/c431dc5e80690c1d8c3727f5992d519df3d38254/src/PermitC.sol#L170-L203


### Normal Permits also are uncaught

https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-periph/blob/2ddbcb1cde03b548e13421b2dba66435d2ac8eb5/contracts/tapiocaOmnichainEngine/extension/TapiocaOmnichainExtExec.sol#L170-L179

```solidity
    function marketPermit(bytes memory _data) public {
        MarketPermitActionMsg memory approval = TapiocaOmnichainEngineCodec.decodeMarketPermitApprovalMsg(_data);
        _sanitizeTarget(approval.target);
        /// @audit The permits still revert!!!!
        if (approval.permitAsset) {
            _marketPermitAssetApproval(approval);
        } else {
            _marketPermitCollateralApproval(approval);
        }
    }
```


https://github.com/Tapioca-DAO/tapioca-periph/blob/2ddbcb1cde03b548e13421b2dba66435d2ac8eb5/contracts/tapiocaOmnichainEngine/extension/TapiocaOmnichainExtExec.sol#L245-L255

```solidity
    function _marketPermitAssetApproval(MarketPermitActionMsg memory _approval) internal {
        IPermit(_approval.target).permit(
            _approval.owner,
            _approval.spender,
            _approval.value,
            _approval.deadline,
            _approval.v,
            _approval.r,
            _approval.s
        );
    }
```

Meaning all xChain operations that uses permit can be made to revert since the permits can still revert and are not caught

This means that a front-runner can simply consume the nonces to cause xChain operations to revert

### Mitigation

All permit calls must be caught, if you wish to catch a public call from permitC, you can use:

```solidity
function safePermitToSelf(bytes memory DATA) public {
    try this.updateApprovalBySignature(DATA) {} catch {}
}
```
as a means to ensure that the consumed approval doesn't cause reverts


