# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Inaccurate calculation of token amounts and uncollected fees.

## Proof of Concept
The `getPositionBreakdown` function returns the breakdown of a Uniswap V3 position, including the token0, token1, fee tier, liquidity, current token amounts, and uncollected fees. It calculates the current token amounts based on the current pool price (state.sqrtPriceX96). It also calculates the uncollected fees based on the fee growth inside the position's tick range. These calculations rely on the pool's fee growth globals, which are derived from the pool prices. 

```solidity
function getPositionBreakdown(uint256 tokenId)
        public
        view
        override
        returns (
            address token0,
            address token1,
            uint24 fee,
            uint128 liquidity,
            uint256 amount0,
            uint256 amount1,
            uint128 fees0,
            uint128 fees1
        )
    {
        PositionState memory state = _initializeState(tokenId);
        (token0, token1, fee) = (state.token0, state.token1, state.fee);
        (amount0, amount1, fees0, fees1) = _getAmounts(state);
        liquidity = state.liquidity;
    }
```

The issue here is that the derived pool price is not validated against the reference pool price obtained from the configured oracles.

In the _getAmounts function, amount0` and `amount1` are calculated based on the current pool price (state.sqrtPriceX96)

```solidity
function _getAmounts(PositionState memory state)
        internal
        view
        returns (uint256 amount0, uint256 amount1, uint128 fees0, uint128 fees1)
    {
        if (state.liquidity > 0) {
            state.sqrtPriceX96Lower = TickMath.getSqrtRatioAtTick(state.tickLower);
            state.sqrtPriceX96Upper = TickMath.getSqrtRatioAtTick(state.tickUpper);
            (amount0, amount1) = LiquidityAmounts.getAmountsForLiquidity(
                state.sqrtPriceX96, state.sqrtPriceX96Lower, state.sqrtPriceX96Upper, state.liquidity
            );
        }

        (fees0, fees1) = _getUncollectedFees(state, state.tick);
        fees0 += state.tokensOwed0;
        fees1 += state.tokensOwed1;
    }
```

The `_getUncollectedFees` function calculates the uncollected fees based on the pool's fee growth globals, derived from the pool prices

```solidity
function _getUncollectedFees(PositionState memory position, int24 tick)
        internal
        view
        returns (uint128 fees0, uint128 fees1)
    {
        (uint256 feeGrowthInside0LastX128, uint256 feeGrowthInside1LastX128) = _getFeeGrowthInside(
            position.pool,
            position.tickLower,
            position.tickUpper,
            tick,
            position.pool.feeGrowthGlobal0X128(),
            position.pool.feeGrowthGlobal1X128()
        );

        // allow overflow - this is as designed by uniswap - see PositionValue library (for solidity < 0.8)
        uint256 feeGrowth0;
        uint256 feeGrowth1;
        unchecked {
            feeGrowth0 = feeGrowthInside0LastX128 - position.feeGrowthInside0LastX128;
            feeGrowth1 = feeGrowthInside1LastX128 - position.feeGrowthInside1LastX128;
        }

        fees0 = uint128(FullMath.mulDiv(feeGrowth0, position.liquidity, Q128));
        fees1 = uint128(FullMath.mulDiv(feeGrowth1, position.liquidity, Q128));
    }

```

## Tools Used
Manual 

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Validate the pool price before calculating token amounts and fee growth by adding this check to _getUncollectedFees and _getAmounts functions.

```solidity
_checkPoolPrice(state.token0, state.token1, state.fee, state.sqrtPriceX96);
```


