# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-revert-lend/blob/main/src/V3Vault.sol#L604-L646
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-revert-lend/blob/main/src/transformers/V3Utils.sol#L112-L352


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Users can decrease their liquidity and collect it using the `decreaseLiquidityAndCollect()`, which naturally changes the global interest rate. However, in the `execute()` users can also decrease their liquidity and collect it, but the global interest is not being changed. The effect of this could be immense, since after a while the interest rate disruption will grow immensely leading to a completely broken and unfixable financial system.

## Proof of Concept
You can run the following test below to see that the interest rate has not changed, yet the liquidity has been taken.

The test should be ran in the `V3Utils.t.sol` file.
You have to import the following:
```js
import "../../src/V3Vault.sol";
import "../../src/InterestRateModel.sol";
import "../../src/V3Oracle.sol";
```

You have to also get the following constant and properties:
```js
uint256 constant Q96 = 2 ** 96;

V3Vault vault;
InterestRateModel interestRateModel;
V3Oracle oracle;
```

Then you have to initialize them in the constructor:
```js
vault = new V3Vault("Revert Lend USDC", "rlUSDC", address(USDC), NPM, interestRateModel, oracle, IPermit2(PERMIT2));

// 0% base rate - 5% multiplier - after 80% - 109% jump multiplier (like in compound v2 deployed)  (-> max rate 25.8% per year)
interestRateModel = new InterestRateModel(0, Q96 * 5 / 100, Q96 * 109 / 100, Q96 * 80 / 100);

oracle = new V3Oracle(NPM, address(USDC), address(0));
```

Finally you should paste and run the test below:
```js
    function testDecreaseLiquidityAndCollectUsingExecuteToSkipUpdatingInterest() external {

        uint256 debtExchangeRateX96Before = vault.lastDebtExchangeRateX96();

        // add liquidity to existing (empty) position (add 1 DAI / 0 USDC)
        _increaseLiquidity();

        uint256 countBefore = NPM.balanceOf(TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT);

        (,,,,,,, uint128 liquidityBefore,,,,) = NPM.positions(TEST_NFT);

        // swap half of DAI to USDC and add full range
        V3Utils.Instructions memory inst = V3Utils.Instructions(
            V3Utils.WhatToDo.CHANGE_RANGE,
            address(USDC),
            0,
            0,
            500000000000000000,
            400000,
            _get05DAIToUSDCSwapData(),
            0,
            0,
            "",
            type(uint128).max, // take all fees
            type(uint128).max, // take all fees
            100, // change fee as well
            MIN_TICK_100,
            -MIN_TICK_100,
            liquidityBefore, // take all liquidity
            0,
            0,
            block.timestamp,
            TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT,
            TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT,
            false,
            "",
            ""
        );

        vm.prank(TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT);
        NPM.approve(address(v3utils), TEST_NFT);

        vm.prank(TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT);
        v3utils.execute(TEST_NFT, inst);

        uint256 countAfter = NPM.balanceOf(TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT);
        assertGt(countAfter, countBefore);

        (,,,,,,, uint128 liquidityAfter,,,,) = NPM.positions(TEST_NFT);
        assertEq(liquidityAfter, 0);

        uint256 debtExchangeRateX96After = vault.lastDebtExchangeRateX96();

        assertEq(debtExchangeRateX96Before, debtExchangeRateX96After);
    }
```

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Adding a check to allow only transformers to use the access the `execute()` or adding the same logic for changing the global interest rate in the `execute()` as it is in the `decreaseLiquidityAndCollect()`.


