# Vulnerability details

## Impact
`_requireLoanIsHealthy` calls `_checkLoanIsHealthy`, `_checkLoanIsHealthy` calls `calculateTokenCollateralFactorX32` which just gets the collateralFactorX32 which is a static value that doesn't reflect the liquidity in the position.

collateralFactorX32 just reflects how much the tokens(token0 and token1) in the uniswap V3 lp position are valued as collateral.


1. The issue here is that even if there was liquidity in the uniswap V3 lp position NFT , The owner of the NFT can still remove its liquidity via `V3Vault.decreaseLiquidityAndCollect()` 
```solidity
 function decreaseLiquidityAndCollect(DecreaseLiquidityAndCollectParams calldata params)// @audit-issue will revert.
        external
        override
        returns (uint256 amount0, uint256 amount1)
    {
        // this method is not allowed during transform - can be called directly on nftmanager if needed from transform contract
        if (transformedTokenId > 0) {
            revert TransformNotAllowed();
        }

        address owner = tokenOwner[params.tokenId];

        if (owner != msg.sender) {
            revert Unauthorized();
        }

        (uint256 newDebtExchangeRateX96,) = _updateGlobalInterest();

        (amount0, amount1) = nonfungiblePositionManager.decreaseLiquidity(
            INonfungiblePositionManager.DecreaseLiquidityParams(
                params.tokenId, params.liquidity, params.amount0Min, params.amount1Min, params.deadline
            )
        );

        INonfungiblePositionManager.CollectParams memory collectParams = INonfungiblePositionManager.CollectParams(
            params.tokenId,
            params.recipient,
            params.feeAmount0 == type(uint128).max ? type(uint128).max : SafeCast.toUint128(amount0 + params.feeAmount0),
            params.feeAmount1 == type(uint128).max ? type(uint128).max : SafeCast.toUint128(amount1 + params.feeAmount1)
        );

        (amount0, amount1) = nonfungiblePositionManager.collect(collectParams);

        uint256 debt = _convertToAssets(loans[params.tokenId].debtShares, newDebtExchangeRateX96, Math.Rounding.Up);
        _requireLoanIsHealthy(params.tokenId, debt);//@audit

        emit WithdrawCollateral(params.tokenId, owner, params.recipient, params.liquidity, amount0, amount1);
    }
```
The `_requireLoanIsHealthy()` within the above function won't be able to stop this because its logic doesn't check the liquidity of the uniswap V3 lp position NFT.

The owner of the NFT can remove its liquidity, leaving the loan he took with an empty collateral tokenId which is a loss for the protocol.

2. it will never be possible to liquidate borrows backed with collateral tokenIds that have no liquidity since `_requireLoanIsHealthy()` doesn't check the liquidity of the uniswap V3 lp position NFT, so as long as `collateralFactorX32 * fullValue / Q32` is > or == `debt`, the borrow is still assumed to be healthy.
```solidity
 function _checkLoanIsHealthy(uint256 tokenId, uint256 debt)
        internal
        view
        returns (bool isHealthy, uint256 fullValue, uint256 collateralValue, uint256 feeValue)
    {
        (fullValue, feeValue,,) = oracle.getValue(tokenId, address(asset));
        uint256 collateralFactorX32 = _calculateTokenCollateralFactorX32(tokenId);
        collateralValue = fullValue.mulDiv(collateralFactorX32, Q32);
        isHealthy = collateralValue >= debt;// @audit
    }
```

3. It is possible to borrow and use uniswap v3 tokenIds that have no liquidity as collateral. This is a loss to the protocol and lenders because a malicious fellow could take mssive borrows with empty uniswap v3 tokenIds

## Proof of Concept
The logic within `_requireLoanIsHealthy()` doesn't check the liquidity of the uniswap V3 lp position NFT

