# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-revert-lend/blob/main/src/V3Vault.sol?plain=1#L1205-L1244


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

When a loan's collateral is updated via V3Vault._updateAndCheckCollateral(), Revert assumes that the NFT position has tokens applied equally to both tokens in the position and applies a debt share update to both of the position's tokens. 

However, a Uniswap V3 NFT position can have an uneven distribution between both tokens. The position can also have liquidity applied to just one token. When NFT positions like this are deposited into the vault and Revert updates its collateral, Revert unfairly updates both token's totalDebtShares not taking into account the possibility of unequal distribution. This leads to cases where a token's totalDebtShares is miscalculated, inflating the value of totalDebtShares, and leading to premature collateral limits being reached. This can prematurely block certain features within Revert, such as borrowing Vault assets.

## Proof of Concept

Below is the code for the _updateAndCheckCollateral() function:

```solidity
function _updateAndCheckCollateral(
    uint256 tokenId,
    uint256 debtExchangeRateX96,
    uint256 lendExchangeRateX96,
    uint256 oldShares,
    uint256 newShares
) internal {
    if (oldShares != newShares) {
        (,, address token0, address token1,,,,,,,,) = nonfungiblePositionManager.positions(tokenId);

        // remove previous collateral - add new collateral
        if (oldShares > newShares) {
            tokenConfigs[token0].totalDebtShares -= SafeCast.toUint192(oldShares - newShares);
            tokenConfigs[token1].totalDebtShares -= SafeCast.toUint192(oldShares - newShares);
        } else {
            tokenConfigs[token0].totalDebtShares += SafeCast.toUint192(newShares - oldShares);
            tokenConfigs[token1].totalDebtShares += SafeCast.toUint192(newShares - oldShares);

            // check if current value of used collateral is more than allowed limit
            // if collateral is decreased - never revert
            uint256 lentAssets = _convertToAssets(totalSupply(), lendExchangeRateX96, Math.Rounding.Up);
            uint256 collateralValueLimitFactorX32 = tokenConfigs[token0].collateralValueLimitFactorX32;
            if (
                collateralValueLimitFactorX32 < type(uint32).max
                    && _convertToAssets(tokenConfigs[token0].totalDebtShares, debtExchangeRateX96, Math.Rounding.Up)
                        > lentAssets * collateralValueLimitFactorX32 / Q32
            ) {
                revert CollateralValueLimit();
            }
            collateralValueLimitFactorX32 = tokenConfigs[token1].collateralValueLimitFactorX32;
            if (
                collateralValueLimitFactorX32 < type(uint32).max
                    && _convertToAssets(tokenConfigs[token1].totalDebtShares, debtExchangeRateX96, Math.Rounding.Up)
                        > lentAssets * collateralValueLimitFactorX32 / Q32
            ) {
                revert CollateralValueLimit();
            }
        }
    }
}
```

As you can see above, whenever the debt shares is updated, the following code is executed:

```solidity
(,, address token0, address token1,,,,,,,,) = nonfungiblePositionManager.positions(tokenId);

// remove previous collateral - add new collateral
if (oldShares > newShares) {
    tokenConfigs[token0].totalDebtShares -= SafeCast.toUint192(oldShares - newShares);
    tokenConfigs[token1].totalDebtShares -= SafeCast.toUint192(oldShares - newShares);
} else {
    tokenConfigs[token0].totalDebtShares += SafeCast.toUint192(newShares - oldShares);
    tokenConfigs[token1].totalDebtShares += SafeCast.toUint192(newShares - oldShares);
```

This code will update token0 and token1's totalDebtShares based on the shares delta. Unfortunately, Revert does not take into account that NFT positions can have an arbitrary token distribution. For example, a NFT position can have 100% distribution set to token0 and 0% distribution set to token1. When a NFT position like this is deposited into the vault and Revert needs to update the collateral, Revert assumes that the debt shares should be updated for both tokens, regardless of the distribution levels. This results in totalDebtShares for both tokens incorrectly updated.

Below is a forge test which shows how a one-side NFT position still applies totalDebtShares to a token even though the position holds none of the token.

```solidity
function testOneSidedNFTTotalDebtShareEscalation() external {
    // lend 10 USDC
    _deposit(10000000, WHALE_ACCOUNT);


    // Create one-sided NFT position
    INonfungiblePositionManager.MintParams memory mintParams = INonfungiblePositionManager.MintParams({
        token0: address(DAI),
        token1: address(WETH),
        tickLower: int24(200),
        tickUpper: int24(1000),
        fee: uint24(10000),
        recipient: TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT,
        amount0Desired: 10e18,
        amount1Desired: 0,
        amount0Min: 0,
        amount1Min: 0,
        deadline: block.timestamp + 15 minutes
    });

    vm.startPrank(TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT);
    deal(address(DAI), TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT, 30e18);
    deal(address(WETH), TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT, 30e18);

    // AUDIT: 0xa80964C5bBd1A0E95777094420555fead1A26c1e matches the DAI/WETH uniswap v3 pool
    DAI.approve(0xa80964C5bBd1A0E95777094420555fead1A26c1e, 20e18);
    WETH.approve(0xa80964C5bBd1A0E95777094420555fead1A26c1e, 20e18);

    (uint mintedTokenId ,,uint daiInNFTPosition, uint wethInNFTPosition) = NPM.mint(mintParams);

    // add collateral
    NPM.approve(address(vault), mintedTokenId);
    vault.create(mintedTokenId, TEST_NFT_ACCOUNT);
    (address token0, address token1,,, uint amount0Owed, uint amount1Owed,,) = oracle.getPositionBreakdown(TEST_NFT);
    (, uint256 fullValue, uint256 collateralValue,,) = vault.loanInfo(mintedTokenId);

    // borrow
    vault.borrow(mintedTokenId, collateralValue);

    // check results
    (,,uint192 daiDebtShare) = vault.tokenConfigs(address(DAI));
    (,,uint192 wethDebtShare) = vault.tokenConfigs(address(WETH));

    console.log("Vault DAI debt share: ", daiDebtShare);
    console.log("Vault WETH debt share: ", wethDebtShare);
    console.log("DAI in NFT position", daiInNFTPosition);
    console.log("WETH in NFT position", wethInNFTPosition);

    // AUDIT: debt share is the same for both DAI and WETH
    // Vault DAI debt share:  8999014
    // Vault WETH debt share:  8999014
    // DAI in NFT position 10000000000000000000
    // WETH in NFT position 0
}
```

## Tools Used

Manual inspection.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

When the collateral is updated, the protocol should calculate the distribution levels of token0 and token1 for the collateralized NFT position. With the correct distribution levels, Revert can then proportionally apply the shares delta between both token's totalDebtShares:

```solidity
(,, address token0, address token1,,,,,,,,) = nonfungiblePositionManager.positions(tokenId);

(,,,, amount0, amount1,,) = oracle.getPositionBreakdown(tokenId);

uint totalAmount = amount0 + amount1;

uint amount0Distribution = amount0 / totalAmount; // AUDIT: use OZ's Math library here
uint amount1Distribution = amount1 / totalAmount; // AUDIT: use OZ's Math library here

// remove previous collateral - add new collateral
if (oldShares > newShares) {
    tokenConfigs[token0].totalDebtShares -= SafeCast.toUint192((oldShares - newShares) * amount0Distribution / totalAmount); // AUDIT: use OZ's Math library here
    tokenConfigs[token1].totalDebtShares -= SafeCast.toUint192((oldShares - newShares) * amount1Distribution / totalAmount); // AUDIT: use OZ's Math library here
} else {
    tokenConfigs[token0].totalDebtShares += SafeCast.toUint192((newShares - oldShares) * amount0Distribution / totalAmount); // AUDIT: use OZ's Math library here
    tokenConfigs[token1].totalDebtShares += SafeCast.toUint192((newShares - oldShares) * amount0Distribution / totalAmount); // AUDIT: use OZ's Math library here
``` 









