# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The current implementation of the loan health assessment lacks a safety buffer between the collateral value and the debt, potentially exposing borrowers to immediate liquidation risks due to minor market fluctuations. To check if a loan is healthy this function is used

```javascript
 function _checkLoanIsHealthy(uint256 tokenId, uint256 debt)
        internal
        view
        returns (bool isHealthy, uint256 fullValue, uint256 collateralValue, uint256 feeValue)
    {
        (fullValue, feeValue,,) = oracle.getValue(tokenId, address(asset));
        uint256 collateralFactorX32 = _calculateTokenCollateralFactorX32(tokenId);
        collateralValue = fullValue.mulDiv(collateralFactorX32, Q32);
        isHealthy = collateralValue >= debt;
    }
```

which is then checked during liquidation

```javascript
(state.isHealthy, state.fullValue, state.collateralValue, state.feeValue) =
            _checkLoanIsHealthy(params.tokenId, state.debt);
        if (state.isHealthy) {
            revert NotLiquidatable();
        }
```

based on this line

```javascript
isHealthy = collateralValue >= debt;  
```

Borrowers with collateral values exactly matching their debts are susceptible to immediate liquidation even with slight market downturns.
Immediate liquidation due to minor fluctuations could unfairly penalize borrowers, especially if their loans are collateralized at the maximum loan-to-value (LTV) ratio.

## Proof of Concept
Consider a scenario where a borrower's debt exactly matches their collateral. If the collateral value experiences even a minor drop, the loan becomes undercollateralized, triggering immediate liquidation. This demonstrates the lack of a safety margin between the collateral value and the debt, leaving borrowers vulnerable to liquidation risks.

## Tools Used
manual analysis

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Introduce a safety margin between the collateral value and the debt, ensuring that loans are considered healthy only when collateral exceeds debt by a predefined margin.


