# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Denial of Service when Difference is Equal Minimum Allowed Difference in the V3Oracle contract
## Proof of Concept
```solidity
    function setMaxPoolPriceDifference(uint16 _maxPoolPriceDifference) external onlyOwner {
>>>        if (_maxPoolPriceDifference < MIN_PRICE_DIFFERENCE) {
            revert InvalidConfig();
        }
        maxPoolPriceDifference = _maxPoolPriceDifference;
        emit SetMaxPoolPriceDifference(_maxPoolPriceDifference);
    }
```
The function above shows how _maxPoolPriceDifference is set in the setMaxPoolPriceDifference(...) function, from the pointer whenever _maxPoolPriceDifference  is less than MIN_PRICE_DIFFERENCE the code reverts, but when it is equal or greater than MIN_PRICE_DIFFERENCE, then it can be set. The point of interest is the fact that when _maxPoolPriceDifference  is exactly equal to MIN_PRICE_DIFFERENCE the value should be set without issue.
The problem and reason for this report is that the validity of the equality of _maxPoolPriceDifference  was not put into consideration during usage as provided in the code below. 
```solidity
   function _checkPoolPrice(address token0, address token1, uint24 fee, uint256 derivedPoolPriceX96) internal view {
        IUniswapV3Pool pool = _getPool(token0, token1, fee);
        uint256 priceX96 = _getReferencePoolPriceX96(pool, 0);
>>>        _requireMaxDifference(priceX96, derivedPoolPriceX96, maxPoolPriceDifference);
    }

 function _requireMaxDifference(uint256 priceX96, uint256 verifyPriceX96, uint256 maxDifferenceX10000)
        internal
        pure
    {
        uint256 differenceX10000 = priceX96 > verifyPriceX96
            ? (priceX96 - verifyPriceX96) * 10000 / priceX96
            : (verifyPriceX96 - priceX96) * 10000 / verifyPriceX96;
        // if too big difference - revert
>>>        if (differenceX10000 >= maxDifferenceX10000) {
            revert PriceDifferenceExceeded();
        }
    }
```
When `differenceX10000` is exactly equal to `maxDifferenceX10000` i.e `maxPoolPriceDifference`, the code reverts forgeting that equality is a validity since it is exactly equal to the minimum allowed as explained in the first provided code earlier.
## Tools Used
Manual Review
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
The code should not revert during equality as adjusted in the code below
```solidity
 function _requireMaxDifference(uint256 priceX96, uint256 verifyPriceX96, uint256 maxDifferenceX10000)
        internal
        pure
    {
        uint256 differenceX10000 = priceX96 > verifyPriceX96
            ? (priceX96 - verifyPriceX96) * 10000 / priceX96
            : (verifyPriceX96 - priceX96) * 10000 / verifyPriceX96;
        // if too big difference - revert
---        if (differenceX10000 >= maxDifferenceX10000) {
+++        if (differenceX10000 > maxDifferenceX10000) {
            revert PriceDifferenceExceeded();
        }
    }
```


