# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-abracadabra-money/blob/1f4693fdbf33e9ad28132643e2d6f7635834c6c6/src/oracles/aggregators/MagicLpAggregator.sol#L37-L38


# Vulnerability details

The `MagicLpAggregator` is used to fetch prices of closely related assets such as MIM/USDB pairs.
The contract will use a RedStone price feed with the `latestAnswer()` method in order to fetch the price of USDB. The `latestAnswer()` data feed function will return the latest properly reported value of the data feed, but the issue is that this data could be stale or outdated.

## Impact

Stale feeds may be used because of insufficient validation which will lead to inaccurate prices for transactions. 

## Proof of Concept

The [latestAnswer()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-abracadabra-money/blob/1f4693fdbf33e9ad28132643e2d6f7635834c6c6/src/oracles/aggregators/MagicLpAggregator.sol#L37-L38) function in the `MagicLpAggregator.sol` contract will fetch oracle feed with the `latestAnswer()` function as well. 

The [latestAnswer()](https://github.com/redstone-finance/redstone-oracles-monorepo/blob/61389e31a994f27693d5afbf1f6cd5eee4fa30a7/packages/on-chain-relayer/contracts/price-feeds/PriceFeedBase.sol#L116C1-L126C4) function in the redstone protocol will fetch the data from [getValueForDataFeed](https://github.com/redstone-finance/redstone-oracles-monorepo/blob/61389e31a994f27693d5afbf1f6cd5eee4fa30a7/packages/on-chain-relayer/contracts/core/RedstoneAdapterBase.sol#L314C1-L322C4)
However as mentionned before, no validations are made and the data could be stale.

## Tools Used


## Recommended Mitigation Steps

In order to mitigate this issue I would suggest implementing fetch function that checks the data before using it, in smart contracts safety always comes first.
Here is how we can achieve this:

```diff

 ++  function latestAnswer(address oracle) private returns(int256) {
 ++     ( , rawPrice, , updatedAt, ) = oracle.latestRoundData();
 ++     require(block.timestamp - updatedAt < 20 minutes, "stale data");
 ++     return rawPrice;
    }

    function latestAnswer() public view override returns (int256) {
  ++      uint256 baseAnswerNomalized = uint256(latestAnswer(baseOracle)) * (10 ** (WAD - baseOracle.decimals()));
  ++      uint256 quoteAnswerNormalized = uint256(latestAnswer(quoteOracle)) * (10 ** (WAD - quoteOracle.decimals()));

   --     uint256 baseAnswerNomalized = uint256(baseOracle.latestAnswer()) * (10 ** (WAD - baseOracle.decimals()));
   --   uint256 quoteAnswerNormalized = uint256(quoteOracle.latestAnswer()) * (10 ** (WAD - quoteOracle.decimals()));
  ...
```








