# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-wise-lending/blob/79186b243d8553e66358c05497e5ccfd9488b5e2/contracts/WiseOracleHub/WiseOracleHub.sol#L44-L55


# Vulnerability details

## Bug Description
ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER is supposed to be a contract address that must have [IPriceFeed](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-wise-lending/blob/79186b243d8553e66358c05497e5ccfd9488b5e2/contracts/InterfaceHub/IPriceFeed.sol#L5) functionalities implemented like `latestRoundData()` etc

Only contract where this address is initialized is in WiseOracleHub's constructor . The Problem lies in the assumptions of controllable address , what i mean by that is the codebase is encoding hard-coded string "ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER" to derive the address from it.

```solidity
constructor(address _wethAddrss, address _ethPricingFeed, address _uniswapFactoryV3) {
   ...
   ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER = address(
            uint160(
                uint256(
                    keccak256(
                        abi.encodePacked(
                            "ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER"
                        )
                    )
                )
            )
        );
...
}
```

once the address is derived from it, there is no way to deploy contract with IPriceFeed functionalities on it, because that is not how the EVM works.

`You can read more about how contract address is calculated here` -> [1](https://ethereum.stackexchange.com/questions/17927/how-to-deploy-smart-contract-in-predefined-contract-address-in-private-ethereum) [2](https://ethereum.stackexchange.com/questions/760/how-is-the-address-of-an-ethereum-contract-computed/761#761) [3](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-1820) [4](https://ethereum.stackexchange.com/questions/760/how-is-the-address-of-an-ethereum-contract-computed)

Since codebase assumes that ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER is a contract address that has implemented IPriceFeed functionalities, all the instances across codebase where there is function call to ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER address, it will result in EVM Revert error, because there is no implementation on this address

`Lets demonstrate with an example`

[getETHPriceInUSD()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-wise-lending/blob/79186b243d8553e66358c05497e5ccfd9488b5e2/contracts/WiseOracleHub/OracleHelper.sol#L265) is an important function in OracleHelper.sol that is used to get price of ETH in dollars, which is used while various lending and borrowing operations
```
    function getETHPriceInUSD() public view returns (uint256)
    {
        if (_chainLinkIsDead(ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER) == true) {
            revert OracleIsDead();
        }

        ...
    }
```
it triggers `_chainLinkIsDead(address)` with ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER, which it self calls `getLatestRoundId(ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER)`
```
function _chainLinkIsDead(address _tokenAddress) internal view returns (bool){

        ...

        uint80 latestRoundId = getLatestRoundId(
            _tokenAddress
        );

        ...
}
```
Finally, `getLatestRoundId(ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER)` is going to revert because it calls `latestRoundData()` on ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER address, 

since we know there is no implementation on ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER address, therefore the function will revert will EVM error
```
 function getLatestRoundId(address _tokenAddress)public view returns(uint80 roundId) {
        (roundId , , , ,) = priceFeed[_tokenAddress].latestRoundData();
    }
```
Therefore all the functions dependent on the above functions will get DOS'ed and the whole contract functionalities are broken.

## Impact
Since WiseLending is designed modularly, there are lot of interdependent functions that rely on the function calls to ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER, since there is no way to deploy the contract with assumed functionalities (IPriceFeed) on that address because of the way it is calculated in codebase, All the dependent functions will result in EVM revert causing major Denial of Service, rendering the whole protocol useless.



## Proof of Concept
Here is the [GIST](https://gist.github.com/burhankhaja/664c67e9526f21ba071bb996458c5eb0) containing the foundry POC demonstrating that it is impossible to deploy WiseOracleHub contract because after the ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER is wrongly calculated, `_recalibratePreview()` triggers `getLatestRoundId()` which triggers `latestRoundData()` on ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER that eventually results in DOS (EVM Revert)
```solidity
constructor(...) {
....
heartBeat[ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER] = _recalibratePreview(ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER);
}

```


## Tools Used
Manual Analysis, Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Take address parameter in constructor for the ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER, that must be deployed with the IPriceFeed functionalities
```
 constructor(
        address _wethAddrss,
        address _ethPricingFeed,
        address _uniswapFactoryV3,
        address _ethUsdPlaceholder
    )
        Declarations(
            _wethAddrss,
            _ethPricingFeed,
            _uniswapFactoryV3
        )
    {
        ...
        ETH_USD_PLACEHOLDER = _ethUsdPlaceholder;
}
```



