# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-wise-lending/blob/79186b243d8553e66358c05497e5ccfd9488b5e2/contracts/WiseOracleHub/OracleHelper.sol#L131


# Vulnerability details

## **Vulnerability Details:**

The protocol uses two data sources to fetch prices within the [_validateAnswer](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-wise-lending/blob/79186b243d8553e66358c05497e5ccfd9488b5e2/contracts/WiseOracleHub/OracleHelper.sol#L131) function: the Uniswap time-weighted average price (TWAP) over a 30-minute period, and the most recent Chainlink price. These prices are assessed against each other, and if the deviation between them is within the allowed range (2.5%), the Chainlink price is used.

```solidity
    function _validateAnswer(
        address _tokenAddress
    )
        internal
        view
        returns (uint256)
    {
        UniTwapPoolInfo memory uniTwapPoolInfoStruct = uniTwapPoolInfo[
            _tokenAddress
        ];

        uint256 fetchTwapValue;

        if (uniTwapPoolInfoStruct.oracle > ZERO_ADDRESS) {
            fetchTwapValue = latestResolverTwap(
                _tokenAddress
            );
        }

        uint256 answer = _getChainlinkAnswer(
            _tokenAddress
        );

        if (tokenAggregatorFromTokenAddress[_tokenAddress] > ZERO_AGGREGATOR) {
            _compareMinMax(
                tokenAggregatorFromTokenAddress[_tokenAddress],
                int192(uint192(answer))
            );
        }

        if (fetchTwapValue > 0) {

            uint256 relativeDifference = _getRelativeDifference(
                answer,
                fetchTwapValue
            );

            _compareDifference(
                relativeDifference
            );
        }

        return answer;
    }
```

There are a few possible problems with this setup:

- The 2.5% threshold for price differences might render the system ineffective in periods of sharp price movements. The discrepancy in the methods for price determination—Chainlink offering latest prices and Uniswap providing a 30-minute TWAP—means significant market shifts will likely cross the allowed difference.
- Additionally, the absence of an alternative latest price increases the impact. If the Chainlink feed reports inaccurately or if price changes exceed the allowed difference, the protocol lacks a fallback mechanism.

As a result, in the following situation users will be prevented from executing essential transactions such as withdrawals, loans, or the liquidation of unhealthy positions. This could significantly impair the functionality of a large portion of the protocol.

## **Tools Used:**

Manual analysis

## **Recommendation:**

The protocol needs to incorporate a fallback mechanism for situations where the standard process for validating price requests fails. Considering the high volatility in cryptocurrency markets, a 2.5% tolerance level may be overly stringent, leading to numerous transaction reverts.


