https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/main/contracts/ousg/ousgInstantManager.sol#L388


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
OUSGInstantManager.sol relies on the [SHV ETF](https://etherscan.io/address/0xc04611C43842220fd941515F86d1DDdB15F04e46#readContract) price feed from Chainlink. However, the contract incorrectly assumes 18 decimals instead of 8 decimals. Consequently, the functions `_mint()` and `_redeem()` are likely to consistently fail. If no failures occur, the incorrect conversion rate between USDC and OUSG will lead to significant losses.

## Proof of Concept
OUSGInstantManager.sol utilizes RWAOracleExternalComparisonCheck.sol, which fetches the price feed from Chainlink to calculate the conversion rate between USDC and OUSG.
```solidity
  function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
    (price, ) = oracle.getPriceData();
    require(
      price > MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE,
      "OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice: Price unexpectedly low"
    );
  }
```
The function `getOUSGPrice()` incorporates a Minimum OUSG check to prevent the use of bad data by verifying `price` against `MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE`. Notably, the constant `MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE = 105e18` is defined in 18 decimals. However, the [SHV ETF](https://etherscan.io/address/0xc04611C43842220fd941515F86d1DDdB15F04e46#readContract) returns price values in 8 decimals.

This significant discrepancy is likely to cause `_mint()` and `_redeem()` to revert almost all the time. It is improbable for the SHV/USD price to increase by this much.

n the rare event of such occurrence, `_mint()` calculates a significantly larger `ousgAmountOut` in `_getMintAmount()`, where the price feed is incorrectly assumed to be in 18 decimals.

```solidity
  function _getMintAmount(
    uint256 usdcAmountIn,
    uint256 price
  ) internal view returns (uint256 ousgAmountOut) {
    uint256 amountE36 = _scaleUp(usdcAmountIn) * 1e18;
    ousgAmountOut = amountE36 / price;
  }
```

Conversely, for `_redeem()`, a significantly smaller `usdcAmountToRedeem` is calculated by `_getRedemptionAmount()` due to the incorrectly assumed 18 decimal price feed.
```solidity
  function _getRedemptionAmount(
    uint256 ousgAmountBurned,
    uint256 price
  ) internal view returns (uint256 usdcOwed) {
    uint256 amountE36 = ousgAmountBurned * price;
    usdcOwed = _scaleDown(amountE36 / 1e18); 
  }
```

## Tools Used
Manual Review
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
`MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE` should be 105e8.
`_getMintAmount()` and `_getRedemptionAmount()` should also adjust accordingly.


