# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/78779c30bebfd46e6f416b03066c55d587e8b30b/contracts/ousg/ousgInstantManager.sol#L480


# Vulnerability details

# No staleness check on Oracle in instantRedeem in Manager contract and unwrap in rOUSG flow

Within the redemption/minting flow for OUSGInstantManager, if the `RWADynamicOracle` or any oracle for that matter is stale value will not be accrued. And the oracle will return the previous range end. Consequenty if the `range.end` has elapsed value is not being accrued. This is especially dangerous when pairing with instant minting and redemption functionality. A user may unknowingly instanlty redeem their rOUSG/OUSG tokens in the period after `range.end` has elapsed prior to a new range being set and consequently forfeit their yield. 

**recomendation**
Add an oracle livelyness check on in the manager contract. It seems that the `RWADynamicOracle` allows for the timestamp to be passed but it will always return the current timestamp. I would recomend returning the timestamp from which the price was derived.

```contracts/rwaOracles/RWADynamicOracle.sol:L#77
  function getPrice() public view whenNotPaused returns (uint256 price, uint256 derivedTimestamp) {
    uint256 length = ranges.length;
    for (uint256 i = length; i > 0; --i) {
      Range storage range = ranges[i - 1];
      if (range.start <= block.timestamp) {
        if (range.end <= block.timestamp) {
          return (derivePrice(range, range.end - 1), range.end - 1);
        } else {
          return (derivePrice(range, block.timestamp), block.timestamp);
        }
      }
    }
  }
```
Then pass this additional return to the `getPriceData` function, and then validate the timestamp from which the rOUSG/OUSG price is derived like so.

```contracts/ousg/ousgInstantManager.sol:L#479
  function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
    uint256 timestamp;
    (price, timestamp) = oracle.getPriceData();
    require(
      price > MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE,
      "OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice: Price unexpectedly low"
    );
    require(
        timestamp == block.timestamp,
        "Oracle Price is Stale"
    );
  }
```

## Impact 
User may mint/redeem OUSG/rOUSG at an incorrect value, resulting in a financial loss to either the protocol or the user.




