# Vulnerability details

# Pausing `RWADynamicOracle` Inability to call Admin Function burn shares even if rOUSG remains unpaused

If the `RWADynamicOracle` is paused the admin function `burn(account,amount)` will cease to work, Even if rOUSG is in an `unPaused` state.

This is due to the conversion between amount and shares that this function implies. It is not best practice to have pause functionality on a tertiary contract break admin functions on the token contract.

```
function burn(
    address _account,
    uint256 _amount
  ) external onlyRole(BURNER_ROLE) {
    uint256 ousgSharesAmount = getSharesByROUSG(_amount);
    if (ousgSharesAmount < OUSG_TO_ROUSG_SHARES_MULTIPLIER)
      revert UnwrapTooSmall();

    _burnShares(_account, ousgSharesAmount);

    ousg.transfer(
      msg.sender,
      ousgSharesAmount / OUSG_TO_ROUSG_SHARES_MULTIPLIER
    );
    emit Transfer(address(0), msg.sender, getROUSGByShares(ousgSharesAmount));
    emit TransferShares(_account, address(0), ousgSharesAmount);
  }
```


## Tools Used
Visual analysis, Foundry

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Given that shares are just ousg units scaled up by 1e5, it would be better to have this function burn shares as opposed to having the function take rOUSG `_amount` as a parameter.

eg:
```
function burn(
    address _account,
    uint256 _shares
  ) external onlyRole(BURNER_ROLE) {

    if (_shares < OUSG_TO_ROUSG_SHARES_MULTIPLIER)
      revert UnwrapTooSmall();

    _burnShares(_account, _shares);

    ousg.transfer(
      msg.sender,
      _shares / OUSG_TO_ROUSG_SHARES_MULTIPLIER
    );
    emit TransferShares(_account, address(0), _shares);
  }
```

If this change is made, rOUSG will remain burnable via the admin even though the `RWADynamicOracle` is in a paused state





