Invalid Validation

# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/main/contracts/ousg/rOUSG.sol#L378-L380


# Vulnerability details

In order to know the `OUSG` price, contracts `ousgInstantManager` and `rOUSG` query the oracle via the function `getOUSGPrice()`. Before using the price from the oracle, the contract `ousgInstantManager` does a sanity check that ensures that the price isn't unexpectedly low, the minimum allowed value is `105e18`.

However, the contract `rOUSG` doesn't do this sanity check. Therefore, in a scenario where the oracle malfunctions and it returns a price lower than `MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE`, all the mint and redeem functions on `ousgInstantManager` will revert, preventing an unsafe usage of the oracle. 

On the other hand, when the oracle malfunctions and it returns a price lower than `MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE`, the `rOUSG` contract will not block any functionality, and that will cause loss of funds for users unaware of the current oracle malfunction. 

Given this scenario, a user could easily lose funds by the following ways:

1. Transfering too many shares to other users/contracts by specifying an amount of tokens relative to the correct (and higher) price.
2. Unwrapping too many shares and receiving less tokens due to the wrong price

## Impact

When the `OUSG` oracle malfunctions and it returns a price unexpectedly low, the functionality at `rOUSG` contract won't be halted, causing losses of funds to users unaware of the problem. 

## Proof of Concept

The `ousgInstantManager` contract performs a sanity check when getting the `OUSG` price:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/main/contracts/ousg/ousgInstantManager.sol#L481-L484
```solidity

  // Safety circuit breaker in case of Oracle malfunction
  uint256 public constant MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE = 105e18;

  // ...

  /**
   * @notice Returns the current price of OUSG in USDC
   *
   * @dev Sanity check: this function will revert if the price is unexpectedly low
   *
   * @return price The current price of OUSG in USDC
   */
  function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
    (price, ) = oracle.getPriceData();
    require(
      price > MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE,
      "OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice: Price unexpectedly low"
    );
  }
```

However, the `rOUSG` contract doesn't do the sanity check:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/main/contracts/ousg/rOUSG.sol#L378-L380
```solidity
  function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
    (price, ) = oracle.getPriceData();
  }
```

## Tools Used

Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

To mitigate this issue is recommended to implement the sanity check on the reported `OUSG` price withing the `rOUSG` contract:

```diff
  function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
    (price, ) = oracle.getPriceData();
+   require(price > 105e18, Price unexpectedly low); 
  }
```


## Assessed type

Oracle

