# Vulnerability details

## Impact
In `rOUSG::getOUSGPrice()` and `ousgInstantManager::getOUSGPrice()`, there are no checks to verify if the price data returned from the [`RWAOracleExternalComparisonCheck`](https://etherscan.io/address/0x0502c5ae08E7CD64fe1AEDA7D6e229413eCC6abe#code) oracle is stale. Consequently, if this oracle fails to update its price for more than 24 hours, both contracts will receive outdated information.

## Proof of Concept
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/main/contracts/ousg/ousgInstantManager.sol#L479-L485

ousgInstantManager.sol
```solidity
    function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
       (price,) = oracle.getPriceData(); /// @audit no check for staleness of price data
       require(price > MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE, "OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice: Price unexpectedly low");
    }
```

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/main/contracts/ousg/rOUSG.sol#L378-L380

rOUSG.sol
```solidity
    function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
        (price,) = oracle.getPriceData(); /// @audit no check for staleness of price data
    }
```

## Tools Used
Manual Analysis

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
To address this issue, you should retrieve the `priceTimestamp` returned from the [`RWAOracleExternalComparisonCheck`](https://etherscan.io/address/0x0502c5ae08E7CD64fe1AEDA7D6e229413eCC6abe#code) oracle, indicating the last time it received correct data. Then, in the `getOUSGPrice()` function, you should check if this timestamp is stale by verifying if it is not more than 24 hours old (underlying chainlink heartbeat).

rOUSG.sol
```diff
    function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
-        (price,) = oracle.getPriceData();
+        (price, priceTimestamp) = oracle.getPriceData();
+        require(block.timestamp <= priceTimestamp + 86400, "Stale price returned from oracle");
    }
```

ousgInstantManager.sol
```diff
    function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
-       (price,) = oracle.getPriceData();
+       (price, priceTimestamp) = oracle.getPriceData();
+       require(block.timestamp <= priceTimestamp + 86400, "Stale price returned from oracle");
        require(price > MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE, "OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice: Price unexpectedly low");
