# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Chainlink data feeds do not provide data stream, but rather an answer in a `latestAnswer` value. The protocol uses a custom price feed oracle where the price needs to be updated at least once every 23 hours, as seen in: https://etherscan.io/address/0x0502c5ae08E7CD64fe1AEDA7D6e229413eCC6abe#code

```javascript
function setPrice(int256 newPrice) external override onlyRole(SETTER_ROLE) {
...

    ChainlinkRoundData memory round = _getLatestChainlinkRoundData();
    // Chainlink price update must be recent 25 hours
    if (block.timestamp > round.updatedAt + MAX_CL_WINDOW) {
      revert ChainlinkOraclePriceStale();
    }

    // Ensure at least `MIN_PRICE_UPDATE_WINDOW` seconds have passed since
    // last RWA price update               23 hours
    if (block.timestamp < priceTimestamp + MIN_PRICE_UPDATE_WINDOW) {
      revert PriceUpdateWindowViolation();
    }
...
    rwaPrice = newPrice;
    priceTimestamp = block.timestamp;
...
```

The price data is saved in `rwaPrice` and `priceTimestamp` variables, which are then read by the protocol by calling `getPricaData()`:
```javascript
function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
  (price, ) = oracle.getPriceData();
}
```

However `getPriceData()` just returns the values of price and timestamp.

If the external oracle fails to update or some of the checks fails, the price will become stale and there is no check in the current implementation for stale price. This will cause the code to execute with prices that don’t reflect the current pricing resulting in a potential loss of funds for users.

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Add a stale price check

```diff
+      uint256 private constant MAX_TIME_LIMIT = 25 hours;
...
  function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
+    uint256 timestamp;
+    (price, timestamp) = oracle.getPriceData();
-    (price, ) = oracle.getPriceData();
    require(price > MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE, "OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice: Price unexpectedly low");
+    require(timestamp < block.timestamp + MAX_TIME_LIMIT, "OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice: Stale price");
  }
```





