## Recommended Mitigation Steps
I think there could be multiple steps to mitigate the issue. However, my recommendation is the following:

1. First of all, check inside [setFeeReceiver](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/be2e9ebca6fca460c5b0253970ab280701a15ca1/contracts/ousg/ousgInstantManager.sol#L650-L656) if account isn't blacklisted using `isBlacklisted` method from USDC contract. You'll need to provide new interface

### interface - IUSDC
```solidity
// SPDX-LICENSE-Identifier: NONE
pragma solidity 0.8.16;

import "contracts/external/openzeppelin/contracts/token/IERC20.sol";

interface IUSDC is IERC20 {
  function isBlacklisted(address _account) external view returns (bool);
}
```

### OUSGInstantManager
```diff
// USDC contract
-  IERC20 public immutable usdc; // 0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48;
+  IUSDC public immutable usdc; // 0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48;
```

*constructor*
```diff
require(
  IERC20Metadata(_usdc).decimals() == IERC20Metadata(_buidl).decimals(),
  "OUSGInstantManager: USDC decimals must be equal to BUIDL decimals"
);
- usdc = IERC20(_usdc);
+ usdc = IUSDC(_usdc);
  usdcReceiver = _usdcReciever;
  feeReceiver = _feeReceiver;
  oracle = IRWAOracle(_ousgOracle);
  ousg = IRWALike(_ousg);
```

*setFeeReceiver*
```diff
function setFeeReceiver(
  address _feeReceiver
) external override onlyRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE) {
  require(_feeReceiver != address(0), "FeeReceiver cannot be 0x0");
+ require(!usdc.isBlacklisted(_feeReceiver), "feeReceiver is blacklisted");
  emit FeeReceiverSet(feeReceiver, _feeReceiver);
  feeReceiver = _feeReceiver;
}
```

2. However `feeReceiver` can get blacklisted while already being set. So to prevent this we can add a new state variable that will track fee amount and function that will withdraw those fees. If `feeReceiver` is blacklisted we can simply set a new `feeReceiver` which he'll easily withdraw fees:

```diff
+  uint256 private usdcFees;

+  function withdrawFees() {
+    require(msg.sender == feeReceiver, "Not fee receiver");
+    usdc.transfer(feeReceiver, usdcFees);
+  }
```

In this code snippets you need to change transferring USDC to adding amount of fees to `usdcFees` variable:

- https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/be2e9ebca6fca460c5b0253970ab280701a15ca1/contracts/ousg/ousgInstantManager.sol#L317-L317

- https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/be2e9ebca6fca460c5b0253970ab280701a15ca1/contracts/ousg/ousgInstantManager.sol#L451-L451


