# Vulnerability details

## Issue Description

In `OUSGInstantManager`, a minimum oracle price for OUSG is set `MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE` and is used as a safety circuit breaker in cases when the oracle experiences a malfunction.

This min price is checked when fetching the OUSG price in `getOUSGPrice()` function, and it will revert in case the price drop below that minimum disabling in the process any mint/redeem operations (as `getOUSGPrice()` is invoked in all of them):

```solidity
function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
(price, ) = oracle.getPriceData();
    require(
        price > MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE,
        "OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice: Price unexpectedly low"
    );
}
```

The issue now is that the same safety measure is not implemented in the `ROUSG` contract, there also the price of OUSG is used to value the amount of shares to be transferred/burned when transferring or unwrapping ROUSG respectively:

```solidity
function unwrap(uint256 _rOUSGAmount) external whenNotPaused {
    require(_rOUSGAmount > 0, "rOUSG: can't unwrap zero rOUSG tokens");
    uint256 ousgSharesAmount = getSharesByROUSG(_rOUSGAmount);
    if (ousgSharesAmount < OUSG_TO_ROUSG_SHARES_MULTIPLIER)
      revert UnwrapTooSmall();
    _burnShares(msg.sender, ousgSharesAmount);
    ...
}


function _transfer(
    address _sender,
    address _recipient,
    uint256 _amount
) internal {
    uint256 _sharesToTransfer = getSharesByROUSG(_amount);
    ...
}
```

Because the `ROUSG.getOUSGPrice()` function just fetches the OUSG price and doesn't checks it, users might be at risk of losing a portion of their funds when trying to transfer or unwrap ROUSG if the oracle did experience a malfunction and price dropped below that minimum price.

## Impact

Oracle safety circuit breaker not implemented in `ROUSG` which could potentially result in users losing funds while trying to transfer or unwrap their ROUSG tokens.

## Tools Used

Manual review, VS Code

## Recommended Mitigation

Implement the safety circuit breaker in `ROUSG.getOUSGPrice()` function as it is done in the `OUSGInstantManager.getOUSGPrice()` function.



