# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/78779c30bebfd46e6f416b03066c55d587e8b30b/contracts/ousg/rOUSG.sol#L378-L380


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

User get less amount of `rOUSG`  than what it should (for the worst case if `getOUSGPrice` return 0, then user got 0 amount) and amount of shares will locked in the `OUSGInstantManager`

## Proof of Concept

The scenario will be :

1. Alice call `OUSGInstantManager::mintRebasingOUSG()`, she have 100 000 USDC
2. Let see in the `OUSGInstantManager::mintRebasingOUSG()` codebase :

```solidity
  function mintRebasingOUSG(
    uint256 usdcAmountIn
  )
    external
    override
    nonReentrant
    whenMintNotPaused
    returns (uint256 rousgAmountOut)
  {
    uint256 ousgAmountOut = _mint(usdcAmountIn, address(this));
    ousg.approve(address(rousg), ousgAmountOut);
    rousg.wrap(ousgAmountOut);
    rousgAmountOut = rousg.getROUSGByShares(
      ousgAmountOut * OUSG_TO_ROUSG_SHARES_MULTIPLIER
    );
    rousg.transfer(msg.sender, rousgAmountOut);
    emit InstantMintRebasingOUSG(
      msg.sender,
      usdcAmountIn,
      ousgAmountOut,
      rousgAmountOut
    );
  }
```

- First, `OUSG` will be minted in `OUSGInstantManager` according to the amount of `USDC` given by Alice and`OUSG` approve `rOUSG` address according to `OUSG` amount that minted
- Second, amount of `OUSG` [wrap](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/78779c30bebfd46e6f416b03066c55d587e8b30b/contracts/ousg/rOUSG.sol#L415-L422) in `rOUSG` contract and convert to shares then update the shares for `OUSGInstantManager`
- Third, amount of shares will be convert to `rOUSG` using [rOUSG.getROUSGByShares](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/78779c30bebfd46e6f416b03066c55d587e8b30b/contracts/ousg/rOUSG.sol#L373-L376)
- Last, with [rOUSG.transfer](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/78779c30bebfd46e6f416b03066c55d587e8b30b/contracts/ousg/rOUSG.sol#L220-L223) function, `rOUSG` will be convert to shares, reduce amount of shares in `OUSGInstantManager`, and update shares for Alice

The main issue is, there are no prevent mechanism in `rOUSG`::`getOUSGPrice()` which is used on [rOUSG.getROUSGByShares](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/78779c30bebfd46e6f416b03066c55d587e8b30b/contracts/ousg/rOUSG.sol#L373-L376) . If the return value not worth what it should be because `oracle.getPriceData()` malfunction, in worst case if return value = 0 then user got nothing and shares will locked in `OUSGInstantManager`. 

This also happens because the protocol is inconsistent, in `OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice()` there is a prevent mechanism using a minimum value for the price so that if the return value is below the minimum value, the function will revert. But in `rOUSG`::`getOUSGPrice()` this mechanism doesn’t exist.

Below are the differences in the logic of the `getOUSGPrice` function :
`rOUSG`::`getOUSGPrice()` , there is no prevent mechanism 

```solidity
  function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
    (price, ) = oracle.getPriceData();
  }
```

`OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice()`, have prevent mechanism

```solidity
  function getOUSGPrice() public view returns (uint256 price) {
    (price, ) = oracle.getPriceData();
    require(
      price > MINIMUM_OUSG_PRICE,
      "OUSGInstantManager::getOUSGPrice: Price unexpectedly low"
    );
  }
```

Similar case on `OUSGInstantManager::redeemRebasingOUSG()` :

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-03-ondo-finance/blob/78779c30bebfd46e6f416b03066c55d587e8b30b/contracts/ousg/ousgInstantManager.sol#L362-L386

