# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-uniswap-foundation/blob/5a2761c8277541a24bc551fbd624413b384bea94/src/V3FactoryOwner.sol#L181-L198


# Vulnerability details

## Impact
MEV searchers provide a fixed payoutAmount of WETH to collect the pool's protocol fees. 
Generally, MEV searchers are incentivized to do so when the value of the protocol fee is slightly greater than the value of the payoutAmount amount of WETH, and competition among MEV searchers ensures that the protocol value is leaked as low as possible.

```solidity
  function claimFees(
    IUniswapV3PoolOwnerActions _pool,
    address _recipient,
    uint128 _amount0Requested,
    uint128 _amount1Requested
  ) external returns (uint128, uint128) {
    PAYOUT_TOKEN.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(REWARD_RECEIVER), payoutAmount);
    REWARD_RECEIVER.notifyRewardAmount(payoutAmount);
    (uint128 _amount0, uint128 _amount1) =
      _pool.collectProtocol(_recipient, _amount0Requested, _amount1Requested);

    // Protect the caller from receiving less than requested. See `collectProtocol` for context.
    if (_amount0 < _amount0Requested || _amount1 < _amount1Requested) {
      revert V3FactoryOwner__InsufficientFeesCollected();
    }
    emit FeesClaimed(address(_pool), msg.sender, _recipient, _amount0, _amount1);
    return (_amount0, _amount1);
  }

```
However, the problem here is that the pool's protocol fee does not grow linearly, the protocol fee grows as the trade's amount increases. 
This leads to a situation where at the edge, a single transaction suddenly grows the pool's protocol fee, while the MEV searchers only need to provide the fixed payoutAmount of WETH, which may significantly leak the pool's value.
```solidity
            if (cache.feeProtocol > 0) {
                uint256 delta = step.feeAmount / cache.feeProtocol;
                step.feeAmount -= delta;
                state.protocolFee += uint128(delta);
            }
```
Consider the payoutAmount of 1, i.e. the MEV searcher provides 1 ETH worth 3500 USD.
The pool fee is currently worth 3000 USD and there is no MEV searcher acting.
Then, a transaction bumps the pool fee to 8000 USD and the MEV searcher calls claimFees, which significantly leaks the pool's value.

