```

An attacker sees that the PrincipalToken contract is about to be deployed and front runs the transaction by depositing a large amount of tokens into the specified ibt vault. The `ibtRate` is then set at a really low rate. The attacker can then withdraw from the vault and now the token has been deployed with a very small `ibtRate` affecting all future users and depositors of the Principal token. The attacker could also deflate the value returned by `previewRedeem` and cause the `ibtRate` to be very small therefore also benefiting from the price manipulation.

