**Step 4** -> In the [`UTBExecutor::execute()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-decent/blob/main/src/UTBExecutor.sol#L41) function, it will get it's initial balance of the ERC777 tokens, it would return 0. Then it will transfer the ERC777 tokens from the `UTB` contract to itself (remember, the UTB approved it to spend them).

**Step 5** -> When the `UTBExecutor` contract in the `execute()` function tranfers the ERC777 tokens from UTB to itself, the `tokensReceived()` hook function will be called in the malicious contract set as the interface implementer for the `UTBExecutor` contract (Check Step 1).

**Step 6** -> When the `tokensReceived()` function is triggered in the malicious contract, the malicious contract wants to make the `UTBExecutor` execute an arbitrary call to transfer the ERC777 tokens the `UTBExecutor` currently owns (beloning to victim), to the attacker. For it to do so, it'll call the [`UTB::swapAndExecute()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-decent/blob/main/src/UTB.sol#L108) function and instruct it to conduct a swap and an arbitrary call. The swap is not needed for the attack, but it's needed for the function to work and reach the point where we can make the `UTBExecutor` execute an arbitrary call. The malicious contract will call the [`UTB::swapAndExecute()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-decent/blob/main/src/UTB.sol#L108) function as I mentioned and instruct it to conduct a swap between 1 USDC and DAI (malicious contract approved UTB to spend the 1 USDC previously) and then instruct it to execute an arbitrary call to the ERC777 token contract with `transferFrom(UTBExecutor, attacker)` calldata

**Step 7** -> The UTBExecutor will execute an [arbitrary call](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-decent/blob/011f62059f3a0b1f3577c8ccd1140f0cf3e7bb29/src/UTBExecutor.sol#L65) to the ERC777 token contract and transfer the 1,000 ERC777 tokens it owns (belonging to the victim), to the attacker. Then it will [refund the attacker his 1 DAI](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-decent/blob/011f62059f3a0b1f3577c8ccd1140f0cf3e7bb29/src/UTBExecutor.sol#L80) resulting from the swap conducted by UTB. It will refund it because the 1 DAI was not used in the arbitrary call. It knows how much to refund after an arbitrary call by comparing the values of [`initBalance`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-decent/blob/011f62059f3a0b1f3577c8ccd1140f0cf3e7bb29/src/UTBExecutor.sol#L59) and [`remainingBalance`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-decent/blob/011f62059f3a0b1f3577c8ccd1140f0cf3e7bb29/src/UTBExecutor.sol#L73).

**Step 8** -> The execution flow will now return to the victim's arbitrary call, [at line 62](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-decent/blob/011f62059f3a0b1f3577c8ccd1140f0cf3e7bb29/src/UTBExecutor.sol#L62C23-L62C30).

