```
The performSwap(...) Funcion above shows how swap is done between two token, based on how the code is implemented in this contract, the conditional statemnet that checks if swapParams.tokenIn == address(0), if true, is interpreted to mean tokenIn is a native Token or Eth after which deposit is done. At the same time if the condition is false necessary implementation is done since tokenIn is not a native token.
the problem is after this two conditional statement a non-native token approval is done for swapper, this would be correct for the non native token but it would be an error for the native token as it would mean Swapper can double spend by using both the native and non-native token.
It should be noted that address can still use the approval to spend token even outside of this function, as long as the approval is not revoked or expired. This is because the approval is stored in the ERC-20 token contract, not in the function that grants it. The approval allows the address to call the transferFrom function of the ERC-20 token contract, which can be done from any other contract or externally owned account (EOA) that has access to the address

More details on approval of Token transfer can be seen in this stack exchange discussion at https://ethereum.stackexchange.com/questions/134524/can-you-approve-tokens-held-in-one-smart-contract-to-another-smart-contract
