# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Wrong Amout Approval For Target Address when _executeWeth(...) function is called in DecentBridgeExecutor Contract which would allow target address to spend amount than expected of it
## Proof of Concept
```solidity
  function _executeWeth(
        address from,
        address target,
        uint256 amount,
        bytes memory callPayload
    ) private {
        uint256 balanceBefore = weth.balanceOf(address(this));
>>>        weth.approve(target, amount);

        (bool success, ) = target.call(callPayload);

        if (!success) {
            weth.transfer(from, amount);
            return;
        }

        uint256 remainingAfterCall = amount -
            (balanceBefore - weth.balanceOf(address(this)));

        // refund the sender with excess WETH
>>>        weth.transfer(from, remainingAfterCall);
    }
```
The Code provided above shows the implementation of the _executeWeth(...) function, The point of interest is the Approval done for target address to use a token amount, but at the last line of the function excess value from this same amount was sent back to the "from" address, but the fact is that the approval given to target address still stand no matter what, the correct implementation would be to approve the amount minus the excess value to the target since the excess value would be sent back and not the whole amount.
It is important to note that the address can still use the approval to spend token outside of that function, as long as the approval is not revoked or expired. This is because the approval is stored in the ERC-20 token contract, not in the function that grants it. The approval allows the address to call the transferFrom function of the ERC-20 token contract, which can be done from any other contract or externally owned account (EOA) that has access to the address.
## Tools Used
Manual Review
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
The approval given to target address should only be the amount minus the excess value as adjusted in the code provided below since the excess value would be sent back
```solidity
