# Vulnerability details

## [M-1] `UTBExecutor`: `execute()` Can Have Unnecessary Approvals If the Target Call Fails

Only reporting this here because the project specifically asked wardens to look for leftover/unnecessary approvals.

`UTBExecutor.execute()` approves then calls the intended target with a low-level call, which when reverted doesn't revert the whole tx. However, the approval amount remains unused and can then be used unintentionally afterwards, though the contract isn't designed to have tokens stored.

